const e={P2400:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Control Circuit/Open","P2400 is stored when the engine computer finds the drive line of the evaporative leak detection pump open, so the pump cannot be switched for the tank leak test. GM's tables for the sealed fuel system of the Volt (2011, 2016) compare the commanded and actual driver state and treat a low voltage in the off state, equal to more than 200 kOhm to ground, as an open;",["Corroded or loose pump connector, broken wire in the drive line","Open winding or internal fault in the leak detection pump","Coolant in the pump's vacuum supply line from a failed coolant pump changeover valve (VW Touareg 3.6)","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light","EVAP readiness monitor stays incomplete","No noticeable change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P2401","P2402","P2404","P043E"],"משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2401:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Control Circuit Low","P2401 means the control line of the leak detection pump is pulled to ground level, usually by chafed insulation touching the body or by an internal pump fault. GM's 2016 Volt table checks the low-side driver while it is switched off; a near-zero impedance of about 0.5 Ohm to controller ground counts as a short, and 20 of 25 samples of 250 ms set a Type B code over two trips.",["Control wire chafed through and touching ground near the tank or rear wheel arch","Internal short inside the leak detection pump","Water ingress in the pump connector causing a leakage path to ground"],["Check engine light","Leak test not completed, EVAP readiness missing"],2,1,["P2400","P2402","P2405"],"משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2402:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Control Circuit High","P2402 points to the opposite fault of P2401: the pump control line sits at supply voltage or the pump draws too much current. GM's Volt tables call it a short to power detected while the driver is on; when it is active the ECM runs an intrusive check, running the pump for 15 s on command, with a Type B code after 20 failed samples out of 25.",["Leak detection pump motor seized or drawing excessive current","Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage feed","Control module software that does not clear the fault after repair (Acura TLX Type S recall)"],["Check engine light that may persist after repair until software is updated","EVAP readiness incomplete, inspection may fail"],2,1,["P2400","P2401","P2406"],"משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2403:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Sense Circuit/Open","The sense circuit carries the feedback by which the engine computer knows what the leak detection pump is actually doing. P2403 is logged when that feedback is missing as if the line were open. The January 2014 Golf book from VW sets it once the sense signal stays at a low voltage for more than 0.5 s.",["Broken feedback wire or backed-out terminal at the pump connector","Water or ice trapped in the pump or its filter (Jaguar XJ)","Failed feedback element inside the pump"],["Check engine light","EVAP monitor not completed","More often after winter driving or car washes"],2,1,["P2404","P2405","P2406","P2400"],"חישת משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2404:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P2404 is a plausibility code: the pump feedback is electrically present but does not behave as the leak test expects. VW's 2014 Golf data book sets it when the sense signal stays high for more than 30.4 s (12 s on another engine) over 30 checks, or when high signal time during pumping adds up to more than 10 s.",["Condensation inside the leak check module (Subaru ELCM, software update available)","Worn or sticking pump that no longer reaches its expected state in time","Coolant or debris in the pump's vacuum or vent line"],["Check engine light, often returning after clearing","EVAP readiness not set"],2,1,["P2403","P2407","P24B9","P0442"],"משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P2405:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Sense Circuit Low","P2405 is set when the feedback signal of the leak detection pump stays below its permitted window, typically from a short to ground on the sense line or a fault inside the pump. No public source states a voltage threshold for this code. It appears in Maserati's sheet MAS002203 (2020) for DMTL-equipped M156/M157/M161 petrol models from MY17, which notes that most DMTL checks run with the key off;",["Internal DMTL pump fault, often after dirt ingress through the dust filter","Sense wire shorted to ground","Corroded connector at the pump mounted near the rear wheel arch"],["Check engine light, possibly set while the car is parked","No effect on drivability"],2,1,["P2403","P2406","P2401"],"משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P2406:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Sense Circuit High","P2406 is the mirror image of P2405: the pump feedback reads above its allowed range, as with a short to a voltage source or a sense line that floats high. Thresholds are not published. Jaguar's JTB00436 for the XJ (X351) includes P2406 among DMTL faults caused by water or ice from tyre spray caught in the pump filter and has the canister and filler pipe renewed.",["Water or ice from road spray in the pump filter (Jaguar XJ)","Sense wire shorted to a voltage feed or open ground at the pump","Pump damaged by contamination entering through the dust filter"],["Check engine light","Fault often appears after wet or freezing weather"],2,1,["P2403","P2405","P2402"],"משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P2407:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Sense Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2407 reports a pump feedback that jumps around instead of staying steady. On current-measuring DMTL pumps VW's 2014 Golf and Touareg books define it precisely: the pump current fluctuates by more than 1 mA during the reference measurement, or it drops by more than 6 mA for at least 3 s while pumping, checked with the engine off and on.",["Over-sensitive diagnostic calibration, fixed by ECM software update (Audi, VW 2022-23)","Loose contact or corrosion at the pump connector","Worn pump motor with unstable current draw"],["Check engine light, sometimes only after the car has been parked","Code returns irregularly after clearing"],2,1,["P2404","P2403","P0442"],"חישת משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2408:["Fuel Cap Sensor/Switch Circuit","P2408 is the general circuit code for a sensor or switch that tells the engine computer whether the fuel cap or filler is closed. It is set when that circuit shows a fault not narrowed down to low, high, plausibility or dropout, which are P2410, P2411, P2409 and P2412. No manufacturer publicly documents this code; most systems infer the cap state from pressure instead.",["Faulty fuel cap or filler switch","Damaged wiring or connector at the filler neck","Aftermarket cap that does not actuate the switch correctly"],["Check engine light or fuel cap warning","EVAP leak test may be skipped"],1,1,["P2409","P2410","P2411","P2412","P0457"],"חיישן/מתג מכסה דלק — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2409:["Fuel Cap Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance","P2409 is the plausibility code of the fuel cap sensor family: the circuit is electrically sound, but the reported cap state does not fit other information. A switch that never changes over a refuelling event, or one that reports closed while the leak test sees a gross leak, would be typical cases. No manufacturer publicly documents P2409.",["Cap switch mechanically stuck in one position","Wrong or damaged cap that does not operate the sensor","Misaligned filler door or neck after body repair"],["Check engine light or fuel cap message although the cap is tight","EVAP test results may be rejected"],1,1,["P2408","P2412","P0457"],"חיישן/מתג מכסה דלק — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P240A:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Heater Control Circuit/Open","Some leak detection pump modules, such as the DMTL units on VW, Jaguar Land Rover and Maserati petrol engines, carry a small heating element that keeps moisture and ice from upsetting the pump and its pressure measurement. P240A is set when the heater's drive circuit appears open. The 2014 data books for the VW Golf and Touareg take a heater-line voltage of about 4.7-5.4 V as the criterion.",["Burnt-out heating element inside the pump module","Broken heater wire or corroded terminal at the module connector","Missing supply voltage to the heater (fuse, relay)"],["Check engine light","Further EVAP pump codes in cold or wet conditions"],2,1,["P240B","P240C","P2400"],"גוף חימום משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P240B:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Heater Control Circuit Low","P240B covers a heater control line of the leak detection pump that is held at too low a voltage, which in practice means a short to ground on the wire or inside the module. Per VW's 2014 data books for the Golf and Touareg, the code appears when the heater signal falls below roughly 2.74-3.26 V.",["Heater wire shorted to ground near the pump","Internal fault in the DMTL pump module (Land Rover replaces the pump)","Moisture in the connector creating a path to ground"],["Check engine light","EVAP readiness not completed"],2,1,["P240A","P240C","P2401"],"גוף חימום משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P240C:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Heater Control Circuit High","P240C flags the heater circuit of the leak detection pump at the high end: VW's 2014 Golf and Touareg books set it when the heater current exceeds about 2.2-4 A, which points to a shorted element or a line touching battery voltage. Jaguar's JTB00436 for the XJ (X351) quotes both P240C-00 and P240C-85, the 85 suffix marking a signal above range, among faults from water or ice in the DMTL filter;",["Shorted heating element in the pump module, often after water ingress","Heater control wire shorted to battery voltage","Faulty heater output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light","Other DMTL codes after frost or heavy rain"],2,1,["P240A","P240B","P2402"],"גוף חימום משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P240D:["Alternative Fuel Low Pressure System Leak","P240D applies only to vehicles running on a gaseous alternative fuel such as CNG or LPG, which CARB counts as alternate-fueled. It indicates a leak in the low-pressure part of the gas system, downstream of the pressure regulator.",["Leaking fitting or hose on the regulated low-pressure side","Leaking seal at the low-pressure filter or oil separator housing","Gas rail or gas injector seal leaking"],["Check engine light, gas mode may be disabled","Gas smell in the engine bay","Higher gas consumption"],3,3,["P240E","P0093","P01A5"],"דליפת מערכת לחץ נמוך דלק חלופי"],P240E:["Alternative Fuel High Pressure System Leak","P240E concerns the high-pressure side of a gaseous alternative-fuel system, from the storage cylinder through the tank valve and high-pressure line and filter up to the regulator. Pressures there are far higher than in the rail: CNG is stored at about 200-250 bar, and GM's PI1330 rates the 2015 Impala bi-fuel tank at 3,600 psi, with a high-pressure cut-off solenoid at the tank and a coalescing filter that is drained…",["Leaking high-pressure fitting or line between cylinder and regulator","Leaking tank valve or high-pressure cut-off solenoid","Leaking fill receptacle or its check valve","Leak at the high-pressure inlet of the regulator"],["Check engine light, vehicle switches to petrol or will not run on gas","Gas gauge falls while parked","Hissing noise or gas smell near the tank"],4,3,["P240D","P0093","P01A0"],"דליפת מערכת לחץ גבוה דלק חלופי"],P240F:["EGR Slow Response","P240F means the EGR system takes too long to follow a changed flow target. CARB has required diesel OBD to catch such slow response since model year 2010. VW's 2014 data call it EGR System Dynamic Check on the 2.0 TDI (CJAA) and rate rising and falling target air mass against a characteristic above 20; the Touareg 3.0 V6 TDI (CNRB) uses 35 for falling and 30 for rising demand.",["Carbon-coated EGR valve moving sluggishly","Faulty position sensor in the EGR valve (e.g. Hyundai solder-flux contamination)","Intermittent fault in the engine harness (Volvo/Mack D11/D13)","Engine software requiring an update"],["Check engine light","Hesitation or smoke during load changes","Engine power derate on heavy trucks"],2,3,["P0401","P0402","P0404","P049D","P0405","P2413"],"EGR — תגובה איטית"],P2410:["Fuel Cap Sensor/Switch Circuit Low","P2410 reports that the fuel cap sensor or switch circuit is held below its expected voltage window. Depending on how the switch is wired, this can mean a signal wire shorted to ground, a switch that is permanently closed to ground, or a sensor with a failed supply. No manufacturer publicly documents this code or its threshold;",["Signal wire shorted to ground at the filler neck","Switch internally shorted","Missing supply voltage to the sensor"],["Check engine light","Fuel cap warning stays on or never appears"],1,1,["P2408","P2411"],"חיישן/מתג מכסה דלק — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2411:["Fuel Cap Sensor/Switch Circuit High","P2411 is stored when the fuel cap sensor or switch circuit reads above its normal window. With a pulled-up signal line this is what an open circuit, an unplugged connector or a short to the battery feed looks like, so it is often the code that follows a bodywork job or a filler-neck replacement. No manufacturer publicly documents P2411 or a threshold for it.",["Open signal wire or unplugged connector, e.g. after body or filler-neck work","Signal wire shorted to battery voltage","Sensor or switch failed open"],["Check engine light","Cap warning behaves as if the cap were permanently open"],1,1,["P2408","P2410"],"חיישן/מתג מכסה דלק — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2412:["Fuel Cap Sensor/Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2412 covers a fuel cap sensor or switch whose signal drops out or flickers rather than holding one state, for instance from a loose terminal, a cracked wire that flexes each time the filler door is opened, or a worn switch contact. Brief interruptions of this kind can make the cap look open for a moment and spoil an EVAP test. No manufacturer publicly documents P2412.",["Loose or corroded terminal in the sensor connector","Wire cracked where it flexes at the filler door","Worn switch contact"],["Check engine light that comes and goes","Occasional fuel cap warning with the cap closed"],1,1,["P2408","P2409"],"חיישן/מתג מכסה דלק — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2413:["EGR System Performance","P2413 is a broad EGR performance code, and makers fill it in different ways. GM's 2011 6.6 L LGH Duramax uses it for insufficient flow: the air-mass controller deviation must pass a map value of 1.8 to 2.4 g per revolution for 10 s under steady fuelling, rated Type B.",["Soot or carbon restricting the EGR valve or passages","EGR valve not reaching commanded lift (actuator or position sensor)","Partly blocked EGR cooler","Air-mass or pressure sensor error distorting the flow calculation"],["Check engine light","Reduced power or derate on diesels","Knocking or pinging under load on petrol engines","Failed emissions inspection"],2,3,["P0401","P0402","P0404","P0400","P240F"],"מערכת EGR — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2414:["O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2414 means the front air-fuel ratio sensor of bank 1 reports a reading that cannot come from real exhaust, usually a lean value caused by air leaking in ahead of the sensor or a sensor that is damaged. VW's January 2014 Golf/GTI data book uses two windows, a signal voltage of 3.10-4.81 V and a sensor signal of 2.5-3.2 V, with a second set near 2.5 V; another engine uses 3.1-4.77 V and 2.5-3.06 V.",["Air drawn in through a leak ahead of the sensor (manifold, gasket, cracked pipe)","Front sensor damaged by the catalyst-heating strategy (VW Jetta/Beetle 2.0, software update)","Loose, aged or contaminated air-fuel sensor"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption or uneven idle","Ticking noise from an exhaust leak"],2,1,["P2415","P2237","P2A00","P0171"],""],P2415:["O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2415 indicates that the upstream air-fuel sensor on bank 2 is not reading a representative exhaust sample - typically because outside air is drawn in through a leak near the sensor or the sensor is not seated correctly, so the reading is implausibly lean.",["Exhaust leak ahead of or near the sensor (manifold, gasket, flex pipe)","Sensor loose or installed incorrectly","Aged or contaminated wide-band sensor"],["Check engine light","Ticking exhaust noise when a leak is present","Higher fuel consumption or uneven running"],2,1,["P2414","P0174","P2254"],""],P2416:["O2 Sensor Signals Swapped (Bank 1 Sensor 2 / Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P2416 means the engine computer concludes that the two downstream oxygen sensors of bank 1 - sensor 2 after the first catalyst and sensor 3 after a second catalyst, as used mainly on SULEV/PZEV vehicles - are connected the wrong way round. No manufacturer publicly documents the detection logic for P2416.",["Sensor 2 and sensor 3 connectors swapped after a repair","Wrong sensor type or harness length fitted in one position","Wires crossed in a harness repair"],["Check engine light shortly after an exhaust or sensor repair","Catalyst monitor not completing or giving implausible results","Usually no noticeable driveability change"],1,1,["P2417","P0041","P0040","P0136","P0142"],""],P2417:["O2 Sensor Signals Swapped (Bank 2 Sensor 2 / Bank 2 Sensor 3)","P2417 is set when the engine computer finds that the two downstream oxygen sensors on bank 2 - sensor 2 behind the first catalyst and sensor 3 behind a second one - respond as if their wiring were exchanged. Such three-sensor layouts are typical of V-engines built to SULEV/PZEV limits. No manufacturer publicly documents the detection logic for P2417;",["Sensor 2 and sensor 3 connectors swapped after a repair","Wrong sensor type or harness length fitted in one position","Wires crossed in a harness repair"],["Check engine light shortly after an exhaust or sensor repair","Catalyst monitor for bank 2 not completing","Usually no noticeable driveability change"],1,1,["P2416","P0041","P0040","P0156","P0162"],""],P2418:["EVAP System Switching Valve Control Circuit/Open","P2418 is the electrical check of the control circuit of the EVAP switching valve - an extra valve in the evaporative system whose job depends on the design. Ford calls it EVAP switching valve or vapor blocking valve; its 2012 and 2020-2023 OBD summaries check the driver continuously and set P2418 when a short, open or intermittent fault persists for more than 5 s, so at Ford this one code covers all circuit faults.",["Broken control wire or unplugged valve connector","Open solenoid coil in the switching valve","Corroded connector near the tank (road salt, splash water)"],["Check engine light","EVAP readiness not set","Possible fuel vapour odour or slow refuelling"],2,1,["P2419","P2420","P2450","P2451"],"שסתום מיתוג מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2419:["EVAP System Switching Valve Control Circuit Low","P2419 reports that the control circuit of the EVAP switching valve reads low - usually the control line is shorted to ground, or the driver stage measures too little voltage. Karma's Revero/GS-6 bulletin lists P2419 for the rear fuel tank isolation valve controlled by the ECM.",["Control wire shorted to ground (chafed near tank or frame)","Shorted coil in the switching valve or leak check module","Water ingress into the leak check module"],["Check engine light","EVAP readiness not set","Often stored together with leak detection pump codes"],2,1,["P2418","P2420","P2404","P2401"],"שסתום מיתוג מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P241A:["O2 Sensor Signals Swapped (Bank 1 Sensor 1 / Bank 1 Sensor 2)","With P241A the engine controller has concluded that the oxygen readings of the sensor ahead of the bank 1 catalyst and of the sensor behind it fit the opposite mounting positions, so the two plugs or harness legs are most likely crossed. FCA uses the code on the 2011 Ram 2500/3500 with the 6.7L Cummins diesel and calls it an oxygen concentration mismatch between sensors 1/1 and 1/2; bulletin 18-012-12 Rev.",["Upstream and downstream sensor plugs connected the wrong way round after a repair","Sensor harness rerouted or wrong replacement harness fitted","Detection software needing an update (FCA 6.7L Cummins)"],["Check engine light after work on the exhaust or the oxygen sensors","Mixture adaptation drifts, fuel trims look implausible","Catalyst or sensor codes set as follow-up faults"],1,1,["P241B","P2416","P0040","P0130","P0136"],""],P241B:["O2 Sensor Signals Swapped (Bank 2 Sensor 1 / Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P241B concerns only engines with a second exhaust bank, typically V engines: the controller has decided that the front and rear oxygen sensors of bank 2 deliver signals that belong to each other's position. No manufacturer bulletin names P241B publicly; the only published use of this check found is FCA's bank 1 version P241A on the inline-six Cummins, where it is described as an oxygen concentration mismatch.",["Bank 2 sensor plugs swapped during a sensor or exhaust repair","Bank 2 sensor plugged into the bank 1 harness side","Sensor with the wrong type or cable length fitted"],["Check engine light shortly after work on bank 2","Bank 2 fuel trims or catalyst monitor results implausible"],1,1,["P241A","P2417","P0041","P0150","P0156"],""],P241C:["Throttle Actuator Control System - Ice Blockage (Bank 2)","P241C is the bank 2 counterpart of P2072 and only makes sense on engines that use a separate electronic throttle per bank. The controller records that the throttle plate of that bank was frozen in place, recognised by a blade that will not follow its command in cold weather. No manufacturer publishes P241C.",["Condensate from crankcase ventilation freezing on the throttle blade","Water or snow drawn into the intake tract","Damaged or poorly routed ventilation or make-up air hose"],["Reduced power or capped engine speed in frost","Engine will not start after a cold night","Warning lamp depending on manufacturer"],2,3,["P2072","P2110","P2118","P2111","P2112"],""],P241D:["SCR Inducement - Forced Engine Shutdown","P241D marks the last step of the diesel SCR inducement: after repeated warnings about a reductant problem were ignored, the engine module blocks further engine starts. On FCA's 3.0L EcoDiesel (Ram 1500, Jeep Grand Cherokee from 2014) a DEF-related code first triggers a dash message, after 50 miles a restart countdown, and after 150 miles no restart; P241D is then stored and only sets alongside the causing code.",["DEF tank run empty after warnings were ignored","Unrepaired SCR or DEF system fault (pump, pressure, quality, NOx sensor)","Causing code erased while the inducement remains active"],["Engine will not restart, message to service the DEF system","Earlier countdown warnings in the cluster","Check engine light with further SCR codes"],2,3,["P203F","P20E8","P2BAE","P2BAF","P232A"],""],P241E:["Reductant Heater Coolant Control Valve Stuck Closed","Many SCR systems thaw frozen DEF with engine coolant routed through the tank or supply module; an electrically switched valve lets coolant in. P241E means that valve stays shut although the controller has opened it, so the expected warm-up does not appear. Deutz assigns P241E-00 in its EMR L1 list to the heating valve of the DEF pump and finds it through the defrost check;",["Valve seized or diaphragm stuck in the closed position","Kinked, blocked or air-locked coolant hoses to the DEF heater","Low coolant level or weak circulation"],["SCR or DEF warning in cold weather, DEF does not thaw","Higher NOx, possibly further SCR codes","Countdown to restart or power limitation if left unrepaired"],2,3,["P20B1","P20B2","P20B3","P20B4","P20B9"],"שסתום בקרת נוזל קירור גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקוע במצב סגור"],P241F:["EGR Cooler B Efficiency Below Threshold","Engines with two EGR loops can carry two coolers; P241F flags that the second one, cooler B, no longer removes enough heat from the recirculated gas. GM's 2020 diesel tables (20OBDG04) pin cooler B to the low-pressure EGR path: efficiency is derived from the gas temperatures before and after the cooler, corrected for flow, averaged and failed below 50 percent, a Type B fault (two trips) with coolant between 60 and…",["Soot or lacquer deposits on the cooler passages","Drifting EGR temperature sensor before or after the cooler","Weak coolant flow through the cooler (air pocket, thermostat, pump)","Cooler bypass flap not closing"],["Check engine light after two trips","Higher NOx, possibly more frequent DPF regenerations"],3,1,["P2457","P245A","P245B","P0401","P2425"],""],P2420:["EVAP System Switching Valve Control Circuit High","P2420 means the control circuit of the EVAP switching valve reads high - typically a short to battery voltage on the control line or an overcurrent detected by the driver stage. Karma lists P2420 for the rear fuel tank isolation valve of the Revero and GS-6, which the ECM operates, and Subaru's bulletin 09-103-23 for 2015 Legacy/Outback with an evaporative leak check module (ELCM) includes P2420 among the codes to…",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Switching valve coil with too low resistance (overcurrent)","Faulty driver stage in the ECM"],["Check engine light","EVAP readiness not set","No noticeable driveability change"],2,1,["P2418","P2419","P2404","P2402"],"שסתום מיתוג מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2421:["EVAP System Vent Valve Stuck Open","The vent valve closes off the evaporative system, letting a leak test hold pressure or vacuum. P2421 says the valve stays open when the controller has commanded it shut; the test then fails to seal, much like a gross leak. Which valve is meant depends on the design. GM's Volt with a sealed tank and leak check pump (16OBDG01) reports a stuck-open diurnal control valve as one result of its pump test sequence, Type B.",["Valve seat or membrane contaminated by charcoal dust or dirt","Vent or tank isolation valve mechanically stuck open","Disintegrating charcoal canister shedding particles"],["Check engine light, no driveability change","EVAP readiness not set, leak codes possible"],2,1,["P2422","P0455","P0442","P0446","P0496"],"שסתום אוורור מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2422:["EVAP System Vent Valve Stuck Closed","P2422 is the opposite case: the vent path stays shut even with the valve commanded open, so tank pressure or vacuum cannot equalise. GM's Volt table (16OBDG01) is specific: with more than 697 Pa of pressure or vacuum in the sealed tank, the diurnal control valve is opened, and a fuel tank pressure change of less than 249 Pa within 10 s fails the test, Type B. Honda (bulletin 15-010, 2013-2015 Accord;",["Dust, dirt or insects blocking the canister vent tube or filter","Vent valve or tank isolation valve stuck closed","Detection logic needing an update (Hyundai 2020 Sonata)"],["Check engine light","Fuel nozzle shuts off early when refuelling","Hissing when the fuel cap or flap is opened"],2,1,["P2421","P0446","P0449","P0451","P0498"],"שסתום אוורור מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2423:["HC Adsorption Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 1)","Some very low emission petrol engines add a hydrocarbon trap: an adsorbing layer holds back unburned fuel during a cold start and releases it once the main catalyst has lit off. P2423 means the bank 1 trap no longer retains enough. Nissan uses the code, named HC adsorption catalyst function, on the 2010-2012 Altima with the QR25DE in California SULEV form.",["Adsorber layer aged or saturated with deposits","ECM calibration affected by a manufacturer campaign (Nissan Altima SULEV)","Damage from misfires or oil consumption"],["Check engine light, no noticeable driving change","Higher cold-start hydrocarbon emissions"],3,1,["P2424","P0420"],""],P2424:["HC Adsorption Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2)","P2424 applies the same check to the bank 2 hydrocarbon trap, so it can only appear on V or flat engines that have such a trap in each exhaust branch. No manufacturer documents P2424 publicly. The only published case of the family is Nissan's P2423 on the four-cylinder Altima SULEV, which has a single bank;",["Bank 2 adsorber layer aged or contaminated","Exhaust leak ahead of the bank 2 trap distorting the measurement","Thermal damage from misfires on bank 2"],["Check engine light","Possible failed emission inspection"],3,1,["P2423","P0430"],""],P2425:["EGR Cooling Valve Control Circuit/Open","The EGR cooling valve, often a bypass flap, decides whether recirculated gas passes through the cooler or around it, for example to warm up faster. P2425 reports that the driver stage sees no load on the control line, typically an open wire, a loose connector or a burnt-out actuator.",["Broken wire in the control circuit near the hot exhaust side","Loose or corroded connector at the valve","Open coil or motor inside the valve actuator"],["Check engine light","Slow warm-up or higher NOx depending on flap position"],2,1,["P2426","P2427","P245A","P245B","P2457"],"שסתום קירור EGR — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2426:["EGR Cooling Valve Control Circuit Low","P2426 is set when the command wire of the cooling valve reads too low, which on most driver stages means the wire is shorted to ground or the output cannot pull up. In Ford's Power Stroke summary the low and high faults are detected together by a short-circuit check of the cooler bypass actuator that runs all the time and fails after 2 seconds.",["Control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Internal short in the valve actuator","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light","Bypass flap no longer moves"],2,1,["P2425","P2427","P245A","P2457"],"שסתום קירור EGR — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2427:["EGR Cooling Valve Control Circuit High","P2427 points to the high side: the control line of the EGR cooling valve is pulled towards battery voltage or the stage sees excessive current. VW's 2014 Touareg 3.0 TDI chart (CNRB) states the criterion as a current above 2.20 A, a sign of a short in the actuator winding or wiring to supply.",["Control wire shorted to a supply voltage","Shorted turns in the actuator, drawing excess current","Water ingress in the valve connector"],["Check engine light","Flap remains in spring position, possibly slower warm-up"],2,1,["P2425","P2426","P245B","P2457"],"שסתום קירור EGR — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2428:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Too High (Bank 1)","P2428 is a protection code: the exhaust on bank 1 has become hot enough to endanger the aftertreatment, above all the diesel particulate filter. GM's 2014 diesel tables (14OBDG04) list five triggers, any of which fails the test after 6 seconds: about 800 °C ahead of the oxidation catalyst, 900 °C behind it, 800 °C behind the filter, or rises of more than 600 °C across the catalyst and 400 °C across the filter.",["Uncontrolled soot burn in an overloaded particulate filter","Leaking injector or excessive post-injection reaching the catalyst","Exhaust temperature sensor reading too high"],["Warning lamp on immediately, often with reduced power","Strong heat or burning smell from the exhaust","Particulate filter or catalyst damage in severe cases"],3,3,["P2429","P2463","P242F","P0544","P2080"],"טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — ערך גבוה מדי (בנק 1)"],P2429:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Too High (Bank 2)","P2429 reports excessive exhaust heat on bank 2 and therefore exists only on engines with two separately monitored exhaust branches, such as V diesels with an aftertreatment line per bank. No manufacturer publishes P2429.",["Excessive soot burn in the bank 2 filter","Leaking injector or misfire on bank 2 sending fuel into the exhaust","Bank 2 exhaust temperature sensor reading high"],["Warning lamp with reduced engine power","Unusual heat or smell from one side of the exhaust"],3,3,["P2428","P0547","P2463"],"טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — ערך גבוה מדי (בנק 2)"],P242A:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P242A is the general circuit code for the third exhaust temperature probe on bank 1. Where that probe sits is up to each manufacturer: VW counts it behind the oxidation catalyst on the 2014 Touareg TDI, Deutz places it downstream of the SCR catalyst on its EMR L1 controller. VW sets P242A once the signal voltage climbs above 2.61 V, which fits an open circuit.",["Open circuit or corroded terminal in the sensor connector or harness near the exhaust","Exhaust temperature sensor 3 failed internally","Ground fault or sensor supply out of range (failure types -F0/-1C on Deutz)","On Ford diesels, sensor reading deviating from the exhaust temperature model"],["MIL on","Particulate filter regeneration or DEF dosing suspended","Implausible or missing value for sensor 3 in the scan tool"],2,1,["P242B","P242C","P242D","P242E","P2031","P0544","P2466","P20E3"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P242B:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P242B flags a reading from exhaust temperature sensor 3 on bank 1 that is electrically fine but makes no physical sense. Most checks start from a cold soak: GM's 3.0 L LZO (25OBDG04B) waits for more than 10,800 s engine-off and then expects the probe to warm up enough, which exposes a probe that has slipped from the gas stream or is frozen at one value (Type B).",["Sensor loose or no longer reaching into the exhaust stream","Sensor drifted or stuck at one value","ECM software miscalculating soak time (Volvo/Mack 2015–2016, software update)","Sensors swapped or wrong part fitted after repair"],["MIL on, often together with P2080 or P2084","No DEF dosing or parked regeneration refused","DPF warning lamp on"],2,1,["P242A","P242C","P242D","P242E","P2080","P2084","P20E3","P20E4"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P242C:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P242C means the signal of exhaust temperature sensor 3 on bank 1 sits below its valid range. What that says about the wiring depends on the sensor type. GM's 2020 diesel tables (20OBDG04) read a resistance under 158 Ω as a grounded circuit and need 10 bad samples in a window of 20 (Type B); on the 3.0 L LZO a digital thermocouple module reporting below -72.8 °C counts the same way, with 19 of 25 samples.",["Signal wire chafed and shorted to ground near the exhaust","Connector damaged, wet or with pushed-back terminals","Sensor shorted internally"],["MIL on after the second faulty trip on GM","Sensor 3 shows an implausibly low temperature in the scan tool","Regeneration blocked, filter load rising"],2,1,["P242A","P242B","P242D","P2032","P2468"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P242D:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P242D is the mirror case of P242C: bank 1 probe 3 reports more than its plausible maximum, typically because the circuit is open or touches a supply. GM's 2020 diesel tables trigger above 900 Ω after 10 of 20 samples, the 3.0 L LZO above 100 MΩ for an analog probe or above 1,289.85 °C for a digital one; both tables rate it Type A, so the MIL comes on in the first faulty trip.",["Open signal or return wire, broken by heat or vibration","Connector unplugged or corroded","Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage","Low battery voltage during diagnosis (Ram 2025–2026 note)"],["MIL on in the first faulty trip (GM Type A)","Sensor 3 shows an implausibly high temperature or the maximum value","Regeneration and DEF dosing restricted"],2,1,["P242A","P242B","P242C","P2033","P2469"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P242E:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P242E is set when exhaust temperature sensor 3 on bank 1 jumps between two samples faster than real exhaust gas can change, even though each single value is inside the valid range. GM documents this as a quick-change monitor that runs every 100 ms. The 2020 diesel tables look at the resistance step between consecutive samples and fail after 15 of 30 samples;",["Loose or fretted terminal in the sensor connector","Harness insulation damaged by exhaust heat, intermittent contact","Sensor element breaking up internally"],["MIL after the second faulty trip","Sensor 3 value jumps in the scan tool live data","Code comes and goes, often after rough roads or washing"],2,1,["P242A","P242B","P242C","P242D","P2085","P246A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P242F:["Particulate Filter Restriction - Ash Accumulation (Bank 1)","P242F reports that so much incombustible ash has collected in the bank 1 particulate filter that it restricts flow and no regeneration can clear it. Ash comes mainly from oil additives, builds up over the service life and leaves the filter only through cleaning or replacement. Deutz stores P242F-00 as a high ash load warning on its EMR L1 controller.",["Filter has reached its ash capacity after high mileage or operating hours","High oil consumption or unsuitable oil (high ash content) speeding up ash build-up","Calibration setting the code without a defect (Ram 6.7 L 2015, bulletin 18-037-16)","Differential pressure sensor or hoses reporting too much restriction"],["MIL or DPF service message","Regenerations becoming more frequent","Loss of power at high load due to back pressure"],3,3,["P243A","P2463","P24A4","P2459","P2002"],""],P2430:["AIR System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit (Bank 1)","On engines with an electric secondary air (AIR) pump, a pressure sensor in the duct between pump and shut-off valve tells the engine computer whether air is really moving to bank 1. P2430 is the basic signal fault of that sensor.",["Pressure sensor no longer reacts, signal frozen at one value","Sensor port or duct blocked by water, ice or debris from the pump","Corroded connector or damaged harness at the sensor"],["Check engine lamp after two cold starts","Secondary air readiness not set, emissions test refused","No noticeable change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P2431","P2432","P2433","P2434","P2435","P0411"],""],P2431:["AIR System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1)","P2431 flags a bank 1 secondary air pressure signal that can be read but makes no sense. The usual check compares the sensor with barometric pressure: with the pump off both should agree, with the pump running the rise must stay within limits. GM sets the code on the 3.8L V6 (2005–2006) when the gap exceeds 10 kPa with the pump off or 50 kPa with it on for over 30 s, Type B;",["Pressure sensor drifted or reacts too slowly","Wrong barometric reference, e.g. damaged MAP sensor wiring","Restricted or leaking air duct around the sensor port"],["Check engine lamp, often only after cold starts","Secondary air monitor not completed","Possibly further MAP or lean codes if the reference is wrong"],2,1,["P2430","P2432","P2433","P2436","P0411"],""],P2432:["AIR System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1)","P2432 means the bank 1 secondary air pressure signal has fallen below its valid band – typically a broken signal lead, a ground short or a missing 5 V reference. GM's tables give the limit as under 5 % of the reference (400 failed samples out of 1,000 on the 2005 3.8L V6) and, from 2018, under 6 % for 800 of 1,000 samples; the check runs all the time and is rated Type B.",["Signal wire open or shorted to ground","5 V reference missing, often shared with other sensors","Pressure sensor failed internally"],["Check engine lamp, also while driving warm","Secondary air tests not run","Other sensor codes if the shared 5 V line is affected"],2,1,["P2430","P2431","P2433","P2437"],""],P2433:["AIR System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1)","With P2433 the bank 1 secondary air pressure signal sits above its upper limit, pointing to a signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or to battery voltage, an open sensor ground or a failed sensor. GM uses more than 95 % of the reference on the 2005–2006 3.8L V6, more than 94 % on the 2006 Corvette and CTS-V V8s and in the 2018 tables (800 of 1,000 samples), always as a Type B fault watched without a break.",["Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Open sensor ground or corroded ground terminal","Pressure sensor failed internally"],["Check engine lamp after two trips","Secondary air readiness stays incomplete"],2,1,["P2430","P2432","P2438"],""],P2434:["AIR System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 1)","P2434 is meant for a bank 1 secondary air pressure sensor whose signal drops out or jumps for short moments instead of failing for good – typically a loose connector pin, a chafed wire or a sensor with an internal contact problem. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly; GM, for example, covers the same sensor with P2430–P2433 only and folds signal noise into its stuck-in-range and performance checks.",["Loose or widened terminal in the sensor plug","Chafed or heat-damaged wire near engine or exhaust","Intermittent contact inside the sensor"],["Check engine lamp that comes and goes","Fault often not reproducible in the workshop"],2,1,["P2430","P2432","P2433","P2439"],""],P2435:["AIR System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit (Bank 2)","P2435 is the bank 2 version of the basic signal fault of the secondary air pressure sensor. It exists only where each cylinder bank has its own air path with a sensor, for instance Audi's R8 V10 with the bank 2 sensor G610.",["Bank 2 pressure sensor no longer reacts","Plug or harness on the bank 2 side damaged","Sensor port blocked by moisture or debris"],["Check engine lamp after cold starts","Secondary air readiness not reached"],2,1,["P2430","P2436","P2437","P2438","P2439"],""],P2436:["AIR System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2)","P2436 says the bank 2 secondary air pressure reading is electrically valid but does not match what the system expects. Audi documents the code on the 2017 R8 and R8 Spyder V10: bulletin 2049142 (TSB group 01, 18-56) pairs P243600 with P243700 and has the bank 2 pressure sensor G610 replaced, following the guided fault finding.",["Bank 2 pressure sensor drifted or failed (Audi R8 replaces G610)","Sensing port or hose on bank 2 clogged or leaking","Wrong barometric reference value"],["Check engine lamp","Often stored together with P2437","Secondary air readiness incomplete"],2,1,["P2431","P2435","P2437","P2438"],""],P2437:["AIR System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P2437 reports a bank 2 secondary air pressure signal stuck below its valid range. Audi lists it for the 2017 R8 and R8 Spyder, where it often shows up together with P2436; the bulletin's remedy is a new bank 2 pressure sensor G610. GM's 2018 tables name P2437 as a blocking condition for the bank 1 sensor tests, so a low reading on either side halts the whole secondary air diagnosis.",["Bank 2 pressure sensor failed (Audi R8 bulletin replaces G610)","Signal wire open or shorted to ground","5 V supply to the sensor missing"],["Check engine lamp","Secondary air tests on both banks suspended"],2,1,["P2432","P2435","P2436","P2438"],""],P2438:["AIR System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2)","P2438 is the bank 2 counterpart of P2433: the secondary air pressure signal of the second bank reads above its upper limit. GM mentions P2438 next to P2437 among the codes that block its AIR sensor and flow tests in the 2018 tables, but publishes no row of its own for it, because the engines described there have one air path. For comparison, GM's bank 1 sensor fails above 94–95 % of the 5 V reference.",["Signal wire shorted to reference or supply voltage","Open ground circuit of the bank 2 sensor","Bank 2 pressure sensor failed internally"],["Check engine lamp","Secondary air readiness stays incomplete"],2,1,["P2433","P2435","P2437","P2439"],""],P2439:["AIR System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 2)","P2439 covers brief dropouts or jumps in the bank 2 secondary air pressure signal. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; the description rests on CARB's demand that every electrical AIR component be checked for circuit faults and rationality, together with the bank 2 sensor layout known from Audi's R8 V10 (sensor G610).",["Loose or corroded terminal at the bank 2 sensor","Harness near the exhaust side brittle or chafed","Intermittent internal sensor fault"],["Warning lamp appears now and then","Code returns after clearing without visible cause"],2,1,["P2434","P2435","P2437","P2438"],""],P243A:["Particulate Filter Restriction - Ash Accumulation (Bank 2)","P243A is the bank 2 counterpart of P242F: the ash load in the second particulate filter has grown so large that the filter chokes the exhaust and must be cleaned or replaced. A bank 2 filter only exists where each cylinder bank of a V engine feeds its own filter strand. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly.",["Bank 2 filter full of ash after long service","Oil burning on bank 2 (valve stem seals, turbo seal) adding ash","Bank 2 pressure sensor or hose reporting too much restriction"],["MIL or filter service message","Higher fuel consumption from frequent regenerations","Reduced power at high load"],3,3,["P242F","P24A3","P243F","P2003"],""],P243B:["Particulate Filter Restriction - Forced Limited Power (Bank 2)","P243B means the second particulate filter is so restricted that the engine controller cuts power to protect engine and filter. Ford documents the code in its 2024–2025 OBD summary for gasoline engines, as part of the petrol particulate filter monitor next to P246C for bank 1.",["Bank 2 filter overloaded with soot or ash","Damaged or blocked exhaust pipe on bank 2","Pressure sensor or hose on bank 2 reporting too high a pressure"],["Noticeably reduced engine power","MIL on","Poor acceleration at higher speed"],3,3,["P246C","P243F","P24A3","P226E"],""],P243C:["Particulate Filter Regeneration Frequency (Bank 2)","P243C is stored when the bank 2 particulate filter needs regeneration more often than its calibration allows. CARB requires diesel OBD to recognise regeneration so frequent that emissions would rise above the limit.",["Too much soot from bank 2 cylinders (injector, EGR or boost fault)","Pressure sensor or hose overstating the bank 2 soot load","Filter partly filled with ash, leaving little soot capacity"],["Regeneration running unusually often","Higher fuel consumption, rising oil level","MIL on"],3,1,["P2459","P243D","P243E","P24A3"],"תדר התחדשות (רגנרציה) מסנן חלקיקים (בנק 2)"],P243D:["Particulate Filter Regeneration Duration (Bank 2)","P243D says that a regeneration of the bank 2 particulate filter took longer than the calibrated limit. CARB expects the OBD system to notice when a filter fails to regenerate properly under conditions in which it was designed to. No manufacturer publishes this bank 2 code;",["Exhaust on bank 2 not reaching regeneration temperature (short trips, low load)","Oxidation catalyst on bank 2 converting too little fuel into heat","Temperature or pressure sensor giving wrong values"],["Regeneration seems to run for a very long time (fan, idle speed)","Higher fuel consumption","MIL on"],2,1,["P2458","P243C","P243E"],""],P243E:["Particulate Filter Regeneration Incomplete (Bank 2)","P243E is set when the second filter strand has finished regenerating but the soot was not burned off as planned. CARB requires a malfunction to be flagged whenever the filter does not regenerate properly under the manufacturer's intended conditions.",["Regenerations interrupted by short trips or engine shut-off","Too little heat on bank 2 (catalyst, post-injection or dosing fault)","Faulty temperature or differential pressure signal"],["MIL on, filter warning","Regeneration restarts soon after the last one","Rising soot load in live data"],2,1,["P24A2","P243D","P243C","P243F"],""],P243F:["Particulate Filter Restriction - Soot Accumulation Too High (Bank 2)","P243F means the soot load estimated for the bank 2 particulate filter has climbed past the level that a normal regeneration can still handle safely. Burning off too much soot at once can overheat and crack the substrate, so many engines then block automatic regeneration and call for a service regeneration or a new filter. No manufacturer documents P243F publicly.",["Repeatedly aborted regenerations, short trips or long idling","Engine fault raising soot output on bank 2 (injector, EGR, boost)","Pressure sensor or hose overstating the soot load"],["MIL and filter warning on","Automatic regeneration blocked, service regeneration needed","Reduced power possible"],3,3,["P24A4","P24A3","P243B","P243E","P243A"],""],P2440:["AIR System Switching Valve Stuck Open (Bank 1)","P2440 means the bank 1 secondary air shut-off (switching) valve stays open when it should be closed. GM tests it in phase 2 of its air check: the pump runs while the valve is commanded shut, so pressure in the duct should build; if it stays more than 3 kPa below the model (2005–2006 3.8L V6) or under the 2018 table limit, the code sets as Type B.",["Valve held open by debris from a damaged pump filter","Valve seat carboned up or corroded by condensate","Electric or vacuum actuator does not close the valve"],["Check engine lamp after a cold start","Pump noisy or failing later due to exhaust backflow","Often stored together with P2442 or P2445"],2,1,["P2441","P2442","P2444","P0411","P0412"],"שסתום מיתוג מערכת האוויר המשני — תקוע במצב פתוח (בנק 1)"],P2441:["AIR System Switching Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 1)","P2441 flags a bank 1 secondary air valve that does not open when commanded, so pump air never reaches the exhaust ports. Toyota documents it on 2005–2009 4.7L V8 (2UZ-FE) models such as 4Runner, Sequoia, Tundra and Land Cruiser: bulletin T-SB-0230-12 traces it to debris from the air pump contaminating the valves and lists it next to faults of the No. 2 valves.",["Valve seized closed by debris or corrosion","Valve actuator, control solenoid or vacuum supply faulty","Kinked or collapsed air hose downstream of the valve"],["Check engine lamp after a cold start","Higher cold-start emissions, failed readiness check"],2,1,["P2440","P2443","P0411","P0491"],"שסתום מיתוג מערכת האוויר המשני — תקוע במצב סגור (בנק 1)"],P2442:["AIR System Switching Valve Stuck Open (Bank 2)","P2442 is the stuck-open fault of the bank 2 secondary air valve: with the pump on and the valve commanded shut, air still passes, or exhaust flows back towards the pump. Lexus applies it to the 2010–2013 GX 460 with the 1UR-FE engine; bulletin L-SB-0028-14 replaces the bank 2 air switching valve and the pump, because a damaged pump filter sheds debris.",["Bank 2 valve held open by debris from the pump filter","Valve seat or diaphragm damaged by heat or condensate","Actuator does not close the valve"],["Check engine lamp after a cold start","Pump noise or later pump failure","Melted or brittle air hoses"],2,1,["P2440","P2443","P2445","P0492"],"שסתום מיתוג מערכת האוויר המשני — תקוע במצב פתוח (בנק 2)"],P2443:["AIR System Switching Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 2)","P2443 signals that the bank 2 secondary air valve stays shut although the engine computer commands it open, so the second bank gets no added air during warm-up. Subaru lists the code for the 2011–2015 WRX STI and recommends always following the diagnosis for the opposite bank too, since valve or hose faults on one side can show up on the other. Toyota's 2UZ-FE bulletin covers only the bank 1 equivalent.",["Bank 2 valve seized in the closed position","Leaking vacuum line or faulty control solenoid","Kinked air hose on the bank 2 side"],["Check engine lamp after a cold start","Secondary air readiness not set"],2,1,["P2441","P2442","P0492"],"שסתום מיתוג מערכת האוויר המשני — תקוע במצב סגור (בנק 2)"],P2444:["AIR System Pump Stuck On (Bank 1)","P2444 means the secondary air pump keeps blowing after the engine computer has switched it off. GM checks this in phase 3 of its sequence, with the pump commanded off and the valve closed: if duct pressure stays higher than predicted – by more than 1.5 kPa within 5 s on the 2005–2006 3.8L V6, by more than 4.2 kPa within 10 s for the 2006 V8s in Corvette and CTS-V – the code sets as Type A and lights the MIL on the…",["Pump relay contacts welded or sticking","Relay control circuit shorted to power","Output driver in the engine computer faulty"],["Check engine lamp on the first trip","Pump audibly running long after start or with engine off","Discharged battery"],1,1,["P2445","P2446","P0418","P2258","P2440"],"משאבת מערכת האוויר המשני — תקוע במצב פעיל (בנק 1)"],P2445:["AIR System Pump Stuck Off (Bank 1)","P2445 reports that the secondary air pump delivers no air although it is commanded on. Toyota and Lexus use it on several trucks: on 2UZ-FE 4.7L models (T-SB-0230-12, revised in 2013 to include P2445), on the 2010–2013 GX 460 (L-SB-0028-14) and on the 2012 Tacoma with the 1GR-FE (T-SB-0033-17).",["Pump seized by moisture or debris from a damaged filter","Blown pump fuse or failed pump relay","Open pump supply or ground, corroded plug"],["Check engine lamp after a cold start","No pump noise directly after a cold start","Often stored together with P0418"],2,1,["P2444","P2447","P0418","P2257","P2440"],"משאבת מערכת האוויר המשני — תקוע במצב כבוי (בנק 1)"],P2446:["AIR System Pump Stuck On (Bank 2)","P2446 is the bank 2 entry for a secondary air pump that keeps running after being switched off. The code is meaningful only on engines with a separate pump per cylinder bank or where the system reports pump faults per bank; no manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Relay of the bank 2 pump stuck closed","Control circuit shorted to power","Faulty output driver in the engine computer"],["Check engine lamp","Pump keeps humming after the warm-up phase"],1,1,["P2444","P2447","P0418"],"משאבת מערכת האוויר המשני — תקוע במצב פעיל (בנק 2)"],P2447:["AIR System Pump Stuck Off (Bank 2)","P2447 indicates that the bank 2 secondary air pump does not deliver air when commanded. No manufacturer publicly documents this code; Toyota and Lexus, whose V6 and V8 trucks feed both banks from one pump through two valves, log a dead pump as P2445.",["Bank 2 pump seized after water ingress","Blown fuse or failed relay of the bank 2 pump","Corroded pump connector or open ground"],["Check engine lamp after a cold start","Readiness for secondary air not set"],2,1,["P2445","P2446","P0418","P0492"],"משאבת מערכת האוויר המשני — תקוע במצב כבוי (בנק 2)"],P2448:["AIR System High Air Flow (Bank 1)","P2448 means more secondary air reaches bank 1 than the system expects – for example when the shut-off valve leaks, the pump keeps blowing, or the control logic sees a stronger lean shift than modelled.",["Shut-off valve does not seal fully","Pump relay sticks, pump runs longer than commanded","Leaking check valve in the air path"],["Check engine lamp","Lean-running codes or fuel trim deviation after cold start"],2,1,["P2449","P0491","P0410","P2440"],""],P2449:["AIR System High Air Flow (Bank 2)","P2449 is the bank 2 high-flow fault of the AIR system: during or after the air injection phase the second bank receives more air than predicted. Ford assigns it in its 2012 OBD summary to the bank 2 secondary air readiness, next to P0492 for too little flow, so the code belongs to Ford's AIR monitor even though no threshold is published.",["Bank 2 shut-off valve does not seal","Pump keeps running due to a sticking relay","Check valve on bank 2 leaking"],["Check engine lamp","Usually no change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P2448","P0492","P2442"],""],P244A:["Diesel Particulate Filter Differential Pressure Too Low (Bank 1)","P244A means the pressure difference across the bank 1 particulate filter is lower than exhaust flow and soot load predict. That points to a damaged or removed substrate or, far more often, to a pressure line that has slipped off, split or clogged. Ford's 2023 diesels use it as the missing substrate monitor: the measured filter inlet pressure stays below a flow-dependent limit, about 8 kPa at 300 m³/h, for 90 s.",["Upstream pressure hose disconnected, split or blocked","Differential pressure sensor reading too low (Ford 6.7 L, Land Rover TDV6 bulletins)","Filter substrate cracked, melted or removed"],["MIL on in the first faulty trip","Soot load shown near zero, regeneration not triggered","Visible smoke if the substrate is damaged"],2,3,["P244B","P2464","P2452","P2453","P226D"],"לחץ דיפרנציאל מסנן חלקיקים דיזל — ערך נמוך מדי (בנק 1)"],P244B:["Diesel Particulate Filter Differential Pressure Too High (Bank 1)","P244B reports a pressure drop across the bank 1 particulate filter that is too large for the current exhaust flow. On GM's 3.0 L LZO the same monitor also catches a leaking or disconnected downstream pipe: depending on the sensor type it compares either the downstream pressure with a limit or the pressure-to-flow ratio, as a Type A code. A heavily loaded filter is the classic cause;",["Filter heavily loaded with soot or ash","Downstream pressure hose leaking or disconnected (GM LZO)","Water in the differential pressure sensor after washing (GM L5P 2025)","ECM calibration overstating soot load (Cadillac XT4 diesel, update)"],["MIL on, often with reduced power","High soot level indication in the cluster","Regeneration requested repeatedly"],2,3,["P244A","P2465","P2452","P2455","P2463"],"לחץ דיפרנציאל מסנן חלקיקים דיזל — ערך גבוה מדי (בנק 1)"],P244C:["Exhaust Temperature Too Low For Particulate Filter Regeneration (Bank 1)","During an active regeneration the engine raises exhaust temperature with late injections so the soot in the particulate filter can burn. P244C is stored when bank 1 does not get hot enough or does not stay hot long enough.",["Oxidation catalyst aged or face-plugged, so the post-injected fuel does not light off","Regenerations repeatedly cut short by short trips, idling or engine shut-off","Exhaust temperature sensor ahead of catalyst or filter reading too low","Exhaust leak ahead of the catalyst cooling the gas"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and particulate filter warning on","Regenerations noticeably frequent or never finishing","Reduced power once the filter is heavily loaded"],2,3,["P244D","P244E","P2463","P2459","P2458","P2080"],""],P244D:["Exhaust Temperature Too High For Particulate Filter Regeneration (Bank 1)","This is the overheating side of the bank 1 regeneration check. While soot is being burned off, the controller keeps exhaust temperature inside a window; if it climbs past the upper limit, the substrate and the oxidation catalyst risk cracking or melting, so the burn is stopped and P244D is logged.",["Too much fuel reaching the exhaust (leaking injector or aftertreatment doser)","Heavily overloaded filter burning off too fast","Exhaust temperature sensor or its wiring giving implausibly high readings","Control software needing an update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regeneration aborted, filter warning stays on","Reduced power to protect the aftertreatment"],3,3,["P244C","P244F","P2428","P2463","P2080"],""],P244E:["Exhaust Temperature Too Low For Particulate Filter Regeneration (Bank 2)","P244E only exists on engines that have a separate particulate filter for the second cylinder bank, which is rare. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; it mirrors P244C, so the logic described for bank 1 applies here. GM, for example, counts regenerations on its 2017 diesels that end early because the heat-up never reached a stable phase, and gives that bank 1 fault a Type A rating.",["Bank 2 oxidation catalyst no longer converting post-injected fuel","Bank 2 exhaust temperature sensor reading low","Driving pattern too short for a complete regeneration","Exhaust leak on bank 2 ahead of the catalyst"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Filter warning, regeneration does not complete"],2,3,["P244C","P244F"],""],P244F:["Exhaust Temperature Too High For Particulate Filter Regeneration (Bank 2)","The bank 2 counterpart of P244D: during a filter burn the second bank's exhaust gets hotter than the substrate tolerates. No manufacturer documents P244F publicly. The bank 1 version appears in GM's 2011 Duramax tables as a catalyst overtemperature during regeneration, and Ram links P244D on current Cummins trucks to exhaust temperature sensor faults, so a wrong sensor reading deserves suspicion before the hardware.",["Surplus fuel on bank 2 from a leaking injector","Bank 2 exhaust temperature sensor or wiring reading too high","Bank 2 filter heavily overloaded before the burn"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regeneration stopped, possibly reduced power"],3,3,["P244D","P244E"],""],P2450:["EVAP System Switching Valve Performance/Stuck Open","The switching valve sits in the evaporative system and either seals off part of it during the leak test or redirects flow; P2450 means the valve does not do its job or remains open. Ford calls it the vapor blocking valve: in 2020 to 2024 gasoline models the check runs in the third phase of the 0.040 inch cruise leak test, lasts 2 to 3 s and fails when a calculated ratio stays below 2.75 (Mode 6 test $3D, component…",["Switching valve sticking open or not sealing","Internal fault of a leak detection pump that houses the valve","Monitor software needing an update (known on some Ford trucks)","Cracked or loose vapor hose at the valve"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, usually no noticeable driving change","Possible fuel odor near the tank area"],2,1,["P2451","P2418","P2419","P2420","P0455","P0456"],"שסתום מיתוג מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע פתוח"],P2451:["EVAP System Switching Valve Stuck Closed","P2451 is the reverse fault of P2450: the evaporative system switching valve will not open when commanded, so vapor or test pressure cannot pass where the system expects it. It shows up mainly on vehicles with a sealed, pressurized fuel tank, such as plug-in hybrids. Mazda's CX-90 and CX-70 PHEV can set it together with P0451, P2422 and P0441;",["Tank shutter or switching valve stuck closed","Fuel tank pressure sensor giving wrong values to the monitor","Software or test-sequence issue (fuel door handling on some hybrids)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Fuel door or refueling release slow or not working on sealed-tank hybrids"],2,1,["P2450","P2418","P2419","P2420","P0441"],"שסתום מיתוג מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2452:["Diesel Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor A Circuit","The pressure sensor A of the particulate filter, usually a differential sensor with hoses to the filter inlet and outlet, tells the ECM how loaded the filter is. Despite its generic circuit title, P2452 is in practice an offset check made when no exhaust flows. Ford's 2023 diesels run it in after-run and set the code when the sensor still reads more than 1 kPa.",["Sensor offset drifted or moisture inside the sensor","Sensor hose blocked by soot or condensate","Corroded connector or terminals"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regeneration too early, too late or inhibited"],2,1,["P2453","P2454","P2455","P2456"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים דיזל‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2453:["Diesel Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","P2453 means the particulate filter pressure signal is electrically fine but does not behave like a real filter pressure. Manufacturers use two kinds of test. With the engine off there should be almost no pressure difference: GM's 2009 Duramax fails above 4.1 kPa, the 2014 Cruze 2.0 diesel above 3.2 kPa in after-run, and the Opel/GM 2.0 CDTi in the Saab 9-5 (2010) checks once at least 60 s after shutdown.",["Sensor hose disconnected, split, kinked or blocked","Sensor skewed or stuck, for example from moisture ingress","High resistance in sensor wiring or ECM grounds"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DPF warning, regeneration inhibited or too frequent","Reduced power on some vehicles"],2,3,["P2452","P2454","P2455","P2463","P2002"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים דיזל‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2454:["Diesel Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor A Circuit Low","The particulate filter pressure sensor is a three-wire part: the ECM feeds it 5 V and ground and reads a signal that rises with the pressure difference across the filter. P2454 means that signal sits below the lowest plausible value. Ford's 2023 diesels fail below 0.10 V within 2 s, where 0.45 V corresponds to zero pressure difference; GM's 2018 diesels fail below 3 % of the supply with 80 of 160 samples.",["Signal wire open or shorted to ground, connector unplugged","Internal sensor failure, for example from moisture","5 V reference shorted by another sensor on the same supply"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DPF warning or regeneration inhibited"],2,1,["P2452","P2453","P2455","P0641"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים דיזל‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2455:["Diesel Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor A Circuit High","P2455 means the particulate filter pressure sensor signal sits above the highest plausible value, at the top of the 5 V range. Ford's 2023 diesels and the Opel/GM 2.0 CDTi in the Saab 9-5 (2010) both use 4.9 V as the limit, Ford within 2 s and Saab after 1 s; on Ford's 6.7 L the signal follows roughly 0.082 V per kPa above 0.45 V, so 4.9 V would be about 54 kPa.",["Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Sensor low-reference (ground) circuit open","Internal sensor failure"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DPF warning or regeneration inhibited"],2,1,["P2452","P2453","P2454","P2463"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים דיזל‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2456:["Diesel Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","Here the pressure sensor A signal is within range but jumps in a way no real exhaust flow could cause. GM's 2017 and 2018 diesels compare each raw sample with the one before; a step larger than 20 % repeated over 80 or 160 samples sets the code after two trips, but only if no electrical fault is present.",["Loose or corroded sensor connector terminals","Harness chafing or heat damage near the exhaust","Condensate in the sensor or its pressure hoses","Sensor element failing internally"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regeneration started at odd times or blocked"],1,1,["P2452","P2453","P2454","P2455","P2462","P246D"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים דיזל‏ A — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2457:["EGR Cooler A Efficiency Below Threshold","The EGR cooler is supposed to bring recirculated exhaust close to coolant temperature; P2457 says cooler A no longer removes enough heat, as CARB requires diesel systems to detect. GM rates efficiency as the drop across the cooler divided by the gap between inlet gas and coolant; in the 2017 tables the Duramax fails below 60 %, the MDE engine family below 50 %, each after two trips.",["Cooler passages fouled with soot and lacquer","Bypass flap stuck in bypass position or bypass module loose","EGR outlet temperature sensor reading too high","Low coolant level or poor coolant flow through the cooler","Monitor software misjudging efficiency (known on some trucks)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Higher NOx, sometimes reduced EGR or power","Coolant loss or white smoke if the cooler is also leaking"],3,1,["P241F","P24A5","P245B","P0401","P2425"],""],P2458:["Diesel Particulate Filter Regeneration Duration","During a regeneration the engine raises exhaust temperature, mostly by late post-injection burned in the oxidation catalyst, until the soot in the particulate filter oxidises. P2458 means a regeneration took longer than the calibrated limit, so the filter was not cleaned in the expected time. CARB asks diesel OBD to detect regenerations that do not complete as intended.",["ECM calibration that needs an update (documented by Volkswagen)","Short trips that keep regenerations from finishing","Oxidation catalyst too weak to reach regeneration temperature"],["DPF warning or MIL, depending on the manufacturer","Cooling fan and raised idle running on after shutdown","Higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P2459","P2463","P2002","P24A2"],""],P2459:["Diesel Particulate Filter Regeneration Frequency","P2459 means the particulate filter is being regenerated more often than the calibration expects. CARB requires diesel OBD to flag regeneration so frequent that emissions would exceed the limit; frequent regeneration also dilutes oil and costs fuel. Ford's 2023 diesels set it when the average distance between completed regenerations falls below about 40 km.",["High soot output from the engine (injectors, EGR, air leaks)","Differential pressure reading too high (sensor, blocked or swapped hoses)","Filter loaded with ash or defective from manufacture"],["MIL or DPF warning","Higher fuel consumption and rising oil level","Reduced engine power if the fault persists"],3,3,["P2458","P2463","P2453","P2002"],"תדר התחדשות (רגנרציה) מסנן חלקיקים דיזל"],P245A:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1)","The bypass lets cold-start EGR skip the cooler and is switched back to cooling once the engine is warm. P245A flags the bank 1 control circuit, usually as an open. GM's 2017 tables show both actuator types: on the Duramax with a DC-motor flap the controller sees a load resistance above 200 kOhm while the H-bridge is off and needs 160 failures in 200 samples, while the vacuum-switched version needs 24 of 30 samples…",["Open wire or unplugged connector at the bypass actuator","Actuator motor or solenoid winding open","Control software needing an update (some Ford diesels)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EGR cooler bypass no longer switching; possible P2457 or P24A5 as follow-up"],2,1,["P245B","P245C","P245D","P24A5","P248E","P2457"],"מעקף מצנן EGR — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P245B:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1)","P245B is set when the bank 1 bypass is electrically intact but does not reach or hold the commanded position, or when switching it has no visible thermal effect. GM's 2017 Duramax with a position-controlled DC-motor flap compares setpoint and feedback;",["Bypass flap or shaft sticking from carbon deposits","Bypass position feedback inaccurate","Weak vacuum supply or leaking hose on vacuum-operated bypass","Slow EGR temperature sensor after the cooler"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Longer warm-up or higher NOx when the bypass stays in one position"],2,1,["P245A","P245C","P245D","P24A5","P248F","P2457"],"מעקף מצנן EGR — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P245C:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Low (Bank 1)","P245C reports that the control line of the bank 1 bypass actuator is pulled toward ground. GM documents this in its diesel tables: in 2014 the driver stage detects low voltage while it is switched off and treats it as a ground short, and in the 2017 tables the vacuum-switched bypass fails when the resistance to ground drops below 0.5 Ohm in 24 of 30 samples, rated Type B.",["Control wire chafed through and touching ground","Shorted actuator or solenoid winding","Water or corrosion bridging connector pins"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Bypass stuck in one position, possibly with EGR cooler efficiency code"],2,1,["P245A","P245B","P245D","P2490","P2457"],"מעקף מצנן EGR — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P245D:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit High (Bank 1)","P245D is the short-to-supply case of the bank 1 bypass circuit. For the Duramax with a DC-motor bypass, GM's 2017 tables watch the current through the H-bridge while it drives the flap: more than 8 A in 160 of 200 samples sets a Type B fault. On the vacuum-switched version the check looks at resistance to the supply side, and the 2014 tables describe high voltage while the driver is on.",["Control software reporting a false actuator fault (known on some Ram diesels)","Control wire shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Actuator motor drawing excessive current (low-resistance winding, binding)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Bypass actuator switched off by the controller and left in default position"],2,1,["P245A","P245B","P245C","P2491","P2457"],"מעקף מצנן EGR — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P245E:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor B Circuit","Which sensor is B depends on the maker. Ford's 2013 6.7 L Power Stroke has an exhaust pressure sensor ahead of the filter as A and a two-port differential sensor across it as B. Despite its circuit title, P245E is there an offset test during after-run, with the key off and the controller still awake: since no gas flows, the differential reading should be zero, and more than 1 kPa for one second sets the code.",["Sensor B offset drifted or moisture inside the sensor","Pressure hose kinked or blocked so pressure is trapped","Wiring or connector fault on the sensor B circuit"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Soot load estimate unreliable, regeneration timing affected"],2,1,["P245F","P2460","P2461","P2462","P2452","P246D"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P245F:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","With P245F the controller decides that the sensor B value is electrically fine but makes no physical sense. Ford's 2024 gasoline strategy runs three such tests on the B sensor of the gasoline particulate filter: an offset check with the engine stopped that fails once the average reaches 16 to 32 hPa;",["Sensor B hose cracked, disconnected or blocked","Condensate in the pressure line falsifying the reading","Sensor B drifted out of calibration","Control software needing an update (some Jeep models)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Filter regeneration triggered too early, too late or blocked"],1,1,["P245E","P2460","P2461","P2462","P2453","P246D"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2460:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","P2460 means the analog output of pressure sensor B has fallen below the lowest voltage a working sensor can deliver. On Ford's 2013 6.7 L diesel, sensor B is the differential pressure sensor across the filter; its output runs from about 0.45 V at zero to roughly 4.8 V near 38 kPa, and anything under 0.10 V for 2 s with the key on, battery between 9 and 16.25 V, sets the code.",["5 V reference to sensor B missing or shorted","Signal wire chafed and shorted to ground","Sensor B internally failed with output stuck low"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regeneration based on a model only, possibly more frequent"],1,1,["P245E","P245F","P2461","P2462","P2454"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2461:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","When pressure sensor B reports a voltage above its usable range, P2461 is stored. Ford sets the limit at 4.90 V for 2 s on the 2013 6.7 L diesel, where B is the differential sensor across the filter, and at 4.73 V for 5 s on the 2024 gasoline particulate filters. An open ground, a signal wire touching the 5 V reference or a battery feed, or a failed sensor are the classic electrical reasons.",["Condensate in the sensor tubes producing false high readings","Sensor ground open or signal shorted to reference or battery voltage","Sensor B internally failed with output stuck high"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Reduced power because the filter appears heavily loaded"],1,3,["P245E","P245F","P2460","P2462","P2455","P2453"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2462:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2462 covers a sensor B signal that drops out or jumps for short moments without staying outside its range long enough for the low or high codes. Ford is the only maker found documenting it: the 2024 gasoline particulate filter summary lists P2462 next to P2460 and P2461 in the continuously running analog circuit check, with about 5 s needed to register a fault, and no separate threshold is published.",["Terminal losing contact under engine vibration","Harness rubbing on a bracket or exhaust part","Moisture entering the connector intermittently"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, sometimes only after rough roads or rain","Pressure reading jumping in live data"],1,1,["P245E","P245F","P2460","P2461","P2456"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2463:["Diesel Particulate Filter Restriction - Soot Accumulation (Bank 1)","P2463 means the soot load in the particulate filter has passed the level at which the engine still regenerates it on its own. GM's 2009 Duramax sets it at 70 g or more for 5 minutes, the 2014 Cruze 2.0 diesel at more than 32 g for 30 s, both as Type A codes; GM's 2018 diesels use the pressure-based soot model with 120 failures in 150 samples.",["Regenerations not completed because of short trips or long idling","Differential pressure sensor, its hoses or wiring reading too high","Fault that prevents regeneration (fuel doser, temperature sensor)"],["DPF full or exhaust filter message in the cluster","MIL on and reduced engine power","Higher fuel consumption"],2,3,["P2453","P2459","P2458","P2002","P242F"],""],P2464:["Diesel Particulate Filter Differential Pressure Too Low (Bank 2)","P2464 is stored when the pressure drop across the second particulate filter stays smaller than the controller predicts for the current exhaust flow. Only engines that run a separate filter on each bank, typically larger V diesels, can log it.",["Pressure sensing hose of the bank 2 filter detached, cracked or leaking","Upstream sensing port or line blocked with soot or condensate","Filter substrate cracked, melted or removed","Differential pressure sensor drifting low"],["MIL on","Visible soot at the tailpipe if the filter is damaged","Regeneration suspended or reduced power on some engines"],2,3,["P2465","P244A","P2452","P2453","P243F"],"לחץ דיפרנציאל מסנן חלקיקים דיזל — ערך נמוך מדי (בנק 2)"],P2465:["Diesel Particulate Filter Differential Pressure Too High (Bank 2)","P2465 means the second particulate filter builds up more back pressure than the controller accepts for the exhaust flow it calculates. The code is only possible where each cylinder bank has its own filter. No maker documents the bank 2 version in a public table; its bank 1 twin P244B gives the logic.",["Bank 2 filter heavily loaded with soot or ash","Downstream sensing hose blocked, kinked or swapped","Dented or obstructed exhaust pipe behind the filter","Differential pressure sensor drifting high"],["MIL on","Frequent or prolonged regeneration attempts","Loss of power, possibly limp mode"],2,3,["P2464","P244B","P2455","P243F","P243B"],"לחץ דיפרנציאל מסנן חלקיקים דיזל — ערך גבוה מדי (בנק 2)"],P2466:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 3)","P2466 is the general circuit code for the third exhaust temperature probe in the bank 2 exhaust path, so it only appears on engines with two separate aftertreatment lines. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly.",["Temperature probe failed internally or open","Connector or wiring near the exhaust damaged by heat","Probe loose or not reaching into the gas stream"],["MIL on","Implausible or missing value for this probe in live data","Filter regeneration or DEF dosing suspended"],2,1,["P2467","P2468","P2469","P246A","P242A","P2473"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2, חיישן 3)"],P2467:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2 Sensor 3)","P2467 means the third exhaust temperature probe on bank 2 delivers an electrically valid signal that does not match the operating state. A public threshold for this exact code is not available. On bank 1, Ford's 2023 diesels test the matching probe after at least 6 h off by demanding it stays within 50 °C of three other sensors, which reveals a probe that is stuck or out of position.",["Probe aged, drifting or frozen at one value","Probe loose or pulled out of the gas stream","Coolant entering the exhaust through a leaking EGR cooler (Ford 2.0 L EcoBoost)","Controller software judging the probe too strictly"],["MIL on","Temperature value lags or deviates from neighbouring probes","White smoke and coolant loss if the EGR cooler leaks"],2,1,["P2466","P2468","P2469","P246A","P242B","P2474"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 3)"],P2468:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 3)","P2468 reports that probe 3 in the bank 2 exhaust line delivers a signal below the lowest value the input can produce with an intact circuit. With the usual resistive probes this nearly always means the signal line or the sensor itself has a ground short. No manufacturer lists this bank 2 code publicly; the neighbouring low codes show the scale.",["Signal wire chafed through and touching ground","Internal short inside the probe","Connector melted or with water ingress"],["MIL on","Probe shows an implausible value at a standstill","Regeneration or DEF dosing inhibited"],2,1,["P2466","P2467","P2469","P246A","P242C","P2475"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 3)"],P2469:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 3)","P2469 is logged when bank 2 probe number 3 pushes its input above the permitted ceiling. An unplugged connector, a broken wire or a burnt-out sensing element produces exactly that, as does a signal line shorted to a voltage source.",["Connector unplugged or wire broken (open circuit)","Sensing element burnt out","Signal line shorted to a voltage source"],["MIL on, often already in the first trip","Probe shows a maximum or invalid value","Regeneration or DEF dosing inhibited"],2,1,["P2466","P2467","P2468","P246A","P242D","P2476"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 3)"],P246A:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 2 Sensor 3)","P246A flags a third bank 2 exhaust temperature probe whose reading jumps from sample to sample faster than real gas temperature could, even though every single value stays inside the legal range. The bank 2 code itself is not described by any manufacturer in public material.",["Loose or corroded terminal in the probe connector","Harness strands broken by heat and vibration","Cracked sensing element giving unstable contact"],["MIL on after a repeated fault","Temperature trace jumps in live data","Fault may come and go with bumps or engine heat"],2,1,["P2466","P2467","P2468","P2469","P242E","P2477"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 3)"],P246B:["Vehicle Conditions Incorrect for Particulate Filter Regeneration","P246B says the controller wanted to clean the particulate filter but the vehicle did not offer the conditions its strategy needs, for example enough exhaust heat, a long enough run or a functioning air path. It describes a failed or blocked regeneration request rather than a defective part on its own, so the real cause is usually stored beside it.",["Another stored fault (e.g. intake throttle, sensors) blocking regeneration","Failed intake air shutoff throttle (Land Rover TDV6)","Short trips or long idling without enough exhaust heat"],["Regeneration does not start or is aborted repeatedly","Filter warning or rising soot load","MIL on together with the root-cause code on some vehicles"],2,1,["P2463","P2459","P244C","P0234","P246C"],""],P246C:["Particulate Filter Restriction - Forced Limited Power (Bank 1)","P246C is the final stage of the bank 1 filter loading monitor: the filter is judged so clogged that the controller reduces engine output to protect engine and filter. Ford uses it on diesels with an immediate MIL plus wrench light. In the 2015 summary a normalised restriction of twice the normal soot value above 625 rpm for 300 s sets it and EGR is switched off;",["Soot overload after repeatedly missed or aborted regenerations","Mostly stationary or low-speed operation without full regenerations","Filter at the end of its life with high ash content","PCM calibration overestimating soot load (Ford bulletins)"],["MIL and service or wrench light on","Marked loss of power (limp mode)","Drive-to-clean or filter full message"],3,3,["P2463","P243B","P2459","P244B","P246B"],""],P246D:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor A/B Correlation","P246D compares two pressure readings at the particulate filter that ought to agree under steady conditions. Which sensor is A and which is B is decided by each manufacturer. Ford's 2013 to 2015 diesel summaries use it as a rationality test between the filter pressure sensor DPFP and the delta pressure sensor DPS: with coolant above 70 °C, ambient pressure above 745 hPa, filter inlet temperature between 125 and 425…",["Sensing hoses swapped, kinked or leaking","Water or soot in a sensing line","One pressure sensor drifting out of calibration"],["MIL on","Regeneration too early, too late or suspended","Pressure values of the two sensors disagree in live data"],2,1,["P2452","P2453","P245E","P245F","P244A","P244B"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P246E:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 4)","P246E is the general code for the fourth exhaust temperature probe on bank 1, usually the last one in the aftertreatment line. Ford's diesels give it a model check rather than an electrical one: after a cold start the measured EGT14 value may differ from the modelled temperature by no more than 80 °C, the comparison lasting 200 to 400 s and the deviation having to persist for 20 s.",["Probe aged or failed, reading far from the model","Probe loose or not reaching into the gas stream","Exhaust leak near the probe cooling the reading"],["MIL on","Value of the last exhaust probe deviates from expectation","Regeneration or DEF dosing suspended"],2,1,["P246F","P2470","P2471","P2472","P242A","P24C2"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1, חיישן 4)"],P246F:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 4)","P246F stands for a fourth bank 1 exhaust temperature probe whose signal is electrically fine but physically implausible. Both main users test it after a long soak. Ford's diesels compare it with three other probes after at least 6 h off and allow no more than 50 °C between them, which unmasks a probe stuck at one value.",["Probe stuck at one value or drifting","Probe loose or backed out of the exhaust pipe","Probe connectors swapped with a neighbouring sensor"],["MIL on after the second faulty trip","Probe disagrees with neighbouring temperatures after a cold start","Usually no noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P246E","P2470","P2471","P2472","P242B","P2080"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 4)"],P2470:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 4)","P2470 means the signal of bank 1 probe number 4 has dropped below its valid floor, which on resistive probes indicates a short to ground. Ford's diesels flag a voltage under 0.10 V with the key on and 9 to 16.25 V supply, checked continuously over about 2 s.",["Signal wire chafed through and touching ground","Internal short inside the probe","Low battery voltage during diagnosis distorting readings (Ram)"],["MIL on","Implausible value for the last exhaust probe","Regeneration or DEF dosing inhibited"],2,1,["P2471","P2472","P246E","P246F","P242C","P2475"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 4)"],P2471:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 4)","P2471 is set when the fourth bank 1 exhaust temperature probe drives its input above the upper limit, the picture of an open circuit, an unplugged sensor or a short to voltage. Ford's diesels call more than 2.66 V a fault. GM checks both a short to power and an open driver circuit: above 900 Ω in the 2017 and 2020 tables, above 1,400 Ω in 2018, with 10 failed readings in 20;",["Connector unplugged or wire broken (open circuit)","Sensing element burnt out","Signal line shorted to a voltage source"],["MIL on, on GM possibly in the first trip","Last exhaust probe shows maximum or substitute value","Regeneration or DEF dosing inhibited"],2,1,["P2470","P2472","P246E","P246F","P242D","P2476"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 4)"],P2472:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 1 Sensor 4)","P2472 reports that the last bank 1 temperature probe (sensor 4) changes its signal too abruptly between two readings, although each reading on its own lies in range. GM documents it as a quick-change monitor with a 100 ms task: the 2017 and 2018 diesel tables look at the resistance step between consecutive samples (more than 10 Ω) and fail after 15 of 30 samples, the 2025 tables use a temperature step above 100 °C…",["Loose or corroded terminal in the probe connector","Wire fatigue near the hot exhaust pipe","Cracked sensing element giving unstable contact"],["MIL on after the second faulty trip","Temperature value flickers in live data","Fault comes and goes, often after rough roads"],2,1,["P2470","P2471","P246E","P246F","P242E","P2477"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 4)"],P2473:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 4)","P2473 covers the wiring of probe number four in the bank 2 exhaust line as a whole, so it only occurs on engines with two separate exhaust paths and a long sensor chain on each. The controller sets it when the probe line delivers a value it cannot assign to a clean low or high fault, for instance an open circuit or a sensor reporting an internal error. No maker documents P2473 publicly.",["Broken wire or unplugged connector at the bank 2 probe","Probe element burnt out","Fault in the control unit input stage"],["MIL on","No usable value for bank 2 probe 4 in live data","Filter regeneration suspended"],2,1,["P2474","P2475","P2476","P2477","P246E","P2466","P247F"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2, חיישן 4)"],P2474:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2 Sensor 4)","P2474 flags a plausibility problem: the electrical signal of bank 2 probe 4 is valid, yet the temperature it reports does not fit what the engine controller expects. Typical tests compare the probe with its neighbours after a long soak, when all should read about ambient, or with a modelled value during driving. Ford handles the bank 1 analogue P246F as a sensor-to-sensor check on its single-bank diesels;",["Probe aged and reading off by a constant amount","Soot-coated probe tip reacting slowly","Exhaust leak upstream of the probe falsifying the reading"],["MIL on after repeated detection","Probe 4 of bank 2 differs clearly from the other probes after a cold soak","Regenerations incomplete or more frequent"],2,1,["P2473","P2475","P2476","P2477","P246F","P2467","P24C3"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 4)"],P2475:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 4)","P2475 is stored when the voltage from bank 2 probe 4 falls below the lowest value the probe can produce in normal use. With the resistive PTC probes common on diesels this points to a short between signal and ground, or to a sensor shorted internally.",["Signal wire rubbed through against the exhaust or body","Probe shorted internally","Water in the connector bridging the pins"],["MIL on","Bank 2 probe 4 shows an implausibly cold or fixed value","Regeneration or DEF dosing restricted"],2,1,["P2476","P2473","P2474","P2477","P2470","P2468"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 4)"],P2476:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 4)","P2476 covers the opposite end of the scale from P2475: the signal of bank 2 probe 4 sits above its usable ceiling. Because the probe forms a voltage divider with a pull-up resistor in the control unit, an interrupted wire, a disconnected plug or a short to a supply voltage all drive the input high.",["Open signal or ground wire, often heat-damaged","Connector loose or not locked after service work","Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage"],["MIL on","Probe reads maximum or an implausibly hot value","Regeneration blocked"],2,1,["P2475","P2473","P2474","P2477","P2471","P2469"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 4)"],P2477:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 2 Sensor 4)","P2477 targets a signal from bank 2 probe 4 that jumps around, while each individual sample may still be in range. Real exhaust temperature changes only gradually because the probe and pipe have thermal mass, so sudden steps between consecutive readings betray a wiring or contact issue.",["Loose or corroded pins in the probe connector","Wire strands breaking near the hot pipe","Cracked probe element with unstable contact"],["MIL on after the second faulty trip","Value of bank 2 probe 4 jumps in live data","Fault code returns after being cleared"],2,1,["P2473","P2474","P2475","P2476","P2472","P246A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 4)"],P2478:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","Unlike the circuit codes, P2478 judges the temperature itself at the first exhaust probe of bank 1, usually ahead of the oxidation catalyst. Ford's 2015 diesel summary for the 6.7L and 3.2L engines groups it with the EGT circuit check: the test is high-side only and trips at roughly 1150 °C, because the PTC probe curve leaves no separate low threshold.",["Real overheating from excess fuel or a leaking injector","Overly sensitive diagnosis needing a software update (VW Passat 2012)","Probe reading too high due to ageing","Lack of air from a boost leak or turbocharger fault"],["MIL on","Power reduced to protect the exhaust parts","Smoke or a hot smell from the exhaust in real overheating"],3,3,["P2479","P247A","P247B","P247C","P0544","P0546","P2080"],"טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — מחוץ לטווח (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2479:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P2479 applies the same temperature-limit idea to the second bank 1 probe. On the 2015 Ford 6.7L layout this is EGT12 at the oxidation catalyst outlet, where the exotherm of a regeneration shows up first, so a runaway burn or excessive post-injection can push the reading towards the limit. Ford's 2015 diesel summary lists P2479 alongside P2032 and P2033 and uses a high-side threshold of about 1150 °C;",["Excessive heat during regeneration, e.g. too much post-injection","Leaking injector adding unburnt fuel to the catalyst","Probe reading too high"],["MIL on","Regeneration aborted","Reduced power"],3,3,["P2478","P247A","P247B","P247D","P2031","P2033","P2084"],"טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — מחוץ לטווח (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P247A:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P247A is the out-of-range verdict for the third bank 1 probe, which sits further down the aftertreatment line. It is the best documented code of this series. Volkswagen's 2014 quick-reference books for the 2.0L TDI CJAA (Golf, Beetle) compare the control deviation with an engine-speed and torque map, while the 3.0L TDI in the 2014 Touareg flags a gap between target and measured temperature above 200 K or below -100…",["Overloaded particulate filter burning off too fast","Regeneration not reaching target temperature (VW low-side check)","Probe aged and misreporting"],["MIL on","Filter regeneration aborted or repeated","Emergency mode with reduced power possible"],3,3,["P2478","P2479","P247B","P247E","P242A","P242D","P242B"],"טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — מחוץ לטווח (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P247B:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range (Bank 1 Sensor 4)","P247B concerns the last probe in the bank 1 chain. In Ford's 2015 6.7L overview that is EGT14, mounted downstream of the particulate filter, so it sees the heat that leaves the filter during regeneration. Ford's 2015 diesel summary is the only public maker document with this code; it pairs it with P2470 and P2471 and apply the same high-side limit of about 1150 °C, monitored continuously over some 2 s.",["Thermal runaway in the particulate filter","Probe reading too high","Unburnt fuel reaching the filter from injectors or a dosing valve"],["MIL on","Regeneration stopped, filter load warning possible","Power reduction"],3,3,["P2478","P2479","P247A","P247F","P246E","P2470","P2471"],"טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — מחוץ לטווח (בנק 1, חיישן 4)"],P247C:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P247C is the bank 2 counterpart of P2478: the first exhaust probe on the second cylinder bank reports a temperature outside its permitted window, typically next to the turbine outlet or catalyst inlet of that bank. It needs a V engine with separate exhaust paths and its own probe per bank. No maker documents P247C in public material;",["Bank 2 running hot from extra fuel or a faulty injector","Bank 2 probe 1 reading too high","Air shortage on bank 2 from a boost leak or turbo fault"],["MIL on","Reduced power to protect the exhaust","Bank 2 probe reads clearly above bank 1"],3,3,["P2478","P247D","P247E","P247F","P0547","P0549"],"טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — מחוץ לטווח (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P247D:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P247D applies to the second probe on bank 2, by analogy with P2479 normally downstream of that bank's oxidation catalyst, where the heat released by burning fuel during a regeneration is measured. It is set when the reported temperature leaves the plausible window, in practice mostly on the high side. There is no public maker document for P247D;",["Too much heat in the bank 2 catalyst during regeneration","Probe reading high even on a cold engine","Leaking injector on bank 2"],["MIL on","Regeneration cancelled","Bank 2 probe 2 differs from its bank 1 twin"],3,3,["P2479","P247C","P247E","P247F","P2034","P2036"],"טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — מחוץ לטווח (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P247E:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range (Bank 2 Sensor 3)","P247E does not question the wiring but the value itself: the third exhaust probe on cylinder bank 2 reports a temperature the engine control unit will not accept, in practice mostly an implausibly hot one. The code only makes sense on a V engine whose two banks keep separate exhaust paths up to the third measuring point. No maker publishes P247E;",["Uncontrolled soot burn or too much post-injection fuel on bank 2","Probe drifted and reports values too high","Leaking injector or turbo oil leak on bank 2"],["Warning lamp on, regeneration may be aborted","Reduced power to protect the aftertreatment"],3,3,["P247A","P247C","P247D","P247F"],"טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — מחוץ לטווח (בנק 2, חיישן 3)"],P247F:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range (Bank 2 Sensor 4)","P247F flags an unacceptable reading from the fourth exhaust temperature probe of bank 2, the position that on most layouts sits behind the particulate filter. A genuine reading near the limit there means heat is leaving the filter, which points to a runaway regeneration. No manufacturer documents P247F publicly.",["Overloaded particulate filter burning off too fast","Probe ageing with readings drifting upwards","Probe swapped with another position after a repair"],["Engine warning lamp lit","Regeneration blocked or power limited"],3,3,["P247B","P247C","P247D","P247E","P246E"],"טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — מחוץ לטווח (בנק 2, חיישן 4)"],P2480:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 5)","P2480 is the general circuit or open-circuit fault of a fifth exhaust temperature probe on bank 1. Five probes in one line are rare; GM's small diesels with oxidation catalyst, SCR, second catalyst and filter are among the few layouts that use them.",["Broken or chafed lead to probe 5","Corroded or loose connector near the exhaust","Measuring element of the probe burned through"],["Warning lamp on","Missing or frozen value for probe 5 in live data","Filter regeneration may be suppressed"],2,3,["P2481","P2482","P2483","P2484","P2485"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 5)"],P2481:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 5)","P2481 means the signal of the fifth bank 1 exhaust probe has dropped below its lower electrical limit, which on a resistive probe usually indicates a short to ground. GM documents it codegenau for its diesel ECMs: the 2017 and 2020 tables fail a probe resistance under 158 Ω, the 2018 table under 500 Ω, each after 10 of 20 samples at 100 ms, as a Type B fault.",["Signal lead chafed through and touching ground","Internal short in the probe after heat damage","Neighbouring probe replaced because positions were confused"],["Engine warning lamp after two trips","Probe 5 reads implausibly in live data"],2,3,["P2480","P2482","P2483","P2484","P2486"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 5)"],P2482:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 5)","With P2482 the fifth bank 1 exhaust probe delivers a signal above its upper electrical limit. On GM diesels this code also covers the open circuit: the 2018 table sets it above 1400 Ω, both as a short to power with the driver off and as an interruption with the driver on, after 10 of 20 samples, Type B. The 2020 table makes it Type A.",["Loose, corroded or unplugged connector","Broken lead from heat or vibration","Probe element open or high-resistance"],["Warning lamp, on GM from 2020 after a single trip","Probe 5 shows a fixed extreme value","Regeneration suppressed"],2,3,["P2480","P2481","P2483","P2484","P2487"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 5)"],P2483:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 5)","P2483 is the plausibility test for the fifth bank 1 exhaust probe: the circuit is electrically fine, but the reading does not behave like a real exhaust temperature. GM's 2025 diesel tables describe the check in detail. After the engine has been off for more than 10,800 s (three hours), the value frozen at key-on serves as reference;",["Probe not fully seated in its boss after exhaust work","Probe output stuck or responding too slowly","Heavily sooted probe tip insulating the element"],["Warning lamp after two trips","Probe 5 barely changes while the other probes heat up"],2,1,["P2480","P2481","P2482","P2484","P2488"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 5)"],P2484:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 1 Sensor 5)","P2484 catches a fifth bank 1 exhaust probe whose signal jumps faster than any real exhaust temperature can change. GM's diesel ECMs compare consecutive samples taken every 100 ms. In the 2018 table the resistance difference between two samples is evaluated, and 15 failed samples out of 30 set a Type B code.",["Intermittent contact in the probe connector","Harness insulation worn by heat or rubbing","Probe element cracking internally"],["Warning lamp, sometimes going out again","Erratic jumps of probe 5 in live data"],2,1,["P2480","P2481","P2482","P2483","P2489"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 5)"],P2485:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit/Open (Bank 2 Sensor 5)","P2485 reports a circuit or open-circuit fault at a fifth exhaust temperature probe on bank 2. That requires a V engine with two separate aftertreatment lines carrying five probes each, a layout no public maker document shows. No manufacturer documents P2485.",["Interrupted lead between control unit and probe","Connector left unplugged after exhaust work","Probe element open"],["Warning lamp on","No valid value for this probe"],2,3,["P2480","P2486","P2487","P2488","P2489"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 5)"],P2486:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 5)","P2486 is set when the signal of the fifth bank 2 exhaust probe sits below its lower electrical limit, typically because the lead or the probe itself shorts to ground. No manufacturer documents P2486 publicly; it presupposes two exhaust banks with five probes each.",["Lead insulation damaged and touching ground","Internal short of the probe"],["Engine warning lamp","Implausible reading of this probe"],2,3,["P2481","P2485","P2487","P2488","P2489"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 5)"],P2487:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 5)","With P2487 the control unit sees the fifth bank 2 exhaust probe above its upper electrical limit, the picture of a short to supply voltage or, on many designs, of an open circuit. There is no public maker document for P2487. For bank 1 GM treats probe 5 under P2482: above 1400 Ω in the 2018 tables, beyond 100 MΩ or about 1290 °C in 2025, rated Type A since 2020, so the lamp comes on after one trip.",["Connector loose or disconnected","Signal lead shorted to a supply line","Probe element open or high-resistance"],["Warning lamp after one trip","Probe shows maximum or no value"],2,3,["P2482","P2485","P2486","P2488","P2489"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 5)"],P2488:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2 Sensor 5)","P2488 is the rationality check for the fifth bank 2 exhaust probe: the signal is electrically valid but does not follow the operating state. No manufacturer documents P2488; a second bank with five probes is unknown in public maker material.",["Aged probe responding too slowly","Probe not reaching into the gas flow","Exhaust leak cooling the measuring point"],["Warning lamp after two trips","Regeneration may be inhibited"],2,1,["P2483","P2485","P2486","P2487","P2489"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 5)"],P2489:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 2 Sensor 5)","P2489 points to an unsteady signal from the fifth exhaust probe on bank 2: the value stays within its electrical limits but jumps or drops out briefly. This code is not documented by any manufacturer, as no public layout carries five probes per bank on a twin-bank engine.",["Loose terminal in the connector","Harness touching hot exhaust parts","Internal crack in the probe"],["Warning lamp coming and going","Jumping value in live data"],2,1,["P2484","P2485","P2486","P2487","P2488"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 5)"],P248A:["Reductant Heater A Sense Circuit Low","P248A concerns the sense line with which the control unit measures the supply voltage reaching DEF heater A, and reports that voltage as too low. GM uses it on its diesels with an SCR power module for the tank heater: the 2016 to 2018 tables subtract the heater supply voltage from system voltage and fail a gap of more than 3 V while heating is commanded, after 10 of 12 checks at 500 ms;",["Corroded heater supply connector at the tank","Worn heater relay contact causing voltage drop","Weak battery or charging fault during heating"],["Warning lamp or DEF system message","Frozen DEF not thawed in winter, dosing delayed"],2,1,["P248B","P248C","P248D","P20B9","P20BB"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P248B:["Reductant Heater A Sense Circuit High","P248B is the upper counterpart to P248A: the sense signal for the supply of DEF heater A reads higher than permitted, for example when the line shorts to battery voltage, when the supply stays live although the heater is switched off, or when the sense input itself fails. No manufacturer documents P248B in public material.",["Heater relay sticking closed","Sense lead shorted to battery voltage","Faulty sense input in the control module"],["Warning lamp","Possible battery drain if the heater stays powered"],2,1,["P248A","P248C","P248D","P20BC","P20B9"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P248C:["Reductant Heater B Sense Circuit Low","P248C reports too little voltage on the sense circuit of DEF heater B. In GM's diesel tables from 2016 to 2018 heater B is the line heater, i.e. the heated hose from the pump to the dosing valve.",["Corroded plug at the heated DEF line","Voltage drop across fuse or relay of the line heater","Damaged supply lead along the frame"],["DEF warning or engine lamp","Dosing faults at low temperatures"],2,1,["P248A","P248B","P248D","P20BD","P20BE"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P248D:["Reductant Heater B Sense Circuit High","P248D means the heater B sense input reads too high, typically the heated line. Possible pictures are a sense wire shorted to battery positive, a supply that remains on after the heater has been switched off, or a faulty input stage. Public maker documentation for P248D does not exist. GM tests the line heater sense circuit only for undervoltage (P248C);",["Line heater relay sticking closed","Sense wire shorted to battery positive","Defective input stage in the module"],["Warning lamp","Battery discharging while parked"],2,1,["P248A","P248B","P248C","P20C0","P221C"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P248E:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2)","P248E is the bank 2 counterpart of P245A: the engine controller sees no proper load on the output that drives the EGR cooler bypass of the second cylinder bank, most often because the circuit is open. Only engines with a separate EGR path per bank can set it, which in practice means V engines with two coolers. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; the published diesel tables we checked only list bank 1.",["Unplugged connector or broken wire at the bank 2 bypass actuator","Open motor or solenoid winding in the bank 2 actuator","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Longer warm-up or higher NOx on one bank because the bypass stays put"],2,1,["P245A","P248F","P2490","P2491","P24A6"],"מעקף מצנן EGR — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P248F:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2)","With P248F the bank 2 bypass circuit is electrically sound, yet the flap does not do what the controller asks: it lags behind the setpoint, stops short of its end position or switching shows no effect on the gas temperature after the cooler. No manufacturer publishes a bank 2 version of this check.",["Bypass flap on bank 2 sluggish from soot and carbon","Leaking vacuum line or weak vacuum on pneumatic actuators","Bank 2 position feedback reading off"],["Check engine light on","Often no noticeable change in driving"],2,1,["P245B","P248E","P2498","P24A6"],"מעקף מצנן EGR — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2490:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P2490 means the drive line of the bank 2 cooler bypass actuator sits too close to ground potential, typically a grounded wire between controller and actuator. It mirrors P245C on bank 1. No manufacturer documents P2490 publicly. GM's 2017 diesel tables give an idea of the bank 1 test: the vacuum-switched bypass is failed when the resistance to ground falls below 0.5 Ohm in 24 of 30 samples.",["Drive wire rubbed through and touching engine ground","Water or corrosion in the bank 2 actuator connector","Internal short in the actuator"],["Check engine light on","Bypass on bank 2 stuck in one mode, possibly followed by cooler efficiency codes"],2,1,["P245C","P248E","P2491"],"מעקף מצנן EGR — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2491:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit High (Bank 2)","P2491 reports excess voltage or excess current in the drive circuit feeding the bypass actuator on bank 2, the classic sign of a short to supply or of a winding whose resistance has collapsed. It is the bank 2 sibling of P245D, and no maker publishes its own description of it.",["Control wire touching a battery or ignition feed","Actuator winding with too low resistance or seized motor","Controller software reporting a false actuator fault"],["Check engine light on","Bypass flap on bank 2 rests in its default position"],2,1,["P245D","P248E","P2490"],"מעקף מצנן EGR — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2492:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit (Bank 1)","The position sensor tells the controller where the bank 1 cooler bypass flap actually is; position-controlled flaps cannot be regulated without it. P2492 is the general circuit code for that sensor, used when the fault cannot be classed as a short to ground or to the supply. No manufacturer documents P2492 publicly.",["Damaged sensor wiring near hot exhaust parts","Loose or corroded connector at the bypass valve","5 V sensor supply missing or shared circuit shorted"],["Check engine light on","Bypass flap no longer position-controlled"],2,1,["P2493","P2494","P2495","P2496","P2497","P24C4"],"חיישן מצב מעקף מצנן EGR — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P2493:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Range/Performance (Bank 1)","P2493 is a plausibility fault: the bank 1 bypass position signal stays inside its electrical limits, but its value or behaviour does not fit the commanded flap position or the learned end stops. GM names the code in preliminary bulletin PI1449 for the 2015 Silverado and Sierra with the LML Duramax, where it showed up together with P2495, P24C4 and P06A3.",["Worn or defective bypass valve with integrated sensor","Deposits shifting the learned end positions","Unstable 5 V reference shared with other sensors"],["Check engine light on, often with further bypass codes","Bypass position in the live data does not match the command"],2,1,["P2492","P2494","P2495","P2498","P24C4","P06A3"],"חיישן מצב מעקף מצנן EGR — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2494:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1)","P2494 is set when the raw voltage of the bank 1 bypass position sensor drops toward zero. GM documents it for the Duramax diesel: in the 2017 tables the signal must be below 1 % of the 5 V reference in 200 of 250 samples, checked every 6.25 ms once cranking is over and the powertrain relay supplies more than 11 V. The 2018 tables keep the test and the Type B rating, so the lamp comes on after two trips.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","Open 5 V reference wire to the sensor","Internal sensor fault in the bypass valve"],["Check engine light after two trips","Bypass control falls back to a default position"],2,1,["P2492","P2493","P2495","P2499","P24C4"],"חיישן מצב מעקף מצנן EGR — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2495:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1)","P2495 covers a bank 1 bypass position signal that climbs close to the reference voltage. On GM Duramax diesels the 2017 calibration fails it above 99 % of 5 V in 200 out of 250 samples, with the same enable conditions as the low test, and rates it Type B.",["Open sensor ground wire","Defective bypass valve with integrated sensor","Fault in the shared 5 V reference circuit","Signal wire touching a voltage source"],["Check engine light after two trips","Additional sensor supply codes stored at the same time"],2,1,["P2492","P2493","P2494","P249A","P24C4","P06A3"],"חיישן מצב מעקף מצנן EGR — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2496:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 1)","P2496 targets a bank 1 bypass position signal that jumps, drops out briefly or changes faster than the flap can physically move, without staying outside the electrical limits long enough for P2494 or P2495. No manufacturer documents P2496 publicly; GM's Duramax tables, which do cover the same analog sensor, only list the low, high and learning checks.",["Loose or spread terminal in the sensor connector","Wire breaking inside the insulation from engine movement","Worn contact track inside the sensor"],["Check engine light that comes and goes","Bypass position value jumps in the live data"],2,1,["P2492","P2494","P2495","P249B"],"חיישן מצב מעקף מצנן EGR — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2497:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit (Bank 2)","P2497 is the generic circuit fault of the position sensor on the bank 2 cooler bypass, so it can only appear on engines whose second bank has its own EGR cooler with feedback-controlled flap. We found no manufacturer that documents a bank 2 bypass sensor; all published examples, such as GM's Duramax tables, are single-bank engines that use P2494 and P2495 on bank 1.",["Damaged wiring to the bank 2 position sensor","Connector not latched or corroded","Failed position sensor or bypass valve"],["Check engine light on","Bypass on bank 2 no longer regulated"],2,1,["P2492","P2498","P2499","P249A","P249B"],"חיישן מצב מעקף מצנן EGR — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2)"],P2498:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Range/Performance (Bank 2)","With P2498 the bank 2 bypass position signal is electrically valid but not believable, for example because it does not change when the flap is commanded, settles at an unexpected value or no longer matches the end stops learned earlier. There is no public manufacturer description for this bank 2 code.",["Worn bank 2 bypass valve with built-in sensor","Flap binding so the sensor reads a position other than commanded","End-stop learn values invalid after a repair"],["Check engine light on","Measured and commanded bypass position differ on bank 2"],2,1,["P2493","P2497","P2499","P249A","P248F"],"חיישן מצב מעקף מצנן EGR — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P2499:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P2499 stands for a bank 2 bypass position voltage that has fallen to the bottom of its range. No manufacturer documents the bank 2 code publicly. For orientation, GM's 2017 Duramax tables fail the bank 1 sensor (P2494) once its output drops under one percent of the supply and need 200 bad results out of 250 before the Type B fault is stored.",["Bank 2 signal wire touching ground","5 V sensor supply interrupted or pulled down","Sensor output stage failed"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 bypass position reads near zero"],2,1,["P2494","P2497","P2498","P249A"],"חיישן מצב מעקף מצנן EGR — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P249A:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2)","P249A is logged when the bank 2 bypass position signal sits near the top of the reference voltage. Like its siblings on this bank, it is not described by any manufacturer in public documents. The bank 1 analogue P2495 is set by GM's Duramax logic once the raw value exceeds 99 % of 5 V in most of a 250-sample window, rated Type B with the lamp after two trips.",["Lost ground at the bank 2 position sensor","Signal wire in contact with a supply line","Water ingress in the sensor connector"],["Check engine light after two trips","Bank 2 bypass position shows full scale"],2,1,["P2495","P2497","P2498","P2499"],"חיישן מצב מעקף מצנן EGR — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P249B:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 2)","P249B flags short dropouts or implausible jumps in the bank 2 bypass position signal that are too brief to count as a steady low or high fault. Public manufacturer documentation for it does not exist, and even the well documented bank 1 sensor on GM's Duramax only has low, high and learning checks, without an erratic test of its own.",["Fretting or loose terminal in the bank 2 sensor plug","Harness brittle from heat near the turbocharger","Intermittent fault inside the sensor"],["Check engine light appears now and then","Bank 2 position value flickers in the live data"],2,1,["P2496","P2497","P2499","P249A"],"חיישן מצב מעקף מצנן EGR — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 2)"],P249C:["Excessive Time To Enter Closed Loop Reductant Injection Control","P249C covers the SCR dosing strategy rather than a part: after start-up the engine controller is expected to switch from fixed, map-based urea dosing to dosing corrected by the NOx sensor signal, and this code means that switch happened too seldom or too late.",["Downstream NOx sensor slow to become ready or faulty, so closed loop cannot start","Implausible exhaust gas temperature signal upstream or downstream of the SCR","Mostly short or cold trips keep the SCR below its working temperature","Engine control software calibration requiring an update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Often no noticeable change in driving behaviour","NOx sensor or exhaust temperature codes may be stored as well"],3,1,["P249D","P249E","P20EE","P202E"],""],P249D:["Closed Loop Reductant Injection Control At Limit - Flow Too Low","With P249D the NOx feedback loop of the SCR system has pushed its long-term correction as far as it may go because the delivered amount of DEF appears too small for the measured NOx. GM's tables judge this via the long-term adaptation value: above 1.69 in the 2014 diesel table and above 1.99 in the 2018 table; both rate it Type B, lamp after the second failing trip.",["Dosing valve partly blocked by urea crystals or deposits","Weak DEF pump or restricted supply line and filter","Diluted or wrong fluid in the DEF tank","NOx sensor reading too high and misleading the controller"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Increased DEF warnings or later speed or power limitation","SCR efficiency code may follow"],2,3,["P249E","P249C","P20EE","P202E"],""],P249E:["Closed Loop Reductant Injection Control At Limit - Flow Too High","P249E is the counterpart to P249D: here the SCR feedback has trimmed the dosing down to the lowest correction it is allowed, because more reductant seems to arrive than the NOx reading calls for. GM's 2014 diesel table flags a long-term adaptation factor below 0.41 (Type B); the 2018 table lists the low-side check as a two-trip Type B fault. Ford's 2023 summary uses the same 30 s clip rule as for P249D.",["Dosing valve leaking or sticking partly open","Ammonia slip from an aged or overloaded SCR catalyst seen by the NOx sensor","NOx sensor reading too low","Fluid concentration outside specification"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Ammonia smell from the exhaust","White crystalline deposits at the dosing point"],2,1,["P249D","P249C","P20EE","P202E"],""],P249F:["Excessive Time To Enter Closed Loop Particulate Filter Regeneration Control","During an active filter regeneration the controller is meant to steer the temperature ahead of the particulate filter with feedback from the exhaust temperature sensors, usually by adjusting late fuel injection or a hydrocarbon dosing valve in the exhaust. P249F is stored when the regeneration spent too little of its duration in that feedback mode.",["Engine or aftertreatment module software needing an update","Exhaust temperature sensor ahead of the oxidation catalyst or filter reading wrongly","Hydrocarbon dosing valve in the exhaust restricted or slow to respond","Regenerations repeatedly interrupted by short trips or changing load"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regeneration may take longer or repeat more often","Often no change in driveability"],3,1,["P24A0","P24A1","P244C","P244D"],""],P24A0:["Closed Loop Particulate Filter Regeneration Control At Limit - Temperature Too Low","P24A0 means the regeneration temperature loop is already giving all the extra heat it may, yet the gas ahead of the particulate filter stays below target. GM describes it as an HC injector control deviation: the gap between setpoint and measured temperature ahead of the DPF is watched while the filter warms up, and 10 failing out of 20 samples set a Type B fault;",["Hydrocarbon dosing valve or its fuel supply restricted","Oxidation catalyst aged or face-plugged, so the fuel does not burn ahead of the filter","Exhaust temperature sensor reading too low","Exhaust leak ahead of the sensors cooling the gas"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regenerations take long or do not finish","Soot load codes may follow"],3,3,["P24A1","P249F","P244C","P24A2"],""],P24A1:["Closed Loop Particulate Filter Regeneration Control At Limit - Temperature Too High","Here the regeneration loop has reduced its heat input as far as possible, but the temperature ahead of the filter still runs above target. GM lists P24A1 as the negative-deviation branch of the HC injector control check in steady regeneration, again a Type B fault counted over samples;",["Hydrocarbon doser or fuel injector leaking extra fuel into the exhaust","Fuel supply part causing unstable doser pressure (Hino 2020 bubbler filter)","Exhaust temperature sensor reading too high","Heavy soot load burning faster than the controller can follow"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regeneration aborted early","Possible high exhaust temperature warning"],3,3,["P24A0","P249F","P244D","P24A2"],""],P24A2:["Particulate Filter Regeneration Incomplete (Bank 1)","P24A2 judges the outcome of a regeneration on the bank 1 filter: the event ended, but the estimated soot left in the filter is still above the allowed level. Ford's 2023 diesel summary runs this once per regeneration for up to 40 minutes and compares the soot estimate at the end with a threshold.",["Regenerations interrupted by short trips or engine shut-off","Exhaust temperature not reaching target (doser, oxidation catalyst, sensors)","Differential pressure sensor or its hoses giving a wrong soot estimate","Regeneration stopped by over-temperature protection"],["Malfunction indicator lamp or filter warning on","More frequent regenerations, higher fuel consumption","Reduced power if soot keeps building"],2,3,["P243E","P24A4","P2463","P2459","P24A0"],""],P24A3:["Particulate Filter Restriction - Soot Accumulation (Bank 2)","P24A3 is the bank 2 entry for a particulate filter whose soot load, estimated from differential pressure, exhaust flow and a soot model, has climbed to the point where it noticeably restricts flow and needs a regeneration. It only appears on engines with two separate filter strands, such as some V engines.",["Mostly short trips so passive and active regeneration cannot finish","Excess soot from injectors, EGR or boost problems","Differential pressure sensor or hoses on bank 2 giving a false high reading"],["Particulate filter or engine warning lamp","Reduced power or slow response","Higher fuel consumption"],2,3,["P2463","P243F","P243E"],""],P24A4:["Particulate Filter Restriction - Soot Accumulation Too High (Bank 1)","P24A4 marks the critical stage for the bank 1 filter: the soot load is so high that a normal regeneration risks overheating and cracking the substrate. Deutz names P24A4-00 a critical soot load. GM's 2016 and 2018 diesel tables use P24A4 for a clogged filter that has to be replaced, judged from the filtered flow resistance derived from differential pressure, 5 failures in 10 samples, Type A with one trip;",["Earlier soot warnings or failed regenerations not dealt with","Excess soot from injectors, EGR valve or turbocharger faults","Filter saturated with ash at end of service life","Differential pressure measurement reading falsely high"],["Marked loss of power, limp mode","Automatic regeneration no longer runs","Malfunction indicator and filter warning lamp on"],4,3,["P2463","P242F","P243F","P24A2"],""],P24A5:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Stuck/Open (Bank 1)","P24A5 means the bank 1 cooler bypass is mechanically stuck, and makers read that in both directions. GM's 2017 Duramax DC-motor flap is judged stuck in bypass if the position is still above 15 % after P245B; the 2018 vacuum version is moved between both modes and fails when the gas temperature after the cooler barely reacts, both Type B.",["Bypass flap seized by soot and carbon deposits","Actuator, linkage or vacuum supply no longer moving the flap","Incorrect EGR cooler fitted at the factory","Engine software that sets the fault too readily"],["Check engine light on","Slow warm-up or more soot when the flap is stuck in cooling","Higher NOx and EGR gas temperatures when stuck in bypass"],3,1,["P24A6","P245B","P2457","P245A","P2493"],""],P24A6:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Stuck/Open (Bank 2)","P24A6 is reserved for a mechanically stuck cooler bypass on bank 2. No manufacturer documents it publicly; the Ford and GM diesel summaries that describe the stuck test all apply it to a single bank and use P24A5.",["Bank 2 flap seized by deposits","Bank 2 actuator or linkage failed","Missing vacuum on a pneumatically switched bypass"],["Check engine light on","Uneven exhaust temperatures between the two banks"],3,1,["P24A5","P248E","P248F","P2490","P2491"],""],P24A7:["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Control Circuit/Open","Some diesel engines feed the EGR cooler with an electric auxiliary coolant pump so the cooler gets flow at low engine speed or after shut-off, independent of the main pump. P24A7 means the engine controller sees an open or otherwise faulty control line to this pump, typically when the driver stage detects no load while switching.",["Loose, corroded or unplugged pump connector","Broken control wire in the harness","Open winding or electronics in the pump"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EGR may be reduced, NOx output rises"],2,1,["P24A9","P24AA","P24A8","P24AB"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן EGR — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P24A8:["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Performance/Stuck Off","Unlike the circuit codes, P24A8 is about the pump's effect: it is commanded on, the wiring looks fine, yet the controller concludes that it does not deliver, for example because its speed feedback stays low or the expected temperature drop across the EGR cooler is missing. Air trapped after a coolant change, a blocked impeller, low coolant level or a seized motor are the usual reasons.",["Air pocket in the auxiliary circuit after service or a leak","Pump motor seized or impeller blocked","Low coolant level"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Coolant loss or bubbling at the expansion tank","EGR temperature or cooler efficiency codes may follow"],2,1,["P24AB","P24A7","P2457","P24AC"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן EGR — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P24A9:["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Control Circuit Low","P24A9 reports that the voltage on the control line of the electric EGR cooler coolant pump is lower than the driver stage expects in its current switching state, which usually points to a harness or pump-internal short to ground, or to a chafed wire touching the engine block.",["Control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Insulation melted near exhaust or EGR parts","Internal short in the pump electronics"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Pump may run continuously or not at all"],2,1,["P24AA","P24A7","P24A8"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן EGR — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P24AA:["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Control Circuit High","With P24AA the controller finds the control line of the EGR cooler coolant pump at a higher voltage than its switching state allows. The classic causes are a short circuit toward battery voltage, for example where the harness rubs against a powered wire, moisture in the connector, or a pump that no longer draws current so the line floats up.",["Control wire shorted to a battery voltage feed","Water or corrosion in the pump connector","Pump electronics failed so no current is drawn"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Pump may not run when commanded"],2,1,["P24A9","P24A7","P24AB"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן EGR — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P24AB:["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Stuck On","P24AB is set when the EGR cooler coolant pump keeps running although the controller has switched it off, seen for instance in continued speed feedback or current draw. Causes include a driver stage or relay that stays closed, a short that bypasses the switching side, or pump electronics that ignore the command.",["Relay or controller output stage stuck closed","Short in the harness bypassing the switched side","Pump electronics no longer responding to the command"],["Pump audible after engine shut-off","Battery drained after standing","Malfunction indicator lamp on"],2,1,["P24A8","P24A9","P24AA"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן EGR — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P24AC:["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Feedback Circuit Low","Electronically commutated coolant pumps often report their state back to the controller on a separate feedback wire, typically as a speed or diagnostic signal. P24AC means that this return line sits below its valid range: shorted to ground, pulled down by a damaged pump, or permanently in an error level the pump uses to signal a dry run or blockage.",["Feedback wire shorted to ground","Pump signalling an internal fault, dry run or blockage","Corroded feedback pin in the connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EGR possibly reduced"],2,1,["P24AD","P24A8","P24A9"],"משוב משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן EGR — אות נמוך במעגל"],P24AD:["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Feedback Circuit High","P24AD is the high-side counterpart of P24AC: the return signal from the EGR cooler coolant pump stays above its valid band. Since such feedback lines are usually pulled up inside the controller, a broken wire or a disconnected pump often shows as a constantly high level, as can a short to a voltage feed. The pump itself may still run normally, but the controller can no longer prove it.",["Feedback wire broken or pump unplugged, line pulled high","Feedback wire shorted to a voltage feed","Pump electronics no longer pulling the signal down"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Often no noticeable effect while driving"],2,1,["P24AC","P24A7","P24AA"],"משוב משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן EGR — אות גבוה במעגל"],P24AE:["Particulate Matter Sensor Circuit","The resistive particulate matter sensor behind the diesel particulate filter collects soot on interlocking electrodes; a rising current between them shows that particles are leaking through the filter. P24AE covers a fault in that electrode circuit.",["Sensor element contaminated or damaged by moisture","Harness or connector to the sensor control unit damaged by heat or water","Fault in the separate sensor control unit"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Filter efficiency monitor cannot complete"],2,1,["P24AF","P24B0","P24B1","P24B3","P2002"],"חיישן חלקיקים — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P24AF:["Particulate Matter Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P24AF tests whether the particulate matter sensor behaves plausibly while it burns itself clean. During that heated phase the electrodes must show a small but definite current, and the heater must change the signal in an expected way. Ford's 2023 diesel summary sets P24AF when the current during sensor regeneration at 770 to 800 °C stays below 0.094 µA, judged over 120 s.",["Sensor element aged or glazed, no longer responding","Sensor heater weak so the regeneration temperature is not reached","Element cracked by condensate after cold start"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Often no change in driveability"],2,1,["P24AE","P24B0","P24B1","P24B3","P2002"],"חיישן חלקיקים — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P24B0:["Particulate Matter Sensor Circuit Low","P24B0 flags an electrode signal of the particulate matter sensor that sits too low, typically an open line or a cracked element that no longer conducts as expected. Ford's 2023 diesel summary watches the electrode supply continuously while the sensor measures and sets the code when it drops below 41.55 V for about 1.6 s.",["Sensor element cracked or electrode interrupted","Open electrode line between sensor and sensor control unit","Sensor control unit cannot supply the electrode voltage"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24B1","P24B2","P24AE","P24AF","P24D0"],"חיישן חלקיקים — אות נמוך במעגל"],P24B1:["Particulate Matter Sensor Circuit High","P24B1 reports the electrode side of the particulate matter sensor reading high, which usually points to a short to a voltage source or to a soaked, conductive element. Ford's 2023 diesel summary sets it when electrode current exceeds 41 µA for about 3 s during measurement.",["Condensate on the sensor element making it conductive","Electrode line shorted to a voltage source","Internal sensor fault, replacement sensor needed","Control software needing an update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24B0","P24B2","P24AE","P24AF"],"חיישן חלקיקים — אות גבוה במעגל"],P24B2:["Particulate Matter Sensor Circuit Intermittent","P24B2 stands for a PM sensor electrode reading that cuts out or jumps for short moments rather than staying permanently low or high. Such dropouts usually come from a loose pin, a chafed harness near the hot exhaust or moisture in the connector.",["Loose or corroded pin in the sensor connector","Harness chafing on hot exhaust parts","Engine control software that needs reprogramming","Intermittent internal sensor fault"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, sometimes going out again","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24B0","P24B1","P24AE","P24CA"],"חיישן חלקיקים — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P24B3:["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Control Circuit/Open","P24B3 means the heater inside the particulate matter sensor cannot draw the current it should while it is switched on, typically because the heater line is open. The heater is needed to burn soot off the electrodes. Ford's 2023 diesel summary checks continuously during sensor regeneration and sets the code when heater current stays below 0.2 A for about 2 s.",["Heater element burnt out inside the sensor","Open heater wire or connector","False detection in the control software"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24B4","P24B5","P24B6","P24B7","P24D1"],"גוף חימום חיישן חלקיקים — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P24B4:["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Control Circuit Range/Performance","P24B4 is a plausibility check on the heater of the particulate matter sensor, and makers apply it differently. Ford's 2023 diesel summary looks during measurement, with the heater switched off, and sets the code if heater voltage still exceeds 7 V for 2 s.",["Protection tube of the sensor blocked by soot or deposits","Heater element aged and heating too slowly","Extra resistance in the heater harness","Heater output in the sensor control unit not switching off"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on (not with every manufacturer)","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24B3","P24B5","P24B6","P24B7"],"גוף חימום חיישן חלקיקים — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P24B5:["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low","P24B5 points to the heater line of the particulate matter sensor being pulled toward ground, so the heater control sees an implausible current while heating is requested. GM's 18OBDG04 table describes it as a ground fault on the heater line and flags it when current is under 0.5 A or above 15 A with the heater commanded on, 30 of 60 samples, Type B with two trips.",["Heater line shorted to ground","Internal heater fault in the sensor","False detection by the control software"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24B3","P24B4","P24B6","P24B7"],"גוף חימום חיישן חלקיקים — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P24B6:["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Control Circuit High","P24B6 reports the heater of the particulate matter sensor carrying current although it is commanded off, the classic sign of a battery-side short or a stuck driver stage in the sensor control unit. GM's 18OBDG04 table sets it when more than 0.2 A flows with the heater off or when the switch state disagrees with the command in one of the last five readings, Type B.",["Heater line shorted to battery voltage","Heater output stage in the sensor control unit stuck on","Sensor element damaged by uncontrolled heating"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete","Sensor may fail again quickly if the short is not fixed"],2,1,["P24B3","P24B4","P24B5","P24B7"],"גוף חימום חיישן חלקיקים — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P24B7:["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Resistance","P24B7 concerns the resistance of the heater element in the particulate matter sensor, which drifts as the platinum track ages. Ford's 2023 diesel summary measures it once per drive right after key-on, with the sensor between -30 and 150 °C, and sets the code if resistance leaves 1.06 to 2.93 Ω at the cold end or 1.81 to 4.12 Ω at the warm end.",["Heater track aged, resistance drifted","Corroded connector adding resistance","Wrong sensor temperature distorting the expected value"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Sensor regeneration may stay incomplete"],2,1,["P24B3","P24B4","P24B5","P24B6","P24D1"],"התנגדות גוף חימום חיישן חלקיקים"],P24B8:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit","P24B8 is the general circuit fault of the pressure sensor that sits inside an evaporative leak check module together with the pump and the switching valve. The sensor gets a 5 V reference from the engine computer and reports canister-side pressure during the engine-off leak test. No manufacturer documents P24B8 publicly; GM, Mitsubishi and Subaru use the more specific P24B9 to P24BB for this sensor.",["Open or shorted 5 V reference, ground or signal wire to the leak check module","Corroded or loose connector at the leak check module near the canister","Pressure sensor inside the leak check module failed","Engine control module does not supply the sensor reference"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EVAP readiness monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24B9","P24BA","P24BB","P24BC","P2400","P2403"],"חיישן לחץ משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P24B9:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P24B9 means the leak check module's pressure sensor delivers a signal that is electrically valid but not believable. GM's 2018 Volt table (ELCP) compares the absolute sensor reading with barometric pressure from the MAP sensor while pump and valve rest;",["Pressure sensor in the leak check module drifted or noisy","Engine control software needing an update (FCA bulletins)","Moisture or dirt in the module's pressure port","Chafed wiring or loose pin causing signal disturbance"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EVAP leak test aborted, readiness not set","Usually no noticeable change in driving"],2,1,["P24B8","P24BA","P24BB","P24BC","P2404","P0451"],"חיישן לחץ משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P24BA:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P24BA reports that the voltage from the leak check module's pressure sensor has fallen below the lowest value a working sensor can produce. In GM's ELCP tables (2018 Volt) the limit is 0.70 V, about 14 % of the reference or roughly 47 kPa absolute, with 640 failures in 800 samples taken every 12.5 ms; the check runs whenever the controller is awake and is Type B.",["Sensor signal wire shorted to ground","5 V reference open or pulled down by another sensor on the same supply","Pressure sensor inside the leak check module failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EVAP leak test not run"],2,1,["P24BB","P24B9","P24B8","P24BC","P2404"],"חיישן לחץ משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות נמוך במעגל"],P24BB:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P24BB is stored when the leak check module's pressure signal climbs above the top of its usable range. GM uses 4.85 V, about 97 % of the reference or roughly 120 kPa, again with 640 of 800 samples and Type B; the limit appears unchanged from the 2018 Volt up to GM's 2025 table 25OBDG03A for conventional ELCP systems. Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV flags the code above 4.9 V lasting 2 s.",["Open sensor ground or signal wire, letting the input float high","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Pressure sensor inside the leak check module failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EVAP leak test not run, readiness incomplete"],2,1,["P24BA","P24B9","P24B8","P24BC","P2404"],"חיישן לחץ משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות גבוה במעגל"],P24BC:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent","P24BC is meant for a pressure signal from the leak check module that drops out or jumps briefly, too short to latch the low or high limit. No manufacturer documents P24BC publicly. The closest published logic is Mitsubishi's noise check on the same sensor in the 2023 Outlander PHEV, which counts signal crossings during the engine-off test and fails above 20 events, but Mitsubishi reports that under P24B9.",["Loose or spread terminal in the leak check module connector","Harness chafing near the canister or tank, intermittent short or break","Water or corrosion in the module connector","Sensor in the leak check module failing intermittently"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, sometimes going out again","EVAP readiness monitor completes only occasionally"],2,1,["P24B8","P24B9","P24BA","P24BB","P2407"],"חיישן לחץ משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P24BD:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Switching Valve Control Circuit/Open","P24BD points to the drive circuit of the switching valve inside the leak check module. This small solenoid moves the canister vent path between open air and the reference orifice, so the module can first measure a known leak and then test the real system. The code stands for an open or generally faulty control circuit. No manufacturer documents P24BD publicly;",["Switching valve coil open inside the leak check module","Open control or supply wire, blown fuse or relay fault","Corroded connector at the module","Output driver in the engine control module faulty"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EVAP leak test does not run","On some designs fuel door locked or purge disabled"],2,1,["P24BE","P24BF","P24C0","P24C1","P2418"],"שסתום מיתוג משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P24BE:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Switching Valve Control Circuit Low","P24BE says the voltage on the switching valve control line is too low while the valve should be idle. Mitsubishi documents it for the 2023 Outlander PHEV: the valve sits in the ELCM leak check unit, is supplied by the MFI relay and grounded by a transistor in the engine computer, and the code sets when the line reads 3 V or less for 2 s with the valve not commanded.",["No supply from the relay to the valve (fuse, relay, wire)","Switching valve coil open inside the module","Control wire between module and ECM shorted to ground"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Fuel filler door does not open with the opener switch","Refuelling system service message on the display"],2,1,["P24BD","P24BF","P24C0","P24C1","P2419"],"שסתום מיתוג משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P24BF:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Switching Valve Control Circuit High","P24BF flags too much current in the switching valve circuit while the valve is energised. Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV measures coil current through its low-side driver and sets the code when it reaches 2 A or more for 2 s with the valve commanded on. Such a value suggests a shorted coil or a control wire that touches battery voltage, so the driver is effectively feeding a dead short.",["Switching valve coil shorted inside the module","Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Output driver in the engine control module faulty"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Fuel filler door stays locked","Canister purge switched off"],2,1,["P24BD","P24BE","P24C0","P24C1","P2420"],"שסתום מיתוג משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P24C0:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Switching Valve Stuck On","P24C0 is a mechanical fault found during the leak test itself: the switching valve stays in its energised position, or the pump around it does not do its job. Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV checks this when the parked car wakes its controller 5 h, 6 h or 8.5 h after shutdown. While the reference pressure is being measured, the canister pressure must fall at a set rate;",["Switching valve mechanically stuck inside the leak check module","Leak detection pump stuck on or not running","Open or shorted pump circuit or connector damage","Module pressure sensor frozen at one value"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Fuel filler door does not open","Refuelling system service message"],2,1,["P24C1","P24BE","P24BF","P24BD","P2401","P2402","P043E"],"שסתום מיתוג משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P24C1:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Switching Valve Performance/Stuck Off","P24C1 means the switching valve does not respond when commanded, so the vent path stays where it was. Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV recognises this after the reference measurement of the engine-off leak test: energising the valve should change the canister pressure, and if the difference to the first or second reference value stays below a limit for 10 s, the code is stored.",["Switching valve stuck in rest position inside the module","Open or shorted valve circuit so the valve never moves","Dirt or water from the vent line jamming the valve seat"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Fuel filler door does not open","EVAP readiness not set"],2,1,["P24C0","P24BD","P24BE","P24BF","P2450","P2451"],"שסתום מיתוג משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P24C2:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Measurement System - Multiple Sensor Correlation Bank 1","Diesel exhaust lines often carry three or four temperature probes in a row, ahead of the oxidation catalyst, the particulate filter and the SCR catalyst. P24C2 says that on bank 1 the readings of these probes no longer agree with each other, without pinning the error on one of them.",["One exhaust temperature probe has drifted with age and reads too high or too low","Corroded or heat-damaged connector adding resistance to one probe signal","Engine control software with too tight correlation limits (update available on some models)","Probes swapped between mounting positions after a repair"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter regeneration suppressed or aborted","Often no noticeable change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P24C3","P2080","P2084","P242B","P246F"],""],P24C3:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Measurement System - Multiple Sensor Correlation Bank 2","P24C3 is the bank 2 counterpart of P24C2 and only makes sense on engines whose two cylinder banks feed separate exhaust strings, each with its own set of temperature probes. The controller has found that the probes of the second string disagree among themselves beyond what the operating state allows. No manufacturer documents P24C3 publicly.",["One bank 2 temperature probe has drifted and no longer matches the others","Contact resistance in a bank 2 probe connector or harness","Exhaust leak near one probe cooling its tip"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter regeneration may be inhibited"],2,1,["P24C2","P2082","P2086","P2467","P2474"],""],P24C4:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Exceeded Learning Limit Bank 1","The bypass flap of the EGR cooler learns its end stops, and P24C4 means the learned values for bank 1 have left the window the software accepts. GM's diesel tables from 2017 on run the learning after key-off with coolant between 70 and 129 °C: the raw signal must lie between 16 and 24 % of 5 V in cooling position and between 72 and 85 % in bypass position; outside, the code is stored as Type B.",["Worn bypass valve whose integrated position sensor no longer reaches its learned values","Soot deposits shifting the end stops of the flap","Signal offset from connector corrosion or a weak 5 V reference","Learning repeatedly cut short because the controller is woken right after key-off"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after the second trip","Reduced EGR cooling, higher NOx output","Often no change in driveability"],3,1,["P24C5","P2493","P2494","P2495","P245B"],""],P24C5:["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Exceeded Learning Limit Bank 2","P24C5 belongs to engines with a second EGR cooler and bypass flap on bank 2. It reports that the end positions learned by that flap's position sensor fall outside the accepted window, so the controller can no longer trust where the flap really stands. No manufacturer documents P24C5 publicly; GM's diesel engines in the available tables use one bypass valve and only show the bank 1 code P24C4.",["Worn bank 2 bypass valve or sensor track","Deposits changing the end positions of the bank 2 flap","Signal shift caused by wiring or connector resistance"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Higher NOx emissions due to poorly controlled EGR cooling"],3,1,["P24C4","P2498","P2499","P249A","P248F"],""],P24C6:["Particulate Matter Sensor Temperature Circuit","Inside the particulate matter sensor a meander-shaped platinum track measures element temperature, which the sensor needs to control its heater. P24C6 is the general circuit fault of that temperature signal. Ford's 2023 diesel summary flags a signal below 0.3 V or above 3 V for 2 s; VW's 2014 Touareg list and GM's 14OBDG04 table use the same band (GM Type B).",["Sensor element cracked by condensate","Open or shorted temperature line in the harness","Fault in the sensor control unit"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24C7","P24C8","P24C9","P24CA","P24AE"],"טמפרטורת חיישן חלקיקים — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P24C7:["Particulate Matter Sensor Temperature Circuit Range/Performance","P24C7 checks whether the temperature the particulate matter sensor reports fits the exhaust around it. Ford's 2023 diesel summary does an offset test after a cold soak of at least 6 hours, flagging more than 45 °C against the mean of the exhaust temperature sensors, and a dynamic test while driving that fails below -150 or above 60 °C against a model. VW's 2014 Touareg list uses 60 K and -100 K.",["Sensor element damaged or temperature track drifted","Extra resistance between sensor and sensor control unit","Faulty exhaust temperature sensor used as reference"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24C6","P24C8","P24C9","P24CA"],"טמפרטורת חיישן חלקיקים — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P24C8:["Particulate Matter Sensor Temperature Circuit Low","P24C8 would be set when the temperature signal of the particulate matter sensor sits below its valid range, for example because the meander line is shorted to ground. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; the available summaries fold low and high readings into other codes.",["Temperature line shorted to ground","Water in the sensor connector","Internal fault of the sensor element"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24C6","P24C7","P24C9","P24CA"],"טמפרטורת חיישן חלקיקים — אות נמוך במעגל"],P24C9:["Particulate Matter Sensor Temperature Circuit High","P24C9 reports the PM sensor temperature reading stuck at the high end, which GM explains as a short toward supply voltage or a broken meander line. In GM's 25OBDG04A diesel table the sensor control unit checks the meander signal and its reference: a signal under 0.3 V or over 3.5 V, or a reference under 4.5 V, counts as a failure, and 24 failures in a row or 24 of 96 samples set a Type B code with two trips.",["Broken temperature lead near the sensor body","Temperature line shorted to a voltage source","Reference voltage of the temperature circuit too low"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24C6","P24C7","P24C8","P24CA"],"טמפרטורת חיישן חלקיקים — אות גבוה במעגל"],P24CA:["Particulate Matter Sensor Temperature Circuit Intermittent","P24CA is reserved for a PM sensor temperature reading that fails only now and then instead of staying out of range. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. For comparison, Ford's 2023 diesel summary treats any temperature signal outside 0.3 to 3 V for 2 s as P24C6, and GM's 25OBDG04A table uses a counter of 24 failures within 96 samples for P24C9, so short glitches can stay below those limits.",["Connector loosening when hot","Lead chafing on the exhaust","Cracked joint inside the sensor lead"],["Malfunction indicator lamp coming and going","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24C6","P24C7","P24C8","P24C9"],"טמפרטורת חיישן חלקיקים — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P24CB:["Reductant Tank Cap Switch Circuit","Some SCR diesels have a switch at the DEF filler neck that tells the engine controller when the cap is opened, so a refill can be recognised and the tank level and fluid quality reassessed. P24CB is the general circuit code for this switch: the controller sees a signal that fits neither the open nor the closed state.",["Cap microswitch sticking, especially in hot and humid conditions","Corroded connector or chafed wire at the filler neck","Dried DEF crystals around the switch actuator"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, often right after refilling DEF","Refill not recognised, DEF warnings may persist"],2,1,["P24CC","P24CD","P24CE","P24CF"],"מתג מכסה מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P24CC:["Reductant Tank Cap Switch Circuit Range/Performance","P24CC is a plausibility fault: the cap switch at the DEF filler neck delivers an electrically valid signal, but its behaviour does not match what else the controller knows, for instance a switch that still reports an open cap long after refilling, or one that never changes state while the tank level clearly rose.",["Switch stuck in one position so it no longer follows the cap","DEF residue hindering the switch plunger","Damaged or non-original filler cap that does not actuate the switch"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after a DEF refill","Fill level or refill message not updated"],2,1,["P24CB","P24CD","P24CE","P24CF"],"מתג מכסה מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P24CD:["Reductant Tank Cap Switch Circuit Low","P24CD means the signal line of the DEF cap switch sits below its valid voltage band. With the usual pull-up input that points to the line being pulled to ground: a short in the harness near the filler neck, a switch with an internal short, or moisture bridging the contacts. Whether the controller then reads the cap as permanently open or closed depends on how the switch is wired.",["Signal wire chafed through to ground near the filler neck","Moisture or DEF in the switch or connector bridging to ground","Switch with internal short"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Cap state shown permanently wrong, refills not detected"],2,1,["P24CB","P24CC","P24CE","P24CF"],"מתג מכסה מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל"],P24CE:["Reductant Tank Cap Switch Circuit High","With P24CE the controller sees the DEF cap switch signal above its permitted band. On a pull-up input this typically happens when the line is open, because the input then floats up to the reference, or when it touches a supply wire; a broken switch contact can look the same. Unlike P24CD, a simple unplugged connector after tank work is a frequent trigger here. No manufacturer documents P24CE publicly.",["Disconnected plug or broken wire letting the input float high","Signal wire touching a supply line","Broken contact inside the switch"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Refill of DEF not registered"],2,1,["P24CB","P24CC","P24CD","P24CF"],"מתג מכסה מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל"],P24CF:["Reductant Tank Cap Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P24CF is stored when the DEF cap switch signal jumps between states or drops out briefly although nobody touches the cap, typically while driving over rough roads. The controller counts unexpected changes and flags the circuit as unstable even if every single value lies within limits. Loose terminals, a cracked solder joint in the switch or a harness rubbing on the tank are the usual reasons.",["Loose or corroded terminal in the switch connector","Switch that sticks only partly and chatters","Harness rubbing on the tank or body"],["Malfunction indicator lamp, sometimes coming and going","Spurious refill or cap-open messages"],2,1,["P24CB","P24CC","P24CD","P24CE"],"מתג מכסה מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P24D0:["Particulate Matter Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P24D0 concerns the power feed of the particulate matter sensor and its control unit, which sinks when the supply line has excess resistance or a short toward ground. Ford's 2023 diesel summary compares battery voltage with the voltage at the sensor while the heater runs at 35 % duty or more, and sets the code if the drop exceeds 1.1 V, 2.1 V or 3 V depending on battery level, within 2 s.",["Corroded fuse, relay contact or ground adding resistance","Supply line shorted to ground","Weak battery or charging system","Fault in the sensor control unit"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete","Further particulate sensor codes stored at the same time"],2,1,["P24B0","P24B3","P24AE","P0562","U02A3"],"חיישן חלקיקים — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P24D1:["Particulate Matter Sensor Regeneration Incomplete","Before each measurement the particulate matter sensor heats its element to burn off collected soot. P24D1 means that this cleaning phase did not finish properly. Ford's 2023 diesel summary flags the code when the sensor cannot return to measuring after regeneration, judged over 120 s.",["Sensor heater degraded, not reaching cleaning temperature","Heavy deposits on the sensor element","Control software needing an update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24B7","P24B3","P24AF","P24AE"],""],P24D2:["Reductant Heater A Sense Circuit","Besides the control output, many DEF heaters have a sense line on which the controller reads back the voltage actually reaching the element. P24D2 marks a general fault on this sense circuit for heater A, such as an open lead or a reading that makes no sense at all, as opposed to the voltage being merely too low (P248A) or too high (P248B). GM and Ford call heater A the tank heater.",["Broken or disconnected sense wire to heater A","DEF creep or water corroding the heater connector","Faulty measuring input in the SCR or engine control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF warnings in cold weather, dosing delayed after a cold start"],2,1,["P24D3","P248A","P248B","P20B9"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P24D3:["Reductant Heater B Sense Circuit","P24D3 is the same kind of fault for heater B, which GM and Ford assign to the heated DEF line from pump to dosing valve. The read-back line of this heater is broken or delivers nonsense, so the controller cannot tell whether the hose is really powered; the narrower low and high cases are P248C and P248D. No manufacturer documents P24D3 in this sense.",["Open sense wire or loose plug at the heated DEF line","Damaged heated line with internal conductor fault","Manufacturer-specific use of the code (FCA uses it for PM sensor supply), software update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF dosing faults or warnings at low temperatures"],2,1,["P24D2","P248C","P248D","P20BD"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P24D4:["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Feedback Circuit","Where an electric auxiliary pump moves coolant through the EGR cooler, the pump usually reports back to the engine controller on a separate wire, for example with a speed or status signal. P24D4 is the general fault of that feedback circuit: the signal is missing or cannot be interpreted, while the narrower cases of a line stuck below or above its band are P24AC and P24AD. The drive side may be fine;",["Open feedback wire or loose connector at the pump","Failed pump electronics no longer sending a status signal","Blown fuse or failed relay leaving the pump without power"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EGR reduced, possibly higher NOx and changed engine noise","Coolant temperature warnings if the pump really stops"],2,3,["P24AC","P24AD","P24A7","P24A8"],"משוב משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן EGR — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P24D5:["EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch B Circuit","P24D5 is the general circuit code for a second EVAP pressure sensor, called B to tell it apart from the main sensor A (P0450 range). Which sensor is B depends on the maker: Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV uses it for an absolute fuel tank pressure sensor on its sealed tank, GM for a canister vapour pressure sensor, and Audi's bulletin 2069531 assigns sensor 2 to the G950 part in the purge path.",["Open or shorted reference, ground or signal wire of sensor B","Loose or corroded connector at sensor B","EVAP pressure sensor B failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EVAP readiness monitor incomplete"],2,1,["P24D6","P24D7","P24D8","P24D9","P0450"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P24D6:["EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch B Circuit Range/Performance","P24D6 is a plausibility fault of EVAP pressure sensor B. GM's 2023 table 23OBDG03A checks the canister vapour pressure sensor at the start of a cold drive: after more than 3,600 s soak the offset must sit within a window around barometric pressure; a filtered ratio above 0.73 sets the code, Type A.",["Wrong sensor version installed (GM HD trucks, narrow-range instead of wide-range)","Sensor offset drifted away from barometric pressure","Kinked hose or blocked port at the sensor","Engine control software needing an update (FCA, Audi)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Other EVAP codes such as a switching valve fault may appear alongside","No driveability change"],2,1,["P24D5","P24D7","P24D8","P24D9","P0451","P2B7B"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P24D7:["EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch B Circuit Low","P24D7 is set when EVAP pressure sensor B sends a voltage below its valid window. GM's 2023 table (23OBDG03A) watches its canister pressure sensor continuously and fails below 0.15 V, 3 % of the reference, with 640 of 800 samples, Type B; the sensor normally works between 0.5 and 4.5 V. Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV uses a far higher floor for its absolute tank pressure sensor: under 1.0 V for 2 s.",["Signal wire of sensor B shorted to ground","5 V reference open or shorted","EVAP pressure sensor B failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EVAP tests suspended"],2,1,["P24D8","P24D6","P24D5","P24D9","P0452"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P24D8:["EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch B Circuit High","P24D8 reports EVAP pressure sensor B reading above its valid voltage. In GM's 2023 table 23OBDG03A the canister pressure sensor fails above 4.85 V, 97 % of the reference, counted over 640 of 800 samples and treated as Type B. Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV applies 4.1 V for 2 s to its absolute tank pressure sensor, which shows about 101 kPa at sea level when healthy.",["Open ground of sensor B, signal floats high","Signal wire shorted to reference or battery voltage","EVAP pressure sensor B failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","EVAP readiness monitor incomplete"],2,1,["P24D7","P24D6","P24D5","P24D9","P0453"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P24D9:["EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch B Circuit Intermittent","P24D9 covers a sensor B signal that keeps flickering instead of failing outright. Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV runs this check once per drive cycle inside the parked leak test, when the controller wakes at its scheduled times and coolant and intake air lie between 4 and 35 °C. It counts how often the tank pressure signal crosses the sensor's own filter value and stores the code after more than 20 crossings;",["Loose terminal or poor contact at the tank pressure sensor","Harness chafed along the fuel tank","Tank pressure or tank differential pressure sensor unstable"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Refuelling system service message on the display"],2,1,["P24D5","P24D6","P24D7","P24D8","P0454"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ B — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P24DA:["Particulate Matter Sensor Exhaust Sample Error Bank 1","P24DA checks that the particulate matter sensor actually samples exhaust gas, which is how the system detects a sensor that has been pulled out, sits in a blocked protection tube or is mounted wrongly. Ford's 2023 diesel summary runs it once per drive in protective heating mode and fails it if the summed sensor voltage change during exhaust flow changes stays under 0.5 V, over about 3 minutes.",["Protection tube clogged","Sensor removed from the exhaust or installed wrongly","Sensor no longer responding to exhaust flow"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P24AE","P24AF","P24B4","P2002"],""],P24DB:["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Circuit/Open","After shut-down an SCR system empties its lines back into the tank so no fluid freezes in them; in Bosch's Denoxtronic 2.2 a 4/2-way valve in the supply module reverses the flow for this. Valve B is a second purge valve, for instance in layouts with two dosing branches. P24DB reports a drive circuit fault of valve B, mostly an interruption. No manufacturer documents P24DB publicly.",["Broken wire or unplugged connector to purge valve B","Open solenoid winding in valve B","DEF-induced corrosion in the supply module connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF line not purged after shut-off, freezing risk in winter"],2,1,["P24DC","P24DD","P24DE","P20A0"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P24DC:["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Performance","P24DC judges purge valve B by its effect, not by its wiring: once the controller switches the valve to purge, the pressure in the DEF line it serves should fall noticeably, and here it did not. No manufacturer documents P24DC publicly.",["Valve B mechanically stuck by crystallised DEF","Blocked return path or filter in the supply module","DEF pressure sensor reading incorrectly"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Frozen DEF line or dosing fault after cold nights"],2,1,["P24DB","P24DF","P24E0","P20A1"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P24DD:["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Circuit Low","P24DD means the control line of purge valve B shows too little voltage at a moment when it should be high. With the low-side switching that GM uses for valve A, this is checked while the driver is off: the line should then carry battery voltage through the coil, and a low reading indicates a short to ground between valve and controller, so the valve may sit energised permanently.",["Control wire chafed to ground near tank or frame","Valve coil shorted to its housing","Water or DEF in the connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Valve may remain in purge position, dosing pressure not reached"],2,1,["P24DB","P24DE","P20A2"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P24DE:["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Circuit High","With P24DE the control line of purge valve B stays at high voltage while the controller is actually pulling it to ground to switch the valve. That points to a short to the battery feed on the wire between valve and controller, or a valve coil with too little resistance, so that the driver protects itself and the valve never shifts. No manufacturer documents P24DE publicly.",["Control wire touching a supply line","Valve coil with shorted turns and too low resistance","Damaged driver stage in the control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF line not purged, frozen line after frost"],2,1,["P24DB","P24DD","P20A3"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P24DF:["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Stuck Open","Stuck open means purge valve B remains in, or leaks toward, its emptying position while the system should be dosing. Part of the pump flow then goes back to the tank, so working pressure builds slowly, drops quickly when the pump stops, or needs a high pump duty to hold. No manufacturer documents P24DF publicly, and the public GM tables cover only the opposite failure of valve A (no pressure drop in purge, P20A1).",["Internal leak or worn seat in purge valve B","DEF crystals preventing the valve from returning to dosing position","Control circuit fault keeping the valve energised"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF pressure too low, reduced dosing and rising NOx","Warnings about reduced SCR function, possibly later engine power limits"],3,3,["P24E0","P24DC","P20A4"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P24E0:["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Stuck Closed","Stuck closed means purge valve B does not move into its emptying position when commanded after shut-down, so the line it serves stays filled with fluid under residual pressure. In normal dosing this goes unnoticed; the risk appears in frost, when the trapped DEF freezes in hose, pump or injector and can crack them. No manufacturer documents P24E0 publicly.",["Valve B seized by crystallised DEF or corrosion","Weak coil that no longer pulls the valve over","Intermittent open in the control circuit during shut-down"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Frozen or burst DEF line or injector after frost"],3,1,["P24DF","P24DC","P20A5"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — תקוע במצב סגור"],P24E1:["NH3 Sensor Circuit","An NH3 sensor behind the SCR catalyst measures ammonia that slipped through unused, letting the controller trim dosing and detect overdosing or an aged catalyst. P24E1 is the general circuit code for this sensor: its signal is missing, implausible or erratic. Deutz lists P24E1 for its MD1 engine controller with SPN 4377 and FMI 2, i.e. unstable or wrong data.",["NH3 sensor element or its electronics failed from heat and age","Heat-damaged wiring or connector near the exhaust","Software calibration issue, update available on some engines"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Less precise DEF dosing, possible ammonia smell or higher NOx"],2,1,["P24E2","P24E3","P24E4","P24E5","U02A4"],"חיישן אמוניה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P24E2:["NH3 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P24E2 flags an NH3 sensor whose signal is electrically valid but makes no sense: the ammonia value sticks, drifts or contradicts what the dosing model expects from the SCR catalyst. On heavy trucks the sensor is a smart unit with its own electronics that test probe and circuitry and report over J1939.",["Sensing element aged or poisoned by deposits, giving a drifting ammonia value","Urea crystals around the sensor tip after overdosing","Exhaust leak near the sensor diluting the sample"],["Check engine light after two trips","DEF consumption noticeably higher or lower than usual","Possible ammonia smell at the tailpipe"],2,1,["P24E1","P24E3","P24E4","P24E5"],"חיישן אמוניה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P24E3:["NH3 Sensor Circuit Low","P24E3 means the NH3 sensor signal lies below the lowest value an intact sensor can deliver. Usual culprits are a short to ground between probe and its electronics module, a terminal pushed back in the connector or a defect inside the probe. On International trucks with the 2013 N13 engine, a matching condition is reported as SPN 5848 with failure mode 4, i.e.",["Chafed harness between probe and sensor module shorting to ground","Internal fault in the ammonia probe","Corroded or pushed-back terminal at the probe connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Scan tool shows ammonia reading stuck at minimum"],2,1,["P24E1","P24E2","P24E4","P24EB"],"חיישן אמוניה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P24E4:["NH3 Sensor Circuit High","P24E4 is set when the NH3 sensor signal climbs above anything a working sensor could report, so the value is rejected as electrically impossible rather than merely implausible. Typical reasons are a short to a supply voltage, a broken line pulled up internally, or failing electronics that output a saturated value.",["Signal line shorted to a supply voltage in the harness","Open line between probe and module read as maximum value","Sensor electronics module outputting a saturated value"],["Check engine light on","Ammonia reading pinned at the upper limit","Possible reduced DEF dosing"],2,1,["P24E1","P24E2","P24E3","P24EC"],"חיישן אמוניה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P24E5:["NH3 Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P24E5 covers an NH3 sensor signal that jumps or drops out for short moments while staying mostly in range. Vibration, heat cycling of the exhaust and road salt make loose connector pins and cracked insulation near the SCR can the main suspects. Ram fitted such a sensor to the 2014 3500 to 5500 cab chassis with the 6.7 L Cummins;",["Loose or corroded pins at the sensor or module connector","Harness insulation cracked by exhaust heat and vibration","Sporadic internal fault in the sensor electronics"],["Warning lamp that comes and goes","Live data shows spikes in the ammonia value"],2,1,["P24E1","P24E2","P24E3","P24E4"],"חיישן אמוניה — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P24E6:["NH3 Sensor Heater Circuit/Open","Like a NOx sensor, the ammonia sensor only measures once its ceramic element is hot, so it carries an electric heater. P24E6 reports that this heater circuit is open or otherwise electrically faulty: the driver commands heating but sees no current flowing. Common reasons are a burnt heater element, a broken wire in the pigtail or a terminal that lost contact.",["Heater element inside the NH3 probe burnt through","Broken wire in the sensor pigtail near the hot exhaust","Heater terminal without contact in the connector"],["Check engine light on","No ammonia reading after warm-up"],2,1,["P24E7","P24E8","P24E9"],"גוף חימום חיישן אמוניה — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P24E7:["NH3 Sensor Heater Circuit Low","P24E7 points to a heater circuit of the NH3 sensor that reads too low: the feedback voltage stays near ground, or the current is far below what the heater should draw. Most often the heater feed is shorted to ground, which can also blow the fuse or switch off the driver to protect it; a heater whose resistance has risen sharply gives a similar picture.",["Heater supply line shorted to ground","Heater element with strongly increased resistance","Blown fuse in the heater supply"],["Check engine light on","Ammonia value missing or delayed after start"],2,1,["P24E6","P24E8","P24E9"],"גוף חימום חיישן אמוניה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P24E8:["NH3 Sensor Heater Circuit High","With P24E8 the heater circuit of the NH3 sensor reads too high. Either the line is shorted to a supply voltage so that the heater cannot be switched off, or the driver measures overcurrent because the element has failed with low resistance. A heater stuck on can overheat and crack the ceramic, so the controller normally shuts it down and stops evaluating ammonia until the fault clears.",["Heater control line shorted to battery voltage","Heater element failed with low resistance, causing overcurrent","Heater driver in the sensor module defective"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Ammonia sensor reading switched off"],2,1,["P24E6","P24E7","P24E9"],"גוף חימום חיישן אמוניה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P24E9:["NH3 Sensor Heater Circuit Performance","P24E9 is not about a broken wire but about how the heater works: the circuit is intact, yet the NH3 probe does not reach or hold its operating temperature in the expected time, or its temperature control swings. Deutz lists P24E9 for its MD1 engine controller as SPN 4382 with FMI 2, meaning erratic or incorrect heater data.",["Aged heater element no longer delivering full power","Condensate on the ceramic cooling it or causing thermal shock","Low supply voltage limiting heater power"],["Check engine light, often together with an NH3 sensor performance code","Ammonia reading available late or unstable"],2,1,["P24E6","P24E7","P24E8","P24E2"],"גוף חימום חיישן אמוניה — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P24EA:["NH3 Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit","The NH3 sensor is a smart unit: its electronics module needs its own power feed, usually switched battery voltage through a fuse or relay, to run the probe, the heater and the J1939 link. P24EA is the general fault of that supply, set when the measured feed voltage is missing, unstable or otherwise outside the valid window without being classed as clearly low or high.",["Fuse or relay in the sensor feed faulty or loose","Damaged or corroded power or ground wire to the sensor module","Supply monitoring in the sensor module defective"],["Check engine light on","Further NH3 sensor or communication codes stored"],2,1,["P24EB","P24EC","P24E1"],"חיישן אמוניה — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P24EB:["NH3 Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P24EB reports that the power feed of the NH3 sensor module sags below its lower limit. Below that point the heater cannot bring the probe up to temperature and the electronics may reset, so ammonia readings and sensor messages become unreliable.",["Weak or discharged batteries pulling system voltage down","High resistance in the ground path of the sensor module","Corroded fuse or relay contacts causing voltage drop"],["Warning lamp, often after cold starts","NH3 sensor drops off the data link at times"],1,1,["P24EA","P24EC","P24E3"],"חיישן אמוניה — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P24EC:["NH3 Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit High","P24EC is stored when the feed voltage measured at the NH3 sensor module exceeds its upper limit. Overvoltage can damage the heater driver and the electronics, so the module may switch off heating and measurement to protect itself. Likely triggers are a charging system that regulates too high, jump-starting with a higher-voltage source, or a short from a higher feed onto the sensor supply line.",["Alternator regulator charging too high","Overvoltage from jump-starting or a booster charger","Sensor supply line shorted to another higher feed"],["Check engine light on","Other modules may also report high system voltage"],2,1,["P24EA","P24EB","P24E4"],"חיישן אמוניה — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P24ED:["NH3 Sensor Calibration Memory","Every NH3 sensor leaves the factory with individual correction values for offset and gain stored in its own electronics. P24ED means this memory fails its integrity check, for instance a checksum mismatch or unreadable data, so the module cannot convert the raw probe signal into a trustworthy ammonia value. The fix is normally a new sensor; wiring rarely plays a part.",["Calibration data in the sensor module corrupted","Power loss while the module was writing data"],["Check engine light on","No valid ammonia value although wiring tests pass"],2,1,["P24EE","P24E1"],"זיכרון כיול חיישן אמוניה"],P24EE:["NH3 Sensor Processor Performance","P24EE says the microcontroller inside the NH3 sensor module has failed its own self-test, for example a watchdog reset, a RAM or ROM error or a timing fault. The engine controller only learns this through the status the sensor sends, because the processor is what runs the probe, the heater and the J1939 messages.",["Electronics of the NH3 sensor module failed","Unstable supply voltage causing processor resets","Module damaged by heat or water ingress"],["Check engine light on","NH3 sensor data missing or frozen"],2,1,["P24ED","P24E1"],"מעבד חיישן אמוניה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P24EF:["Control Module Wake-up Circuit/Open","Some control modules drive a discrete wake-up output that switches other units on before or alongside the network. P24EF reports an open circuit on that line. GM uses it in the HPC2 battery-side processor of its 2016 and 2019 hybrid tables: with the output commanded off, a control voltage between 2.82 and 7.04 V counts as open, because an intact line would be pulled clearly low.",["Broken wake-up wire in the harness","Pin pushed back or corroded in a module connector","Wake-up output of the control module defective"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Connected module stays asleep, with related communication codes"],3,3,["P24F0","P24F1"],""],P24F0:["Control Module Wake-up Circuit Low","P24F0 means that a control module drives its wake-up output on, but the line voltage stays down, pointing to a ground short or a load drawing far too much current. In GM's 2016 and 2019 hybrid tables the HPC2 module runs this check whenever the output is commanded on and reports a fault if the control voltage is at or below 5.52 V.",["Wake-up line shorted to ground at a chafe point","Moisture in a connector bridging the line to ground","Receiving module loading the wake-up input too heavily"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Hybrid or charging functions unavailable"],3,3,["P24EF","P24F1"],""],P24F1:["Control Module Wake-up Circuit High","With P24F1 the wake-up line carries voltage while its driving module has the output switched off, so a short to a battery feed or a second source keeps it live. GM's HPC2 module in the 2016 and 2019 hybrid tables flags 13.21 V or more in the off state, using the same 480-of-560 sample count at 12.5 ms and Type A, MIL after one trip.",["Wake-up line shorted to a battery feed","Signal timing between ignition module and receiving unit, solved by coding","Voltage fed back from another module that stays awake"],["Check engine light and several warning messages","Temporary no-start condition","Possible battery drain while parked"],3,3,["P24EF","P24F0"],""],P24F2:["EGR Temperature/Charge Air Cooler Temperature Correlation","P24F2 compares two readings in the intake path of a diesel with cooled exhaust gas recirculation: the gas temperature after the EGR cooler and the air temperature behind the charge air cooler. When conditions say both should be close, for instance after the engine has cooled down, a wide gap shows that one of the two sensors cannot be trusted.",["Outdated PCM calibration flagging the correlation without a real fault (Chrysler 3.0 L diesel)","EGR temperature sensor drifting or sooted up","Charge air cooler outlet temperature sensor reading wrong","Corroded connector adding resistance to one sensor signal"],["Check engine light, often without any noticeable driving fault","EGR operation reduced as a precaution on some calibrations","Implausible EGR or charge air temperatures in live data after a cold soak"],2,1,["P040B","P040C","P0097","P0098","P24C2"],""],P24F3:["Reductant Tank Temperature/Fuel Temperature Correlation","P24F3 sets the temperature reported from the DEF (reductant) tank against the fuel temperature. After a long soak both liquids rest close to ambient, so a clear mismatch exposes a sensor that reads wrong although each signal may be electrically valid. No manufacturer explains P24F3 in a public service document.",["DEF tank temperature sensor (often integrated in the tank or sender module) reading wrong","Fuel temperature sensor drifting","Local heat source such as an exhaust leak warming one sensor","Contact resistance in a sensor connector"],["Warning lamp, often after a cold start","DEF tank and fuel temperature far apart in live data after an overnight stop"],2,1,["P205B","P205A","P0181","P0182","P0183"],""],P24F4:["NOx Sensor Delayed Response - High to Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P24F4 concerns the dead time of the upstream NOx sensor on bank 1 when engine-out NOx falls, typically on lift-off into overrun: the reading stays put too long before it starts dropping, even if the later descent is normal. CARB defines this split for exhaust sensors, delayed response being the wait before the first reaction and slow response a sluggish transition. No manufacturer documents P24F4 publicly.",["Soot or oil ash on the diffusion barrier of the front sensor","Aged measuring cells reacting late to falling NOx","Exhaust leak ahead of the sensor distorting the transient"],["Check engine light on","Front NOx value lingers on lift-off","Engine runs normally"],2,1,["P24F5","P22FA","P22F9","P23C2"],""],P24F5:["NOx Sensor Delayed Response - High to Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P24F5 is the same delay check for NOx sensor 2 on bank 1, which sits behind the SCR catalyst and judges its conversion. If its value lags when NOx at the outlet falls, the efficiency estimate is distorted and the SCR monitor could pass or fail wrongly, so the sensor must react in time. A late reaction means the first visible change comes too long after the expected drop. No manufacturer publishes P24F5.",["DEF crystals or ammonia slip attacking the rear sensor element","Aged measuring cells of sensor 2 reacting late","Condensate in the cold tailpipe area affecting the sensor"],["Check engine light on","Possibly an SCR efficiency code alongside"],2,1,["P24F4","P22FD","P22FC","P23C2"],""],P24F6:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Stuck Open","Heavy Volvo and Mack trucks regenerate the particulate filter with an aftertreatment hydrocarbon injector (AHI, the 7th injector) that sprays diesel ahead of the oxidation catalyst; compressed air from the truck supply then blows the line to the nozzle clear. P24F6 means the fuel/air purge valve in the AHI module seems to stay open, so air keeps flowing when it should not.",["Oil or water in the purge air from an unsuitable or worn air-dryer cartridge","Debris holding the purge valve in the AHI module open","Damaged AHI nozzle or leaking fuel/air line toward the nozzle","Doser air supply pressure outside the 221 kPa specification"],["Particulate filter regeneration does not complete","Warning lamp and aftertreatment message on the dash","Rising soot load and more frequent regeneration requests"],3,3,["P24F7","P24F8","P20CF","P20DC","P20DE"],"שסתום טיהור אוויר דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P24F7:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Stuck Closed","P24F7 is the reverse case of P24F6: the purge valve of the aftertreatment fuel/air system will not open when commanded, so no compressed air reaches the dosing line and the 7th injector after a dosing phase. In Volvo and Mack trucks this valve sits in the AHI dosing block, mounted on the fuel filter housing from model year 2017 and on the engine block side before.",["Purge valve jammed by oil, water or particles from the air system","Air supply to the AHI module restricted or below specification","Coked or kinked line between AHI module and nozzle","Internal fault of the AHI dosing module"],["Active regeneration aborted or not started","Warning lamp with aftertreatment message","Possible engine derate as soot load climbs"],3,3,["P24F6","P24F8","P20D0","P20DC","P20DE"],"שסתום טיהור אוויר דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — תקוע במצב סגור"],P24F8:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Control Circuit","P24F8 is the electrical fault of the fuel/air purge valve: the control unit finds the solenoid drive circuit not working, typically an open wire or a coil that draws no current. Volvo and Mack report it as P24F813, the suffix 13 meaning open circuit.",["Broken wire or chafed harness between engine controller and AHI module","Corroded or loose plug at the AHI dosing module","Interrupted coil of the purge valve solenoid"],["Warning lamp right after the circuit test runs","Active regeneration blocked or incomplete"],2,3,["P24F9","P24FA","P24FB","P24F6","P2697"],"שסתום טיהור אוויר דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],P24F9:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Control Circuit Range/Performance","P24F9 covers a purge valve control circuit that is electrically present but behaves implausibly, for example when measured current or a feedback signal does not follow the commanded state within the expected time. Unlike P24F8, P24FA and P24FB, this variant appears in none of the Volvo/Mack AHI documents, and no manufacturer documents P24F9 publicly.",["Purge valve moving slowly because of deposits","Solenoid coil resistance drifting with heat or age","High-resistance contact in the module plug"],["Warning lamp, sometimes only under heat","Irregular or aborted filter regenerations"],2,1,["P24F8","P24FA","P24FB","P24F7"],"שסתום טיהור אוויר דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P24FA:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Control Circuit Low","P24FA reports that voltage on the purge valve control line is lower than the driver stage expects in the current switching state: a short to ground on the wire, a coil with too little resistance or a weak supply. Volvo and Mack name P24FA00 in the electrical section of their AHI troubleshooting guide for US10+OBD13 and newer engines;",["Control wire chafed through to chassis ground","Purge valve coil with shorted turns","Moisture in the AHI module connector"],["Warning lamp shortly after key-on or during dosing","Regeneration not possible"],2,3,["P24F8","P24F9","P24FB"],"שסתום טיהור אוויר דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P24FB:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Control Circuit High","With P24FB the purge valve control line sits higher than allowed, a pattern that points to a short to battery voltage or to a broken low-side path, so the controller cannot pull the line down. In the Volvo/Mack AHI guide P24FB00 is listed right beside P24FA00 among the electrical codes, and the first check is the harness and the plug at the dosing module.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage feed in the harness","Interrupted return path between valve and controller","Controller output stage protecting itself against overcurrent"],["Warning lamp and aftertreatment message","Filter regeneration unavailable"],2,3,["P24F8","P24F9","P24FA"],"שסתום טיהור אוויר דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P24FC:["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P24FC concerns the output stage that powers the heater of the particulate matter sensor: the driver reports excessive current or an internal temperature past its limit, which suggests a heater with shorted turns or too little resistance, or an overheating sensor electronics unit. On heavy trucks this sensor works as a self-diagnosing device after the SCR catalyst and reports over J1939.",["Internal failure of the smart PM sensor (heater or electronics)","Water ingress cracking the ceramic element or shorting the heater","Unusually high exhaust temperature at the sensor, e.g. during repeated regenerations"],["Warning lamp","No soot reading from the PM sensor, DPF monitoring not completed"],2,1,["P24B3","P24B5","P24B6","P24B7","P24D1"],"גוף חימום חיישן חלקיקים — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה"],P24FD:["Particulate Filter A Incorrect","P24FD is intended to flag that the particulate filter in position A is not the expected part or is absent, for example after a filter delete or when an unsuitable replacement has been fitted. No manufacturer documents P24FD publicly. CARB's rules for light and heavy-duty diesels require the OBD system to notice a substrate that is destroyed, removed or swapped for a silencer or plain pipe.",["Particulate filter removed or replaced by a straight pipe","Non-approved or wrong-specification filter fitted","Leaking or blocked pressure lines making a present filter look absent"],["Check engine light","Visible soot at the tailpipe if the filter is missing","Emissions inspection failed"],3,1,["P244A","P226D","P2002","P24FE"],""],P24FE:["SCR Catalyst Incorrect","P24FE means the controller concludes that the SCR catalyst is missing or not the expected part. Ford runs this test on the 6.7 L diesel (2023 summary) for about 60 s with SCR inlet at 195–340 °C and feedgas NOx of 70–500 ppm, and sets the code when cumulative SCR efficiency falls below 0 %.",["Upstream or downstream NOx sensor misreading (Ford sensor 11, Hino NOx sensors)","SCR catalyst removed or replaced by a non-matching part","Controller software detecting removal falsely, fixed by reprogramming","Diluted DEF or faulty DEF injector collapsing NOx conversion"],["Warning or service lamp (Hino sets the service lamp, MIL stays off)","Reduced engine power","NOx downstream of the SCR as high as upstream in live data"],3,3,["P20EE","P24FD","P2201","P2209","P220E"],""],P24FF:["Reductant Temperature Too High","P24FF signals that the diesel exhaust fluid itself has become too hot while the engine runs. The controller reads the DEF temperature sensor in the tank and flags a value above its limit during operation; hot urea solution ages faster and can form deposits.",["DEF tank coolant solenoid valve installed against its flow direction (Volvo)","Tank heating valve stuck open so hot coolant keeps flowing","Missing heat shield or exhaust leak warming the tank or lines","DEF temperature sensor reading too high"],["Warning lamp with SCR or DEF message","DEF tank temperature far above ambient in live data"],2,1,["P205A","P205B","P205C","P205D","P20B9"],"טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue) — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2500:["Generator Lamp/L-Terminal Circuit Low","P2500 points to the L line, the turn-on wire between engine module and alternator regulator that on many older layouts also runs through the charge warning lamp. The module reads back the voltage on this wire; when it stays below the expected level, for instance because the line is chafed to ground or the regulator holds it down, this code is logged.",["L wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Alternator regulator faulty and pulling the L terminal low","Corroded or loose plug at the alternator","Output stage for the L line in the engine module defective"],["Battery or charge warning lamp on","Battery voltage falls while driving","Hard or no start after some time"],2,0,["P2501","P0621","P0620"],""],P2501:["Generator Lamp/L-Terminal Circuit High","With P2501 the engine module sees too much voltage on the L line to the alternator regulator. The wire is then either touching a battery-fed conductor, or the module cannot pull it down because the regulator side or the lamp path is open, so the line floats up to supply level.",["L wire shorted to a battery-fed wire in the harness","Break in the L circuit or plug off at the alternator","Regulator electronics faulty"],["Charge lamp does not light during the bulb check or stays on","Charging voltage unusually high or not controlled","Battery drains if charging stops"],2,0,["P2500","P0621","P0620"],""],P2502:["Charging System Voltage","P2502 is the general charging-system code: the engine module compares the voltage the generator actually delivers with what it has requested and finds a mismatch that it does not classify as simply too low or too high. Mazda uses it as a malfunction in the voltage produced by the generator. On 2022–2023 Mazda2 mild hybrids built in Mexico the charge lamp came on while driving;",["Alternator or regulator not reaching the requested voltage","High resistance at ground or B+ connections (Mazda mild hybrid DC-DC converter)","Slipping drive belt or worn tensioner","Battery with internal fault distorting the charging voltage"],["Charge warning lamp on while driving","Fluctuating battery voltage, flickering lights","Battery not fully charged"],2,0,["P2503","P2504","P0620","P0562"],"מתח מערכת טעינה"],P2503:["Charging System Voltage Low","P2503 means the charging output is below target: with the engine running the module expects the generator to lift system voltage, but it stays too low. FCA calls the code Charging System Output Low.",["Loose or burnt B+ connection between alternator and fuse box","Worn alternator (brushes, diodes, regulator)","Failed overrunning pulley or slipping belt","Poor engine or chassis ground"],["Battery lamp and check engine lamp on","Dim lights, electrical consumers dropping out","Engine stalls or will not start"],2,1,["P2502","P2504","P0562","P0620"],"מערכת טעינה — מתח נמוך"],P2504:["Charging System Voltage High","P2504 is logged when the charging output overshoots: the measured voltage rises above what the module asked the generator to produce. FCA names it Charging System Output High and publishes several cases. A 2021 Ram 1500 lit the check engine lamp after a repair, with P2504 set and P2503 stored, and the advice was to voltage-drop every circuit involved.",["High resistance at B+ fuse array or ground straps distorting the reading","Regulator stuck and overcharging","Battery current or voltage sensor delivering wrong values"],["Check engine lamp, sometimes battery lamp","Very bright lights, bulbs failing early","No crank in connection-related cases"],2,1,["P2502","P2503","P0563"],"מערכת טעינה — מתח גבוה"],P2505:["ECM/PCM Power Input Signal","P2505 covers the supply inputs of the engine module in general. GM documents it in the 2014 diesel engine table 14OBDG04: the module checks its permanent battery feed, the line that keeps the engine-off timer alive while the ignition is off. If that constant supply was interrupted, the module flags P2505 as soon as the ignition is on;",["Battery disconnected or permanent-feed fuse removed or blown","Open or corroded permanent supply wire or connector","Supply monitoring inside the module defective"],["MIL after two trips (GM)","Often no drivability complaint","Learned values may be lost"],2,1,["P2506","P2507","P2508","P2509","P0560"],"אות כניסת כוח מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM)"],P2506:["ECM/PCM Power Input Signal Range/Performance","P2506 is the plausibility variant: the supply reaching the engine module is electrically present but its value or behaviour does not fit the operating state. No passenger-car maker publishes how it detects this.",["Resistance in supply fuse, relay contact or connector","Excessive current drawn through the module supply (Deutz)","Internal supply monitoring of the module faulty"],["Check engine lamp (Ford lists it as MIL code)","Sporadic stalling or restarts of the module possible"],2,3,["P2505","P2507","P2508","P2509"],"אות כניסת כוח מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2507:["ECM/PCM Power Input Signal Low","P2507 reports that a supply input of the engine module sits too low. Makers read this differently. Mazda calls it a low PCM battery voltage input: on 2013–2020 models from CX-5 to MX-5 it appears together with P2610 when the engine was started three or more times after stops shorter than 15 s while the 15 A room fuse was pulled for transport;",["Supply fuse missing, pulled for transport or not fully seated","Weak battery or voltage dips during repeated starts","Corroded supply wire, ground or relay contact","Internal 5 V supply of the module failing (Ford diesel)"],["Often no symptom, code found during service (Mazda)","Several warning lamps, blank displays","No-start in severe cases"],2,3,["P2505","P2508","P0562","P2610"],"כניסת כוח מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM) — אות נמוך"],P2508:["ECM/PCM Power Input Signal High","P2508 is set when a supply input of the engine module reads above its permitted range. Ford documents it for the 2023 6.7 L Power Stroke diesel: the module checks its internal 5 V supply rail and flags P2508 once that rail exceeds 5.5 V, with continuous monitoring, roughly 5 s to mature, and the module awake (key on, running or after-run).",["Internal 5 V regulator of the engine module defective","Supply or sensor wire shorted to battery voltage","Overvoltage from charging fault or jump start"],["Check engine lamp","Other diagnostics such as the DEF quality test suspended","Erratic sensor values possible"],3,3,["P2505","P2507","P0563","P06A6"],"כניסת כוח מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM) — אות גבוה"],P2509:["ECM/PCM Power Input Signal Intermittent","P2509 records a brief loss of the engine module's supply, a dropout rather than a lasting low or high value. Two Cummins-powered pickups show how easily it appears. Nissan warns for the 2016 Titan XD with the 5.0 L diesel: wait at least two minutes after switching off before disconnecting either 12 V battery, otherwise P2509 and P181B are stored; such codes may be erased but are not a warranty repair.",["Battery disconnected before the module finished its after-run","Loose battery clamp, ground or supply connector","Module software too sensitive, fixed by reflash (Ram 6.7 L)","Intermittent main relay contact"],["MIL on, often without drivability complaint","Code appears right after battery work"],1,1,["P2505","P2506","P2507","P2508"],"אות כניסת כוח מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM) — תקלה לסירוגין"],P250A:["Engine Oil Level Sensor Circuit","P250A is the general circuit code for the engine oil level sensor, a unit in the sump that today mostly measures by heated element or ultrasound and often reports oil temperature as well. Its use varies. GM's 2018 preliminary information for several trucks, SUVs and V8 cars lists P250A among codes caused by a jumper harness chafed near connector X154 on the front cover.",["Sensor harness chafed or pinched (GM X154 jumper harness)","Engine oil overfilled, sensor reading out of range (Mazda CX-9)","Oil level sensor defective or leaking at its seal","Corroded or oily connector at the sump"],["Oil level warning or message in the cluster","Oil level display missing or wrong","With harness damage, further engine codes and stalling (GM)"],2,0,["P250B","P250C","P250D","P250E","P250F"],"חיישן מפלס שמן מנוע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P250B:["Engine Oil Level Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P250B fires when the oil level sensor answers electrically but its reading is implausible, for instance a level that jumps, stays frozen while the engine runs, or contradicts the value after a stop. Continuous sensors see a lower level in operation than at rest, so the plausibility logic has to account for running state, temperature and inclination.",["Plausibility logic in the engine module too strict, fixed by update (Alfa Romeo)","Sensor element aged or contaminated by sludge","Oil level far outside the calibrated range after a service"],["Oil level message without real oil loss","Level display jumps or stays fixed"],2,0,["P250A","P250E","P250F"],"חיישן מפלס שמן מנוע — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P250C:["Engine Oil Level Sensor Circuit Low","P250C means the oil level sensor's signal line is pulled too low, the classic picture of a short to ground or, depending on the input design, a break that lets the line drop. Deutz describes its P250C-00 the same way: level sensor line grounded or interrupted.",["Signal wire shorted to ground near the sump","Open circuit or unplugged sensor connector","Warning logic in the engine module, fixed by reflash (Hyundai 2.0 Nu)","Sensor electronics shorted internally"],["Oil level warning lamp on","No oil level reading in the cluster"],2,0,["P250A","P250D","P250E"],"חיישן מפלס שמן מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל"],P250D:["Engine Oil Level Sensor Circuit High","P250D is stored when the oil level sensor line rises above its valid range. The usual explanation is contact with a positive conductor; with pull-up inputs an interrupted line or missing sensor ground can also drive the signal high. Deutz gives the clearest definition: its EMR controller files P250D-00 as the level sensor shorted to battery. Ford lists P250D in the 2014 BOSS 302S engine code table.",["Signal wire shorted to supply voltage","Sensor ground open or signal line interrupted","Sensor electronics faulty"],["Oil level warning or message","Level display permanently at maximum"],2,0,["P250A","P250C","P250E"],"חיישן מפלס שמן מנוע — אות גבוה במעגל"],P250E:["Engine Oil Level Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P250E flags an oil level signal that drops out or jumps in an unrealistic way while the circuit otherwise looks intact. Typical sources are a loose terminal, a wire that breaks only under engine movement, or a sensor that loses its echo or heating cycle intermittently. Modern sensors deliver level and temperature as a timed or digital signal, so a single disturbed cycle can already be detected.",["Loose or oily terminal in the sensor connector","Wire breaking intermittently from engine movement","Sensor losing its measuring cycle sporadically"],["Oil level message appears and disappears","Jumping level display"],2,0,["P250A","P250B","P250C","P250D"],"חיישן מפלס שמן מנוע — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P250F:["Engine Oil Level Too Low","P250F is not a wiring code: the oil level sensor works, and the measured level is below the minimum. Mazda used it on 2021 models with the 2.5 L turbo (Mazda3, Mazda6, CX-30, CX-5, CX-9) where a low-oil message and the check engine light appeared after roughly 5,000 to 7,500 km without visible leaks;",["Oil burned past valve stem seals or piston rings","External oil leak or too little oil after a service","Warning logic triggering with correct level, fixed by update (Hyundai)"],["Low engine oil message and check engine light","Oil level near or below minimum on the dipstick"],1,1,["P250A","P250B","P0520","P0524"],"מפלס שמן מנוע — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2510:["ECM/PCM Power Relay Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P2510 judges whether the main relay of the engine module behaves as commanded, based on what the module senses on the switched supply. GM's 2014 diesel tables describe two checks. A stuck relay is one that ignores the power-down command, recognised when timer values after the after-run are longer than possible;",["Main relay contacts welded or sticking","Relay dropping out early (weak coil, poor socket contact)","Battery disconnected or supply lost during after-run","Relay driver or EEPROM handling in the module faulty"],["MIL after two trips (GM type B)","Battery drain if the relay stays closed","Lost adaptations if the relay opens too early"],2,1,["P2511","P0685","P0689","P0690"],"ממסר כוח מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P2511:["ECM/PCM Power Relay Sense Circuit Intermittent","P2511 covers short dropouts on the line through which the engine module reads back the output of its main relay. The relay is commanded on, yet the sensed voltage briefly vanishes and returns, typical of a chattering contact, a cracked solder joint in the relay or a loose terminal in the fuse box. No manufacturer documents this code publicly with thresholds or a bulletin;",["Worn or chattering main relay contact","Loose relay socket or fuse box terminal","Sense wire breaking intermittently"],["Engine may stall briefly or hesitate","Several modules logging voltage-related codes"],2,1,["P2510","P0689","P0690"],"חישת ממסר כוח מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM) — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2512:["Event Data Recorder Request Circuit/Open","P2512 concerns the wired request line between the event data recorder and the engine module. The recorder, normally part of the airbag control unit, stores a short history of speed, throttle, brake and other pre-crash data when it senses a crash or near-crash, and needs powertrain values for that. Via the request circuit it can ask the engine module to deliver or freeze them.",["Request wire broken or connector unplugged","Airbag/recorder module missing, replaced or not configured","Engine module configured for a recorder line that is not fitted"],["Code stored without noticeable symptoms","Possibly a service or wrench indicator"],2,0,["P2513","P2514"],""],P2513:["Event Data Recorder Request Circuit Low","P2513 is set when the event data recorder request line reads too low at the engine module. A wire rubbed through to body ground, a crushed harness after body work, or water in a floor connector are the obvious suspects; a low line may also be read as a permanent request.",["Request wire shorted to ground","Moisture or corrosion in an under-floor connector","Recorder or engine module input stage faulty"],["Code stored without drivability effect","Possibly a service or wrench indicator"],2,0,["P2512","P2514"],""],P2514:["Event Data Recorder Request Circuit High","P2514 tells you the request line between the event data recorder and the engine module sits at too high a level. The recorder, normally housed in the airbag control unit, keeps a short log of speed, pedal and brake data around a collision and fetches engine values through this line.",["Request wire chafed against a powered circuit","Missing ground or unplugged connector at the airbag/recorder module","Input stage in engine or recorder module faulty"],["Code stored with no effect on driving","Possibly a wrench or service indicator instead of the check engine light"],2,0,["P2512","P2513"],""],P2515:["A/C Refrigerant Pressure Sensor B Circuit","P2515 is the general circuit fault of a second refrigerant pressure sensor, called B. Heat pump systems and vehicles with electric compressors often measure pressure at several points in the circuit; which position is B is up to the maker.",["Pressure sensor electronics failed (Audi early build sensors)","Connector corroded or wiring to the sensor damaged","Evaluating module (thermal management or engine) faulty"],["A/C does not cool or cools only intermittently","Compressor stays off","Further A/C pressure codes such as P0530 stored"],2,0,["P2516","P2517","P2518","P0530"],"חיישן לחץ גז מזגן‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2516:["A/C Refrigerant Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2516 flags a pressure sensor B whose reading is electrically valid but does not behave like real refrigerant pressure. In GM's hybrid OBD tables sensor B is the low-side sensor, evaluated by the hybrid processor that also runs the electric compressor.",["Pressure sensor stuck at one value","Compressor runs but hardly changes pressure (very low charge, blockage)","High resistance in signal or ground wire"],["A/C cools poorly","Check engine light after two drives (GM type B)","Refrigerant charge diagnosis not completed"],2,1,["P2515","P2517","P2518","P0534"],"חיישן לחץ גז מזגן‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2517:["A/C Refrigerant Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","P2517 means the signal of refrigerant pressure sensor B has dropped below its usable floor. GM's hybrid tables, where B is the low-side sensor, compute the ratio of signal to the 5 V reference and fail it below 2 % (0.10 V): in 2019 if that holds for 1.6 s of a 2 s window, in 2016 for 16 of 20 samples, in 2011 for 40 of 50 samples taken every 100 ms; each time type B, so the lamp comes on after two drives.",["Signal wire open or shorted to ground","5 V reference missing (wire or shared supply pulled down)","Pressure sensor without output"],["A/C compressor does not switch on","Check engine light after two drives on GM hybrids"],2,1,["P2515","P2516","P2518","P0532"],"חיישן לחץ גז מזגן‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2518:["A/C Refrigerant Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","P2518 is stored when pressure sensor B reports a signal close to its supply voltage. GM, which uses B for the low-side sensor in its hybrid tables, sets the limit at 98 % of the reference, about 4.90 V.",["Signal wire shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Sensor ground open","Moisture or corrosion in the sensor connector"],["Check engine light after one drive on newer GM hybrids","A/C compressor disabled, no cooling"],2,1,["P2515","P2516","P2517","P0533"],"חיישן לחץ גז מזגן‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2519:["A/C Request A Circuit","P2519 covers the general circuit fault of a wired input through which the climate control asks the engine module for compressor operation. The engine module needs this request early, to raise idle speed, add torque reserve and then energise the compressor clutch relay.",["Request wire broken or connector loose","Climate control unit or A/C switch not sending a valid signal","Engine module input stage faulty"],["A/C compressor never engages","Idle speed does not rise when A/C is selected"],2,0,["P2520","P2521","P2522","P0645"],"בקשת מזגן‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P251A:["PTO Enable Switch Circuit/Open","P251A concerns the switch the operator uses to arm the power take-off on a work truck. The control module reads this switch line and only allows PTO mode, often with a raised working idle, when the signal is plausible. This code means the module sees no valid state, typically an interrupted wire or a switch that no longer closes.",["Poor PTO or engine-to-frame ground (paint under the eyelet, corrosion, bolt bottoming out)","Broken or unplugged wire between PTO enable switch and module","Worn PTO enable switch that no longer makes contact","Faulty connection made during body or equipment installation"],["PTO cannot be engaged or drops out intermittently","Working idle speed is not raised when PTO is selected","Stored code with normal driving behaviour"],2,0,["P251B","P251C","P258E","P253A","P251D"],"מתג אפשור PTO — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P251B:["PTO Enable Switch Circuit Low","With P251B the module reads the PTO enable switch input as stuck at a low level, below what either switch position should produce. A wire chafed through to chassis ground, water in a connector or a switch shorted internally are the usual explanations. No maker publishes P251B with thresholds;",["Switch signal wire chafed against frame or body","Moisture or corrosion in the switch connector","PTO enable switch shorted internally"],["PTO will not engage, or engages without being selected","PTO indicator lamp behaves incorrectly","Readiness monitors may stay incomplete"],2,0,["P251A","P251C","P258E","P253C"],"מתג אפשור PTO — אות נמוך במעגל"],P251C:["PTO Enable Switch Circuit High","P251C is logged when the PTO enable switch line sits above its valid window, close to supply voltage. That points to a signal wire touching a battery or ignition feed, a reference that has lost its ground, or a pull-up that the switch can no longer pull down. A lost ground matters here: GM's bulletin PIP6108 for P251A on 2019–2023 medium-duty Silverado trucks sends technicians to the PTO and frame grounds first.",["Switch signal wire shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Missing ground on the switch or module reference","Switch stuck in the applied position"],["PTO engages or high idle starts without operator request","PTO cannot be switched off normally","Emissions readiness stays not ready"],2,0,["P251A","P251B","P258E","P253D"],"מתג אפשור PTO — אות גבוה במעגל"],P251D:["PTO Engine Shutdown Circuit/Open","P251D covers the engine shutdown line of a power take-off installation. On trucks with body equipment such as cranes, pumps or aerial devices, a hard-wired signal lets the PTO controller or an equipment stop button tell the engine module to switch the engine off. P251D means the module cannot read a valid state on that line, usually because the wire or plug is open.",["Open shutdown wire or loose connector at the body interface","Fault in the body equipment's stop switch or controller output","Shutdown input enabled in calibration but not wired by the upfitter"],["PTO locked out or equipment will not run","Equipment stop button no longer shuts down the engine"],2,0,["P251E","P251F","P251A","P253A"],"כיבוי מנוע PTO — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P251E:["PTO Engine Shutdown Circuit Low","P251E reports that the PTO engine shutdown input reads too low. Whether low means stop now or all clear depends on the maker's wiring, so the practical effect varies: the module may treat the line as an active stop request and refuse to keep the engine running in PTO mode, or it may simply flag the line as shorted and ignore it.",["Shutdown wire chafed through to chassis ground","Corroded connector at the body builder interface","Equipment stop switch shorted to ground"],["Engine stops or will not stay running while PTO is used","PTO function disabled"],2,0,["P251D","P251F","P251B"],"כיבוי מנוע PTO — אות נמוך במעגל"],P251F:["PTO Engine Shutdown Circuit High","P251F is the high-side fault of the PTO engine shutdown input: the voltage stays near supply level where the module expects a defined switching state. A shutdown wire touching a powered circuit in the body harness, a missing ground on the equipment controller, or an add-on module that drives the line permanently are typical.",["Shutdown wire shorted to a powered circuit in the body harness","Body equipment controller without ground","Retrofitted control module holding the line high"],["Engine does not stop when equipment shutdown is triggered","PTO operation blocked"],2,0,["P251D","P251E","P251C"],"כיבוי מנוע PTO — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2520:["A/C Request A Circuit Low","P2520 is set when the voltage on A/C request input A stays below the band the engine module accepts. Depending on whether the input is active-high or active-low, a grounded wire then reads as a permanent request or as none at all – either way the module distrusts it. Most often a harness rubbed through to body metal, a pinched wire behind the dashboard or a climate panel output stuck low is behind it.",["Request wire shorted to ground","Climate control output stuck low","Engine module input stage faulty"],["A/C does not switch on, or compressor runs although A/C is off","Idle speed behaves oddly when the A/C is toggled"],2,0,["P2519","P2521","P2523"],"בקשת מזגן‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2521:["A/C Request A Circuit High","With P2521 the engine module sees A/C request input A held above its valid range, typically because the wire touches a supply line, the input has lost its pull-down or the sending control unit drives it permanently high. Two makers list the code by number. Ford includes P2521 in the 2014 BOSS 302S engine module table without a lamp mark.",["Request wire shorted to a supply voltage","Climate control unit drives the line permanently high","Code newly reported after an engine software update (Sprinter T21)"],["A/C compressor runs although A/C is switched off","A/C button has no effect","Raised idle speed without A/C request"],2,0,["P2519","P2520","P2524"],"בקשת מזגן‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2522:["A/C Request B Circuit","P2522 is the general circuit code for a second wired A/C request input, B. Why an engine module would need two such lines is left to each maker; plausible uses are a separate rear evaporator, a second request stage or a redundant line to cross-check input A. The common purpose stays the same: the module must learn of the coming compressor load in time to adjust idle and torque.",["Input B wire broken or connector loose","Sending climate module or switch faulty","Engine module input stage faulty"],["A/C function served by input B unavailable","Idle dips when the compressor engages without notice"],2,0,["P2523","P2524","P2519"],"בקשת מזגן‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2523:["A/C Request B Circuit Low","P2523 reports that A/C request input B is pulled below its valid range. On the wire level this usually means a conductor grounded against body metal, a sending module whose output transistor has failed shorted, or a wet connector draining the signal. Whether the engine module then assumes a constant request or none depends on the circuit design, and no maker states it publicly;",["Input B wire shorted to ground","Output stage of the sending module shorted","Moisture in a connector of the request line"],["Compressor not engaging or engaging unasked","A/C-related idle compensation missing"],2,0,["P2522","P2524","P2520"],"בקשת מזגן‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2524:["A/C Request B Circuit High","P2524 indicates that A/C request input B reads above the level the engine module treats as valid. A line chafed against battery or ignition feed, an open pull-down inside the module or a control unit that latches its output high are the usual explanations. Ford is the one maker found to list it: its 2014 BOSS 302S code list shows P2524 without a lamp mark, just like its A-side counterpart P2521;",["Input B wire shorted to battery or ignition voltage","Sending module output latched high","Engine module input stage faulty"],["Compressor engages although not requested","A/C cannot be switched off or on as expected"],2,0,["P2522","P2523","P2521"],"בקשת מזגן‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2525:["Vacuum Reservoir Pressure Sensor Circuit","P2525 is the general circuit fault of the pressure sensor on a vacuum reservoir. Diesels, and many hybrids and electric drives, lack usable intake vacuum and run a separate pump, often driven from the camshaft or by an electric motor, that fills a reservoir. That stored vacuum serves the brake booster and, on many diesels, pneumatic actuators for EGR, turbocharger control, swirl flaps or an exhaust brake.",["Sensor wiring open or connector loose","Reservoir pressure sensor defective","Shared 5 V reference disturbed by another sensor"],["Check engine light depending on maker","Reduced boost or EGR function in default mode"],2,3,["P2526","P2527","P2528","P2529"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל ואקום — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2526:["Vacuum Reservoir Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2526 marks a vacuum reservoir pressure reading that stays inside the electrical range but does not fit the situation, for instance no rise in vacuum after the pump has run, or a value frozen while actuators draw on the reservoir. Because the sensor watches a real system, genuine vacuum faults such as a leaking hose, a worn pump or a cracked reservoir can set it as well as a drifting sensor. Two makers name it.",["Leaking vacuum hose, check valve or reservoir","Mechanical or electric vacuum pump delivering too little","Pressure sensor drifting or stuck"],["Check engine light, often with boost or EGR codes","Weak exhaust brake or reduced power","Hissing noise from a leaking line"],2,3,["P2525","P2527","P2528","P2529","P0027"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל ואקום — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2527:["Vacuum Reservoir Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P2527 means the signal from the vacuum reservoir pressure sensor has fallen below the lowest voltage a working sensor can produce. Whether low volts stand for deep vacuum or for atmospheric pressure depends on the sensor curve, but a reading at the floor is treated as an electrical fault, not as a vacuum value.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","5 V reference open or pulled down","Sensor without output"],["Check engine light","Boost or EGR control in default mode, less power"],2,3,["P2525","P2526","P2528","P2529"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל ואקום — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2528:["Vacuum Reservoir Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P2528 is logged when the vacuum reservoir pressure sensor delivers a voltage near or at its supply, beyond anything the sensing element can output. A signal wire touching 5 V or battery voltage, a broken sensor ground, or corrosion bridging pins in the connector are the classic findings. A real loss of vacuum does not normally push the signal this far; it would appear as a range or performance fault instead.",["Signal wire shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Sensor ground open","Corrosion bridging pins in the connector"],["Check engine light depending on maker","Reduced power with actuators in default position"],2,3,["P2525","P2526","P2527","P2529"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל ואקום — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2529:["Vacuum Reservoir Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent","P2529 covers a vacuum reservoir pressure signal that drops out or jumps for short moments rather than staying wrong. The engine module notices changes faster than a reservoir could physically empty or fill, or brief excursions to the electrical limits that recover again.",["Loose or spread terminal in the sensor connector","Harness chafing or wire breaking under engine movement","Moisture entering the connector"],["Check engine light comes and goes","Occasional brief loss of power or boost"],2,3,["P2525","P2526","P2527","P2528"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל ואקום — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P252A:["Engine Oil Quality Sensor Circuit","P252A is the general circuit code for an engine oil quality sensor, a unit in the sump that judges the state of the oil from its physical properties. Hella's PULS+C variant, for example, adds measurements of viscosity, density and permittivity to ultrasonic level sensing, so oil changes can follow real wear instead of a fixed mileage.",["Sensor connector loose, unplugged or corroded by oil and moisture","Broken signal, supply or ground wire near the oil pan","Internal electronics of the oil quality sensor failed"],["Oil condition or service interval display missing or showing a fault","Warning message in the instrument cluster, usually without engine light"],2,0,["P252B","P252C","P252D","P252E","P253F"],"חיישן איכות שמן מנוע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P252B:["Engine Oil Quality Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P252B covers an oil quality sensor whose signal is electrically valid but makes no sense in context. Plausibility logic can weigh the reported oil properties against oil temperature, time since the last service or the engine's own oil ageing model; a value that stays frozen while conditions change, or leaps after a top-up without reason, is suspect.",["Deposits or sludge on the sensing element distort the measurement","Oil grade or viscosity outside what the sensor calibration expects","Sensor aged or drifting, reading frozen or offset","Plausibility logic in the engine software too strict"],["Oil condition display shows implausible values or a fault message","Service interval calculated inconsistently after an oil change"],2,0,["P252A","P252E","P253F"],"חיישן איכות שמן מנוע — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P252C:["Engine Oil Quality Sensor Circuit Low","P252C is stored when the oil quality sensor's signal sits below the range the engine computer accepts. Typical reasons are a signal wire chafed through to ground, a supply line that has lost its voltage or an internal short in the sensor; depending on the input circuit an open wire can also drag the reading down.",["Signal wire chafed against the oil pan or engine block (short to ground)","Sensor supply voltage missing (fuse, supply wire)","Internal short in the oil quality sensor"],["Oil condition value missing in the cluster or service menu","Service reminder falls back to fixed intervals or shows a fault"],2,0,["P252A","P252D","P252E"],"חיישן איכות שמן מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל"],P252D:["Engine Oil Quality Sensor Circuit High","P252D means the oil quality sensor reports a voltage above its valid window. A short of the signal line to a positive conductor, a broken sensor ground or, with pull-up inputs, an interrupted signal wire can all push the value to the upper stop. Sensor electronics that latch high are a further possibility. Manufacturers do not document trigger values for this code.",["Sensor ground or signal wire interrupted, connector pin pushed back","Signal wire shorted to a supply or battery-voltage wire","Sensor electronics stuck at a high output"],["Warning or blank oil condition value in the cluster","Oil change reminder appears too early, too late or not at all"],2,0,["P252A","P252C","P252E"],"חיישן איכות שמן מנוע — אות גבוה במעגל"],P252E:["Engine Oil Quality Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P252E points to an oil quality signal that briefly drops out or jumps while the circuit is otherwise intact. Typical sources are a terminal that loses contact when the engine shakes, a harness rubbing on the sump or a sensor whose internal measuring cycle is occasionally disturbed.",["Loose or corroded terminal in the sensor connector","Harness rubbing on the oil pan with intermittent contact","Sensor electronics failing intermittently with heat or vibration"],["Oil condition message appears and disappears","Fluctuating oil condition or service interval values"],2,0,["P252A","P252B","P252C","P252D"],"חיישן איכות שמן מנוע — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P252F:["Engine Oil Level Too High","P252F is not a wiring fault: the level sensor works and reports more oil in the sump than the permitted maximum. Deutz's EMR controller files the condition as P252F-00 under oil level parameter SPN 98 with FMI 15, and Ford's 2014 BOSS 302S code table lists P252F without a lamp entry. Besides overfilling at a service, fuel getting into the oil is a common reason.",["Too much oil added at the last oil change or top-up","Fuel dilution from frequent short trips or diesel particulate filter regeneration","Coolant entering the oil (head gasket, oil cooler)"],["Oil level warning in the instrument cluster","Dipstick reading above the maximum mark, oil may smell of fuel","Possible rich mixture codes after long drives"],1,0,["P250F","P250A","P0172","P253F"],"מפלס שמן מנוע — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2530:["Ignition Switch Run Position Circuit","P2530 is the general fault of the hard-wired run signal that tells a powertrain module the ignition switch is in its run position. Modules use this line to wake up, power their outputs and decide when to start their internal shutdown routine; many also cross-check it against the ignition status sent over the network. The code says the signal is missing or unreadable without stating a direction.",["Blown fuse or faulty relay in the run feed","Loose terminal at the module or ignition switch","Worn ignition switch contacts"],["Warning lamps or stored codes in several modules","Engine may stall or not start","Modules staying awake after key-off"],2,0,["P2531","P2532","P2533","P2536"],""],P2531:["Ignition Switch Run Position Circuit Low","The engine module logs P2531 if the run-position input stays low although the vehicle state says the ignition is on, for example while the engine runs or the network reports run. The supply side is the usual suspect: an open fuse, a relay that does not pull in, a wire grounded on the body or a switch contact that no longer carries current.",["Open fuse in the run circuit","Run signal wire shorted to ground","Run relay not closing"],["MIL on","Engine stalls or will not restart","Several warning lamps or communication codes at once"],2,1,["P2530","P2532","P2534"],""],P2532:["Ignition Switch Run Position Circuit High","P2532 means voltage is present on the run-position input when it should be absent, typically after key-off or while the network reports the ignition as off. A run feed backfed through another component, a relay with welded contacts or a wire touching a permanent battery feed can cause it.",["Voltage backfeed into the run circuit through another component","Run relay with welded contacts","Run wire touching a permanent battery feed"],["Battery drained after the vehicle is parked","Modules or fans keep running after key-off"],2,0,["P2530","P2531","P2535"],""],P2533:["Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit","P2533 is the general fault of the circuit that is live in both the on and the start position of the ignition switch, often called run/crank. Unlike the pure run line it must stay powered while the starter turns, so modules rely on it to remain awake during cranking. Ford lists P2533 in its 2014 BOSS 302S code table with the M marker for the MIL.",["Powertrain module software or parameters (Ford Mach-E 2021, reprogramming per TSB 21-2244)","Fuse or relay fault in the run/crank feed","Loose or corroded terminal at the module"],["MIL on","Possible no-start or stall during cranking"],2,1,["P2534","P2535","P2530","P061A"],""],P2534:["Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit Low","P2534 is the most widely documented of this group. GM's 2025 tables let the TCM fail it when its run/crank input is false while the ECM reports run/crank active, 99 failures out of 240 samples at 25 ms, Type A; the brake control module (EBCM) sets it when its primary wakeup line reads low for 3 s while the network says run or crank, Type B. On the 2016 Volt the line must drop below 2.0 V for 2.5 s.",["Engine harness chafed at a bracket (GM HD trucks, upper control arm bracket)","Run/crank relay or fuse open","Module software needing an update (GM 6L50 TCM, Ram eTorque HCP)","Loose terminal on the wakeup line at TCM or BCM"],["MIL on","Stall or no start","Transmission or other modules set follow-up codes"],2,3,["P2533","P2535","P2531","P0700"],""],P2535:["Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit High","P2535 means the run/crank input stays active while it should be off. GM's 2025 tables fail it in the TCM after 320 of 400 samples with run/crank true while the ECM reports it inactive, Type A, and in the brake control module (EBCM) when the primary wakeup line stays high for 3 s against the network status, Type B; the 2016 Volt uses more than 6.0 V on the line with run/crank inactive.",["Voltage backfeed from another module (GM K111 fuel pump driver via water-in-fuel sensor circuit)","Run/crank relay stuck closed","Run/crank wire touching a battery feed"],["MIL on, code returns at every key-on after clearing","Modules stay awake, battery drain"],2,1,["P2533","P2534","P2532"],""],P2536:["Ignition Switch Accessory Position Circuit","P2536 is the general fault of the accessory input, the signal that is live when the key or start button is in the accessory position and that on many vehicles also acts as a wake-up line between body and powertrain modules. The code does not say whether the line is open, low or high, only that its state cannot be used. No manufacturer documents P2536 publicly.",["Fault in the accessory feed or wake-up output of the body module","Loose or corroded terminal on the accessory line","Worn accessory contact in the ignition switch"],["Remote start or key-off functions not working","Accessories behave inconsistently in the accessory position"],2,0,["P2537","P2538","P2530","P2533"],"מצב אביזרי מתג הצתה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2537:["Ignition Switch Accessory Position Circuit Low","P2537 reports that the accessory or accessory wake-up input sits low where a high level is expected. GM documents it in detail: on the 2016 Volt the ECM fails it when the accessory input is false while the propulsion system has been active for more than 0.5 s; it is a Type B fault over 2 trips, and the 6-speed TCM tables evaluate the same input with no MIL.",["Open or high-resistance accessory wake-up circuit between BCM and ECM/TCM","Body control module not driving the wake-up output","Poor terminal contact at ECM or TCM connector"],["Remote start inoperative","Power liftgate works only with ignition on","Blower may keep running after engine shutdown (diesel)"],2,1,["P2536","P2538","P2534"],"מצב אביזרי מתג הצתה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2538:["Ignition Switch Accessory Position Circuit High","P2538 is set when the accessory input reads high in a state where it should be inactive, for instance once the vehicle is switched off and the body module should have released the line. Backfeed from an aftermarket device, a stuck accessory relay or a wire touching a battery feed are the obvious causes. A permanently high accessory line can keep modules awake and drain the battery. No manufacturer publishes P2538;",["Backfeed from aftermarket equipment connected to the accessory line","Accessory relay stuck closed","Accessory wire chafed against a battery feed"],["Battery drain while parked","Radio or accessories stay on after key-off"],2,0,["P2536","P2537","P2532"],"מצב אביזרי מתג הצתה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2539:["Low Pressure Fuel System Sensor Circuit","P2539 is the general circuit code of the sensor that reports the supply pressure ahead of the high-pressure pump. In VW's 2014 specification books for the Passat, CC and Touareg it is set once the signal exceeds 4.80 V, which the Passat book attributes to a broken line or contact with the positive supply; below 0.2 V VW stores P2541 instead.",["Signal or ground wire open, connector not engaged","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Failed low-pressure fuel sensor or pressure switch","Code logged only in a static self-test without a real fault (Ford Transit 2015)"],["Check engine light","Hesitation or reduced power under load","Hard starting, especially after standing"],2,3,["P2540","P2541","P2542","P2543","P0087"],"חיישן מערכת דלק לחץ נמוך — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P253A:["PTO Sense Circuit/Open","The PTO sense circuit tells the powertrain modules whether the power take-off is really engaged, usually through a pressure or limit switch on the PTO unit. This feedback matters for OBD: CARB allows makers to suspend affected monitors only while PTO is active and requires readiness to be cleared after 750 minutes of cumulative PTO runtime, and Ford's 2012 summary notes that readiness flags are set to not ready…",["Open sense wire or disconnected plug at the PTO unit","Failed PTO pressure or limit switch","PTO feedback configured in the module but no PTO fitted"],["PTO status not shown or PTO functions unavailable","Readiness monitors behave unexpectedly"],2,1,["P253B","P253C","P253D","P253E","P251A"],"חישת PTO — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P253B:["PTO Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P253B is not about a broken wire but about a PTO feedback signal that is electrically valid yet does not fit the situation. A module can compare the sense input with the operator request, engine speed or transmission state: PTO reported engaged although nobody selected it, or no engagement feedback although the PTO was commanded long enough ago.",["Limit or position switch on the PTO misadjusted","PTO engagement mechanism or clutch sticking","Low air or oil pressure at the PTO engagement and pressure switch"],["PTO engagement reported wrongly in the cluster or scan tool","Delayed or failed PTO engagement","Monitors not completing"],3,1,["P253A","P253C","P253D","P253E","P258E"],"PTO — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P253C:["PTO Sense Circuit Low","P253C flags a PTO feedback input that reads too low for any valid switch state. Where the sense switch closes to ground on engagement, a grounded wire looks like a permanently engaged PTO; where it pulls up, the same fault hides every engagement. Common causes are a wire rubbed through near the transmission-mounted PTO, oil or water in the switch connector and a shorted pressure switch. No maker publishes P253C;",["Sense wire rubbed through to ground near the PTO","Oil or water in the sense switch connector","PTO pressure switch shorted"],["PTO shown as engaged although it is off, or never shown as engaged","Readiness monitors stay incomplete","Possible MIL"],2,1,["P253A","P253B","P253D","P253E"],"PTO — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P253D:["PTO Sense Circuit High","P253D means the PTO feedback input reads above its valid range. Besides genuine shorts to voltage or an open ground on the sense switch, Ram documents a software cause: bulletin 21-013-15 (replacing 21-005-14) covers 2013–2014 Ram 3500 pickups and 3500, 4500 and 5500 chassis cabs with the 6.7L Cummins and Aisin AS69RC six-speed, where the MIL came on with P253D stored in the transmission module although no defect…",["Outdated TCM calibration (Ram heavy-duty with Aisin AS69RC, reflash per bulletin)","Sense wire shorted to a voltage source","Open ground or reference at the PTO sense switch"],["MIL on without a noticeable PTO problem","PTO status wrong in scan data"],2,1,["P253A","P253B","P253C","P253E"],"PTO — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P253E:["PTO Sense Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P253E is stored when the PTO feedback signal flickers between states faster or more often than a real engagement could explain. Vibration on a frame-mounted or transmission-mounted PTO is the classic trigger: a loose terminal, a cracked wire near a bracket or a bouncing switch contact make the signal chatter.",["Loose or spread terminal in the sense switch connector","Wire cracked by vibration near the PTO","Worn sense switch with bouncing contact"],["PTO indicator flickers","PTO-related idle or shift strategy switches on and off","Readiness monitors keep resetting"],2,1,["P253A","P253B","P253C","P253D"],"חישת PTO — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P253F:["Engine Oil Deteriorated","P253F states that the engine computer considers the oil used up. Depending on the design this verdict comes from an oil quality sensor or, more often, from an oil life model that tallies operating conditions such as load, temperatures and estimated fuel dilution. Ford's 2014 BOSS 302S engine code table contains P253F without a lamp entry; exact criteria are published by no maker.",["Oil change overdue, oil actually aged","Oil life counter not reset after the last oil change","Strong fuel dilution from short trips, cold operation or frequent regenerations","Oil life calculation in the engine software too aggressive (update available)"],["Oil change or oil quality warning in the cluster","Remaining oil life shown as zero or dropping unusually fast"],1,0,["P252A","P252B","P252F"],""],P2540:["Low Pressure Fuel System Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2540 checks whether the low-pressure fuel sensor's reading is credible. The signal stays inside its electrical window, yet the pressure it reports does not fit what the supply side should be delivering. In VW's 2014 Touareg specification book the code appears only in the chapter for engine code CGFA, which also carries the hybrid high-voltage faults;",["Weak in-tank or lift pump causing real pressure deviation","Restricted fuel filter or kinked supply line","Low-pressure sensor reading offset","Outdated engine software (manufacturer update available)"],["Check engine light","Hesitation or power loss under load","Long cranking or hard starting"],2,3,["P2539","P2541","P2542","P2543","P0087"],"חיישן מערכת דלק לחץ נמוך — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2541:["Low Pressure Fuel System Sensor Circuit Low","P2541 means the signal of the low-pressure fuel sensor is below its valid range - typically a short to ground on the signal line or a lost 5 V sensor supply. VW's 2014 specification books set it below 0.2 V on the Passat, CC and Touareg (VW labels it short to ground, low input or out of range low), whereas a signal above 4.8 V leads to P2539.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","5 V reference supply missing or pulled down by another sensor","Failed low-pressure fuel sensor"],["Check engine light","Hesitation under load","Possible hard starting"],2,3,["P2539","P2540","P2542","P2543"],"חיישן מערכת דלק לחץ נמוך — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2542:["Low Pressure Fuel System Sensor Circuit High","P2542 means the low-pressure fuel sensor reports a voltage above its permitted range. Deutz is explicit: its MD1 controller stores P2542 when the supply pressure sensor signal rises beyond its normal voltage or is shorted toward the high side (SPN 94, FMI 3), and the EMR system describes P2542-00 as a battery short. P2542 also appears in the list Ford published for the BOSS 302S engine module of 2014.",["Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Sensor ground wire or pin interrupted","Failed low-pressure fuel sensor with high output"],["Check engine light","Reduced power or stalling if real pressure is low","Hard starting"],2,3,["P2539","P2540","P2541","P2543","P008A"],"חיישן מערכת דלק לחץ נמוך — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2543:["Low Pressure Fuel System Sensor Circuit Intermittent","P2543 reports a low-pressure fuel sensor signal with brief interruptions or spikes, although it remains within its electrical range most of the time - a loose pin, a chafed wire or a sensor with an internal contact problem.",["Loose or corroded pin at the sensor connector","Chafed signal or supply wire with intermittent contact","Outdated engine software (manufacturer update available)"],["Check engine light, often intermittent","Brief stumbling or hesitation","No symptoms between events"],2,3,["P2539","P2540","P2541","P2542"],"חיישן מערכת דלק לחץ נמוך — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2544:["Torque Management Request Input Signal A","P2544 concerns torque requests that another module, usually the transmission control module, sends to the engine module – for example to cut torque during a shift. GM's 2020 table 20OBDG04 checks each TCM message for a wrong protection value (16 of 20), a broken rolling counter (6 of 10), an increase request above 1,298 Nm (6 of 10) or the request type toggling too often (3 of 5), type B with two trips.",["Loose or unseated pins at the transmission connector","Data bus disturbance or failing gateway","Transmission module software or internal fault"],["Check engine light, often with several U-codes","Harsh shifts or reduced engine power","Multiple warning lamps, possibly no-crank"],2,3,["P2545","P2546","P2547","P2548","P0700","U0101"],"אות כניסת בקשת ניהול מומנט‏ A"],P2545:["Torque Management Request Input Signal A Range/Performance","P2545 means torque request A arrives intact but carries values the receiving module cannot accept as plausible – a requested torque outside the expected window, a request that contradicts the operating state, or one that does not follow up as it should. Ford's 2014 BOSS 302S engine module table lists P2545 with M, i.e. with check engine light.",["Transmission module software needs updating","Transmission oil leak or incorrect oil level (JLR 9HP48)","Requesting module sends implausible torque values"],["Check engine light (Ford) or transmission warning","Harsh or delayed shifts"],4,3,["P2544","P2546","P2547","P2549"],"אות כניסת בקשת ניהול מומנט‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2546:["Torque Management Request Input Signal A Low","P2546 says that torque request A, the channel over which one module asks another to raise or cut engine torque, reads below its permitted floor. On a hard-wired request this points to a line pulled toward ground; on a data-bus request it means a value pinned at or under the minimum the receiver accepts.",["Outdated transmission module software (JLR 9HP48 remedy)","Oil leak or low oil level in the transmission","Wired request line shorted to ground"],["Harsh or delayed gear changes","Transmission warning message or check engine light","Fault often stored together with P2545"],4,3,["P2544","P2545","P2547","P2550"],"אות כניסת בקשת ניהול מומנט‏ A — ערך נמוך"],P2547:["Torque Management Request Input Signal A High","P2547 is logged when torque request A sits above the highest value the receiving module will accept. A wired input would read like a line touching a supply voltage or a lost ground at the sender; a bus message would carry an out-of-scale number. The receiver ignores such a request, since following it could mean an unwanted torque increase. No maker documents P2547 publicly.",["Request line shorted to a supply voltage","Requesting module sends a value above the scale","Poor ground at the requesting module"],["Shift-related torque reduction no longer works, firmer shifts","Check engine light depending on make"],4,3,["P2544","P2545","P2546","P2551"],"אות כניסת בקשת ניהול מומנט‏ A — ערך גבוה"],P2548:["Torque Management Request Input Signal B","P2548 is the general fault on a second torque request channel, B, used when a further module besides the transmission may ask the engine for less or more torque. GM spells out who sits on channel B: in the ECM part of its 2017 table 17OBDG04 and again in 19OBDG03A, P2548 checks the traction torque and speed request coming from the electronic brake and traction control module.",["Data bus disturbance between brake module and engine module","Brake/traction control module sends corrupted messages","Weak battery or poor module power supply"],["Check engine light after two trips (GM Type B)","Traction or stability control warning lamp","Reduced traction intervention on slippery roads"],2,1,["P2549","P2550","P2551","P2544","U0121"],"אות כניסת בקשת ניהול מומנט‏ B"],P2549:["Torque Management Request Input Signal B Range/Performance","P2549 covers a torque request on channel B that arrives readable but makes no sense: a requested torque outside the expected band, a request that contradicts the current driving state, or one that changes in a way the sender could not plausibly mean. The wiring or bus link is assumed intact here, which separates it from the general fault P2548. No maker documents P2549 publicly.",["Requesting module (e.g. brake/traction module) computes implausible values","Software levels of sender and engine module do not match","Faulty input data at the requesting module, such as wheel speed"],["Check engine light depending on make","Traction control intervenes abruptly or not at all"],4,1,["P2548","P2550","P2551","P2545"],"אות כניסת בקשת ניהול מומנט‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P254A:["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 1 Circuit/Open","P254A covers the first PTO speed selector: the switch or sensor an operator uses to choose one of the preset working speeds for a power take-off. The engine controller expects a defined signal on this line; with P254A it finds no valid state, typically a broken wire, an unplugged connector or a switch contact that never closes. No maker documents P254A publicly.",["Broken selector signal or return wire","Selector or upfitter connector disconnected or pushed-out pin","Switch contact that no longer closes"],["PTO stays at standby speed instead of the selected step","Selected working speed cannot be called up","Stored code without effect on normal driving"],2,0,["P254B","P254C","P254D","P254E","P255A","P251A"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות PTO‏ 1 — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P254B:["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 1 Range/Performance","P254B is the rationality fault of PTO speed selector 1. The wiring is intact and the voltage sits inside the electrical limits, yet the reading does not fit any configured position, or it contradicts other information the controller holds, for example two speed requests at once or a value that lingers between steps.",["Contaminated or worn multi-position switch","Wrong resistor value in the upfitter's speed coding","Controller configured for a different selector type"],["PTO does not leave standby speed","Wrong working speed for the selected position"],2,0,["P254A","P254C","P254D","P254E","P255B"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות PTO‏ 1 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P254C:["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 1 Circuit Low","P254C reports that the signal from PTO speed selector 1 sits below the lowest voltage the controller accepts, which in practice means the signal wire touches ground or the switch is shorted internally. Whether a maker can detect this at all depends on the design.",["Selector signal wire chafed through to ground","Internal short in the selector switch","Water in an exterior selector connector"],["PTO speed stuck at one step","PTO blocked by the controller"],2,0,["P254A","P254B","P254D","P254E","P255C"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות PTO‏ 1 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P254D:["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 1 Circuit High","With P254D the controller sees the PTO speed selector 1 input above its upper limit. Causes are a signal wire rubbing against a battery-fed circuit, a broken ground or sensor return that lets the line float to the pull-up voltage, or a selector supply that is too high. Deutz separates these on its multi-stage speed selector: P3045-12 for a short to battery and P3045-A1 for a supply voltage outside its range.",["Signal wire shorted to a battery-fed circuit","Open ground or return line letting the input float high","Selector supply voltage too high"],["PTO jumps to the highest preset speed","PTO does not engage"],2,0,["P254A","P254B","P254C","P254E","P255D"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות PTO‏ 1 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P254E:["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 1 Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P254E is set when the signal from PTO speed selector 1 changes faster or more often than a real switch operation can explain, or briefly drops out and returns. Each short glitch can be read as a new speed request, and engine speed then hunts between steps;",["Loose terminal at the selector or upfitter connector","Corroded splice in the upfitter wiring","Vibration on a body-mounted switch panel"],["Engine speed surges while the PTO is running","PTO drops briefly to standby speed","Code comes and goes"],2,0,["P254A","P254B","P254C","P254D","P255E"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות PTO‏ 1 — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P254F:["Engine Hood Switch Circuit","P254F concerns the circuit of the hood switch, which tells the control units whether the engine hood is open. Engines that can start on their own, such as in hybrids or stop/start systems, need this to block an automatic start while someone works under the hood.",["Hood switch dirty, corroded or misadjusted","Damaged wiring or connector at the hood latch","Bent hood latch after a front-end repair"],["Check engine light after two trips (GM Type B)","Auto-stop or hybrid engine start disabled","Hood-open warning while the hood is closed"],1,1,["P257D"],"מתג מכסה מנוע מנוע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2550:["Torque Management Request Input Signal B Low","P2550 marks the second torque request input, B, as stuck below its lower limit. A hard-wired line would be pulled to ground by chafed insulation or a fault in the sending stage; in a networked design the sender would be reporting a value that lies under the bottom of the defined range. The engine module then disregards input B and keeps running on its own torque calculation. No maker documents P2550 publicly.",["Request line chafed through and shorted to ground","Output stage of the requesting module defective","Corroded or water-logged connector"],["Check engine light depending on make","Traction-related torque reduction no longer applied"],2,1,["P2548","P2549","P2551","P2546"],"אות כניסת בקשת ניהול מומנט‏ B — ערך נמוך"],P2551:["Torque Management Request Input Signal B High","P2551 is the high-side fault of torque request B: the signal sits above the top of its valid window. Typical electrical causes would be a line touching a battery feed, an interrupted reference ground or a sender that drives its output to full scale. Because an unexpectedly high request could translate into unwanted torque, the engine module discards it and works without channel B. No maker documents P2551 publicly.",["Request line shorted to battery voltage","Open ground or reference at the sender","Requesting module drives its output to full scale"],["Check engine light depending on make","Traction control warning, engine ignores intervention requests"],2,1,["P2548","P2549","P2550","P2547"],"אות כניסת בקשת ניהול מומנט‏ B — ערך גבוה"],P2552:["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit A Circuit","P2552 is the general circuit fault of throttle/fuel inhibit A, a line over which the engine module can be told, or can itself command, that throttle opening or fuelling must be blocked. It acts as a safety path next to the normal pedal-to-throttle chain. Ford lists P2552 in the engine module code table of its 2014 BOSS 302S race car, worded as circuit/open; its lamp column stays empty, and Ford gives no thresholds.",["Inhibit line open, e.g. broken wire or pushed-out pin","Inhibit relay or its supply defective","Engine module input or output stage faulty"],["Usually no check engine light (Ford non-MIL)","Possible power limitation or no throttle response"],2,2,["P2553","P2554","P2555","P2108"],""],P2553:["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit A Circuit Range/Performance","P2553 means the throttle/fuel inhibit path A is electrically present but does not behave as commanded. GM's 2005 diagnostic table for the 3.5 L L66 engine files it under electronic throttle control and runs it as a function check of the inhibit relay over a serial data link: a healthy relay produces no serial data, so any data seen there counts as a failure.",["Inhibit relay sticking or contacts worn","Fault in the relay control or feedback wiring","Internal fault in the engine or throttle control unit"],["Check engine light on the drive after the fault was found","Possible reduced power or throttle limp mode"],2,3,["P2552","P2554","P2555","P2108"],""],P2554:["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit A Circuit Low","P2554 reports that the voltage on throttle/fuel inhibit circuit A is too low. In GM's 2005 L66 parameter sheet the limit is below 0.498 V on the analogue inhibit circuit, read by the powertrain module while it is still processing after the ignition has been switched off. The table lists a warm engine, coolant at 69.5 °C or more, among the enable conditions.",["Inhibit circuit shorted to ground","Connected relay or control unit pulls the line down","Engine module input stage defective"],["Check engine light on the following drive","Sluggish throttle response or reduced power"],2,3,["P2552","P2553","P2555"],""],P2555:["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit A Circuit High","P2555 indicates excess voltage on throttle/fuel inhibit circuit A. The same 2005 GM document for the L66 V6 uses two limits depending on key state: more than 10 V while the ignition is on, or more than 4.5 V once it is off, with the fault judged after 4 s. As with its sibling checks, monitoring happens after shutdown, a single time per drive cycle, and the lamp waits until the next trip.",["Inhibit circuit shorted to a battery-fed wire","Inhibit relay stuck closed","Missing ground on the receiving side"],["Check engine light on the next trip","Limited throttle opening or reduced power"],2,3,["P2552","P2553","P2554"],""],P2556:["Engine Coolant Level Sensor/Switch Circuit","P2556 is the general circuit code for the coolant level sensor or switch, normally fitted in the expansion tank. Deutz uses it on its EMR L1 engine control for industrial engines with the sub-code P2556-F0, a ground error, under SPN 111. Mercedes-Benz goes its own way and stores P2556-7B, meaning the sensor reports a fluid level that is too low.",["Damaged wiring or ground at the level sensor","Air cushion in the expansion tank (Mercedes EQB)","Real coolant loss, e.g. internal charge air cooler leak"],["Low coolant warning in the cluster","Coolant level appears correct after opening the cap"],2,0,["P2557","P2558","P2559","P2560"],"חיישן/מתג מפלס נוזל קירור מנוע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2557:["Engine Coolant Level Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance","P2557 means the coolant level signal is electrically present but not believable. The Deutz EMR L1 engine control is the one documented user and fills the code twice under SPN 111: P2557-00 for a sensor value outside the valid range, and P2557-1C when the supply voltage feeding the level sensor is itself out of range.",["Sensor supply voltage out of range (Deutz P2557-1C)","Level sensor element contaminated or failing","Air pocket or foam in the expansion tank distorting the reading"],["Coolant level warning appears and disappears","Engine protection warning on industrial engines"],2,0,["P2556","P2558","P2559","P2560"],"חיישן/מתג מפלס נוזל קירור מנוע — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2558:["Engine Coolant Level Sensor/Switch Circuit Low","P2558 reports that the coolant level sensor or switch signal sits too low on the electrical scale. Deutz assigns it on the EMR L1 controller as P2558-14 under SPN 111 and groups two causes together: a grounded line or an interrupted one, which on that input both pull the reading to the bottom.",["Signal line shorted to ground","Broken wire or corroded connector at the expansion tank","Level sensor internally shorted"],["Permanent low coolant warning despite a full tank","No warning possible if the level really drops"],1,0,["P2556","P2557","P2559","P2560"],"חיישן/מתג מפלס נוזל קירור מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2559:["Engine Coolant Level Sensor/Switch Circuit High","P2559 is the high-voltage fault in the circuit of the coolant level sensor or switch. In the Deutz EMR L1 code list it appears as P2559-12 under SPN 111 meaning the line is shorted to battery plus; Deutz keeps open circuits under P2558 on that input, so a high reading there really points to contact with a positive feed.",["Signal line chafed against a positive feed","Open circuit on pull-up type switch designs","Level sensor internally faulty"],["Low coolant warning does not work","Warning lamp or message for the level sensor"],1,0,["P2556","P2557","P2558","P2560"],"חיישן/מתג מפלס נוזל קירור מנוע — אות גבוה במעגל"],P255A:["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 2 Circuit/Open","P255A belongs to the second PTO speed selector input, which lets the operator call up a further preset working speed in addition to selector 1. The controller finds no valid state on this line: a wire is broken, a connector is off, or the switch contact never closes.",["Broken wire between selector 2 and the module","Upfitter connector for selector 2 not mated","Selector 2 contact no longer closes"],["Second preset speed unavailable","Selector 1 presets still work"],2,0,["P255B","P255C","P255D","P255E","P254A"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות PTO‏ 2 — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P255B:["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 2 Range/Performance","P255B flags an implausible reading from PTO speed selector 2 although its circuit is electrically intact. Because a second selector normally works together with the first, the check can compare both: requests that cannot coexist, a level that sits between valid positions, or a selection that the configured number of presets does not allow.",["Sticking selector 2 switch","Upfitter wiring ties selector 1 and 2 together","Number of programmed presets does not match the switch"],["Second preset ignored or wrong speed reached","PTO speed control falls back to standby"],2,0,["P255A","P255C","P255D","P255E","P254B"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות PTO‏ 2 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P255C:["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 2 Circuit Low","P255C means the input of PTO speed selector 2 reads lower than the controller's bottom limit, usually because the signal wire has a short to chassis ground or the switch is shorted inside. On designs where a grounded line is itself the command, as with the switch-to-ground inputs of Ram's 2017 VSIM, a short looks exactly like a permanently held preset 2 request;",["Selector 2 wire shorted to chassis ground","Selector 2 shorted internally","Harness pinched under a body mounting"],["Engine always runs at the second preset in PTO mode","PTO blocked"],2,0,["P255A","P255B","P255D","P255E","P254C"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות PTO‏ 2 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P255D:["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 2 Circuit High","P255D is stored when PTO speed selector 2 delivers a signal above the permitted maximum. A chafed wire touching a battery-fed circuit, a lost sensor ground, or an upfitter feeding 12 V into an input meant to be switched to ground are the realistic causes.",["Selector 2 wire chafed against a battery-fed circuit","Upfitter applies 12 V to a ground-switched input","Lost ground or return line of selector 2"],["Second preset unavailable","PTO switched off by the controller"],2,0,["P255A","P255B","P255C","P255E","P254D"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות PTO‏ 2 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P255E:["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 2 Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P255E concerns short dropouts or rapid changes on the PTO speed selector 2 signal that do not match deliberate operation. Selector 2 is often the remote control on the body, close to pumps, booms or spreaders, so vibration, spray water and cable movement hit it harder than an in-cab switch.",["Spray water or moisture in the body-mounted remote switch","Cable to the remote control flexing at a boom or hinge","Loose crimp or terminal in the selector 2 circuit"],["Engine steps through preset speeds unexpectedly","PTO speed unstable while working","Code appears only under vibration"],2,0,["P255A","P255B","P255C","P255D","P254E"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות PTO‏ 2 — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P255F:["A/C Request A Circuit Range/Performance","P255F flags the A/C request A input as electrically sound but implausible: the request may switch on and off far more often than a real compressor demand would, stay set while the climate control is off, or disagree with what the engine module sees from the compressor side. The request lets the engine prepare for the compressor load by raising idle speed and torque reserve.",["Climate control module sends erratic requests","Loose contact on the request line causing chatter","Refrigerant pressure switch cycling abnormally"],["Idle speed fluctuates when the A/C cycles","A/C cooling intermittent or switched off"],2,0,["P2519","P2520","P2521","P256F","P0645"],"בקשת מזגן‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2560:["Engine Coolant Level Low","P2560 is not an electrical fault but a level finding: the coolant level sensor works, yet it reports less coolant than the minimum. Deutz uses it on the EMR L1 control as P2560-00 under SPN 111 with failure mode 1, meaning the level has fallen under its warning threshold. Ford lists P2560 in the 2014 BOSS 302S engine module table, with no M in the lamp column, i.e. no MIL.",["External leak at hoses, radiator or water pump","Internal leak, e.g. charge air cooler or head gasket","Air trapped after a coolant service"],["Low coolant warning","Rising engine temperature or overheating","Visible coolant traces or sweet smell"],2,2,["P2556","P2557","P2558","P2559","P0217"],"מפלס נוזל קירור מנוע — ערך נמוך"],P2561:["A/C Control Module Requested MIL Illumination","P2561 is a messenger code. The climate control module has found an emission-relevant fault in its own area, such as a component that feeds the engine's A/C idle strategy, and asks the engine module to switch on the warning lamp, since only the master controller may drive it. The engine module stores P2561 as a pointer; the actual fault code sits in the A/C module and must be read there.",["Emission-relevant fault stored in the climate control module","Failed A/C sensor or actuator behind that fault","Climate control module internal or software fault"],["Check engine light on","A/C may not cool or may be switched off","Further codes stored in the climate control module"],2,1,["P2519","P2522","P255F","P256F","P0645"],""],P2562:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Circuit","P2562 flags a general electrical problem in the circuit of the position sensor that reports where turbocharger boost actuator A stands - the variable vane linkage on many diesels, the electric wastegate actuator on turbo petrol engines. The engine computer receives a signal it cannot use at all, as opposed to a wrong position (P2563), a signal pinned low or high (P2564/P2565) or brief dropouts (P2566).",["Open or corroded wiring or connector between position sensor and engine computer","Electronic wastegate actuator rod length out of adjustment","Position sensor inside the actuator failed"],["Reduced power because boost is limited","Check engine light on","P2565 stored at the same time on some engines"],2,3,["P2563","P2564","P2565","P2566","P0045"],"חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2563:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","P2563 means the position feedback of the turbocharger boost control actuator - variable vanes or wastegate - does not match the commanded position, without an open or short being reported. GM's 2009 Duramax diesel table sets it when vane position differs from target by 15 % or more for 5 s (Type B, warning light after two trips).",["Kinked, twisted or leaking vacuum hose to the boost actuator","Leaking actuator diaphragm or sticking vanes","Broken or missing adjustment stud, actuator travel out of tolerance"],["Noticeable loss of power, limp mode","Check engine light","Underboost code P0299 stored at the same time"],3,3,["P2562","P2564","P2565","P2566","P0299"],"חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2564:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Circuit Low","P2564 is stored when the voltage from the boost actuator position sensor stays below the lowest value a working sensor can deliver, which usually points to a short to ground or a lost reference supply. GM's 2009 Duramax table uses 0.277 V (5.5 %, vanes fully open) held for 1 s once the engine has run 3 s, Type B.",["Signal wire chafed through and touching ground near the turbocharger","5 V reference supply to the sensor missing or shorted","Failed position sensor or vane actuator"],["Noticeable loss of power or limp mode","Check engine light on","Other sensors on the same 5 V supply may report faults too"],2,3,["P2562","P2563","P2565","P2566","P003A"],"חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2565:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Circuit High","P2565 means the boost actuator position signal sits above the highest plausible value, typically from an open signal wire, a short to the 5 V reference or battery voltage, or a failed sensor. GM's 2018 diesel ECM table flags it at an analog reading above 95 % in 200 of 250 samples (Type A, warning lamp on the first trip).",["Open signal wire or unplugged actuator connector","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Wastegate actuator rod set to the wrong length (electric wastegate engines)","Failed vane actuator with integrated sensor"],["Loss of power, sometimes limp mode","Check engine light on","Unusual turbocharger noise on some diesels"],2,3,["P2562","P2563","P2564","P2566","P003A"],"חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2566:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Circuit Intermittent","P2566 reports that the signal from the boost control position sensor flickers or drops out briefly instead of being steadily wrong. VW bulletins 21-15-04 (2015) and 21-15-06 (2020) for 2009-2014 Jetta, Golf and Jetta SportWagen with the 2.0 L TDI (CBEA, CJAA) list P2566 together with P2562-P2565 and P0299 for the complaint of lacking power;",["Loose or corroded pin at the position sensor connector","Heat-damaged or chafed sensor wiring near the turbocharger","Worn position sensor in the actuator"],["Intermittent loss of power or limp mode","Check engine light, sometimes going out again","Surging boost"],2,3,["P2562","P2563","P2564","P2565","P0299"],"חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ A — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2567:["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Temperature Sensor Circuit","P2567 is the general circuit fault of the sensor fitted to a direct ozone reduction (DOR) radiator - a radiator with a catalytic coating that converts ground-level ozone in the passing air and earns low-emission vehicles an NMOG credit. CARB section (e)(14) requires the OBD system to detect a missing or deteriorated DOR function. No manufacturer publicly documents P2567 itself.",["Failed radiator identification/temperature sensor","Damaged sensor wiring or connector at the radiator","Replacement radiator without coating or without sensor fitted"],["Check engine light","No change in driveability or engine cooling","Possible failed emissions inspection because of the stored code"],2,1,["P2568","P2569","P2570","P2571"],""],P2568:["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2568 is the plausibility check of the sensor on a direct ozone reduction (DOR) radiator, whose coating converts ozone in the cooling air. VW's 2014 specification books for the CC and Tiguan set it on a failed ID check or a failed functional check of the temperature sensor.",["Aftermarket radiator without ozone coating or without the identification sensor","Identification sensor not bonded after radiator replacement","Identification/temperature sensor failed its self-test"],["Check engine light, often after a radiator replacement","No change in driveability or engine cooling","Possible failed emissions inspection"],2,1,["P2567","P2569","P2570","P2571"],""],P2569:["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","P2569 means the radiator-mounted sensor of a DOR system (direct ozone reduction: a radiator coating that breaks down ozone in the incoming air) shows an electrical fault toward ground. According to VW's 2014 data books for the CC with 2.0 L TSI (CBFA, CCTA) and the Tiguan (CCTA), the sensor talks to the engine computer over a LIN line, and P2569 is set when that link fails because the line is grounded.",["LIN wire to the radiator sensor chafed and shorted to ground","Water or salt corrosion in the radiator sensor connector","Internal short in the radiator sensor"],["Check engine light on","No change in driveability or engine temperature","Emissions inspection may be refused"],2,1,["P2567","P2568","P2570","P2571"],""],P256A:["Engine Idle Speed Selector Sensor/Switch Circuit/Open","P256A refers to the switch or sensor with which the driver chooses a raised idle speed, for example to run a generator, an inverter or belt-driven equipment while parked, independent of any PTO. The controller sees no valid state on this input, which points to an open wire, a disconnected plug or a switch that no longer makes contact. No manufacturer documents P256A publicly.",["Open wire in the idle selector circuit","Selector connector loose or not mated","Idle selector switch without contact"],["Raised idle cannot be selected","Engine stays at normal idle"],1,0,["P256B","P256C","P256D","P256E","P0506","P0507"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות סרק מנוע — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P256B:["Engine Idle Speed Selector Sensor/Switch Range/Performance","P256B means the idle speed selector delivers a value that is electrically valid but makes no sense in context. The controller may, for instance, see a raised-idle request with the truck in motion, a position that does not exist, or a request that conflicts with an active PTO mode;",["Sticking or misadjusted idle selector","Aftermarket idle control wired into the same circuit","Idle or PTO configuration changed without matching hardware"],["Raised idle request ignored","Idle selection works only sometimes"],2,0,["P256A","P256C","P256D","P256E","P254B"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות סרק מנוע — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P256C:["Engine Idle Speed Selector Sensor/Switch Circuit Low","P256C says the idle speed selector input is pulled below its lowest valid level, typically by a signal wire shorted to ground or a switch with an internal short. Where the selector is a simple ground-switched input, the controller would read such a short as a permanent request, so a dedicated low code presupposes a coded or monitored circuit. No manufacturer documents P256C publicly.",["Idle selector wire shorted to ground","Internal short in the idle selector"],["Raised idle unavailable","Code returns after every key cycle"],1,0,["P256A","P256B","P256D","P256E","P0507"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות סרק מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל"],P256D:["Engine Idle Speed Selector Sensor/Switch Circuit High","P256D is logged when the idle speed selector signal rises above the highest value the controller treats as valid. Causes include a wire chafed against a battery-fed circuit, an open sensor return that lets the input float high, or an accessory module that drives the line with system voltage. No manufacturer documents P256D publicly.",["Selector wire chafed against a battery-fed circuit","Open return line letting the input float high","Accessory module feeding system voltage into the line"],["Raised idle cannot be selected","Normal driving unaffected"],1,0,["P256A","P256B","P256C","P256E","P0507"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות סרק מנוע — אות גבוה במעגל"],P256E:["Engine Idle Speed Selector Sensor/Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P256E records an idle speed selector signal that drops out or flickers for short moments, more often than real switch use would cause. Since the selector is usually operated with the engine idling for long periods, engine vibration, a worn rocker switch or a loose crimp can be enough; each interruption can cancel the raised idle and make the engine fall back and rise again.",["Worn rocker or toggle switch","Loose crimp or terminal in the selector circuit","Harness moving with engine vibration at idle"],["Raised idle drops out and comes back","Engine speed rises and falls at standstill","Code stored only intermittently"],1,0,["P256A","P256B","P256C","P256D"],"חיישן/מתג בורר מהירות סרק מנוע — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P256F:["A/C Request B Circuit Range/Performance","P256F is the plausibility fault of a second A/C request input, B. Its wiring checks out, yet the engine module finds the state or timing illogical, for instance a request present while the first input and the climate controller say no cooling is wanted, or one that flickers instead of holding steady. Why a vehicle has two request inputs is up to each maker;",["Climate control logic sends inconsistent B request","Intermittent connection on the B request line","Fault in a second evaporator or compressor stage control"],["Rear or second-stage cooling unreliable","Idle dips or surges with A/C operation"],2,0,["P2522","P2523","P2524","P255F"],"בקשת מזגן‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2570:["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Temperature Sensor Circuit High","P2570 is the high-side electrical fault of the sensor fitted to a DOR radiator, the ozone-converting coated radiator found on some low-emission petrol cars. VW's 2014 Tiguan book (2.0 L TSI, CCTA) logs it when LIN communication with the sensor breaks down because the line is interrupted or carries battery voltage; the 2014 CC book applies the same criterion to its CBFA and CCTA engines.",["Sensor not connected or not fitted after radiator replacement","Broken LIN wire or loose terminal","Radiator sensor failed"],["Check engine light, often right after radiator work","Engine runs and cools normally"],2,1,["P2567","P2568","P2569","P2571"],""],P2571:["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2571 stands for an unsteady or intermittently lost signal from the temperature sensor of a direct ozone reduction (DOR) catalyst. Unlike P2569 and P2570, which describe a lasting low or high fault, this code covers readings that jump around or vanish for moments. No manufacturer publicly documents P2571; the VW specification books that use this sensor family list only P2568 to P2570.",["Loose or corroded terminal at the radiator sensor plug","Sensor no longer firmly bonded to the radiator","Harness damaged by vibration at the radiator mounting"],["Check engine light that may come and go","No noticeable effect on driving or cooling"],2,1,["P2567","P2568","P2569","P2570"],""],P2572:["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Deterioration Sensor Circuit","P2572 points to a general fault in the circuit of a sensor meant to judge how much ozone-converting activity is left on a direct ozone reduction (DOR) catalyst, such as a coated radiator. CARB demands a real deterioration check only when the DOR credit is above 5 mg/mi NMOG on LEV III/IV vehicles (or half the NMOG standard on older ones);",["Damaged wiring or connector at the DOR sensor","Failed deterioration sensor","Replacement radiator without the sensor fitted"],["Check engine light on","No effect on engine power or cooling"],2,1,["P2573","P2574","P2575","P2576","P2577"],""],P2573:["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Deterioration Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2573 means the deterioration sensor watching a DOR (direct ozone reduction) catalyst delivers a signal that is electrically within limits but does not fit the expected behaviour, for example a value that never changes with conditions or contradicts other inputs.",["Deterioration sensor drifting or stuck at one value","Non-original radiator with a sensor that does not match","Radiator face heavily fouled, skewing the sensor reading"],["Check engine light after several drive cycles","No change in how the car drives"],2,1,["P2572","P2574","P2575","P2576","P2568"],""],P2574:["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Deterioration Sensor Circuit Low","P2574 is set when the deterioration sensor circuit of a direct ozone reduction (DOR) catalyst reads below its valid range, the usual signature of a short to ground or a failed sensor pulling the line down. No manufacturer documents P2574 publicly. The nearest documented analogue is P2569 on VW's 2.0 L TSI models, where the 2014 Tiguan book attributes a grounded LIN line of the radiator sensor to that code.",["Sensor wire shorted to ground at the radiator","Deterioration sensor failed internally"],["Check engine light on","Car drives and cools as before"],2,1,["P2572","P2573","P2575","P2576"],""],P2575:["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Deterioration Sensor Circuit High","P2575 reports a deterioration-sensor signal above the valid range on a direct ozone reduction (DOR) catalyst - typical for an open circuit, a missing ground or a short to a supply voltage. No vehicle maker has published how it uses P2575, and no service bulletin naming it turned up in the NHTSA index. As an analogy, VW's 2014 CC book sends an open LIN line or a short to battery from the DOR radiator sensor to P2570.",["Connector left off or damaged during radiator work","Broken signal or ground wire","Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage"],["Check engine light on","No change in power or engine temperature"],2,1,["P2572","P2573","P2574","P2576"],""],P2576:["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Deterioration Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2576 describes a deterioration-sensor signal on a direct ozone reduction (DOR) catalyst that comes and goes or jumps without a physical reason, rather than staying low (P2574) or high (P2575). Loose terminals, a cracked connector housing in the airstream ahead of the engine, or chafing where the harness meets the radiator are typical suspects, since that spot sees vibration, spray water and road salt.",["Loose or corroded terminal in the sensor connector","Harness chafing at the radiator support","Cracked connector housing letting water in"],["Check engine light, possibly only now and then","No noticeable driving symptoms"],2,1,["P2572","P2573","P2574","P2575"],""],P2577:["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold","P2577 means the OBD system has concluded that the direct ozone reduction (DOR) catalyst - usually a radiator coated with an ozone-destroying catalyst such as BASF's PremAir - no longer converts enough ozone. CARB ties the threshold to the credit claimed: for LEV III/IV vehicles with a DOR credit of 5 mg/mi NMOG or less, a malfunction is a system with no measurable ozone reduction left;",["Aftermarket radiator without ozone-reducing coating","Catalytic coating worn, damaged or covered with dirt","Faulty DOR sensor giving a false result"],["Check engine light on","No change in engine cooling or performance","Possible failed emissions inspection"],2,1,["P2572","P2573","P2567","P2568"],""],P2578:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Speed Sensor A Circuit","P2578 is the catch-all electrical fault for speed sensor A, the pickup that counts revolutions of the turbocharger or supercharger shaft, normally by sensing a tone feature on the compressor wheel or its nut. The engine computer logs it when the sensor line is faulty in a way it cannot classify as too low, too high or sporadic;",["Loose, corroded or oil-soaked connector at the speed sensor","Harness chafed or heat-damaged near the hot turbocharger housing","Internal failure of speed sensor A","Fault in the engine control module input stage"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Reduced power because boost is limited as a precaution","Turbo speed missing or frozen in live data"],2,3,["P2579","P2580","P2581","P2582","P2593"],"חיישן מהירות מגדש‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2579:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Speed Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","P2579 means speed sensor A delivers a signal, but the shaft speed it reports does not fit the operating state the engine computer expects from boost, airflow and load. PACCAR bulletin E209 for 2017-2019 MX-11 and MX-13 truck engines treats P2579, alone or with P1581, as a fix-as-fail item: the sensor is replaced, because it tends to fail intermittently with a loss of power that disappears when the driver lifts off…",["Speed sensor A dropping out intermittently","Engine software that misjudges the speed plausibility (update available on some models)","Intake or boost leak that makes the shaft speed differ from the model","Mechanical turbocharger problem such as bearing drag or wheel damage"],["Sudden loss of power that returns after lifting off the accelerator","Malfunction indicator lamp on","Turbo speed in live data jumping or inconsistent with boost"],2,3,["P2578","P2580","P2581","P2582","P2594","P0299"],"חיישן מהירות מגדש‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P257A:["Vacuum Reservoir Control Circuit/Open","P257A is an output fault on the control line of the vacuum reservoir, usually a solenoid or switching valve the engine computer uses to connect, isolate or vent a vacuum storage tank. Such tanks occur mainly on diesels whose EGR valves, turbocharger vanes or flaps are worked by vacuum;",["Loose or corroded connector at the reservoir control valve","Broken wire in the control or supply line","Open solenoid coil in the control valve","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Engine warning lamp on","Vacuum-driven actuators such as EGR or turbo vanes respond poorly"],2,1,["P257B","P257C","P2525","P2526"],"מיכל ואקום — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P257B:["Vacuum Reservoir Control Circuit Low","P257B points to a vacuum reservoir control circuit whose voltage is too low, which in practice usually means a ground short on the line between the control unit and the reservoir valve, or a driver stage that cannot hold the line at its proper level. The valve manages a vacuum store used by pneumatic actuators such as EGR valves or turbocharger vanes, mostly on diesel engines.",["Control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Shorted coil in the reservoir control valve","Damaged output stage in the engine control module"],["Engine warning lamp on","Follow-up codes for EGR or turbocharger position"],2,1,["P257A","P257C","P2526"],"מיכל ואקום — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P257C:["Vacuum Reservoir Control Circuit High","P257C sets when the control line of the vacuum reservoir valve reads too high, typically from a short to battery positive or a fault in the driver stage, so the valve can no longer be switched as commanded. The reservoir serves pneumatic actuators on diesel engines;",["Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage line","Internal fault in the reservoir control valve","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Engine warning lamp on","Weaker boost or EGR response in some cases"],2,1,["P257A","P257B","P2528"],"מיכל ואקום — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P257D:["Engine Hood Switch Circuit Range/Performance","P257D is the plausibility fault of the engine hood switch. The line is electrically readable, but the value falls into a band the module regards as impossible, or two redundant switches disagree. Hood status matters because stop-start, hybrid and remote-start logic must never crank the engine while someone is working in the bay.",["Hood switch or plunger worn, misadjusted or contaminated","Fluid or corrosion in the switch or ECM connector shunting the signal","Second hood switch or latch switch reporting a different state","Replacement switch with wrong resistance coding"],["Check engine lamp after two drives","Hood ajar message although the hood is closed","Auto stop-start or remote start not available"],2,1,["P254F","P257E","P257F","P25A3"],"מתג מכסה מנוע מנוע — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P257E:["Engine Hood Switch Circuit Low","P257E says the hood switch signal has dropped below its lowest valid level, which usually means the signal wire touches ground or the switch is shorted inside. GM's 2018 engine table 18OBDG04 sets it for a resistance-coded switch at 325 ohms or less, the 2019 hybrid table 19OBDG01 at 14.6 % of range or less, each with 80 failures in 100 samples and Type B.",["Hood switch signal wire chafed to ground near the latch","Hood switch and horn connectors swapped after front-end repair","Switch shorted internally by water or impact damage"],["Hood ajar indicator on with the hood shut","Engine stop-start inoperative","Check engine lamp on"],2,1,["P257D","P257F","P254F"],"מתג מכסה מנוע מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל"],P257F:["Engine Hood Switch Circuit High","P257F is the high-side counterpart of P257E: the hood switch reading rises above the top limit, which points to an open signal line, a pin that has backed out of its connector, or a short to a voltage source. In GM's 2018 engine table 18OBDG04 the limit for a resistance-coded switch is 3,620 ohms or more, and the 2019 hybrid table 19OBDG01 uses 71.5 % of range;",["Open hood switch signal wire or unplugged switch","Loose or pushed-back pins in a front harness connector","Signal line shorted to a voltage source"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine stop-start stays inactive","Hood warning may be shown or may be missing when the hood is really open"],2,1,["P257D","P257E","P254F"],"מתג מכסה מנוע מנוע — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2580:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Speed Sensor A Circuit Low","P2580 says the signal from turbocharger or supercharger speed sensor A stays at the low end, so the engine computer sees too little or no usable pulse activity - typically from a short to ground, a weak sensor or a pickup that cannot read the target. A Stellantis STAR case from November 2023 for 2022-2024 Ram 2500 to 5500 trucks reports P2580 with the warning lamp, sometimes after few miles;",["Debris on the tone wheel or an extra O-ring in the sensor bore","Signal wire shorted to ground","Speed sensor A with weak or missing output"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Turbo speed reads zero or very low in live data","Possible boost limitation and reduced power"],2,3,["P2578","P2579","P2581","P2582","P2595"],"חיישן מהירות מגדש‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2581:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Speed Sensor A Circuit High","P2581 is set when speed sensor A reports a level above what a healthy circuit can produce, so the engine computer cannot trust it. Typical triggers are a signal wire shorted to the supply or battery voltage, an open signal or ground path that lets the input float high, or a sensor with a shorted output stage. No manufacturer documents P2581 publicly;",["Signal wire shorted to supply or battery voltage","Open ground or signal wire letting the input float high","Speed sensor A with a shorted output"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Implausibly high or fixed turbo speed in live data","Reduced boost and power"],2,3,["P2578","P2579","P2580","P2582","P2596"],"חיישן מהירות מגדש‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2582:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Speed Sensor A Circuit Intermittent","P2582 points to a speed sensor A signal that cuts out or jumps for short moments while being fine in between, so the fault may be gone by the time the vehicle reaches the workshop. Loose terminals, a cracked wire that opens under vibration or heat, and a sensor failing internally when hot are the usual suspects. No manufacturer publishes P2582 under its own code;",["Loose or spread terminal in the sensor connector","Wire break that opens only under vibration or heat","Speed sensor A failing when hot"],["Brief power dips that come and go","Warning lamp that may switch off again","Turbo speed trace with dropouts or spikes"],2,3,["P2578","P2579","P2580","P2581","P2597"],"חיישן מהירות מגדש‏ A — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2583:["Cruise Control Front Distance Range Sensor Single Sensor or Center","P2583 points to the front distance sensor of adaptive cruise control – the only radar, or the centre unit where several are fitted. The engine module keeps the code because adaptive cruise acts directly on engine torque.",["Snow, ice, dirt or a non-approved grille trim in front of the radar","Radar software needing the manufacturer update","Radar misaligned after a knock or bumper repair","Radar unit or its wiring faulty"],["Adaptive cruise control switches off or cannot be engaged","Warning to clean the radar sensor","Collision mitigation braking unavailable, warning lamps on"],2,1,["P2591","P2592"],""],P2584:["Fuel Additive Control Module Requested MIL Illumination","P2584 belongs to diesel cars that add a fuel-borne catalyst to the tank so the particulate filter can burn off soot at lower exhaust temperatures. A separate additive module meters the fluid after each refuelling, in proportion to fuel added, and watches its pump, level sensor and its own circuits. If it finds an emission-relevant fault, it asks the engine module, which owns the lamp, to switch on the MIL;",["Additive reservoir empty or level sensor faulty","Additive dosing pump or injector failed","Additive module wiring, supply or CAN link faulty","Additive quantity counter not reset after refill or filter change"],["Check engine lamp on","Particulate filter warning, regenerations incomplete","Loss of power as soot load rises"],2,3,["P2585","P2463","P2002"],""],P2585:["Fuel Additive Control Module Warning Lamp Request","P2585 is the softer sibling of P2584. Here the fuel additive module asks for a warning lamp other than the MIL – typically a service or particulate filter indicator – because something needs attention before emissions suffer. The classic trigger is a reservoir running low, so the module warns that dosing will soon stop; a refill that was never registered with the scan tool can produce the same request.",["Additive level low, refill due","Refill or new additive bag not registered with the scan tool","Level sensor in the additive reservoir faulty"],["Service or particulate filter warning lamp on","Message about additive level in the instrument cluster"],1,0,["P2584","P2463"],""],P2586:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Circuit","P2586 covers a general electrical fault at position sensor B, which reports where the second boost control actuator stands - the vane mechanism or electric wastegate of a second turbocharger on engines that regulate two of them separately. The engine computer cannot use the feedback, without the fault being pinned down as low (P2588), high (P2589) or sporadic (P2590);",["Connector or terminal fault at the actuator B position sensor","Harness to actuator B damaged by exhaust heat","Position sensor inside actuator B failed (often replaced as a unit)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Reduced power because boost is capped","No valid position value for actuator B in live data"],3,3,["P2587","P2588","P2589","P2590","P2562"],"חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2587:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2587 is a plausibility fault: position sensor B gives an electrically valid reading, but the reported position of the second boost actuator does not follow the command, or the value lies outside what the mechanism can physically reach. No manufacturer documents P2587 publicly, so the logic is known only from sensor A.",["Sticking variable vanes or wastegate linkage on turbo B","Kinked or leaking vacuum line or diaphragm on pneumatic actuators","Actuator rod or adjusting stud out of adjustment or broken","Drifting position sensor B"],["Noticeable loss of power or overboost cut","Malfunction indicator lamp on","Commanded and actual position of actuator B diverge in live data"],3,3,["P2586","P2588","P2589","P2590","P2563"],"חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2588:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Circuit Low","P2588 is stored when the voltage from position sensor B of the second boost actuator drops below the lowest value a working sensor can deliver - most often a grounded signal line or a missing 5 V reference. No manufacturer documents P2588 publicly; the thresholds known for sensor A give the order of magnitude.",["Signal wire of position sensor B shorted to ground","Lost or shorted 5 V reference supply","Failed position sensor B in actuator B"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Power reduced, boost held low","Further sensor codes if a shared reference is shorted"],3,3,["P2586","P2587","P2589","P2590","P2564"],"חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2589:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Circuit High","P2589 means the signal that position sensor B returns for the second boost actuator sits above its plausible maximum, typically from an open signal or ground wire, a short to the reference or battery voltage, or a sensor with a defective output. No manufacturer documents P2589 publicly.",["Open signal or ground wire of position sensor B","Signal wire shorted to reference or battery voltage","Failed position sensor B","Wastegate rod set so the sensor reads at its upper end"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, often on the first trip","Reduced power with boost capped","Position of actuator B stuck near the maximum in live data"],3,3,["P2586","P2587","P2588","P2590","P2565"],"חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P258A:["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit A/Open","P258A stands for an open or otherwise faulty control circuit A of an electric vacuum pump, which supplies the brake booster on engines that provide too little manifold vacuum, such as hybrids, downsized turbo petrol engines and diesels.",["Faulty pump relay, blown fuse or poor relay contact","False entry after a long engine crank while the pump is unpowered","Open wire or loose connector between module, relay and pump","Failed electric vacuum pump"],["Engine or brake warning lamp on","Harder brake pedal at low speed or after several stops","Start-stop function disabled"],2,1,["P258B","P258C","P258D","P25EE","P050F"],""],P258B:["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit A Range/Performance","P258B is the range/performance code for control circuit A of the vacuum pump: the pump is commanded, but its monitoring feedback or the vacuum it produces does not fit. Ford's 2018-2019 hybrid OBD summary sets it from the brake module when the monitoring line sits outside 1.3-5.0 V with the relay off, or below 250 mV for 1 s with the relay on.",["Worn or failed electric vacuum pump","Leaking hose or check valve that makes the pump run too long","Blown pump fuse, spread terminals or poor ground","Outdated engine software controlling pump duty cycle"],["Engine, brake or stability warning lamp on","Hard brake pedal, less brake assist","Start-stop fault message"],2,1,["P258A","P258C","P258D","P25EF","P0556"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת ואקום‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P258C:["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit A Low","P258C reports that control circuit A of the electrically driven vacuum pump reads too low, typically because the control or relay line is shorted to ground, the relay coil is faulty, or a blown supply fuse leaves the monitoring line without voltage. Depending on how the circuit is laid out, the pump may then run nonstop or not at all. No manufacturer publishes P258C itself.",["Control or relay wire shorted to ground","Blown vacuum pump fuse","Faulty pump relay or relay coil"],["Engine or brake warning lamp on","Pump silent or running constantly","Firmer brake pedal"],2,1,["P258A","P258B","P258D","P25F0","P050F"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת ואקום‏ A — ערך נמוך"],P258D:["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit A High","P258D marks a control circuit A of the vacuum pump whose signal sits above the expected range, most often a short to battery positive on the relay or pump control line, so the control unit can no longer switch the pump as it wants. If the pump keeps running, it wears out early; FCA case S1805000006 notes that pumps forced into excessive run time tend to fail.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage line","Pump relay contacts stuck closed","Faulty output stage in the controlling module"],["Engine or brake warning lamp on","Vacuum pump runs continuously, even with the engine off in some cases"],2,1,["P258A","P258B","P258C","P25F1"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת ואקום‏ A — ערך גבוה"],P258E:["PTO Enable Switch Performance","P258E is the plausibility check of the power take-off enable switch. The line is not open or shorted – those faults are P251A to P251C – but the state of the switch does not fit the other PTO inputs, for instance an enable request without a valid arming step or contact signals that contradict each other.",["PTO switch contacts worn or contaminated, mode signals disagree","Upfitter wiring or load-engage switch interfering with the enable input","Remote enable used without arming sequence or with wrong switch type","PTO module configuration not matching the installed switches"],["PTO cannot be switched on or switches off unexpectedly","Driver information message about PTO conditions"],2,0,["P251A","P251B","P251C"],"מתג אפשור PTO — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P258F:["Torque Management Request Output Signal","P258F concerns the sending side of a torque management link. One controller – for example the engine module talking to a transmission or hybrid controller, or the reverse – transmits torque requests and finds that its own output is faulty, missing or not accepted by the receiver.",["CAN wiring or connector fault between the modules","Software levels of sending and receiving module do not match","Low voltage or poor ground at one of the modules","Sending control module internally faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","Harsh or delayed shifts","Reduced engine power"],3,3,["P2544","P2545","P0700"],"אות יציאת בקשת ניהול מומנט"],P2590:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2590 is set when the position signal of the second boost actuator flickers, jumps or drops out for short moments instead of being steadily wrong. Unlike its sensor A counterpart P2566, this code is defined as intermittent/erratic, so an unsteady signal without full dropouts falls under it as well. No manufacturer documents P2590 publicly.",["Loose terminal or intermittent contact in the sensor B connector","Sensor track worn by vibration, giving a noisy signal","Chafed harness that shorts or opens briefly"],["Power surging or dropping intermittently","Warning lamp that may come and go","Jumping position value for actuator B in live data"],3,3,["P2586","P2587","P2588","P2589","P2566"],"חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2591:["Cruise Control Front Distance Range Sensor Left","P2591 is reserved for the left front distance sensor in cruise systems that combine several radars across the front; a single or centre unit uses P2583 and the right one P2592. No manufacturer documents P2591 publicly. Honda's bulletins on P2583 show what such a sensor typically reports: a view blocked by ice or dirt, or a misalignment the unit detects itself.",["Bumper cover damaged, replaced or repainted over the left sensor","Left sensor bracket bent, sensor aimed wrongly","Ice, mud or stickers covering the sensor area","Sensor or wiring to the left corner faulty"],["Adaptive cruise control not available","Driver assistance warning message"],3,0,["P2583","P2592"],"שמאלי חיישן טווח מרחק קדמי בקרת שיוט"],P2592:["Cruise Control Front Distance Range Sensor Right","P2592 marks a fault of the right-hand front distance sensor in multi-radar adaptive cruise layouts; the left unit reports P2591, a single or centre radar P2583. No maker publishes this code. Compared with a radar behind the grille emblem, a right corner sensor is more exposed to kerb and parking contact, stone chips and road salt reaching its connector, and it is often disturbed when a bumper is replaced on the…",["Right sensor knocked out of alignment by kerb or parking contact","Road salt or water corrosion at the right sensor connector","Sensor not recalibrated after bumper replacement","Right radar sensor internally faulty"],["Adaptive cruise control switched off","Warning message for the radar or driver assistance system"],3,0,["P2583","P2591"],"ימני חיישן טווח מרחק קדמי בקרת שיוט"],P2593:["Turbocharger Speed Sensor B Circuit","P2593 concerns the second turbocharger speed sensor, found where an engine has two turbochargers, for example one per cylinder bank. It marks an electrical fault on that sensor's circuit that is not further classified; the specific forms are P2595 (low), P2596 (high) and P2597 (intermittent), while P2594 covers a plausibility error. Sensor A is reported separately under P2578-P2582.",["Connector problem at speed sensor B","Harness to the second turbocharger damaged by heat or chafing","Internal failure of speed sensor B"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Power reduced, often only slightly with one turbo affected","No speed value for the second turbo in live data"],2,3,["P2594","P2595","P2596","P2597","P2578"],"חיישן מהירות מגדש טורבו‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2594:["Turbocharger Speed Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2594 means the second turbocharger speed sensor produces a signal, but its reported speed does not agree with what the engine computer predicts for that turbo. Bentley documents it on the W12 in the Continental GT/GTC, Flying Spur and Bentayga (bulletin 2053348, versions 5 and 10): after a smoke test of intake and exhaust, a detached divider inside the air filter box on Continental and Flying Spur turned out to be…",["Speed sensor B delivering an implausible signal","Detached divider in the air filter box disturbing the flow to one turbo","Intake or exhaust leak on the bank of the second turbo"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Fault often appears only under particular load or gradient conditions","Turbo speeds of both banks differ noticeably in live data"],3,3,["P2593","P2595","P2596","P2597","P2579"],"חיישן מהירות מגדש טורבו‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2595:["Turbocharger Speed Sensor B Circuit Low","P2595 is logged when the signal of turbocharger speed sensor B stays below the range the engine computer accepts, as with a short to ground or a sensor whose output has collapsed. Bentley names it for the W12 in Continental GT, GTC and Flying Spur from 2018 and later also in the Bentayga, stored in engine control unit 1 or 2.",["Speed sensor B with collapsed output","Signal wire of sensor B shorted to ground","Corroded or contaminated connector at sensor B"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Speed of the second turbo shown as zero or very low","Possible reduction of boost"],3,3,["P2593","P2594","P2596","P2597","P2580"],"חיישן מהירות מגדש טורבו‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2596:["Turbocharger Speed Sensor B Circuit High","With P2596 the engine computer sees the line of turbocharger speed sensor B sitting above its valid window - the usual pattern for a signal shorted to supply voltage, an interrupted ground or a defective sensor output. The code was added to Bentley's W12 speed-sensor bulletin in its later revision (2053348/10, December 2022), which also brought in the Bentayga;",["Signal wire of sensor B shorted to supply or battery voltage","Interrupted ground of sensor B","Defective output stage of speed sensor B"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Implausibly high speed for the second turbo in live data","Possible boost reduction"],3,3,["P2593","P2594","P2595","P2597","P2581"],"חיישן מהירות מגדש טורבו‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2597:["Turbocharger Speed Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","P2597 records short interruptions or jumps in the signal of the second turbocharger speed sensor, between which the circuit works normally. Such faults usually sit in a connector, a wire that breaks contact under engine movement or heat soak, or a sensor that drops out when hot. No manufacturer documents P2597 publicly.",["Loose terminal or poor pin contact at sensor B","Wire breaking contact under engine movement or heat soak","Speed sensor B dropping out when hot"],["Occasional warning lamp, sometimes only after long drives","Short power dips under load","Dropouts in the speed trace of the second turbo"],3,3,["P2593","P2594","P2595","P2596","P2582"],"חיישן מהירות מגדש טורבו‏ B — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2598:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Performance - Stuck Low","P2598 means the boost control position of turbocharger A, normally the vane or wastegate position reported by the actuator, appears stuck toward its low end: the measured value no longer follows the command although the signal is electrically valid.",["Sooted or seized variable vanes that no longer follow the actuator","Vacuum leak or kinked hose on pneumatically driven actuators","Worn or failed electric vane actuator","One-off entry from unusual operation, e.g. after delivery transport"],["Engine warning lamp on","Lack of power under load, boost limited","Unusual turbo noise"],3,3,["P2599","P259A","P2563","P003A","P0046"],""],P2599:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Performance - Stuck High","P2599 is the high-side stuck fault for position sensor A: the turbocharger actuator stays at, or reports, a position beyond where it should be, while the sensor circuit itself works. GM documents it twice. On the 2014 Cruze 2.0 L diesel the ECM compares commanded and actual vane position and logs P2599 when the deviation runs past 10 % in the direction opposite to P2598 for 10 s.",["Vanes or wastegate stuck toward the closed position by soot or corrosion","Weak return spring or binding linkage that keeps the actuator from its rest position","Vacuum control solenoid or hose fault on pneumatic actuators","Defective actuator electronics on smart actuators"],["Engine warning lamp on","Overboost cut-out or noticeable power reduction","Black smoke or rough response under load"],3,3,["P2598","P259B","P2563","P0046","P0234"],""],P259A:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Performance - Stuck Low","P259A applies to engines with a second boost control actuator, for instance a twin-turbo layout or the second stage of a two-stage system, whose position is read by sensor B. The code is stored when that actuator's reported position stays at the low end and stops tracking the command even though the signal is electrically sound. No manufacturer documents P259A publicly.",["Sticking vanes, flap or wastegate on charger B","Weak vacuum or electrical supply to actuator B","Worn actuator B or misadjusted linkage"],["Engine warning lamp on","Weak acceleration, notably in the range where charger B works"],3,3,["P259B","P2598","P2587","P2586"],""],P259B:["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Performance - Stuck High","P259B is logged when the boost control actuator watched by position sensor B is found stuck at the high end of its travel, or fails to return to its rest position, while the sensor signal itself is plausible. A sensor B exists mainly on twin-turbo or two-stage engines. No manufacturer publishes P259B.",["Mechanism of charger B seized toward the closed or high position","Return spring or linkage of actuator B binding","Vacuum solenoid or hose of actuator B faulty (pneumatic systems)"],["Engine warning lamp on","Power cut-out under full load to prevent overboost"],3,3,["P259A","P2599","P2587","P2586"],""],P259C:["Excessive Time To Enter Closed Loop Turbocharger A Boost Control","P259C reports that closed-loop boost control of turbocharger A was not reached within the expected time after its enabling conditions were met. Instead of trimming the actuator from boost or position feedback, the controller stays in open-loop or default mode.",["Boost pressure or actuator position sensor fault that blocks closed-loop control","Actuator A fault, often with its own stored code","Charge air leak preventing boost from reaching the range where control starts","Engine control software issue"],["Engine warning lamp on","Sluggish or uneven boost build-up"],2,3,["P259D","P2263","P0046","P0236"],""],P259D:["Excessive Time To Enter Closed Loop Turbocharger B Boost Control","P259D is the turbocharger B version of the closed-loop timing fault. On engines with two separately regulated chargers, the control unit expects the boost regulation of the second unit to switch to feedback operation within a set time, and here it did not. No manufacturer documents P259D publicly with thresholds;",["Fault on position or pressure sensing for charger B","Actuator B or its control circuit faulty","Leak in the charge air path of charger B"],["Engine warning lamp on","Reduced power, especially at higher load"],2,3,["P259C","P2587","P2586"],""],P259E:["Turbocharger A Boost Control Position At Low Limit","P259E means the boost control of turbocharger A has run out of range at the low end: the actuator is at its limit, yet boost stays well under the target. Ford's 2023 diesel OBD summary places it in the underboost monitor.",["Leak in charge air pipes, intercooler or clamps","Variable vane actuator or vane mechanism not reaching the commanded position","Exhaust leak upstream of the turbine","Boost pressure sensor reading too low"],["Engine warning lamp on","Clear loss of power under load","Whistling or hissing from the charge air side"],2,3,["P259F","P25A0","P2263","P0299","P2598"],""],P259F:["Turbocharger A Boost Control Position At High Limit","P259F is the counterpart of P259E: the regulation of turbocharger A has hit its upper limit, and measured boost runs above the value the engine computer asked for. In Ford's 2023 diesel OBD summary it is the overboost monitor, checked continuously between 800 (6.7 L) or 1300 rpm (3.0 L) and 4000 rpm with at least 50 or 135 Nm of torque;",["Vanes or wastegate stuck toward the closed position","Actuator or its vacuum/electrical control not opening as commanded","Engine control software needing an update","Boost pressure sensor reading too high"],["Engine warning lamp on","Sudden power cut at high load"],2,3,["P259E","P25A1","P0234","P2599"],""],P25A0:["Turbocharger B Boost Control Position At Low Limit","P25A0 says the regulator of turbocharger B has run to its low limit without reaching the boost target, so the second charger delivers too little pressure even with full control authority. It only exists on engines where two chargers are regulated separately. No manufacturer documents P25A0 publicly.",["Leak in the charge air path served by charger B","Wastegate or vanes of charger B not closing as commanded","Worn or damaged charger B"],["Engine warning lamp on","Lower power than usual, uneven pull"],2,3,["P25A1","P259E","P259A"],""],P25A1:["Turbocharger B Boost Control Position At High Limit","P25A1 is set when the boost control for turbocharger B is pinned at its upper limit and still cannot bring pressure down to the requested value, so the second charger overshoots. Like P25A0 it is limited to engines with two individually controlled chargers, and no manufacturer has published its own criteria for P25A1.",["Wastegate or vanes of charger B stuck toward closed","Blocked, leaking or misrouted control line of actuator B","Boost pressure sensor giving wrong values"],["Engine warning lamp on","Power cut-out at high load"],2,3,["P25A0","P259F","P259B"],""],P25A2:["Brake System Control Module A Requested MIL Illumination","P25A2 is a messenger code: the brake system control module has stored an emission-relevant fault of its own and asks the engine module to light the check engine lamp. GM's 2017 engine table 17OBDG04 and 2019 hybrid table 19OBDG01 watch this request continuously from three seconds after power-up and class the engine module entry itself as Type A without a separate lamp request, because the lamp is already on the…",["Emission-relevant fault stored in the brake control module","Weak battery or low system voltage upsetting the brake module","Brake or related module software needing an update","Lost communication with a partner module such as the front camera"],["Check engine lamp on","ABS, stability or driver assistance warnings at the same time","Brake pedal may feel soft in some cases"],3,1,["P25C9","P2561"],""],P25A3:["Engine Hood Open","P25A3 is a state code, not a wiring fault: the hood is reported open at a moment when the control strategy expects it closed, for example while an automatic restart, a remote start or a hybrid engine pull-up is pending. No manufacturer documents P25A3 publicly.",["Hood only on the safety catch, not fully latched","Hood switch or striker misadjusted after body work","Latch-integrated switch sticking in the open position"],["Hood open warning in the cluster","Auto stop-start and remote start locked out","Engine keeps running at standstill instead of stopping"],1,0,["P254F","P257D","P257E"],"מכסה מנוע מנוע — נתק"],P25A4:["Fuel Mode Select Switch Circuit","P25A4 is the general circuit fault for the fuel mode select switch – the button on bi-fuel vehicles with which the driver chooses between gasoline and an alternative fuel such as CNG or LPG. GM's 2015 bi-fuel Impala, described in PI1330, has it on the instrument panel left of the steering wheel; on the 2016 Silverado and Sierra 2500HD CNG trucks it sits in the centre stack and carries the fuel indicator.",["Open wire or unplugged connector at the fuel mode switch","Fuel mode switch failed internally","Faulty connection in a bi-fuel conversion harness"],["Fuel cannot be changed with the switch","Engine runs on gasoline only","Fuel indicator light on the switch dark or flashing"],2,1,["P25A5","P25A6","P25A7","P25A8"],"מתג בחירת מצב דלק — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P25A5:["Fuel Mode Select Switch Performance","P25A5 flags a performance problem with the fuel mode select switch. The circuit is electrically sound, yet the switch behaves in a way that cannot be genuine, such as a momentary button that appears to be held down for minutes or a press that never returns to rest. On GM's bi-fuel trucks the chosen mode is kept across key cycles and each press toggles the fuel, so a stuck contact would keep requesting changes;",["Switch button sticking or contaminated by liquid","Panel trim pressing on the switch after installation work","Replacement switch of the wrong type or coding"],["Fuel mode changes by itself or not at all","Switch indicator keeps flashing"],1,1,["P25A4","P25A6","P25A7","P25A8"],"מתג בחירת מצב דלק — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P25A6:["Fuel Mode Select Switch Circuit Low","P25A6 means the fuel mode select switch signal has fallen below the range the module accepts. On a switch that pulls a reference line towards ground when pressed, this is the signature of a signal wire rubbed through to the body or of moisture bridging the switch contacts; a grounded line could otherwise pass for a button held forever.",["Switch signal wire chafed to ground behind the dash","Moisture or spilt liquid bridging the switch contacts","Switch shorted internally"],["Fuel mode cannot be changed","Vehicle remains in one fuel mode"],2,1,["P25A4","P25A5","P25A7","P25A8"],"מתג בחירת מצב דלק — אות נמוך במעגל"],P25A7:["Fuel Mode Select Switch Circuit High","P25A7 reports a fuel mode select switch signal above the accepted window. With a pull-up input this mostly means the switch never closes its path – an open signal or return wire, a connector half off, a broken switch – or that the line has contact with a supply voltage, for example where an alternative-fuel conversion tapped into nearby wiring. No manufacturer documents P25A7 publicly;",["Open signal or return wire, connector not seated","Signal wire touching a supply voltage, e.g. after aftermarket wiring","Switch contact broken open"],["Switch has no effect","Fuel indicator on the switch may stay dark"],2,1,["P25A4","P25A5","P25A6","P25A8"],"מתג בחירת מצב דלק — אות גבוה במעגל"],P25A8:["Fuel Mode Select Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P25A8 records a fuel mode select switch signal that jumps or drops out briefly instead of staying in a stable state. The module sees transitions it cannot attribute to a real press, often while driving over rough roads, which points to a loose terminal, a cracked solder joint in the switch or a harness rubbing behind the trim.",["Loose terminal or poor contact at the switch connector","Cracked solder joint inside the switch","Harness rubbing behind the trim and shorting briefly"],["Occasional unexpected fuel mode changes","Switch light flickers","Code returns sporadically after clearing"],2,1,["P25A4","P25A5","P25A6","P25A7"],"מתג בחירת מצב דלק — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P25A9:["Piston Cooling Oil Control Circuit/Open","P25A9 covers the electrical circuit of the piston cooling oil control valve, the solenoid that switches the oil jets spraying the underside of the pistons. Under load the jets protect the pistons; when the engine is cold or lightly loaded they can be shut off to warm up faster and save oil pump work.",["Piston cooling valve coil open","Valve connector unplugged, corroded or wire broken","Harness damaged by heat near the engine block","Output driver in the engine control module faulty"],["Check engine lamp on after two drives","Possible power reduction to protect the pistons"],2,3,["P25AA","P25AB","P25AC","P25AD"],"שמן קירור בוכנה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P25AA:["Piston Cooling Oil Control Circuit Low","P25AA flags a voltage at the piston cooling oil control valve output that sits too low for the commanded state, typically a short to ground between the module and the valve. This valve decides whether the oil jets under the pistons spray.",["Valve control wire chafed through and touching ground","Internal short in the piston cooling valve","Water or oil in the valve connector bridging the pins","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp after two drives","Possible power limitation to protect the pistons"],2,3,["P25A9","P25AB","P25AC","P25AD"],"שמן קירור בוכנה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P25AB:["Piston Cooling Oil Control Circuit High","P25AB is the counterpart on the supply side: the control line of the piston cooling oil valve is pulled toward battery voltage. In GM's 18OBDG04 diesel table the check runs while the low-side driver is switched on;",["Control wire pinched against a live supply wire","Valve side of the circuit shorted to its own supply","Damaged or contaminated valve connector","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp after two drives","Piston cooling jets no longer switched","Possible reduced engine power"],2,3,["P25A9","P25AA","P25AC","P25AD"],"שמן קירור בוכנה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P25AC:["Piston Cooling Oil Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P25AC is a functional fault rather than a wiring one: the valve is told to let oil reach the piston jets, but the feedback shows no flow. GM's 18OBDG04 diesel table reads a pressure switch in the jet circuit and fails the test when that switch stays without pressure while the engine turns, main oil pressure is at least 206 kPa and the command has been held for 8 s or more; 40 of 50 samples must fail, Type B.",["Valve jammed by swarf or dirt in the oil","Piston cooling pressure switch faulty or unplugged","Low oil level or weak oil pressure feeding the jet circuit","Restricted oil passage to the jets"],["Check engine lamp after two drives","Engine power reduced under high load","Risk of piston damage if driven hard for long periods"],3,3,["P25A9","P25AD","P25AE"],"מעגל בקרת שמן קירור בוכנה — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P25AD:["Piston Cooling Oil Control Circuit Stuck On","P25AD describes the reverse mechanical failure: the piston cooling valve ought to be shut, yet oil keeps reaching the jets. GM's diesel table 18OBDG04 detects it when the pressure switch in the jet circuit reports pressure although the valve has been commanded to its off state for at least 8 s, with the engine turning and main oil pressure of at least 206 kPa; 40 bad samples out of 50 make it a Type B fault.",["Valve held open by debris","Broken return spring in the valve","Piston cooling pressure switch stuck in the pressure position"],["Check engine lamp after two drives","Longer warm-up in cold weather","Slightly lower oil pressure reading at idle"],3,1,["P25A9","P25AC","P25AA"],"שמן קירור בוכנה — מעגל הבקרה תקוע במצב פעיל"],P25AE:["Piston Cooling Oil Pressure Too Low","P25AE means the oil pressure reaching the piston cooling jets is below what the engine controller requires, even though the valve circuit itself shows no electrical fault. Volvo and Mack heavy trucks store it as P25AE00.",["Low oil level or oil starvation under hard load","Oil temperature sensor reading wrong (Volvo/Mack bulletin)","Worn oil pump or leaking pressure relief valve","Clogged oil filter or piston cooling jets"],["Inactive code after heavy pulling","Low oil pressure warning at the same time","Engine derate possible"],3,3,["P25AC","P25A9","P0520","P0524"],"לחץ שמן קירור בוכנה — ערך נמוך מדי"],P25AF:["Coolant Temperature Control Module Requested MIL Illumination","P25AF is a messenger code. A separate coolant temperature control module, used on some vehicles with electrically managed cooling for engine, battery or power electronics, has stored an emission-relevant fault of its own and asks the engine module to turn on the check engine lamp. CARB's OBD II rule expects lamp requests from other powertrain units to be passed on reliably.",["Emission-relevant fault stored in the coolant temperature control module","Faulty coolant valve, pump or sensor handled by that module","Thermal module software needing an update"],["Check engine lamp on","Possible temperature warnings or reduced heating"],3,1,["P25A2","P25C9","P0700","P2561"],""],P25B0:["Fuel Level Sensor A Stuck","P25B0 means the main fuel level sender keeps reporting the same level although the engine has clearly been burning fuel. Ford runs this as a continuous check: the module totals the fuel injected, converts it into a share of tank capacity and compares that with how far the sender reading has moved.",["Float arm caught on the tank wall, baffle or pump module","Worn spot on the sender resistor track holding the wiper at one value","Float soaked with fuel and sunk to the bottom","Fuel consumption calculation in the PCM not matching the tank"],["Fuel gauge stays at the same mark over a long distance","Engine runs out of fuel while the gauge still shows fuel","Check engine lamp on"],2,1,["P25B1","P25B2","P0460","P0461","P25DC"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ A — תקוע"],P25B1:["Fuel Level Sensor B Stuck","P25B1 points at the second fuel level sender, the one found in the passive half of a saddle tank or in an additional tank. Its reading no longer changes in step with the fuel actually burned. Ford applies the same consumption comparison as for sender A, with mismatch limits between 25 % and 60 % depending on the frozen level, and the 2024 summary maps this fault to P2065 with failure type 2A.",["Float of sender B jammed or resistor track worn","Jet pump or its line no longer drawing fuel from the passive tank half","Blocked or kinked transfer line between the tank chambers"],["Gauge reading too high or barely falling as the tank empties","Engine stalls from fuel starvation with an apparently quarter-full tank","Check engine lamp on"],2,1,["P25B0","P25B2","P2065","P2066","P25DC"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ B — תקוע"],P25B2:["Fuel Level Sensor A or B Stuck","P25B2 is the shared variant for tanks with two senders: the module has found that the level information is frozen but does not commit to which of the two senders is responsible. Ford lists it next to P25B0 and P25B1 under the same consumption-versus-reading check (100 to 120 miles, 25 to 60 % allowed mismatch) and, unlike the other two, keeps P25B2 as its own base code in the 2024 summary with failure type 00.",["One of the two senders mechanically stuck","Fuel no longer moved between tank halves by the jet pump","Corroded connector on the tank unit freezing one signal"],["Gauge stuck or moving far less than fuel used","Range display unreliable","Check engine lamp on"],2,1,["P25B0","P25B1","P0460","P2065"],""],P25B3:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate A Stuck Open","P25B3 says the wastegate of turbocharger A stays further open than the module commands, so exhaust bypasses the turbine and boost falls short. On Ford EcoBoost engines with an electric wastegate actuator and position sensor, the PCM compares commanded and measured position; a gap above 20 mm held for 2.5 s sets the code, provided no circuit fault (P0243, P2ABD) is present.",["Missing retaining clip disconnecting actuator rod from the wastegate lever","Electric wastegate actuator failed or rod bent","Wastegate flap or bushing seized in the open position by heat or carbon","Diagnostic calibration needing an update (Toyota GR Corolla)"],["Clearly reduced power and slow boost build-up","Check engine lamp on, often with an underboost code","Wrench or reduced power warning on some models"],3,3,["P25B4","P25B5","P0243","P0299","P2AB7","P2AB8","P2AB9","P2ABD"],"שסתום Wastegate של המגדש‏ A — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P25B4:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate A Stuck Closed","P25B4 is the reverse of P25B3: the module asked wastegate A to open, yet the valve stays shut or opens far too little. Ford uses the same position comparison for both directions (error over 20 mm for 2.5 s); in 2024 it appears as P0243 with failure type 73. Other makers infer the fault from pressure. Porsche explains that its DME judges the wastegate by the boost building up ahead of the throttle;",["Wastegate flap or spindle seized shut by carbon or corrosion","Actuator or linkage unable to move the valve","False detection by engine software (Porsche Cayenne, Audi RS 5)","Internal turbocharger fault requiring replacement (Ford SSM 50670)"],["Power reduced because the module limits boost","Possible overboost code alongside","Check engine lamp on"],3,3,["P25B3","P25B6","P0243","P0234","P2AB8","P2AB9"],"שסתום Wastegate של המגדש‏ A — תקוע במצב סגור"],P25B5:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate B Stuck Open","P25B5 concerns wastegate B, which on twin-turbo V engines belongs to the second turbocharger, normally on the other cylinder bank. The valve remains open beyond what the PCM commands, so this turbo delivers too little boost while the A side may work normally.",["PCM software needing reprogramming (Ford TSB 23-2353)","Wastegate B linkage loose or disconnected","Actuator B failed or its position sensor reading wrong","Flap of wastegate B seized open"],["Reduced power, especially when accelerating under load","Check engine lamp and/or wrench indicator on"],3,3,["P25B6","P25B3","P0247","P0299","P2ABA","P2ABB","P2ABC","P2ABE"],"שסתום Wastegate של המגדש‏ B — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P25B6:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate B Stuck Closed","With P25B6 the second wastegate refuses to open when commanded, so turbo B cannot be regulated down and may push boost beyond the target; the module then usually caps torque. Ford detects it with the B-side position comparison (over 20 mm for 2.5 s, no P0247 or P2ABE present) and in 2024 files it as P0247 with type 73.",["Loose nut on the turbo actuator arm (Ford Bronco TSB 24-2112)","Wastegate B flap or spindle seized shut","PCM software needing reprogramming (Ford TSB 23-2353)","Actuator B unable to drive the valve open"],["Power limited, sometimes after a short boost spike","Check engine lamp on, possibly with P0299 or an overboost code"],3,3,["P25B5","P25B4","P0247","P0234","P0299","P2ABB","P2ABC"],"שסתום Wastegate של המגדש‏ B — תקוע במצב סגור"],P25B7:["Auxiliary Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit","P25B7 covers the hard-wired input from an auxiliary ignition switch that commands the On and Start positions from a second location, for example a rear panel behind the cab, a work platform or a remote station on a chassis-cab truck. The module flags a state on this line it cannot interpret, such as an open circuit, without saying whether the level is too low or too high. No manufacturer documents P25B7 publicly.",["Open wire or loose connector in the harness to the body or remote panel","Worn or corroded contacts in the auxiliary switch","Faulty or modified upfitter wiring","Input stage of the reading module damaged"],["Engine cannot be started or switched on from the auxiliary position","Normal key or push-button start still works","Stored code, often without other complaints"],2,0,["P25B8","P25B9","P2533"],""],P25B8:["Auxiliary Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit Low","P25B8 means the auxiliary On/Start input sits at a low level when the module expects it to be active, or never rises when the remote switch is operated. Typical reasons are a switch contact that no longer closes, a blown fuse feeding the remote panel, a broken wire in the long harness run to the body or a short to ground at a frame connector.",["Blown fuse or failed relay feeding the auxiliary switch","Signal wire shorted to ground on the frame or body","Auxiliary switch contact no longer closes","Corroded exterior connector with high resistance"],["Remote start or on request is ignored","Engine may shut down when the auxiliary position is used to keep it running","Remote panel indicator stays dark"],2,0,["P25B7","P25B9","P2534"],""],P25B9:["Auxiliary Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit High","With P25B9 the module sees the auxiliary On/Start line at a high level when it ought to be inactive, for example after key-off or with no request from the remote panel. A switch stuck in the start position, a wire rubbing against a battery feed, backfeed through an upfitter relay or moisture bridging terminals in an exterior switch box can all hold the line up.",["Signal wire chafed against a battery or ignition feed","Auxiliary switch stuck in the On/Start position","Backfeed through an upfitter relay or accessory","Moisture in an exterior switch box or connector"],["Battery drains overnight because modules stay awake","Auxiliary start function disabled or behaving erratically","Starter may engage or click unexpectedly"],2,0,["P25B7","P25B8","P2535"],""],P25BA:["Regeneration Control Switch Circuit/Open","P25BA concerns the dash or panel switch with which the driver starts, or on some trucks blocks, a diesel particulate filter regeneration. The engine controller reads the switch as a discrete input and sets this code when the circuit is open or otherwise unusable, so a press no longer reaches it.",["Switch connector loose or unplugged behind the dash","Broken signal or reference wire to the switch","Internal open circuit in the regeneration switch"],["Parked regeneration cannot be started when the cluster asks for it","Filter or regeneration warning lamp stays on longer than usual","Check engine lamp"],1,1,["P25BB","P25BC","P2459"],"מתג בקרת התחדשות (רגנרציה) — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P25BB:["Regeneration Control Switch Circuit Low","P25BB reports that the regeneration switch input reads a low level the switch itself cannot produce. Depending on the wiring, this points to a short to ground in the harness, a contact that is permanently closed to ground or a damaged switch module.",["Switch signal wire shorted to ground","Switch contact stuck closed","Switch panel damaged by liquid or impact"],["Regeneration switch has no effect","Parked regeneration may be unavailable when soot load is high","Check engine lamp"],1,1,["P25BA","P25BC","P2463"],"מתג בקרת התחדשות (רגנרציה) — אות נמוך במעגל"],P25BC:["Regeneration Control Switch Circuit High","P25BC is the high-voltage counterpart: the regeneration switch line carries a level near supply voltage that no switch position can produce. A wire chafed against a battery or ignition feed, water in a switch connector or a switch whose internal resistor network has failed are plausible causes. If the switch requests regeneration by pulling the line up, a stuck high could resemble a permanent start command.",["Switch signal wire shorted to battery or ignition voltage","Moisture in the switch connector","Internal fault in the switch or its resistor network"],["Regeneration switch ignored by the engine controller","Unexpected regeneration messages in the cluster","Check engine lamp"],1,1,["P25BA","P25BB","P2459"],"מתג בקרת התחדשות (רגנרציה) — אות גבוה במעגל"],P25BD:["Unmetered Fuel - Forced Engine Shutdown","P25BD protects against engine runaway, where the engine keeps speeding up although the controller injects no fuel, for instance because oil from a failed turbocharger seal or combustible vapour drawn into the intake is being burned. GM documents the monitor in its diesel ECM tables.",["Turbocharger seal failure feeding oil into the intake","Oil carry-over from crankcase ventilation, e.g. overfilled or diluted oil","Combustible vapour drawn in from the surroundings","Erroneous engine speed signal or controller fault"],["Engine revs up uncontrollably and then shuts off","Heavy smoke from the exhaust before shutdown","Check engine lamp on immediately","Possible severe engine damage after the event"],4,3,["P0219"],""],P25BE:["Alternative Fuel Disable Control Circuit/Open","P25BE concerns the output with which the engine controller tells an alternative fuel system, usually a CNG or LPG installation, to stop gas operation, for example after a fault, with an empty gas tank or while the engine warms up. The code reports an open circuit or a driver fault on this control line, so the command may no longer reach the gas controller or its shut-off valves.",["Open control wire between engine controller and gas system","Poor splice or connector in a retrofit gas installation","Open coil in a gas disable relay","Output driver in the engine controller defective"],["Vehicle stays on gasoline or will not switch to gas","Fuel mode indicator flashes or shows a system fault","Check engine lamp"],2,3,["P25BF","P25C0","P25C1","P25A4"],""],P25BF:["Alternative Fuel Disable Control Circuit High","P25BF flags a voltage on the alternative fuel disable output that is too high for the state the engine controller is commanding. On a low-side driver this usually means a short to battery or ignition voltage, for instance where a gas kit harness has been routed along a hot feed or tapped into the wrong wire.",["Control wire shorted to battery or ignition voltage","Retrofit gas kit tapped into the wrong circuit","Faulty input stage in the gas controller backfeeding voltage"],["Gas operation blocked, vehicle runs on gasoline only","Fuel mode indicator flashes","Check engine lamp"],2,3,["P25BE","P25C0","P25C2"],""],P25C0:["Alternative Fuel Disable Control Circuit Low","P25C0 is set when the alternative fuel disable output reads too low, typically a short to ground somewhere between the engine controller and the gas system. With a high-side driver that pin would then be unable to deliver its voltage; with a low-side driver the line would look permanently switched.",["Control wire shorted to ground, often where routed along the frame","Chafed insulation on a retrofit gas kit harness","Output stage in the engine controller damaged"],["Vehicle refuses to switch to gas","Fuel system fault message or flashing fuel indicator","Check engine lamp"],2,3,["P25BE","P25BF","P25C3"],""],P25C1:["Alternative Fuel Disable Signal Circuit","P25C1 relates to the incoming side of the alternative fuel disable function: a signal line on which the engine controller reads whether gas operation is blocked, either as feedback from the gas system or as a request from it, for example when a CNG or LPG controller detects low tank pressure or its own fault. The code says the signal is missing or unusable without naming a direction.",["Open signal wire from the gas system","Gas controller without power or ground, so no signal is sent","Corroded underbody connector of the gas system"],["Gas mode unavailable or drops out while driving","Fuel mode indicator flashes","Check engine lamp"],2,3,["P25C2","P25C3","P25BE","P25A4"],""],P25C2:["Alternative Fuel Disable Signal Circuit High","P25C2 means the alternative fuel disable signal arriving at the engine controller sits above its valid range. Likely explanations are a short to a voltage feed, a missing ground at the gas controller that lets its output float up, or an open line combined with an internal pull-up in the reading module.",["Signal wire shorted to a voltage feed","Missing ground at the gas controller letting its output float high","Open signal wire pulled up inside the reading module"],["Vehicle stays on gasoline","Gas system fault indication","Check engine lamp"],2,3,["P25C1","P25C3","P25BF"],""],P25C3:["Alternative Fuel Disable Signal Circuit Low","P25C3 is logged when the alternative fuel disable signal reaching the engine controller is too low to be valid. A short to ground on the way from the gas system, a gas controller that has lost its supply, or a damaged output stage in that controller can each pull the line down.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","Gas controller without supply voltage","Damaged output stage in the gas controller"],["No change-over to gas operation","Fuel mode indicator flashes or shows a fault","Check engine lamp"],2,3,["P25C1","P25C2","P25C0"],""],P25C4:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor A Circuit","P25C4 covers the first temperature sensor of an electromechanical brake booster, in which an electric motor and gear set take the place of the vacuum diaphragm, as in Bosch's iBooster. The booster electronics use this value to protect motor and control unit from overheating during long or repeated braking. P25C4 reports an unusable sensor circuit without a direction.",["Temperature sensor inside the booster unit defective","Corroded or loose booster connector","Fault in the booster control electronics"],["Brake system warning in the cluster","Brake pedal may feel harder if assistance is reduced","Stored code, often together with chassis codes"],4,3,["P25C5","P25C6","P25C7","P25C8","C057B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P25C5:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","P25C5 is the plausibility fault for brake booster temperature sensor A: the circuit is electrically intact, but the reported temperature does not fit, for example a value that jumps implausibly, stays frozen while the motor works hard, or disagrees with the second sensor. No manufacturer documents P25C5 publicly.",["Sensor drifted out of its characteristic curve","Contact resistance at the booster connector skewing the signal","Measurement error in the booster electronics"],["Brake warning message, sometimes only after long braking","Brake assistance reduced as a precaution"],4,3,["P25C4","P25C8","C057C","C05B6"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P25C6:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor A Circuit Low","P25C6 means the signal of brake booster temperature sensor A is too low, which GM describes as the sensor line being shorted to ground. GM uses the code on the 2023 Corvette Z06 (table 23OBDG07, EBCM section) and keeps the same logic in its 2024 and 2025 tables 24OBDG07 and 25OBDG03A: the check runs continuously with the ignition on, needs the condition five times in a row within 0.6 s and is rated Type B, so the…",["Sensor signal wire shorted to ground","Moisture in the booster connector","Internal short in the temperature sensor"],["Check engine lamp after two trips","Brake system warning message","Brake assistance may be limited"],4,3,["P25C7","P25C4","C0579","C05B3"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P25C7:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor A Circuit High","P25C7 flags a sensor A signal that is too high; GM interprets it as the temperature line shorted to supply. In the EBCM part of table 23OBDG07 for the 2023 Corvette Z06 the voltage must exceed 3.27 V five consecutive times within 0.6 s with the ignition on, and the fault is Type B with two trips to the MIL. Tables 24OBDG07 and 25OBDG03A repeat these values.",["Sensor signal shorted to the supply line","Open sensor circuit or missing sensor ground","Temperature sensor open internally"],["Check engine lamp after two trips","Brake system warning message","Reduced brake assistance possible"],4,3,["P25C6","P25C4","C057A","C05B4"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P25C8:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P25C8 is meant for a sensor A signal that drops out briefly or jumps faster than any real temperature in the booster could change, the typical footprint of a loose pin, a cracked solder joint or a wire that breaks under vibration. Each event may be too short for the low or high check to confirm, which is why this separate code exists. No manufacturer documents P25C8 publicly.",["Loose or spread terminal in the booster connector","Wire breaking intermittently under vibration","Cracked solder joint inside the booster electronics"],["Brake warning that appears and disappears","Occasional change in pedal feel"],4,3,["P25C4","P25C5","C05B7"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ A — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P25C9:["Brake System Control Module B Requested MIL Illumination","P25C9 tells the engine module that a second brake system control module, labelled B, has found an emission-relevant malfunction and wants the check engine lamp switched on. GM uses the code in its hybrid OBD tables 16OBDG01, 18OBDG01 and 19OBDG01: the engine module listens to the lamp request message from module B continuously, starting three seconds after power-up, and logs P25C9 as Type A but without its own lamp…",["Fault stored in brake system control module B","Weak battery or low system voltage","Communication fault between module B and its partners"],["Check engine lamp on","Brake or stability warnings at the same time"],3,1,["P25A2","P25AF"],""],P25CA:["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1)","Some cam phasers carry a locking pin that holds the rotor in a fixed base or middle position for starting and while oil pressure is still building. Where that pin is released and engaged by its own solenoid, the controller supervises this extra circuit.",["Open winding in the intake phaser lock solenoid","Connector off or terminal pushed back after engine work","Broken wire between module and lock solenoid"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough start or unsteady idle","Intake cam timing held at a default position, less power"],2,3,["P25CB","P25CC","P25CD","P25D0","P25DD","P25DE","P0010"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים יניקה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P25CB:["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit Low (Bank 1)","P25CB points to a control line for the intake phaser lock on bank 1 that reads lower than it should, most often a short to ground on the wire or inside the lock solenoid. Depending on how the driver is wired, the solenoid may then stay energised or never receive current, so the lock pin is either released all the time or cannot be pulled back.",["Lock control wire shorted to ground","Internal short in the lock solenoid","Weak battery or voltage dip during cranking"],["Check engine lamp on","Brief rattle from the timing drive at start","Reduced power with fixed intake timing"],2,3,["P25CA","P25CC","P25CE","P25D1","P2088"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P25CC:["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit High (Bank 1)","With P25CC the controller sees the intake phaser lock control line on bank 1 sitting higher than expected, typically because it touches a live wire or the solenoid's ground path is shorted to supply.",["Lock control wire shorted to a supply voltage","Harness insulation melted near the exhaust or turbo","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Sluggish response with intake timing fixed"],2,3,["P25CA","P25CB","P25CF","P25D2","P2089"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P25CD:["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2)","P25CD is the bank 2 version of the open-circuit lock fault and therefore only appears on V or boxer engines whose second cylinder bank has its own intake phaser with a separately switched lock pin. The controller finds the lock solenoid circuit on that bank interrupted or electrically implausible, so it can no longer release or set the pin deliberately.",["Open circuit inside the bank 2 lock solenoid","Bank 2 lock solenoid connector unplugged or corroded","Wire break in the harness across the engine"],["Check engine lamp on","Uneven idle","Less power, bank 2 intake timing fixed"],2,3,["P25CA","P25CE","P25CF","P25D3","P0020"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים יניקה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P25CE:["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P25CE stands for a low signal on the lock control line of the bank 2 intake phaser: the wire or the solenoid winding has found a path to ground, or the module's output is stuck pulling low. Because the second bank's harness often runs along the back of the engine or under the intake manifold, chafing at brackets and heat damage are frequent findings.",["Bank 2 harness chafed through at a bracket","Shorted winding in the bank 2 lock solenoid","Low system voltage setting lock codes on both banks"],["Check engine lamp on","Clatter at cold start"],2,3,["P25CB","P25CD","P25CF","P25D4","P2092"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P25CF:["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit High (Bank 2)","P25CF is logged when the bank 2 intake phaser lock control line stays above its permitted voltage band. Common reasons are contact with a powered wire, moisture bridging connector pins to a supply terminal, or a failed output transistor in the controller.",["Bank 2 lock control wire touching a powered circuit","Moisture in the connector bridging to a supply pin","Failed output transistor in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Lumpy idle from uneven bank timing"],2,3,["P25CC","P25CD","P25CE","P25D5","P2093"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P25D0:["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1)","P25D0 moves the open-circuit lock fault to the exhaust side: the solenoid that releases the locking pin of the bank 1 exhaust cam phaser can no longer be driven because its circuit is interrupted or reads implausibly. The lock keeps the exhaust cam at a defined position while the engine starts, before the phaser has enough oil pressure to hold itself. No manufacturer documents P25D0 publicly;",["Open winding in the exhaust phaser lock solenoid","Connector damaged by exhaust heat","Broken wire to the exhaust lock solenoid"],["Check engine lamp on","Slightly higher fuel consumption","Rough idle possible"],2,3,["P25D1","P25D2","P25D3","P25CA","P0013"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים פליטה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P25D1:["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit Low (Bank 1)","P25D1 indicates that the control signal for the bank 1 exhaust phaser lock is too low, normally a grounded wire or a solenoid winding that leaks to ground. The exhaust side is the hotter one, so insulation that has hardened and cracked near the manifold or turbocharger is a typical finding.",["Heat-cracked insulation grounding the lock wire","Shorted exhaust lock solenoid","Engine oil wicked into the connector"],["Check engine lamp on","Exhaust timing fixed, slightly less power"],2,3,["P25D0","P25D2","P25D4","P25CB","P2090"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P25D2:["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit High (Bank 1)","P25D2 is set when the bank 1 exhaust phaser lock control line carries more voltage than the controller allows in the current switching state, for example because it is shorted to an ignition-fed wire or the solenoid's return is tied to supply. Most output stages detect overcurrent here and switch off, so the lock solenoid loses its command and the pin goes to the position its spring defines.",["Lock control wire shorted to an ignition-fed circuit","Solenoid return path shorted to supply","Damaged output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Weaker mid-range pull"],2,3,["P25D0","P25D1","P25D5","P25CC","P2091"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P25D3:["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2)","P25D3 concerns engines with two cylinder banks and a lockable exhaust phaser on each: the lock solenoid circuit of the bank 2 exhaust phaser is open or electrically implausible, so the module loses control over its pin. On many V engines the bank 2 exhaust solenoid sits at the rear or close to the firewall, where connectors are easily left loose after timing work.",["Bank 2 exhaust lock connector left loose after timing work","Open winding in the bank 2 exhaust lock solenoid","Open in a supply shared with other phaser solenoids"],["Check engine lamp on","Uneven running between the banks"],2,3,["P25D0","P25D4","P25D5","P25CD","P0023"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים פליטה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P25D4:["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P25D4 reports a lock control line for the bank 2 exhaust phaser that is pulled down below its expected level. Grounding through damaged insulation, a solenoid with shorted turns or oil that has crept into the connector are the usual explanations. Because the exhaust manifold of the second bank radiates onto nearby harness sections, heat sleeving that has slipped out of place is worth checking.",["Heat sleeve slipped, wire grounded at the manifold","Shorted turns in the bank 2 exhaust lock solenoid","Oil in the connector"],["Check engine lamp on","Bank 2 exhaust timing fixed"],2,3,["P25D1","P25D3","P25D5","P25CE","P2094"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P25D5:["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit High (Bank 2)","P25D5 closes this series: the bank 2 exhaust phaser's lock control signal sits above its allowed voltage, pointing to a short to battery or ignition voltage, a return path tied to supply, or a defective output in the module. The protected driver then stops switching, and the lock solenoid stays without command until the next key cycle or until the fault vanishes.",["Bank 2 exhaust lock wire shorted to battery or ignition voltage","Harness fault affecting several actuator lines","Defective output in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Slightly higher fuel consumption"],2,3,["P25D2","P25D3","P25D4","P25CF","P2095"],"נעילת חניית מפעיל גל זיזים פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P25D6:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Stop Performance","An exhaust heat exchanger moves exhaust heat into the coolant after a cold start; a flap (bypass valve A) decides whether gas flows through it or around it, and a position sensor reports where the flap is. P25D6 targets the end-stop values of that sensor: at the fully open and fully closed stops the reading must sit inside a learned or calibrated window.",["Carbon build-up or a bent flap stopping short of its end stop","Worn valve actuator or linkage play","Position sensor shifted on its mount or drifting","End stops not relearned after parts replacement"],["Check engine lamp on without noticeable driving change","Slower engine warm-up or weaker cabin heat in winter"],3,1,["P23A8","P2C22","P2C23","P2C24","P2C25","P00E3","P00E4","P237F"],"עצירת חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P25D7:["Fuel Level Sensor C Circuit","Fuel level sensor C is a third level input, needed only where the fuel is spread over more chambers or tanks than two senders can cover, for instance on trucks with an extra tank. P25D7 is its general circuit code: the module sees an electrical fault on this input but does not classify it as low, high or intermittent. No manufacturer documents P25D7 publicly.",["Damaged wiring between tank C sender and module, often under the vehicle","Corroded or loose connector at the sender","Sender C defective internally"],["Gauge or range wrong or replaced by a default value","Check engine lamp on"],2,1,["P25D8","P25D9","P25DA","P25DB","P0460","P2065"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P25D8:["Fuel Level Sensor C Performance","P25D8 says that the third fuel level input delivers an electrically valid signal whose behaviour is not believable: it jumps, drifts or disagrees with the fuel actually used or transferred. A sender frozen at one value has its own code, P25DC, so P25D8 covers the remaining plausibility faults. No manufacturer documents P25D8 publicly.",["Worn or dirty resistor track in sender C giving jumps","Transfer pump or line fault so the level in tank C does not change as expected","Damaged or loose float on sender C"],["Fuel gauge jumps or shows unrealistic values","Range estimate inconsistent","Check engine lamp on after repeated detection"],2,1,["P25D7","P25DC","P2066","P0461"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P25D9:["Fuel Level Sensor C Circuit Low","P25D9 reports that the signal of the third fuel level sender has dropped below its lowest valid value. With the usual resistor-type sender this points to very low resistance, typically a signal wire shorted to ground or a sender shorted internally. Whether low means empty or full depends on how the sender is wired, so the gauge may stick at either end. No manufacturer documents P25D9 publicly.",["Signal wire of sender C chafed and shorted to ground","Internal short in sender C","Water in the tank connector bridging signal and ground"],["Gauge pinned at full or empty","Check engine lamp on"],2,1,["P25D7","P25DA","P25DB","P0462","P2067"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P25DA:["Fuel Level Sensor C Circuit High","P25DA is set when the third sender's signal climbs above the top of its valid range. On a resistor sender fed through a pull-up, that almost always means an open path: a broken wire, a disconnected plug, a burnt-out spot on the resistor track or a missing ground return. A short to a voltage source has the same effect. No manufacturer documents P25DA publicly.",["Broken signal or ground wire to sender C","Tank connector loose or unplugged after work on the tank","Interrupted resistor track inside sender C","Signal wire shorted to a voltage supply"],["Gauge stuck at one end of the scale","Check engine lamp on"],2,1,["P25D7","P25D9","P25DB","P0463","P2068"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P25DB:["Fuel Level Sensor C Circuit Intermittent","P25DB describes short, repeated dropouts in the third fuel level input: the signal leaves its valid range for moments and returns, rather than staying low or high. Typical culprits are a loose pin, a wire that breaks contact only when the vehicle flexes or the tank moves, and a sender whose wiper briefly lifts off the resistor track over rough roads. No manufacturer documents P25DB publicly.",["Loose or spread terminal in the sender C connector","Wire breaking contact when the frame or tank moves","Sender wiper lifting off a worn resistor track"],["Fuel gauge flickers or drops briefly to empty","Check engine lamp may come and go"],2,1,["P25D7","P25D9","P25DA","P0464","P2069"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ C — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P25DC:["Fuel Level Sensor C Stuck","P25DC is set when a third fuel level sender, sender C, keeps returning the same reading although the engine has consumed a meaningful amount of fuel. Such a third input exists only on vehicles with extra or divided tanks, for example saddle tanks or auxiliary tanks on trucks. No manufacturer documents P25DC publicly.",["Float arm of sender C caught on a baffle, pump bracket or tank wall","Worn spot on the sender C resistor track holding the wiper at one value","Fuel transfer to or from tank C not working, so its level really does not change"],["Fuel gauge or range display frozen over a long distance","Risk of running out of fuel despite a displayed reserve","Check engine lamp on"],2,1,["P25D7","P25D8","P25DB","P25B0","P25B2","P0461"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ C — תקוע"],P25DD:['"A" Camshaft Position - Stuck In Locked Position (Bank 1)',"Many modern cam phasers hold their rotor with a spring-loaded pin at a defined angle, often in mid travel, so the engine starts with stable valve timing before oil pressure builds. P25DD means the intake phaser on bank 1 is still latched at that angle although the controller has asked it to unlock and move, so variable timing is lost on that camshaft.",["Low oil level or pressure, or oil of the wrong viscosity, unable to push the pin out","Oil control valve for the bank 1 intake phaser sticking or its screen clogged","Lock pin seized in its bore by sludge or wear inside the phaser"],["Check engine lamp on","Less pulling power, especially in the mid-speed range","Higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P25DE","P25DF","P25E0","P0011","P0010","P25CA"],""],P25DE:['"A" Camshaft Position - Unable to Achieve Locked Position (Bank 1)',"P25DE is the reverse of P25DD: the intake cam phaser on bank 1 should return to its lock angle and let the pin engage, typically as the engine is about to stop or idles before an automatic stop, but the controller never sees the expected locked position. If the pin is not in place at the next start, the rotor can rattle against its stops and timing wanders until oil pressure takes over.",["Debris or wear in the phaser keeping the pin from dropping into its slot","Oil control valve sticking so the lock range of the spool is never reached","Aged or contaminated oil slowing the phaser at hot idle"],["Check engine lamp on","Short rattle or knock from the timing drive right after starting","Rough start or unsteady idle in the first seconds"],3,3,["P25DD","P25DF","P25E1","P0011","P0016"],""],P25DF:['"A" Camshaft Position Control Performance (Bank 1)',"P25DF belongs to the same block as the lock codes P25DD and P25DE, but it does not describe the latch itself. It flags that the intake phaser on bank 1 is not following its commanded angle as well as the calibration expects, judged as a check of control quality rather than as a plain deviation toward early or late timing (P0011, P0012) or a slow response (P000A).",["Worn or partly clogged oil control valve for the bank 1 intake phaser","Oil overdue, diluted or of the wrong grade","Internal leakage in the phaser letting the angle drift"],["Check engine lamp on","Uneven idle or slight hesitation when accelerating","Somewhat higher fuel consumption"],2,3,["P25DD","P25DE","P25E2","P0011","P0012","P000A"],"בקרת מצב גל זיזים‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P25E0:['"A" Camshaft Position - Stuck In Locked Position (Bank 2)',"On engines with two cylinder banks, P25E0 is the bank 2 counterpart of P25DD: the intake camshaft actuator stays latched at its locking angle when the module wants it free to advance or retard. Because only one side is affected, the cam angles of the two banks no longer match, and the module may hold both sides in a fallback position.",["Insufficient oil pressure at the bank 2 head, low level or clogged feed screen","Bank 2 intake oil control valve sticking","Lock pin mechanically jammed in the phaser"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced power and rough idle","Higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P25DD","P25E1","P25E2","P0021","P0020"],""],P25E1:['"A" Camshaft Position - Unable to Achieve Locked Position (Bank 2)',"P25E1 is set when the intake phaser on bank 2 fails to re-engage its lock. The controller commands the phaser toward the locking angle, usually when shutting down or before an idle stop, and then checks whether the measured cam angle settles there; on bank 2 it does not. No manufacturer has published a description of P25E1.",["Low oil pressure at hot idle from worn pump, bearings or thin oil","Varnish or debris in the bank 2 intake phaser","Control valve unable to move the spool into its lock range"],["Check engine lamp on","Brief rattle from the timing drive on start-up","Unsteady running right after a cold or warm start"],3,3,["P25DE","P25E0","P25E2","P0021","P0018"],""],P25E2:['"A" Camshaft Position Control Performance (Bank 2)',"P25E2 points to poor position control of the bank 2 intake camshaft actuator: the measured angle tracks its target less accurately or with more oscillation than the calibration allows, while no clear lock fault is present. It is the bank 2 sibling of P25DF.",["Bank 2 intake solenoid valve worn or sluggish","Contaminated or overdue engine oil","Internal leakage across the phaser vanes"],["Check engine lamp on","Slightly unsteady idle","Lower fuel economy"],2,3,["P25DF","P25E0","P25E1","P0021","P0022","P000C"],"בקרת מצב גל זיזים‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P25E3:['"B" Camshaft Position - Stuck In Locked Position (Bank 1)',"P25E3 concerns the exhaust side: the bank 1 exhaust phaser, camshaft B, remains held by its lock pin when the controller wants to move it. Exhaust timing then stays at its parking angle, which limits how the module can use valve overlap for internal exhaust gas recirculation and scavenging. The Boss 302S OBD-II list Ford published in 2014 marks P25E3 with the warning lamp, alongside the bank 2 exhaust code P25E6.",["Low or contaminated oil at the exhaust phaser","Bank 1 exhaust oil control valve sticking","Damaged rotor or lock pin inside the exhaust phaser"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough idle","Slight loss of power, possibly failed emissions test"],3,3,["P25E4","P25E5","P25E6","P0014","P0013"],""],P25E4:['"B" Camshaft Position - Unable to Achieve Locked Position (Bank 1)',"P25E4 means the bank 1 exhaust phaser does not reach and engage its locking position when the controller asks for it, for example before shutdown or an automatic engine stop. Stellantis lists P25E4 in several PCM reflash bulletins for Wagoneer and Grand Wagoneer models with the 3.0-litre Hurricane high-output twin-turbo inline six and stop-start, among them 18-022-25 Rev. A for 2025 and 18-040-26 for 2022;",["Engine control software needing an update (documented for Stellantis Hurricane engines)","Low oil pressure at hot idle so the phaser cannot swing into the lock","Debris in the exhaust phaser or a sticking control valve"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine fails to restart after an automatic stop, restarts after an ignition cycle","Rough start"],2,3,["P25E3","P25E5","P25E7","P25DE","P0014"],""],P25E5:['"B" Camshaft Position Control Performance (Bank 1)',"P25E5 reports that the exhaust camshaft actuator on bank 1 is controlled less precisely than intended: its angle lags, overshoots or oscillates around the target beyond calibrated limits, without a latch fault. It is the exhaust-side counterpart of P25DF and overlaps in meaning with P0014 and the slow-response code P000B; no manufacturer documents how P25E5 is told apart from them.",["Worn or dirty control valve for the bank 1 exhaust phaser","Degraded engine oil or a blocked oil filter","Noisy exhaust camshaft position signal making the angle look unstable"],["Check engine lamp on","Unsteady idle","Slightly reduced power or economy"],2,3,["P25E3","P25E4","P25E8","P0014","P000B"],"בקרת מצב גל זיזים‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P25E6:['"B" Camshaft Position - Stuck In Locked Position (Bank 2)',"P25E6 tells that on bank 2 the exhaust cam phaser has not left its locked angle despite a command to adjust. The module then has one exhaust camshaft that can no longer be phased, which shifts valve overlap on that bank and can upset idle quality and the emissions balance between the two banks. Ford's 2014 list for the Boss 302S V8 includes P25E6 as a lamp code, together with the matching intake and bank 1 codes.",["Restricted oil feed or clogged screen to the bank 2 cylinder head","Bank 2 exhaust oil control valve stuck","Lock pin seized in the bank 2 exhaust phaser"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced power, uneven idle","Rattle from the timing drive"],3,3,["P25E3","P25E7","P25E8","P0024","P0023"],""],P25E7:['"B" Camshaft Position - Unable to Achieve Locked Position (Bank 2)',"With P25E7 the module reports that the bank 2 exhaust phaser could not be brought into its locking position: when the lock is requested, the cam angle does not settle at the parking value or the pin does not hold it there. A start without the pin engaged tends to be rough, and on stop-start engines a smooth restart becomes less certain. No manufacturer documents P25E7 publicly;",["Aged or sludged oil slowing the bank 2 exhaust phaser","Spool of the bank 2 exhaust control valve hanging","Worn lock pin or pin bore so the pin no longer holds","Calibration issue fixed by a control unit update"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough or rattling start","Hesitant restart after an automatic engine stop"],3,3,["P25E4","P25E6","P25E8","P25E1","P0024"],""],P25E8:['"B" Camshaft Position Control Performance (Bank 2)',"P25E8 is the last code of the locked-position block and covers the control quality of the bank 2 exhaust camshaft actuator: the module sees the angle wander from, overshoot or trail its setpoint more than allowed, while lock-related faults are absent. Older codes such as P0024 and P000D describe similar exhaust deviations on bank 2;",["Wear in the bank 2 exhaust control valve","Wrong oil viscosity or a clogged oil filter","Worn rotor seals inside the exhaust phaser"],["Check engine lamp on","Uneven idle","Higher fuel use"],2,3,["P25E6","P25E7","P25E5","P0024","P000D"],"בקרת מצב גל זיזים‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P25E9:["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch Stuck Open","Some engines drive their mechanical supercharger through an electromagnetic clutch, so the blower only turns when extra low-speed torque is wanted. Eaton's TVS blower on the T6 Drive-E four-cylinder from Volvo is built this way, where the turbocharger takes over at higher revs.",["Worn friction faces or too large an air gap, so the clutch slips or will not pull in","Clutch coil with an internal fault producing too little magnetic force","Low supply voltage or high resistance at the clutch connector","Accessory drive belt slipping or damaged at the supercharger pulley"],["Check engine lamp on","Weak acceleration from low engine speed","Normal pull once the turbocharger takes over"],3,3,["P25EA","P25FE","P25EB","P0299","P2263"],"מצמד ניתוק מדחס גדישה — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P25EA:["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch Stuck Closed","Here the clutch between pulley and supercharger rotors stays engaged although the engine computer wants the blower uncoupled, for example at idle or steady cruising. The blower then keeps turning, costs drive power and fuel, and its air has to be routed past it.",["Engine control software misjudging the clutch state (Audi Q7 3.0 TFSI, bulletin 2048402)","Clutch plates stuck together by wear debris, corrosion or overheating","Clutch coil kept energised by a wiring fault or a stuck driver stage"],["Check engine lamp on","Higher fuel consumption at part load","Supercharger whine also at idle or cruising"],2,3,["P25E9","P25FE","P25ED","P0234"],"מצמד ניתוק מדחס גדישה — תקוע במצב סגור"],P25EB:["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch Circuit Range/Performance","P25EB covers the electrical drive of the supercharger clutch when it is neither cleanly shorted nor open, yet the values do not fit the command – for example a coil current that is too small or too large for the applied duty cycle, or a signal that drops out briefly.",["Clutch coil whose resistance has changed through heat or partial winding short","Corroded or loose connector at the clutch or engine module","Wire chafed near the hot supercharger housing causing intermittent contact"],["Check engine lamp on","Jerky or missing supercharger engagement at low revs"],2,3,["P25EC","P25ED","P25FE","P25E9"],"מצמד ניתוק מדחס גדישה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P25EC:["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch Circuit Low","The engine module measures a voltage on the supercharger clutch control line that is lower than expected for the commanded state. Most often the line has a short to ground. What that does depends on how the coil is switched: with a ground-side driver a grounded control wire can leave the coil permanently energised, so the blower keeps turning;",["Control wire shorted to ground, often chafed on brackets or the engine block","Clutch coil shorted internally","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Supercharger permanently engaged or permanently off, depending on circuit design","Reduced power at low engine speed"],2,3,["P25EB","P25ED","P25FE","P25EA"],"מצמד ניתוק מדחס גדישה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P25ED:["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch Circuit High","With P25ED the voltage on the clutch control line sits above the expected level. Common reasons are a wire shorted to battery voltage, or – on a ground-switched coil – an open coil or broken lead, because the line is then pulled up to supply voltage. A short to voltage can overload the driver stage, which protects itself by switching off.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Open clutch coil or broken wire on a ground-switched circuit","Output stage in the engine control module damaged"],["Check engine lamp on","Sluggish pull-away, supercharger does not cut in"],2,3,["P25EB","P25EC","P25FE","P25E9"],"מצמד ניתוק מדחס גדישה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P25EE:["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit B/Open","P25EE covers the second control circuit of an electric brake vacuum pump, the part of the wiring that should carry voltage while the pump is switched on. Ford's 2019 OBD summary for its hybrid and plug-in models assigns P25EE to the brake system module, mapped from that module's own code C1036: with the pump relay commanded closed, a monitoring line voltage below 250 mV for one second means the pump is not getting…",["Blown vacuum pump fuse","Pump relay contact not closing","Broken wire or loose connector between relay and pump"],["Hard brake pedal, especially with the engine off or in electric drive","Brake or traction warning lamp in addition to the check engine lamp","Vacuum pump never heard running"],2,1,["P25EF","P25F0","P25F1","P258A","P050F"],""],P25EF:["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit B Range/Performance","P25EF says that the B circuit driving the electric vacuum pump is electrically present but its behaviour does not match the command: the feedback on the switched side looks implausible, or the pump runs without the expected effect on brake vacuum. No manufacturer documents P25EF publicly.",["Worn vacuum pump that runs but builds too little vacuum","Leaking vacuum hose or faulty check valve","Corroded terminals causing an unstable feedback voltage"],["Brake pedal firmer than normal","Vacuum pump running longer or more often","Warning lamp on"],2,1,["P25EE","P25F0","P25F1","P258B","P0556"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת ואקום‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P25F0:["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit B Low","P25F0 is stored when the pump's B control circuit reads lower than expected, usually because the switched supply or feedback line is shorted to ground or loaded down by a pump motor with an internal short. A short to ground on the supply side often blows the pump fuse, so the pump then stops altogether. No manufacturer documents P25F0 publicly.",["Chafed supply or feedback wire shorted to ground","Internal short in the vacuum pump motor","Water ingress in the pump connector"],["Hard brake pedal","Repeatedly blown vacuum pump fuse","Warning lamp on"],2,1,["P25EE","P25EF","P25F1","P258C","P050F"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת ואקום‏ B — ערך נמוך"],P25F1:["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit B High","P25F1 marks a high reading on the vacuum pump's second (B) control circuit: the module sees voltage on the switched side when it should be low, for example because the line is shorted to battery voltage, the relay contacts have welded together or the pump has lost its ground. In the welded-relay case the pump keeps running after it has been switched off, which wears it out and drains the battery.",["Pump relay contacts welded closed","Feedback or supply line shorted to battery voltage","Lost ground connection at the pump"],["Vacuum pump running constantly, even with the vehicle switched off","Discharged 12 V battery","Warning lamp on"],2,1,["P25EE","P25EF","P25F0","P258D"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת ואקום‏ B — ערך גבוה"],P25F2:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor C Circuit","A third boost pressure sensor, C, only makes sense on engines with several charging stages or chargers – for example a supercharger feeding a turbocharger, or a two-stage turbo system – where pressure is measured between the stages as well as ahead of the throttle. Which location carries the letter C is up to the manufacturer.",["Loose, corroded or oily connector at boost sensor C","Signal, 5 V reference or ground wire damaged","Boost sensor C failed internally"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced power, boost limited to base level"],2,3,["P25F3","P25F4","P25F5","U060D","P0235","P0239"],"חיישן לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P25F3:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P25F3 means boost sensor C delivers a signal that is electrically valid but does not agree with what the other pressure readings and the engine model suggest. Saab's 2.0 litre turbo engine, developed with GM, shows how this is checked for sensor A: with the engine stopped the reading must lie between 50 and 115 kPa, roughly matching barometric pressure, and while running it is compared with a model built from…",["Charge air leak near the measuring point of sensor C (hose, clamp, seal)","Sensor port fouled by oil from crankcase ventilation or a drifting sensor","Faulty barometric or manifold pressure sensor skewing the comparison"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced power under load","Hissing noise if a charge air leak is present"],2,3,["P25F2","P25F4","P25F5","P0236","P0240","P2CD7"],"חיישן לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P25F4:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor C Circuit Low","Boost pressure sensors of this kind output a voltage that rises with pressure, so P25F4 – a signal below the lowest valid value – points to the wiring or the sensor rather than to the charge air. Usual reasons are a signal wire shorted to ground, a missing 5 V supply, or an open signal line on an input pulled down by the control unit. No public manufacturer data exist for sensor C;",["Signal wire shorted to ground","5 V reference open or pulled down by another faulty sensor on the same supply","Boost sensor C failed internally"],["Check engine lamp on","Noticeable loss of power","Scan tool shows a pressure far below ambient for sensor C"],2,3,["P25F2","P25F3","P25F5","P0237","P0241"],"חיישן לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P25F5:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor C Circuit High","P25F5 reports a signal from boost sensor C above the highest plausible value. Since the voltage climbs with pressure, a reading at the top end usually means an electrical fault: the signal shorted to 5 V or battery voltage, an open sensor ground, or an open signal wire where the input is pulled up.",["Sensor ground open or high resistance","Signal wire shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Boost sensor C failed internally"],["Check engine lamp on, depending on the manufacturer","Reduced power, boost cut back"],2,3,["P25F2","P25F3","P25F4","P0238","P0242"],"חיישן לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P25F6:["AIR System B","P25F6 is the overall monitor for a second secondary air injection system, lettered B, on engines with two separately controlled air delivery paths; system A reports through P0410 and P0411. During warm-up after a cold start a pump pushes fresh air into the exhaust, so leftover HC and CO burn off and the catalyst lights off sooner.",["Secondary air pump of system B worn, seized or water-damaged","Switching or check valve of system B stuck, often after debris from the pump","Cracked, loose or disconnected air hose or vacuum line","Faulty pump relay, fuse or wiring of system B"],["MIL on, usually after a cold start","Secondary air readiness monitor not complete, emissions test failed","Unusual whining or no pump noise during the first minute after a cold start"],2,1,["P25F7","P0410","P0411","P0415","P0419"],"מערכת האוויר המשני‏ B"],P25F7:["AIR System B Incorrect Flow Detected","With P25F7 the engine controller finds that the air delivered by secondary air system B does not match its expectation while the system is switched on after a cold start. Depending on the design, it judges the flow from how the oxygen sensors on that side react, from a pressure sensor in the air line or from pump behaviour.",["Air pump of system B delivers too little air","Switching or check valve fouled or stuck partly closed","Air passages to the exhaust restricted by carbon deposits","Leaking air hose so that part of the flow escapes"],["MIL on after one or two cold starts","Emissions test failed or readiness incomplete","Driveability normally unchanged"],2,1,["P25F6","P0411","P0410","P0415","P0419"],""],P25F8:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C Control Circuit","Bypass valves in the intake let charge air flow around a compressor: on turbo engines they are the recirculation valves that open on a sudden throttle lift so the compressor does not surge, and on engines with a supercharger they can route air past the blower while it is idling or uncoupled. A third such valve, C, only appears on systems with several compressors; which valve gets the letter is manufacturer-specific.",["Broken wire or loose connector at bypass valve C","Open coil in the valve or its solenoid","Supply voltage missing (fuse, main relay)"],["Check engine lamp on","Fluttering noise when lifting off the throttle","Less boost or slower response"],2,3,["P25F9","P25FA","P25FB","P25FC","P0033","P00C0"],"שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ C — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],P25F9:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C Control Circuit Low","P25F9 tells that the control line of bypass valve C reads too low a voltage, normally because it touches ground somewhere or the coil is shorted. If the engine module switches the valve on the ground side, a grounded wire leaves the valve energised all the time;",["Control wire shorted to ground","Valve coil shorted internally","Output stage in the engine control module faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","Too little boost if the valve stays open","Surging or fluttering on lift-off if it stays shut"],2,3,["P25F8","P25FA","P25FB","P0034","P00C1"],"שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P25FA:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C Control Circuit High","With P25FA the control line of bypass valve C carries more voltage than the engine module expects for the commanded state. A wire shorted to battery voltage is the classic reason; on a ground-switched valve an open coil or broken lead also lets the line float up to supply level. A short to voltage can make the driver stage overheat and cut out, so the valve is no longer operated at all.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Open valve coil on a ground-switched circuit","Damaged output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Fluttering or surging noise when lifting off the throttle"],2,1,["P25F8","P25F9","P25FB","P0035","P00C2"],"שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P25FB:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C Control Circuit Range/Performance","P25FB is set when the control circuit of bypass valve C is not open or shorted, but its electrical behaviour does not match the command – for instance a current that rises too slowly or settles at the wrong level, or a signal that drops out now and then.",["Valve coil resistance changed by heat ageing","Contact resistance or moisture in the valve connector","Sluggish valve armature due to deposits"],["Check engine lamp on","Occasional fluttering on lift-off","Uneven boost build-up"],2,1,["P25F8","P25F9","P25FA","P25FC","P0039","P00C3"],"שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P25FC:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C - Mechanical","P25FC concerns the valve itself, not its wiring: bypass valve C is electrically in order but does not move as commanded, sticking open, shut or somewhere in between. A valve stuck open lets charge air leak back to the compressor inlet, so boost falls short; one stuck shut cannot relieve pressure when the throttle closes, and the compressor surges audibly.",["Oil and soot deposits from crankcase ventilation jamming the valve","Torn diaphragm or broken spring inside the valve","Cracked valve housing or leaking seal"],["Check engine lamp on","Loud fluttering when lifting off the throttle","Lack of boost and power"],2,3,["P25FB","P25FD","P2CD5","P2261","P00C4"],""],P25FD:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C Temperature Too High","This code says bypass valve C has become too hot. Recirculation valves are placed in the charge air path close to the compressor and thus near the hot turbine side, and an electric valve's coil adds its own heat when energised for long periods.",["Heat soak from the turbocharger, e.g. after hard driving or with missing heat shields","Valve coil drawing too much current due to an internal fault","Sluggish valve held energised longer than intended"],["Check engine lamp on","Fluttering on lift-off or reduced boost after hard driving"],2,3,["P25FC","P25F8","P00D7","P00D8","P2BC0"],"טמפרטורת שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ C — ערך גבוה מדי"],P25FE:["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch","P25FE is the umbrella code for the supercharger disconnect clutch: it says the clutch function has failed without naming whether it is stuck, slipping or electrically faulty. Those cases have their own codes – P25E9 and P25EA for the mechanical states, P25EB to P25ED for the control circuit – so a control unit that sets P25FE either does not distinguish them or uses it as a summary.",["Worn or seized clutch on the supercharger pulley","Fault in the coil, wiring or connector of the clutch","Engine control software that misjudges the clutch state"],["Check engine lamp on","Weak response at low engine speed","Higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P25E9","P25EA","P25EB","P25EC","P25ED"],"מצמד ניתוק מדחס גדישה"],P25FF:["Electrical System Voltage Stabilizer Control Module Performance","P25FF reports that the module which steadies the 12 V supply for sensitive electronics does not work as intended. Such stabilizers mainly appear on cars with automatic engine stop/start: every restart drags the battery voltage down hard, according to a semiconductor maker briefly below 4 V, which would otherwise reset radios, displays and similar loads. A DC/DC stage raises the voltage for those moments.",["Internal fault in the voltage stabilizer or DC/DC converter module","Aged or wrong-type 12 V battery so the module cannot hold the voltage","Current backfeed or poor supply/ground connection at the module"],["Automatic stop/start no longer active","Radio or display resets when the engine restarts","Warning light depending on the maker"],2,1,["P0560","P0561","P0562","P0563"],"מודול בקרת מייצב מתח מערכת חשמלית — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2600:["Coolant Pump A Control Circuit/Open","P2600 means the controller sees an open circuit on the line that drives electric coolant pump A, directly or through its relay. GM's 2023 ECM table tests the auxiliary coolant pump relay output while it is off: more than 200 kOhm for 5 of 6 seconds sets the code as Type B, so the MIL follows after two trips. On Ford's 2020-2023 gasoline engines pump A serves the cabin heating loop.",["Internal open circuit in the electric pump or its electronics","Water or coolant ingress causing poor contact at the pump","Chafed or broken control wire, loose connector or failed relay","Coolant level too low (named by Hyundai as possible trigger)"],["MIL or hybrid warning lamp on","Little or no cabin heat","Rising coolant temperature in hybrid or after-run operation"],2,1,["P2601","P2602","P2603","P261A"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2601:["Coolant Pump A Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P2601 is set when electric coolant pump A is commanded on, yet its feedback or its effect shows that it is not really working, while the wiring itself tests sound. GM's 2008 table for the 3.6 L LLT judges its auxiliary pump indirectly: after a shutdown with coolant above 110 °C the pump runs on, and if the coolant does not cool down as the ambient-dependent calibration expects within about 80 s, the code is logged.",["Electric pump seized, worn or running too slowly","Control module software misjudging the pump (update available)","Air pocket or low coolant so the pump runs dry"],["MIL on","Weak cabin heating","Coolant temperature stays high after shutdown"],2,1,["P2600","P2602","P2603","P261B"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2602:["Coolant Pump A Control Circuit Low","P2602 reports that the control circuit of electric coolant pump A reads low - typically a ground short, or a matching fault report from the driver stage. Which pump is A varies: Ford's 2020-2023 gasoline OBD summary defines it as the auxiliary pump of the high-temperature loop for cabin heating, checked continuously over 5 s above 11 V;",["Control wire shorted to ground","Internal fault in the electric coolant pump or its electronics","Coolant or water ingress into the pump connector"],["Fault code stored; MIL depends on the maker (GM 2008 LLT table none, GM 2023 ECM table Type B)","Weak cabin heating","No after-run of the pump after a hot shutdown"],2,1,["P2600","P2601","P2603"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2603:["Coolant Pump A Control Circuit High","P2603 means the drive line of electric coolant pump A reads high - usually a short to the supply side, or an overcurrent seen by the driver stage. Ford's 2020-2023 gasoline OBD summary assigns pump A to the auxiliary high-temperature loop for cabin heating and sets P2602/P2603 when the smart driver reports a fault within 5 s.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Seized or sluggish pump drawing excessive current","Faulty driver stage in the ECM"],["Fault code stored; MIL depends on the maker (GM 2008 LLT table none, GM 2023 ECM table Type B)","Weak cabin heating","Higher coolant temperature after hot shutdown"],2,1,["P2600","P2601","P2602"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2604:["Intake Air Heater A Circuit Range/Performance","P2604 is the functional check of intake air heater A - the grid heater in the intake that warms the charge air of a diesel engine for cold starts. The circuit responds, but current, voltage drop or heating effect do not match the command. Under CARB, a glow plug or intake air heater has to be checked both for reacting correctly when commanded and for plausible current and voltage drop in its circuit.",["Worn or sticking intake air heater relay","Loose or burnt terminals on the heater supply cable","Degraded or partly open heater grid","Outdated engine software (manufacturer update available)"],["Hard starting in cold weather","White smoke and rough running after a cold start","Check engine light"],2,1,["P0540","P0541","P0542","P0543","P2605","P2609"],"גוף חימום אוויר יניקה‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2605:["Intake Air Heater B Circuit/Open","P2605 points to an open circuit at intake air heater B, a second heating element in the intake of a diesel engine; the control unit finds no current path through the element, its relay or the cabling. Volvo's EMS code lists keep heaters A, B and C apart.",["Loose, corroded or burnt terminal at heater element or relay","Preheat relay no longer switching","Heater element B burnt through"],["Hard starting in cold weather","White smoke after a cold start","MIL on"],2,1,["P2606","P2607","P2608","P2609","P0543","P2CE1"],"גוף חימום אוויר יניקה‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2606:["Intake Air Heater B Circuit Range/Performance","P2606 means heater B in the intake does respond, but the current it draws or the voltage drop across its circuit lies outside the window the engine controller expects. Mack documents P2604-7F and P2606-7F for 2014-2017 trucks with MP7, MP8 and MP10 engines and puts them down to extra circuit resistance from corrosion inside the master disconnect switch, so inspecting those contacts comes first.",["Extra resistance from corroded contacts, e.g. in the master disconnect switch","Worn preheat relay contacts","Aged heater element with changed resistance","Outdated engine software (update published by the maker)"],["Sluggish cold starts","White smoke until the engine is warm","MIL on"],2,1,["P2604","P2605","P2607","P2608","P2609","P2CE2"],"גוף חימום אוויר יניקה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2607:["Intake Air Heater B Circuit Low","P2607 says the signal from the circuit of intake air heater B stays too low, which normally means a grounded control or feedback line, or a relay output pulled down. No manufacturer documents P2607 publicly.",["Control or feedback wire chafed through to ground","Internal short in the preheat relay","Moisture or corrosion in a connector of the heater circuit"],["Hard starting in cold weather","White smoke after a cold start","MIL on"],2,1,["P2605","P2606","P2608","P0541","P2CE3"],"גוף חימום אוויר יניקה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2608:["Intake Air Heater B Circuit High","P2608 is logged when the circuit of intake air heater B reads too high, for instance a short to battery positive on the control line or a relay that stays energized when it should be off. Volvo is the one maker that names it in public bulletins: the August 2020 EMS change log for heavy-truck engines lists P2608-00 among the preheater codes reduced by a relay robustness update, and Volvo's 2022 instruction for the…",["Preheat relay contacts welded or sticking closed","Control or feedback wire shorted to battery positive","Engine software needing the maker's update"],["MIL on","Batteries run down after short trips or standstill","Hard cold starts or white smoke"],2,1,["P2605","P2606","P2607","P0542","P2CE4"],"גוף חימום אוויר יניקה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2609:["Intake Air Heater System Performance","P2609 judges the intake air heating as a whole rather than one circuit: the controller compares what the grid heater should achieve with what it measures, for example via the current drawn or the rise in intake air temperature during preheat. Ram has published two service documents for its 6.7 L Cummins pickups. Bulletin 18-012-12 REV.",["Worn heater grid or relay (replace as a set)","Overheated or loose supply cable between relay and grid","Engine software with an outdated diagnostic (reflash available)","Intake air temperature sensor reading implausibly"],["Hard starting in cold weather","White smoke and rough idle after a cold start","MIL on"],2,1,["P0540","P0542","P2604","P2605","P2606"],"מערכת גוף חימום אוויר יניקה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P260A:["PTO Control Circuit/Open","P260A reports an open circuit in the output a control module uses to engage the power take-off, typically the coil circuit of a PTO relay or engagement solenoid. GM's PTO module on 2008-2014 Silverado/Sierra 3500 HD chassis cabs, described in upfitter bulletin UI 80c, switches both the supply and the ground side of an upfitter-installed relay and refuses PTO operation unless both lines are connected;",["Relay coil wiring missing, broken or only one side connected by the upfitter","Open coil in the PTO relay or engagement solenoid","Corroded or loose connector in the chassis wiring"],["PTO does not engage","PTO indicator flashes or stays off"],2,0,["P260B","P260C","P260D","P251A"],"PTO — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P260B:["PTO Control Circuit Low","P260B is stored when the PTO control output reads too low, the classic case being a grounded wire leading to the PTO relay coil. GM documents the code as P260B.00, a low voltage on the PTO relay control line, among the faults the PTO module can set on 2008-2014 Silverado and Sierra 3500 HD chassis cabs.",["Relay control wire chafed against the frame or body","Shorted coil in the PTO relay or solenoid","Relay wired incorrectly during body installation"],["PTO cannot be engaged","Message or flashing PTO indicator"],2,0,["P260A","P260C","P251B"],"PTO — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P260C:["PTO Control Circuit High","P260C signals that the PTO control output reads too high, usually because the relay control line touches a powered wire or the relay coil draws too much current. GM lists it as P260C.00, a high voltage on the PTO relay control line, in the diagnostic table of the PTO module that GM fitted to Silverado and Sierra 3500 HD chassis cab trucks from 2008 to 2014.",["Relay control wire shorted to a powered circuit","Relay or solenoid coil with too low resistance","Faulty splice or add-on wiring from the body installation"],["PTO will not engage or will not release","PTO indicator behaves abnormally"],2,0,["P260A","P260B","P251C"],"PTO — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P260D:["PTO Engaged Lamp Control Circuit","P260D concerns the output that drives the lamp or LED telling the operator that the power take-off is engaged; the module has found a fault in that lamp circuit. For GM's heavy-duty pickup chassis cabs, upfitter bulletin UI 80c explains how such an indicator behaves: the LED in the PTO switch blinks quickly while the relay is energized, turns steady once load feedback confirms engagement or after 3 s without…",["Failed indicator lamp or LED","Open or shorted wire to the indicator, often in add-on wiring","Fault in the PTO switch assembly with integrated LED"],["PTO indicator stays dark or lit regardless of PTO state","PTO itself works normally"],1,0,["P260A","P260B","P260C","P251A"],""],P260E:["Particulate Filter Regeneration Lamp Control Circuit","Diesel machines often have a separate dashboard lamp that tells the operator a particulate filter regeneration is needed or running. P260E covers the circuit that switches this lamp. Deutz documents it for its EMR5/MD1 engine controllers: fault type 11 (J1939 SPN 3697, FMI 4) means the lamp output reads below normal or is shorted to ground, type 12 (FMI 3) means it is too high or shorted to the supply.",["Lamp wire shorted to ground or to supply","Lamp or bulb holder open, or lamp not fitted on this machine","Corroded connector at dashboard or engine controller"],["Regeneration lamp dark or permanently lit","Missed regeneration requests leading to high soot load","Later power reduction by the engine controller"],2,0,["P2002","P2458","P2459"],"נורת התחדשות (רגנרציה) מסנן חלקיקים — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],P260F:["EVAP System Monitoring Processor Performance","Some evaporative leak tests run long after the engine is switched off, so Ford gives them a small dedicated processor that works during the soak. P260F is set when that monitoring processor does not behave as intended. In Ford's 2020–2023 gasoline OBD summary it belongs to the engine-off natural vacuum (EONV) test for 0.020 inch leaks, which may run at most twice a day after the vehicle has soaked for 3.5–6 hours;",["Internal fault in the EVAP monitoring processor or module","Supply, ground or CAN wiring fault at the monitoring module","Software level requiring an update"],["MIL on","EVAP readiness not set, small leak test not completed"],2,1,["P0456","P2610","P0606"],"מעבד ניטור מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2610:["ECM/PCM Internal Engine Off Timer Performance","Several emission monitors need to know how long the engine was off, for example to judge a cold start or an evaporative test after a soak. P2610 reports that the module's engine-off timer gives implausible values. Ford's 2020–2023 gasoline summary flags an engine-off time under 30 s after an inferred soak, an error above 15 s or a missing CAN timer message at start;",["Engine module software prone to false timer faults (update available)","Battery disconnect, transport fuse removed or supply dropout during soak","Timer message from another module (e.g. cluster) missing on CAN","Internal timer fault in the control module"],["MIL on, usually without drivability change","Cold-start and EVAP monitors may not run"],4,1,["P262B","P2507","P0603","P0606"],""],P2611:["A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve A Control Circuit/Open","A refrigerant distribution valve is an electrically switched valve in the A/C circuit that opens or blocks the refrigerant path to one branch, for example a rear evaporator or a battery chiller. P2611 tells you the engine or powertrain module can no longer drive valve A because its control line or coil is open.",["Valve solenoid coil burnt out or internally open","Corroded or loose connector at the valve, often near condensation","Broken control wire between module and valve","Faulty output stage in the controlling module"],["One A/C zone (e.g. rear) blows warm or cannot be shut off","Reduced battery cooling on hybrids or EVs, possibly limited charging power","Stored code, often without warning lamp"],2,0,["P2612","P2613","P0EE3","P0EE2"],"שסתום חלוקת גז מזגן‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2612:["A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve A Control Circuit Low","P2612 is stored when the voltage on the drive line of refrigerant distribution valve A stays lower than the module expects, which normally points to a ground fault in the wire or inside the valve. Volkswagen is an unusual case: its engine control module reports P2612 as a ground short of the A/C compressor regulator valve N280, the electrically controlled valve of the variable-displacement compressor.",["Chafed control wire touching ground","Brittle or corroded connector at the valve (VW N280 plug near the starter)","Internal short in the valve coil"],["A/C does not cool or compressor does not engage (VW)","One cooling branch or zone remains inactive","Code stored, usually no other driveability symptom"],2,0,["P2611","P2613","P0EE4"],"שסתום חלוקת גז מזגן‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2613:["A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve A Control Circuit High","P2613 means the control circuit of refrigerant distribution valve A reads too high: the wire has a short to the supply side, or the driver stage senses excessive current when it switches the valve. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; Ford lists only the open-circuit code P2611, and the VW use of P2612 refers to the compressor regulator valve.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage feed","Valve coil with shorted windings drawing too much current","Defective driver in the controlling module"],["An A/C branch keeps cooling although it should be off","Valve output switched off, so the branch does not work at all","Code stored without engine symptoms"],2,0,["P2611","P2612","P0EE5"],"שסתום חלוקת גז מזגן‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2614:["Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit/Open (Bank 1)","Some engine computers pass a copy of the camshaft position signal on to another module, for example an injector driver unit or a valve timing controller. P2614 means that this outgoing line for camshaft A on bank 1 is broken or its pulses never reach the receiver. On the 2003 Ford 6.0 L Power Stroke diesel the PCM forwards the CMP pulse to the fuel injector control module (FICM);",["Broken wire or loose terminal between sending module and receiving module","Camshaft sensor signal itself missing or out of sync with the crank signal","Receiving module (e.g. injector control module) not reading the signal","Defective output stage in the engine control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Long cranking or no-start","Engine stalls or misfires intermittently"],2,3,["P2615","P2616","P2617","P0340","P0341"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P2615:["Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit Low (Bank 1)","P2615 points to a camshaft A (bank 1) position output line that the engine module finds pulled to ground. GM documents it for the Cadillac CT6 in its 2018 tables: with the driver switched off and the line commanded high, the ECM measures the voltage and flags a short at an impedance to ground of 0.5 ohm or less; at 200 kilohm or more it treats the circuit as open, and some controllers then log P2614 instead.",["Output wire chafed through and touching ground","Moisture or corrosion bridging the connector pins to ground","Internally shorted input in the receiving module","Faulty output driver in the engine control module"],["Stored code, often without warning lamp","Rough or delayed starting","Valve timing control in fallback mode"],2,2,["P2614","P2616","P2618"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2616:["Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit High (Bank 1)","P2616 is the opposite fault to P2615: the outgoing camshaft A position line on bank 1 stays at supply potential although the module has switched its low-side driver on and wants the line low. In GM's 2018 CT6 tables the ECM declares a power short once the impedance toward the supply is 0.5 ohm or less, using the same window of 40 bad readings in 50 at 100 ms intervals, engine not cranking and at least 11 V;",["Output wire shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Low-side driver in the engine module no longer switching","Back-feed through a damaged or corroded connector"],["Stored code without warning lamp","Hard starting or hesitation after start","Cam phasing faults logged by the receiving module"],2,2,["P2614","P2615","P2619"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2617:["Crankshaft Position Signal Output Circuit/Open","When an engine module relays the crankshaft position signal to another controller, P2617 says that this forwarded line is open or the pulses go missing at the receiver. Ford's 2003 6.0 L diesel summary describes the clearest case: the fuel injector control module counts a fault whenever the crank pulse it gets from the PCM is absent or does not line up with the camshaft signal, monitored continuously above 90 rpm,…",["Open wire or pushed-out pin on the crank output line","Crank sensor signal itself missing or out of sync with the cam signal","Receiving module (e.g. injector control module) faulty"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Engine cranks but does not start","Sudden stalling while driving"],2,3,["P2618","P2619","P2614","P0335","P0336"],"יציאת אות מצב גל ארכובה — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2618:["Crankshaft Position Signal Output Circuit Low","P2618 reports a crankshaft position output line that is shorted to ground. GM uses it widely, from the 2011–2012 hybrid tables to the 2019 ECM summaries, wherever the engine module provides a crank position output. The check runs while the output driver is off and the line is commanded high: 0.5 ohm or less toward ground counts as a short, 200 kilohm or more as an open (some controllers then add P2617).",["Harness pinched or chafed so the output touches ground","Water or corrosion in the output connector","Shorted input stage in the receiving module","Output driver failure in the engine control module"],["MIL on after two drive cycles","Related faults or substitute mode in the receiving module","Occasional hesitation or start problems"],2,3,["P2617","P2619","P2615"],"יציאת אות מצב גל ארכובה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2619:["Crankshaft Position Signal Output Circuit High","P2619 is set when the crankshaft position output line is held at supply voltage while the module's low-side driver is switched on and expects it to be pulled down. GM's 2014 hybrid ECM table treats an impedance of 0.5 ohm or less toward power as the fault and evaluates it like the low case: 40 failures in 50 samples every 100 ms, engine not cranking, relay voltage of 11 V or more, Type B with MIL after two trips.",["Damaged insulation lets the output touch a positive feed","Low-side driver in the engine module failed open","Back-feed through a corroded connector"],["MIL on after two drive cycles","Receiving module reports implausible crank signal","Possible reduced power or start problems"],2,3,["P2617","P2618","P2616"],"יציאת אות מצב גל ארכובה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P261A:["Coolant Pump B Control Circuit/Open","P261A reports an open circuit in the drive of an auxiliary electric coolant pump labelled B. Ford's gasoline OBD summaries for 2020-2023 and 2024 define pump B as the high-temperature loop pump for component cooling and check it continuously over 5 s with at least 11 V on board. Ford's EcoSport 1.0 EcoBoost of 2018 (SSM 47359) set P261A because connector C1450 at that pump could not latch fully;",["Pump connector not fully seated or with spread terminals","Auxiliary pump with internal open (electronics or motor)","Broken supply or control wire, or failed relay where fitted"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, sometimes only sporadically","No after-run circulation, heat soak after hot shutdown","Component temperatures (turbo, electronics) rise"],2,1,["P261B","P261C","P261D","P261E","P2600"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P261B:["Coolant Pump B Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","Unlike the wiring codes around it, P261B judges whether coolant pump B actually delivers when commanded. The verdict comes from pump feedback or from its effect on coolant temperatures, so the circuit can test fine while the pump does nothing. Ford's 2020-2023 and 2024 gasoline summaries list it for the component-cooling pump of the high-temperature loop, next to the circuit codes of that pump.",["Auxiliary pump motor or electronics failing intermittently","Air pocket after coolant service, pump runs dry","Impeller blocked by debris or deposits","Low coolant level"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Engine or turbo runs hotter after shutdown, possible boiling noises","Heater or component cooling weak in certain conditions"],2,1,["P261A","P261C","P261D","P261E","P2601"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P261C:["Coolant Pump B Control Circuit Low","P261C points to a control line of coolant pump B pulled toward ground. VW's 2014 Touareg data book sets it when the signal voltage drops below 2.8-3.2 V. Ford (gasoline summaries 2020-2023 and 2024) relies on a smart driver that watches pump B, which cools components in the hot loop, and sets P261C or P261D as soon as it reports an output fault, within a 5 s window above 11 V.",["Chafed wire to ground near exhaust or engine parts","Internal short in the pump electronics, often after water ingress","Corroded connector bridging pins"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Auxiliary pump does not run, no after-run cooling","Rising temperatures at turbo or electronics in heavy use"],2,1,["P261A","P261B","P261D","P2602"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P261D:["Coolant Pump B Control Circuit High","With P261D the module finds the drive of coolant pump B too high, either a short to the supply side or a current above the permitted limit. VW's 2014 Touareg book uses a current test here, roughly 2.2 to 4 A as the threshold. Ford checks the component-cooling pump B of the high-temperature loop through a smart driver that reports output faults within 5 s at 11 V or more.",["Stiff or partly seized pump drawing excess current","Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage circuit","Faulty driver stage in the engine module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Pump switched off for protection or running permanently","Possible battery drain if the pump keeps running after shutdown"],2,1,["P261A","P261C","P261E","P2603"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P261E:["Coolant Pump B Control Circuit Stuck On","P261E covers the case where coolant pump B keeps working although the module has commanded it off. That can be an output that stays energised, a relay with welded contacts, or, on switchable mechanical pumps, a shroud or valve that no longer closes, so coolant circulates during warm-up.",["Pump relay with welded contacts or output stage stuck on","Switchable pump shroud or vacuum/solenoid valve not closing","Control line shorted to battery voltage"],["Engine warms up slowly, heater stays cool longer","Pump audible after the engine is switched off","Warning lamp and possibly a thermostat code"],2,1,["P261F","P261A","P261D","P261B","P0128"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקוע במצב פעיל"],P261F:["Coolant Pump A Control Circuit Stuck On","P261F means electric coolant pump A reports activity while the module has it switched off. GM's 2025 ECM table 25OBDG04B describes the test: with the pump commanded off or below 299 rpm for 2 s and more than 11 V on board, a feedback speed of 3,100 rpm or more for 8 of 10 seconds sets the code as Type B; the warning lamp follows on the second faulty trip.",["Impeller driven by main pump flow at high rpm, fixed by ECM software (GM)","Vacuum leak or contaminated switching valve of a switchable pump (Mercedes OM651)","Pump electronics reporting wrong speed or not switching off"],["Check engine lamp after two faulty trips","Usually no noticeable driveability change","Slower warm-up when the pump really keeps running"],2,1,["P261E","P2600","P2601","P2602","P2603"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2620:["Throttle Position Output Circuit/Open","P2620 concerns a line on which the engine module sends a throttle position value out to another unit, for instance a transmission or body controller, as an analogue or pulse-width signal. The code means the module detects that this output circuit is open, so the receiver gets nothing usable. No manufacturer documents P2620 publicly with thresholds;",["Open wire or loose pin on the throttle position output line","Corroded connector at the sending or receiving module","Output stage in the engine control module defective"],["Stored code, warning lamp behaviour depends on the maker","Irregular shift points or idle control in the receiving module"],2,0,["P2621","P2622","P0121","P0122","P0123"],"יציאת מצב מצערת — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2621:["Throttle Position Output Circuit Low","P2621 flags the throttle position output line as shorted to ground or reading below its permitted voltage band. A receiving module such as a transmission controller would then see a value that looks like a fully closed throttle all the time. No carmaker publishes a code-specific description with limits;",["Output wire chafed against body ground","Corrosion bridging the output pin to ground","Shorted input in the receiving module"],["Stored code in the engine module","Receiver behaves as if the throttle were always closed (late or odd shifts)"],2,0,["P2620","P2622","P0122"],"יציאת מצב מצערת — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2622:["Throttle Position Output Circuit High","P2622 means the throttle position output line sits too high, typically because it is shorted to a supply wire or the driver in the sending module cannot pull it down. The receiver would read a value resembling wide-open throttle even at idle, which can confuse shift scheduling or torque calculations. There is no public manufacturer documentation for this exact code.",["Output wire shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Driver in the sending module unable to pull the line low","Back-feed through a damaged connector"],["Stored code in the engine module","Receiver acts as if at full throttle (harsh or late shifts)"],2,0,["P2620","P2621","P0123"],"יציאת מצב מצערת — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2623:["Injector Control Pressure Regulator Circuit/Open","Engines with hydraulically actuated unit injectors (HEUI) fire their injectors with engine oil pressurised by a high-pressure pump; the injection pressure regulator (IPR) valve sets that oil rail pressure. P2623 says the PCM cannot drive the IPR because its circuit is open.",["Open IPR valve coil","Loose or corroded IPR connector, broken wire on the high-pressure pump cover","Faulty IPR driver in the PCM"],["Engine cranks but does not start","Stalling or severe power loss","Malfunction indicator lamp on"],3,3,["P2624","P2625","P2284","P2285","P2286","P2288"],"וסת לחץ בקרת מזרק — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2624:["Injector Control Pressure Regulator Circuit Low","P2624 is reserved for a control circuit of the injection pressure regulator that sits too low, typically a ground short on the line switched by the PCM. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. On the 6.0 L Power Stroke, the best-known HEUI application, Ford reports every open or short of the IPR driver under P2623 alone, according to its OBD summaries up to 2009;",["IPR control wire chafed to ground near the valley or pump cover","Internally shorted IPR coil","Damaged driver stage in the PCM"],["Hard start or no-start","Rough running, knocking or erratic power","Malfunction indicator lamp on"],3,3,["P2623","P2625","P2284","P2288"],"וסת לחץ בקרת מזרק — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2625:["Injector Control Pressure Regulator Circuit High","With P2625 the module sees the injection pressure regulator circuit at too high a level: the switched line is shorted to battery voltage, or the IPR coil draws more current than the driver allows. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; Ford's 6.0 L Power Stroke summaries from 2003 to 2009 fold every IPR driver fault into P2623, and International's HEUI truck engines report through their own codes.",["IPR control line shorted to a battery-voltage circuit","IPR coil with reduced resistance causing overcurrent","Faulty IPR driver in the PCM"],["Long cranking or no-start","Low power, engine may stall","Malfunction indicator lamp on"],3,3,["P2623","P2624","P2284","P2290"],"וסת לחץ בקרת מזרק — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2626:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","Wide-band lambda probes such as the Bosch LSU 4.9 carry a calibration resistor in their plug; the engine module uses it to scale the pumping current. P2626 says this trim path at the front probe of bank 1 looks open. Makers detect it differently: GM's 2023 tables let the sensor chip measure the resistor after each start and fail an LSU 4.9 above 379.5 ohms (NGK ZFAS-U2: above 4,644 ohms), type B.",["Front wide-band probe defective (trim resistor, pump cell or heater damage)","Trim line broken or pin pushed back in the six-pin probe connector","Moisture or corrosion in the probe connector raising the measured resistance","Engine software requiring an update after probe replacement (some makes)"],["Check engine light","Fuel control falls back to open loop on bank 1","Slightly higher fuel consumption or rough idle"],2,1,["P2627","P2628","P2629","P2237","P2243","P2195","P0130"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2627:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2627 marks a trim signal below its plausible range at the first wide-band probe of bank 1. On Ford petrol engines with NTK probes the interface chip sets it when the resistor line (RL) is open or touches ground; Bosch-equipped Fords do not use it.",["Trim/resistor line open or chafed to ground between probe and engine module","Wide-band probe or NOx sensor internally faulty","Loose or leaking charge-air ducts on diesel engines (GM L5P)"],["Check engine light","Further oxygen or NOx sensor codes stored at the same time","On diesels possibly boost or aftertreatment codes and reduced power"],2,1,["P2626","P2628","P2630","P2237","P2A00","P0299"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2628:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","With P2628 the trim input of the front wide-band probe on bank 1 lies above its permitted range. Ford's 2020-23 petrol summary reserves it for NTK probes, where the interface chip reports the resistor line shorted to battery voltage. In GM's 2005 table for the Honda-sourced 3.5 L V6 it is the opposite end of P2627: the label resistor voltage drops under 0.29 V for 5 s.",["Trim line shorted to battery or another supply in the harness or plug","Wide-band probe or NOx sensor delivering an implausible value","Exhaust leak ahead of the sensor drawing in outside air"],["Check engine light","Mixture control without probe feedback, higher consumption","On diesels NOx-related codes and possible SCR warnings"],2,1,["P2626","P2627","P2631","P2237","P0132"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2629:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit/Open (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2629 is the bank 2 counterpart of P2626 and only exists on V or boxer engines with two front wide-band probes. The module finds the trim branch of that probe interrupted. GM's 2023 table 23OBDG07 calculates the parallel resistance between the probe's APE and MES pins and fails values above 240 ohms as an open compensation resistor, two trips.",["Bank 2 front probe faulty, including heater damage (Mercedes M278/M157)","Open trim wire or loose terminal at the bank 2 probe connector","Outdated engine software (update called for together with new probes)"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 fuel control without wide-band feedback","Possibly further bank 2 fuel trim codes"],2,1,["P2626","P2630","P2631","P2240","P2247","P2197","P0150"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P262A:["Fuel Injector - Pilot Injection Not Learned","Common-rail diesels learn how long each injector must be energised to deliver its tiny pilot shot. Ford's 6.7 L Power Stroke does this with Zero Fuel Calibration: during overrun with rail pressure set to 300 bar, one injector fires small test pulses and the resulting rise in crankshaft speed tells the module the real quantity; the learned offset then corrects every pilot injection of that injector.",["Driving pattern rarely offers long overrun phases in high gear (towing, city use)","Injector drift or wear so the test pulse does not give a usable response","Disturbed crankshaft speed or rail pressure signal","Non-original engine calibration interfering with the learning routine"],["Check engine light","Louder combustion knock, especially at idle and light load","Often no noticeable change in driveability"],3,1,["P02CC","P02CD","P02DA","P2B11"],""],P262B:["Control Module Power Off Timer Performance","P262B concerns the timer that keeps counting inside a control module while the vehicle is shut down, used to measure how long it has been off. GM runs two checks on it: a count-up test while run/crank is inactive, failing when two consecutive readings differ by over 1.5 s in 4 of 20 one-second samples, and a range test comparing the hardware timer with a mirror timer at shutdown or restart (deviation above 25 % in…",["Poor ECM power or ground connection, momentary supply loss","Ignition relay or its control circuit not supplying the module","Diagnostic calibration too sensitive to fast engine cool-down","Internal timer hardware fault in the control module"],["MIL on after two drive cycles","Possibly other control module codes stored at the same time"],4,1,["P2610","P0606","P0601","P062B","P0513"],""],P262C:["Sensor Reference Voltage G Circuit/Open","Engine modules supply groups of sensors from separately regulated 5 V outputs, lettered A, B, C and so on; G is the seventh such supply. P262C is the general fault of this output, typically an interruption so that the sensors behind it lose their feed and report signals near zero together. No manufacturer documents P262C publicly, and which sensors hang on circuit G depends entirely on the application.",["Broken reference wire or splice feeding the sensors of circuit G","Loose or corroded pin at the engine module or a sensor plug","Internal regulator of the engine module for output G failed"],["Check engine light","Several sensor codes appearing at the same time","Reduced power or limp mode depending on the affected sensors"],2,3,["P262D","P262E","P262F","P06D6","P06D2","P0641"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן‏ G — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P262D:["Sensor Reference Voltage G Circuit Low","P262D says the 5 V reference output G of the engine module is being dragged below its lower limit. Usually something on the line conducts to ground: a chafed wire, water in a plug, or one sensor with an internal short loading the whole group. A useful test is to unplug the sensors on circuit G one by one and watch whether the voltage recovers. No manufacturer documents P262D publicly;",["Reference wire G chafed to ground or engine metal","One sensor on circuit G with internal short pulling the supply down","Water or corrosion in a connector of the group","Weak internal regulator of the engine module"],["Check engine light","Several sensors report low or invalid values together","Limp mode, reduced power or starting problems possible"],2,3,["P262C","P262E","P262F","P06D7","P0642"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן‏ G — אות נמוך במעגל"],P262E:["Sensor Reference Voltage G Circuit High","With P262E the 5 V supply G that the engine module feeds to a sensor group sits above its upper limit. That points to an external voltage source getting onto the line, for example a reference wire rubbed through against a 12 V feed or a sensor signal wire, or to a regulator inside the module that no longer holds its setpoint.",["Reference wire G shorted to a 12 V feed or another powered circuit","Sensor on the group feeding voltage back into the reference","Internal regulator of the engine module out of tolerance"],["Check engine light","Readings of several sensors too high or implausible","Limp mode or reduced power possible"],2,3,["P262C","P262D","P262F","P06D8","P0643"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן‏ G — אות גבוה במעגל"],P262F:["Sensor Reference Voltage G Circuit Range/Performance","P262F is the plausibility check of reference output G. The voltage is neither shorted nor missing, yet it wanders outside a tighter tolerance band or jumps around, which falsifies every ratiometric sensor on that circuit. Ford's 2012 summary shows the idea for its references A to C on Bosch Tricore modules: below 4.7 V or above 5.2 V for 0.5 s counts as a range fault.",["Loose pin or splice on circuit G opening briefly under vibration","Poor ground connection of the engine module","Sensor on the group drawing excessive current","Drifting internal regulator of the engine module"],["Check engine light","Sporadic implausible values from several sensors","Occasional hesitation or limp mode"],2,3,["P262C","P262D","P262E","P06D9","P06A6"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן‏ G — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2630:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2630 reports a trim input that is too low at the upstream wide-band probe of bank 2, the cylinder bank without cylinder 1. Ford's petrol summaries of 2020-23 set it only with NTK probes, where the sensor interface chip sees the resistor line open or grounded; the same chip check runs for about 10 s before a fault is stored.",["Resistor line of the bank 2 probe open or rubbed through to ground","Bank 2 upstream probe internally defective","Damaged or heat-affected connector near the exhaust"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 running in open loop","Fuel economy slightly worse"],2,1,["P2627","P2629","P2631","P2240","P0151"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2631:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2631 flags a trim value above the valid window for the first wide-band probe on bank 2. Ford assigns it to NTK probe installations: the interface chip notices the resistor line pulled up to battery voltage, as from a chafed wire touching a powered circuit. GM's 2005 table for the 3.5 L V6 of Honda origin uses the mirror logic, with the bank 2 label resistor voltage below 0.29 V for 5 s.",["Bank 2 resistor line shorted to a powered wire in the harness","Bank 2 front probe with internal short","Non-matching replacement probe or repaired connector without the original resistor"],["Check engine light","Lambda control on bank 2 disabled","Possibly additional circuit codes from the same harness"],2,1,["P2628","P2629","P2630","P2240","P0152"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2632:["Fuel Pump B Control Circuit/Open","Fuel pump B is a second pump beside the main one: a transfer pump between two tanks, an in-line booster or a second in-tank pump. P2632 reports an open in its control circuit. On the 6.6 L LML Duramax with dual tanks, GM's 2014 table 14OBDG10 drives the transfer pump relay through a low-side driver and sets the code as Type B after 3 s above 200 kOhm.",["Failed transfer pump relay, fuse or relay socket","Open wire or corroded connector at the pump or tank","Pump motor or pump driver module open internally","Outdated scan tool cannot command the pump (GM PIT5212B)"],["Fuel from the second tank is not transferred, gauge drops faster","Possible stalling when the main tank runs dry","Warning lamp depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P2633","P2634","P2636","P0230","P0627"],"משאבת דלק‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2633:["Fuel Pump B Control Circuit Low","P2633 is the ground-short code of the second fuel pump circuit. GM's 2014 LML diesel table checks the ground-switched relay output of the fuel transfer pump while it is off and flags 0.5 ohm or less between signal and ground, held for 3 s, as Type B.",["Chafed pump wire grounded against frame or tank strap","Shorted pump motor windings","Water in the connector under the vehicle"],["Blown fuse, second pump does not run","Fuel not transferred from the auxiliary tank","Warning lamp depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P2632","P2634","P2636","P0628"],"משאבת דלק‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2634:["Fuel Pump B Control Circuit High","P2634 indicates that the drive of the second fuel pump reads as shorted to battery voltage or carries too much current. For the 6.6 L LML with dual tanks, GM's 2014 table judges the transfer pump relay output while it is switched on and treats 0.5 ohm or less toward controller power, lasting 3 s, as a Type B fault.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage feed","Worn or binding pump drawing excess current","Relay with shorted coil or stuck contacts"],["Second pump runs constantly or is shut off by the module","Fuel level display between tanks inconsistent","Warning lamp depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P2632","P2633","P2636","P0629"],"משאבת דלק‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2635:["Fuel Pump A Low Flow/Performance","P2635 judges the main fuel pump by its result rather than its wiring: the module compares the measured fuel pressure with the commanded value and flags a pump that falls short or overshoots. GM's 2019 tables do this with filtered rail pressure error against calibrated low and high limits, with pump circuit and pressure sensor codes excluded first, and store it as Type B after two trips;",["Worn or leaking in-tank pump module","Clogged filter or blocked pickup, e.g. gelled diesel in cold weather","Low supply voltage or poor ground at the pump or pump control module","Fuel pressure sensor reading wrong without its own code"],["Hesitation, surging or loss of power under load","Hard starting or stalling","Whining noise from the fuel tank","Malfunction indicator lamp on"],2,3,["P2636","P0087","P018B","P0230","P0627"],""],P2636:["Fuel Pump B Low Flow/Performance","P2636 is the flow check for fuel pump B, in practice mostly the transfer pump of trucks with two tanks. GM's 2014 table for the 6.6 L LML compares how fast the levels in both tanks fall while the pump runs; if they do not move as expected for 140 s, a Type B fault is stored.",["Weak transfer pump not moving enough fuel between tanks","Restricted transfer line or design-related flow limit (GM recall 17067)","Refuelling with engine or ignition on confuses the level-based check","Faulty fuel level sender in one of the tanks"],["Fuel gauge shows empty although the second tank holds fuel","Engine may stall when the main tank runs dry","Malfunction indicator lamp on"],2,1,["P2635","P2632","P2633","P2634","P0461"],""],P2637:["Torque Management Feedback Signal A","Many automatic transmissions ask the engine to cut torque briefly during an upshift and then check whether the engine actually did so. P2637 is stored by the transmission controller when that feedback for request A shows the engine did not follow.",["Engine control module calibration not following the torque reduction request","Transmission calibration not matched to the engine","J1939/CAN data link fault between engine and transmission"],["Check transmission lamp on","Harsh or too quick upshifts","Gear range limited"],4,2,["P2638","P2639","P2641","P0614"],"אות משוב ניהול מומנט‏ A"],P2638:["Torque Management Feedback Signal A Range/Performance","P2638 says the torque feedback for request A is present but its value does not fit the situation, for example an engine torque figure that drifts away from what the transmission expects during a shift.",["Idle learn not completed after PCM reset or delivery","Outdated transmission software with oversensitive torque monitoring","Engine torque estimate skewed by air leaks or sensor errors"],["MIL on and gear position indicator flashing","Rough or delayed gear changes"],4,1,["P2637","P2639","P2642"],"אות משוב ניהול מומנט‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2639:["Torque Management Feedback Signal A Low","P2639 means the torque management feedback signal A stays below its valid range, so the transmission controller cannot read a usable torque confirmation from the engine. No manufacturer explains this exact code publicly.",["Engine and transmission software versions not matched","Torque feedback message missing or corrupted on the data bus","Hard-wired feedback line shorted to ground"],["Transmission warning or stored code","Firm or flared shifts"],4,2,["P2637","P2638","P2643"],"אות משוב ניהול מומנט‏ A — ערך נמוך"],P263A:["MIL Control Circuit Low","P263A means the engine module has found the line that switches the malfunction indicator lamp shorted to ground. GM checks it while the low-side driver is off: if the voltage stays low with an impedance to ground of about 0.5 ohm, the lamp control is faulty; the 2014 tables need 50 of 63 samples at 50 ms intervals, the 2019 tables a single sample, with run/crank voltage of at least 11 V and remote start inactive.",["MIL control wire chafed and touching ground","Loss of ignition 1 voltage via main relay or fuse block terminal","Faulty lamp input in the instrument cluster"],["Engine warning lamp lit permanently","Code stored even though the lamp cannot report it reliably"],2,0,["P263B","P0650"],"נורית תקלה (MIL) — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P263B:["MIL Control Circuit High","P263B is stored when the MIL control line is stuck at supply voltage while the module has switched its driver on to light the lamp. GM treats an impedance toward power of about 0.5 ohm as the fault and needs 4 failures within 5 samples, each 50 ms apart, provided run/crank voltage is at least 11 V and no remote start is running.",["MIL control wire shorted to a positive feed","Ignition 1 supply interrupted at relay or fuse block","Lamp driver in the engine module failed"],["Engine warning lamp does not light, not even at key-on bulb check","Other emissions codes stored without warning"],2,0,["P263A","P0650"],"נורית תקלה (MIL) — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P263C:["Glow Plug Control Driver Performance","Modern diesel glow systems switch each plug through a semiconductor driver inside a glow plug control module (GPCM). P263C reports that such a driver does not behave as commanded. Ford's 6.7 L and 3.0 L Power Stroke GPCM talks to the engine module over a private CAN bus and flags any internal output, whether it serves the plugs, the DEF heaters or a relay, that fails to switch or overheats for more than 1 s;",["Output stage inside the glow plug control module failed","Glow plug or plug wire with short, overloading the driver","Poor GPCM power feed or ground causing erratic switching"],["Check engine light, glow indicator may flash","Hard or long cranking when cold","White smoke and rough running after a cold start"],2,1,["P064C","P06E5","P263E","P0671","P0381"],"נהג בקרת מצת להט — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P263D:["Reductant Heater Driver Performance","DEF turns solid at about -11 °C, so SCR systems heat the tank, pump and lines electrically. P263D concerns the power stage that switches these heaters rather than a heater element. On Ford's 6.7 L Power Stroke the heaters are switched by the glow plug module; the plausibility test runs once per trip at peak heater power and sets P263D when the driver circuits exceed 125 °C.",["Heater power stage overheating from excessive load current","Partially shorted heater element or wiring drawing too much current","Internal fault of the module that drives the heaters"],["Check engine light and DEF/SCR warning","DEF not thawing in cold weather, dosing delayed","Countdown to speed or power limitation possible"],3,3,["P20BA","P20BE","P20C2","P20B9","P205B"],"נהג גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue) — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P263E:["Glow Plug Control Module 1 Over Temperature","The first glow plug control module measures its own internal temperature and reports P263E when it runs too hot, since its power semiconductors carry tens of amps during glowing. GM's 6.6 L L5P Duramax tables set it at a module temperature above 123 °C while the plugs are commanded on and coolant is below 60 °C, type B. Ford's 2023 diesel summary for the 6.7 L and 3.0 L names more than 125 °C inside the module.",["Defective glow plugs drawing excess current (e.g. Ram ProMaster plugs without O-ring)","Repeated start attempts or very long glow periods in severe cold","Internal fault or poor heat dissipation of the glow plug module"],["Check engine light, glow lamp flashing","Glowing cut short, hard cold starts","White smoke after cold start"],2,1,["P263C","P263F","P064C","P06E5","P0671"],"מודול בקרת מצת להט‏ 1 — חום יתר"],P263F:["Glow Plug Control Module 2 Over Temperature","P263F is reserved for engines with a second glow plug control module, for instance one per cylinder bank on large V engines; it reports that this second unit has exceeded its permitted internal temperature. No manufacturer documents P263F publicly, and the documented North American V8 diesels from Ford and GM manage all eight plugs with a single module, so they only use the module 1 code P263E.",["High-current or shorted glow plugs on the bank served by module 2","Long or repeated glow phases in severe cold","Internal fault or poor cooling of glow plug module 2"],["Check engine light, glow lamp flashing","Harder cold start, uneven running until warm"],2,1,["P263E","P263C","P06F5","P06FA","P06FC"],"מודול בקרת מצת להט‏ 2 — חום יתר"],P2640:["Torque Management Feedback Signal A High","P2640 is the high-range fault of torque management feedback signal A: the confirmation that the transmission controller receives after asking the engine for a torque change carries a value above the plausible upper limit.",["Engine ECM software reports torque values the transmission calibration does not accept","Outdated or wrong transmission controller calibration","Hard-wired feedback line shorted to voltage (where used)"],["Check transmission lamp or MIL on, depending on calibration","Firm or abrupt upshifts","Torque reduction during shifts no longer active"],4,2,["P2637","P2638","P2639","P2644","P0614"],"אות משוב ניהול מומנט‏ A — ערך גבוה"],P2641:["Torque Management Feedback Signal B","On Allison automatics, feedback B belongs to Low Range Torque Protection (LRTP): in the low ranges the TCM caps engine torque to spare gears and output shaft and checks that the engine respects the cap. P2641 sets when the engine reports more torque than permitted.",["Engine ECM software below the level required for the transmission (Cummins, Mack, Volvo)","Engine broadcasts torque above the low-range limit requested by the TCM","Transmission calibration not matched to the engine"],["CHECK TRANS lamp on","Low Reverse or other low ranges unavailable","Code appears under high load, often without noticeable drivability change"],4,2,["P2637","P2642","P2643","P2644","P0614"],"אות משוב ניהול מומנט‏ B"],P2642:["Torque Management Feedback Signal B Range/Performance","P2642 means feedback signal B arrives and lies inside its valid range, yet its value makes no sense for the current operating state, for example a torque figure that drifts away from what a limited request should produce or that changes implausibly fast. No manufacturer explains P2642 publicly. Allison ties request B to its low-range torque cap (LRTP) and logs the general code P2641 when the engine exceeds the cap;",["Engine and transmission software versions do not match","Idle or torque adaptation not learned after service","Faulty input to the engine torque model (air mass, intake air temperature)"],["Rough or delayed shifts","Transmission warning lamp on","Low ranges restricted"],4,2,["P2641","P2643","P2644","P2638"],"אות משוב ניהול מומנט‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2643:["Torque Management Feedback Signal B Low","With P2643 the transmission controller sees feedback signal B below its lower limit, so it cannot confirm that the engine is holding the torque level it asked for. No manufacturer describes this exact code in public documents.",["Torque message missing or sent with a default value on the data link","Engine and transmission calibrations incompatible","Bus or signal wiring damaged, short to ground"],["Transmission warning lamp on","Low ranges or reverse low not selectable","Harsh shifts because torque reduction is missing"],4,2,["P2641","P2642","P2644","P2639"],"אות משוב ניהול מומנט‏ B — ערך נמוך"],P2644:["Torque Management Feedback Signal B High","P2644 reports that torque management feedback B exceeds its upper range limit. No manufacturer publishes a code-specific description. The closest documented case is Allison's P2641: a 2013 Cummins ISX12 calibration reported more torque than the low-range cap allowed, and Mack and Volvo trucks showed the same code under heavy load until the engine software was updated.",["Engine software sends torque with a scaling the transmission does not expect","Engine calibration older than the level required by the transmission maker","Wired feedback line shorted to voltage"],["Transmission warning lamp on","Low ranges blocked","Shift quality reduced"],4,2,["P2641","P2642","P2643","P2640"],"אות משוב ניהול מומנט‏ B — ערך גבוה"],P2645:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1)',"Engines that switch valve lift or deactivate cylinders through their rocker arms use an actuator, usually an oil control solenoid, to send oil to the locking pins. P2645 means the engine controller sees the drive circuit of actuator A on bank 1 as open: the state it commands and the state it reads back on the line disagree.",["Open coil in the rocker arm oil control solenoid","Loose, corroded or oil-soaked solenoid connector","Broken wire in the control or supply line","Faulty output driver in the engine control module"],["MIL on, often on the first trip","No change to high lift, weak pull at high engine speed","Cylinder deactivation or economy mode no longer engages"],2,3,["P2648","P2649","P2646","P2655","P2650"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P2646:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator System Performance/Stuck Off (Bank 1)',"P2646 is a mechanical-hydraulic plausibility fault: actuator A on bank 1 was commanded to switch the rocker arms, yet the engine did not change lift, or responded too weakly. GM's 2015 table 15OBDG05 tests this intrusively by toggling between high and low lift at 1,200 to 1,800 rpm and 40 to 230 Nm with warm oil (30 to 130 °C) and judges the resulting phaser oil-pressure ripple with a filtered average;",["Low oil level, wrong viscosity or sludged oil","Sticking spool or clogged screen in the oil control solenoid","Seized locking pin in the switching rocker arm","Faulty lift controller or outdated ECM calibration (Toyota Valvematic)"],["MIL on after a completed test drive","Engine feels flat above mid-range speed","Higher fuel consumption"],2,3,["P2647","P2645","P2656","P2651","P265B"],"מערכת מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי (בנק 1)"],P2647:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator System Stuck On (Bank 1)',"Here actuator A on bank 1 is believed to stay engaged: the rocker arms remain locked in the switched mode although the controller has asked for the default lift. GM's 2015 four-cylinder table 15OBDG05 detects this with the same intrusive lift toggle as P2646 but flags a filtered pressure-ripple value that falls below its limit;",["Oil control solenoid leaks oil while switched off","Locking pin jammed in the engaged position","Faulty rocker arm oil pressure switch (Honda VTEC)"],["Rough or lumpy idle","Misfire at low load","Sluggish response when pulling away"],2,3,["P2646","P2645","P2657","P2652"],"מערכת מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — תקוע במצב פעיל (בנק 1)"],P2648:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 1)',"P2648 points to a low-side electrical fault on the control line of rocker arm actuator A, bank 1: the line reads low, typically a short to ground or a solenoid with shorted turns. GM's 2015 table 15OBDG05 tests the driver for short-to-ground faults with ignition in crank or run and more than 11 V, trips after 100 bad samples out of 120 and lights the MIL at once (Type A).",["Control wire chafed through to ground","Shorted turns in the solenoid winding","Moisture or oil bridging pins in the connector"],["MIL on immediately","No switching to the second lift stage","Reduced top-end power"],2,3,["P2645","P2649","P2658","P2653"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2649:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 1)',"The counterpart to P2648: the control circuit of rocker arm actuator A on bank 1 reads high, which means a short to battery voltage or a driver that cannot pull the line down. In GM's 2015 table 15OBDG05 the check needs the output driver commanded on, ignition in crank or run and supply above 11 V; 100 failures in 120 samples set a Type A fault.",["Control wire shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Output driver in the engine controller no longer switches","Open ground side of the solenoid circuit"],["MIL on immediately","Lift switching disabled or permanently active","Rough running at idle if the actuator stays energised"],2,3,["P2645","P2648","P2659","P2654"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P264A:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit (Bank 1)',"Some valve lift systems report back where the rocker arm actuator actually is, rather than relying on oil pressure; continuously variable designs driven by an electric motor, such as Toyota Valvematic, work this way. P264A is the general circuit fault for the position sensor of actuator A on bank 1: signal missing or implausible without a clear low or high pattern.",["Loose or corroded position sensor connector","Damaged signal, supply or ground wire","Position sensor failed internally"],["MIL on","Lift held at a fixed value, less power","Higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P264B","P264C","P264D","P264E","P2645","P266A","P265A"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P264B:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1)',"Range/Performance means the bank 1 feedback sensor for actuator A delivers a signal inside its electrical limits that still does not fit what the engine expects, for example a position that lags or overshoots the commanded one, or that fails to move when the actuator is driven. CARB requires valve lift systems to catch target errors and slow response before emissions exceed set limits.",["Actuator or linkage moving sluggishly","Sensor loose or misaligned on its mount","Control software needing an update"],["MIL on after a drive cycle","Hesitation or uneven power delivery","Idle speed fluctuating"],3,3,["P264A","P2646","P266B","P265B"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1)"],P264C:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1)',"P264C is set when the signal from the position sensor of rocker arm actuator A, bank 1, sits below its valid window. Typical electrical explanations are a short of the signal wire to ground, a lost 5 V reference, or a sensor that has failed internally. CARB lists such out-of-range checks for every sensor in a lift or timing system under the comprehensive component rules. No carmaker publishes P264C with a threshold;",["Signal wire shorted to ground","5 V sensor supply missing","Position sensor failed internally"],["MIL on","Weaker pull, lift no longer varied","Higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P264A","P264D","P266C","P265C"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P264D:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1)',"With P264D the position signal of actuator A on bank 1 reads above its plausible maximum. An open ground return, a signal line touching the 5 V or battery feed, or water in the connector can push it up. Because a reading at the upper stop looks like an impossible position, the controller rejects it and runs a fixed lift. No public manufacturer documentation gives a threshold;",["Open sensor ground","Signal wire shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Water ingress in the sensor connector"],["MIL on","Engine runs on a fixed lift setting","Noticeably less power"],3,3,["P264A","P264C","P266D","P265D"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P264E:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 1)',"P264E covers a feedback signal from the position sensor of actuator A, bank 1, that drops out or jumps for short moments rather than staying low or high. Loose terminals, a cracked wire flexing with engine movement, or interference on an unshielded line are the usual reasons, and the fault may vanish when the vehicle is parked.",["Loose or spread terminal in the sensor connector","Wire cracked inside the insulation by engine movement","Electrical interference on the signal line"],["MIL on, sometimes clearing by itself","Surging or hesitation","Uneven idle"],3,3,["P264A","P264B","P266E","P265E"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 1)"],P264F:["Engine Serial Number Not Programmed or Incompatible","Some engine controllers store the serial number of the engine they belong to, much like the VIN. P264F is logged when that entry is empty or does not fit. Ford Special Service Message 47823 covers 2013 to 2019 E-Series, Super Duty, F-53/F-59 and F-650/750 models: after a PCM replacement the MIL comes on with P264F until the engine serial number, taken from the build records in OASIS, is written into the new PCM with…",["Engine serial number not written after PCM/ECM replacement","Serial number from another engine or used control module","Stored configuration lost through a memory fault in the module"],["MIL on after control module replacement","Usually no change in how the engine runs"],4,1,["P0630","P0610","P0602"],""],P2650:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1)',"Some engines split rocker arm switching into two stages or groups, each fed by its own oil control solenoid; the second one is called actuator B. P2650 is logged when the engine controller finds the drive line of that B solenoid on bank 1 open, so switching the output on or off brings no matching electrical response. No carmaker publishes this code with limits.",["Open winding in the B rocker arm oil control solenoid","Terminal pushed out or corroded in the solenoid B connector","Wire chafed through near the valve cover or harness clips","Failed output stage for solenoid B in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Second switching stage never engages, less power or economy in that range","Possibly no other noticeable change in driving"],2,3,["P2653","P2654","P2651","P2645","P2660"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P2651:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator System Performance/Stuck Off (Bank 1)',"In the generic definition, P2651 says the B stage of rocker arm switching on bank 1 did not engage when requested, or engaged too weakly to be confirmed. Controllers usually verify the change through an oil pressure switch in the rocker gallery or through a measurable shift in engine behaviour.",["Intermittently failing rocker arm oil pressure switch (Honda i-VTEC)","Oil level too low or oil of the wrong grade","Clogged filter screen or sticking spool in solenoid B","Locking pin in the switchable rocker arm seized by deposits"],["MIL on, sometimes only now and then","Engine lacks pull in the speed range served by stage B","Fault may not return right after clearing"],2,3,["P2652","P2650","P2646","P2661"],"מערכת מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי (בנק 1)"],P2652:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator System Stuck On (Bank 1)',"P2652 means the controller thinks stage B of the bank 1 rocker switching stays engaged after release was commanded, usually because the confirming oil pressure switch still signals pressure. Honda documents it in two ways.",["Rocker arm oil pressure switch B reporting pressure permanently","Solenoid B lets oil through in its closed position","Locking pin stuck in the engaged position","Switch signal line shorted to voltage (Honda four-cylinder meaning)"],["MIL on, possibly together with P3400 on Honda V6","Rough or uneven running, especially at low load","Cylinder deactivation no longer works"],2,3,["P2651","P2650","P2647","P2662","P3400"],"מערכת מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — תקוע במצב פעיל (בנק 1)"],P2653:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 1)',"P2653 points to a voltage that is too low on the control line of rocker arm solenoid B, bank 1. On a solenoid switched from the supply side, a line rubbing against the engine block or a shorted coil pulls the signal down while the output is active; the controller's driver then reports an overcurrent or a low-voltage state. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Control wire of solenoid B shorted to engine ground","Shorted turns inside the solenoid B coil","Engine oil inside the connector creating a leakage path"],["MIL on soon after the fault appears","B stage switched off, reduced power or economy"],2,3,["P2650","P2654","P2648","P2663"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2654:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 1)',"P2654 reports a voltage that is too high on the wire that drives rocker solenoid B, bank 1, typically when the line touches a battery-fed wire or the driver's ground side is bridged. With a ground-switched solenoid, that kind of short can energise the valve permanently, so the B stage may stay engaged regardless of the command, which the engine feels as rough idle or misfire at low speed.",["Solenoid B control wire shorted to a battery-fed circuit","Internal short in solenoid B lowering its resistance","Shorted output transistor in the engine control module"],["MIL on","Rough idle or misfire if the B stage stays engaged","Possible blown fuse on the solenoid supply"],2,3,["P2650","P2653","P2649","P2664"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2655:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2)',"P2655 is the bank 2 twin of P2645: on a V or boxer engine with a separate rocker arm actuator per cylinder bank, the drive circuit of actuator A on the side without cylinder 1 is open, so the state the controller sets and the state it sees on the wire differ. No manufacturer documents P2655 publicly.",["Broken wire in the harness to the bank 2 solenoid","Terminal pushed out of the connector housing","Open coil in the bank 2 oil control solenoid"],["MIL on","Banks run unevenly, slight roughness","Reduced power or economy"],2,3,["P2658","P2659","P2656","P2645","P2660"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P2656:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator System Performance/Stuck Off (Bank 2)',"For bank 2, P2656 reports that actuator A was told to switch the rocker arms but the expected change in valve lift did not show up, or it was too small. Since such engines give every bank a separate oil feed and solenoid, a clogged screen or sticking spool on that side alone is enough. No manufacturer publishes P2656;",["Low, wrong or sludged engine oil","Clogged oil screen or sticking spool at the bank 2 solenoid","Seized locking pin in a bank 2 rocker arm"],["MIL on after a completed test","Weaker response at higher engine speed","Higher fuel consumption"],2,3,["P2657","P2655","P2646","P2661"],"מערכת מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי (בנק 2)"],P2657:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator System Stuck On (Bank 2)',"P2657 is the stuck-on case for bank 2: actuator A keeps the rocker arms of the second bank in their switched mode after the controller has asked for the base setting. On a cylinder deactivation design that could mean valves stay closed on that side; on a two-step design the high-lift profile stays active at idle. No manufacturer documents P2657 publicly;",["Bank 2 solenoid passing oil while switched off","Locking pin stuck in the engaged position","Debris in the bank 2 oil passage"],["Misfire codes on bank 2 cylinders","Lumpy idle","Poor low-speed driveability"],2,3,["P2656","P2655","P2647","P2662"],"מערכת מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — תקוע במצב פעיל (בנק 2)"],P2658:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)',"P2658 flags the bank 2 control line of rocker arm actuator A as too low, the classic sign of a short to ground or a coil with damaged windings. The test is purely electrical and runs whenever the controller drives the output, regardless of oil condition. No manufacturer documents P2658 publicly; GM's equivalent for bank 1 (P2648 in 15OBDG05) needs more than 11 V and 100 failures out of 120 samples, Type A.",["Bank 2 control wire shorted to ground","Damaged winding in the bank 2 solenoid","Harness insulation damaged by exhaust heat"],["MIL on immediately","Lift switching disabled","Less power or higher consumption"],2,3,["P2655","P2659","P2648","P2663"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2659:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 2)',"P2659 covers the bank 2 control circuit of actuator A reading high: the wire is shorted to a voltage source or the controller's driver stage no longer switches it to ground. No manufacturer documents P2659 publicly. On bank 1, GM's 2015 table 15OBDG05 checks this as P2649 only while the driver is commanded on, again with 100 failures out of 120 samples and a Type A fault.",["Bank 2 control wire shorted to a voltage source","Controller output stage no longer switching to ground","Neighbouring pins bridged in the connector"],["MIL on immediately","Bank 2 lift stays switched or switching is disabled","Rough idle in some cases"],2,3,["P2655","P2658","P2649","P2664"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P265A:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit (Bank 1)',"Lift systems that move the rocker geometry with an electric motor, such as Toyota Valvematic, need a sensor that tells the engine controller the actual adjustment angle. P265A flags a general electrical problem with the feedback sensor that reports where actuator B on bank 1 sits: the controller sees no usable signal but cannot classify it as simply too low or too high.",["Loose or corroded connector at the B position sensor","Open 5 V reference or sensor ground wire","Failed position sensor inside the lift controller"],["MIL on","Lift held at a fixed value, sluggish response","Higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P265B","P265C","P265D","P265E","P264A","P2650"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P265B:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1)',"Toyota documents this code on Valvematic engines, where an electric lift controller turns a shaft that alters rocker geometry and reports its angle back. P265B is set when that feedback stays electrically valid but does not track the target. Bulletin T-SB-0011-14 (2014 Corolla, 2ZR-FAE) pairs it with P2646 and fixes it by reflashing the ECM.",["Outdated ECM calibration (Toyota 2014 Corolla)","Continuously variable lift controller sticking or worn","Stored learn values no longer match the mechanism","Drifting angle sensor in the controller"],["MIL on, often together with P2646","Reduced power and slower throttle response","Fault may return after a short rev to 3,500 rpm"],3,3,["P265A","P2646","P264B","P265C","P265D"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1)"],P265C:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1)',"The angle or position sensor of rocker arm actuator B, bank 1, normally works inside a voltage band that never touches the lower rail. If the reading falls below that band, the engine controller logs P265C, because a value near zero cannot correspond to any real actuator position.",["Sensor B signal wire grounded through damaged insulation","Sensor supply voltage missing","Internal fault in position sensor B"],["MIL on","Engine runs with fixed lift, less power"],3,3,["P265A","P265D","P265B","P264C"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P265D:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1)',"P265D stands for a feedback signal from position sensor B, bank 1, that sits above its valid ceiling. A reading pinned near the supply voltage usually means the signal is no longer pulled toward a real value: the sensor ground has opened, the signal wire touches a reference or battery line, or moisture has bridged pins in the plug.",["Open ground wire of position sensor B","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Moisture bridging pins in the sensor plug"],["MIL on","Lift frozen at default, weaker acceleration"],3,3,["P265A","P265C","P265E","P264D"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P265E:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 1)',"Here the bank 1 position signal for actuator B is neither stuck low nor high; instead it jumps, flickers or briefly vanishes faster than the mechanism could physically move. The engine controller compares successive readings and flags P265E when the rate of change or the number of dropouts exceeds what a motor-driven lift mechanism can produce.",["Fretting corrosion on sensor B terminals","Conductor broken inside its insulation, opening under vibration","Interference from ignition or other high-current wiring"],["MIL on and off over several trips","Surging or uneven power delivery"],3,3,["P265A","P265B","P265D","P264E"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 1)"],P265F:["Variable A/C Compressor Control Circuit Range/Performance","Variable-displacement A/C compressors change their output through an electric control valve on the back of the compressor housing. On Ford's externally controlled design the PCM drives that valve with a pulse-width signal and aims for an evaporator temperature of roughly 3 to 8 °C; Volkswagen calls the part regulator valve N280, a coil of around 10 ohms.",["Control valve sticking or internally worn","Refrigerant charge too low, so pressures do not follow the valve command","Corroded connector or high resistance in the valve circuit","A/C pressure sensor reading wrong"],["A/C cools weakly or inconsistently","Compressor runs at fixed or minimum output"],2,0,["P06A0","P06A1","P06A2","P0645"],"מדחס מזגן משתנה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2660:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2)',"P2660 concerns V-type or boxer engines with switchable rocker arms on both cylinder banks: the controller sees the drive circuit of solenoid B on bank 2, the side without cylinder 1, as broken. An open coil, a disconnected plug after valve cover work, or a cut wire leaves the output without load, so the command and the electrical feedback disagree.",["Solenoid B plug on bank 2 left unplugged or not latched after repairs","Open coil in bank 2 solenoid B","Cut or broken wire on the bank 2 harness branch"],["MIL on","Bank 2 B stage inactive, uneven running between banks possible"],2,3,["P2663","P2664","P2661","P2650","P2655"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P2661:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator System Performance/Stuck Off (Bank 2)',"P2661 is the functional check of rocker arm stage B on bank 2: although the solenoid circuit is electrically sound, the commanded switch did not happen or the confirmation (an oil pressure switch reading or a change in cam phaser or engine response) stayed too small. Bank 2 means the engine has two cylinder heads, so the fault concerns only half of the cylinders, which may show as a difference between the banks.",["Low oil level or poor oil supply to the bank 2 head","Partly blocked oil gallery or screen on bank 2","Sticking solenoid spool or seized locking pins on bank 2"],["MIL after a completed drive cycle","Less power in the range where stage B should engage","Higher fuel consumption"],2,3,["P2662","P2660","P2651","P2656"],"מערכת מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי (בנק 2)"],P2662:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator System Stuck On (Bank 2)',"With P2662 the controller concludes that stage B on bank 2 stays switched after it has requested the default mode. Detection depends on the design: a pressure switch that keeps indicating oil pressure, or engine behaviour on that bank that still matches the engaged state. A solenoid that seeps oil when closed, a return path that cannot drain, or locking pins jammed by debris or wear keep the rockers coupled.",["Bank 2 solenoid B seeping oil when closed","Blocked drain path keeping oil pressure on the rockers","Locking pins jammed in the coupled position by debris or wear"],["MIL on","Uneven idle or misfire on bank 2, worse when cold"],2,3,["P2661","P2660","P2652","P2657"],"מערכת מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — תקוע במצב פעיל (בנק 2)"],P2663:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)',"P2663 is stored when the control line to solenoid B on bank 2 reads too low, most often a short to ground somewhere between the module and the second cylinder head. On V engines that harness branch often runs along the back of the block or under the intake manifold, where heat and vibration wear through insulation. A coil whose resistance has collapsed gives the same picture.",["Bank 2 control wire worn through and touching ground","Bank 2 solenoid B coil with collapsed resistance","Faulty output driver for bank 2 solenoid B"],["MIL on","Stage B on bank 2 out of action, power or economy reduced"],2,3,["P2660","P2664","P2653","P2658"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2664:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 2)',"P2664 signals excessive voltage on the control line of solenoid B, bank 2. Contact with a powered conductor, for example where several solenoid and injector feeds share a connector, or a driver that can no longer pull the line down, are the typical causes. Depending on how the output is wired, the valve may then be energised all the time, keeping stage B on that bank engaged, or not work at all.",["Short to a powered feed inside a shared engine connector","Output driver in the control module stuck off","Internally shorted solenoid B on bank 2"],["MIL on","Misfire or rough idle on bank 2 if the stage stays engaged"],2,3,["P2660","P2663","P2654","P2659"],"מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2665:["Fuel Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit/Open","Engines that can burn a second fuel such as compressed natural gas use electric shut-off valves to keep that fuel locked in when it is not wanted. GM's 2015 Impala Bi-Fuel has two of them, both normally closed: a high-pressure cut-off at the tank and a low-pressure cut-off at the regulator, which the ECM energises only in CNG mode while the engine cranks or runs.",["Open valve coil","Loose or corroded connector at the valve (often exposed under the vehicle)","Broken wire in the control circuit"],["Engine runs only on gasoline, gas mode not available","Fuel mode lamp flashes or shows an error"],2,2,["P2666","P2667","P0005","P2668"],"שסתום ניתוק דלק‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2666:["Fuel Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit Low","P2666 is stored when the control line of fuel shut-off valve B sits at too low a voltage, the typical sign of a short to ground between module and valve or inside the coil. Depending on how the driver is built, the valve may then open whenever the ignition is on, or the module switches the output off for protection. No manufacturer documents P2666 publicly.",["Control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Valve coil shorted internally","Water ingress in the valve connector"],["Gas mode switched off, engine runs on gasoline","Fuel mode lamp flashes rapidly"],2,2,["P2665","P2667","P0006"],"שסתום ניתוק דלק‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2667:["Fuel Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit High","With P2667 the module measures excess voltage on the wire that drives shut-off valve B, usually because the wire touches a supply circuit. Safety matters here: on a low-side driven valve a short to voltage can keep the coil energised even when the module wants the valve closed, so the gaseous fuel may not be shut off reliably. No manufacturer explains P2667 publicly.",["Control wire shorted to a voltage supply","Corrosion bridging pins in the valve connector","Faulty output stage in the control module"],["Gas mode disabled, operation on gasoline only","Fuel mode lamp indicates an error","Possible gas smell if the valve does not close"],2,2,["P2665","P2666","P0007"],"שסתום ניתוק דלק‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2668:["Fuel Mode Indicator Lamp Control Circuit","Bi-fuel vehicles tell the driver which fuel is in use through a small indicator, often built into the fuel selector button. On GM's 2016 Silverado and Sierra with CNG the light is off on gasoline, steady on natural gas, flashes once per second during a changeover and flashes about ten times per second when the CNG system has a fault; the 2015 Impala Bi-Fuel uses a similar light in its CNG switch.",["Indicator LED or bulb in the selector switch failed","Open wire or loose connector at the switch","Lamp driver in the control module defective"],["Fuel mode lamp stays dark in gas mode","No flashing during fuel changeover or on errors"],1,0,["P26E2","P26E3","P25A4","P2665"],"נורת חיווי מצב דלק — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],P2669:["Actuator Supply Voltage B Circuit/Open","Many transmission controllers feed their solenoids through internal high-side switches, called actuator supply A and B. Ford's 6R140 splits its Transmission Solenoid Power Control into two wires: TSPC-A powers shift solenoids A, C and E (fault P0657), TSPC-B powers SSB, SSD, TCC and line pressure control (P2669).",["Open supply wire or connector between module and transmission bulkhead","Damaged internal transmission harness or lead frame","High-side switch inside the controller failed"],["Transmission stuck in a fixed gear (failsafe)","Harsh engagements due to maximum line pressure","MIL or transmission warning on"],3,3,["P2670","P2671","P0657","P2684"],"מתח אספקה מפעיל‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P266A:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit (Bank 2)',"P266A is the basic circuit fault for the bank 2 position sensor of rocker arm actuator A. It only applies to engines that have a lift actuator with position feedback on each cylinder bank, which is rare; most switching rocker systems on V engines rely on oil pressure switches or none at all.",["Poor contact at the bank 2 sensor connector","Damaged wiring between sensor and engine controller","Failed bank 2 position sensor"],["MIL on","Lift on bank 2 no longer adjusted","Reduced power and smoothness"],3,3,["P266B","P266C","P266D","P266E","P2655","P264A"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2)"],P266B:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2)',"For bank 2, P266B means the position reported for actuator A is electrically valid but does not match what was commanded or changes too slowly. CARB expects variable lift monitors to notice when the commanded position is missed or reached too late, and a sensor whose reading drifts from the real actuator position defeats both. No manufacturer publishes P266B;",["Bank 2 actuator or linkage binding","Sensor reading drifting from the true position","Control software calling for an update"],["MIL on after a drive cycle","Uneven running between the banks","Hesitation under load"],3,3,["P266A","P2656","P264B"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2)"],P266C:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2)',"P266C reports a bank 2 position sensor signal for actuator A that has fallen under its lower plausibility limit. Grounded signal wires, a missing sensor supply or an internal sensor short pull it down; a connector left half unplugged after other work on the harder-to-reach side of the engine is another possible trigger. No manufacturer documents P266C publicly, so there are no published thresholds.",["Bank 2 sensor signal shorted to ground","Connector not fully seated after other repairs","Missing sensor supply voltage"],["MIL on","Bank 2 held at fixed lift","Less pulling power"],3,3,["P266A","P266D","P264C"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P266D:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2)',"P266D is logged when the bank 2 position feedback of rocker arm actuator A climbs above its upper limit. Typical reasons are an interrupted sensor ground, a signal wire chafed through onto a supply line, or corrosion that raises resistance. Since the value no longer represents a reachable actuator position, the engine controller discards it. No manufacturer documents P266D publicly;",["Interrupted ground of the bank 2 sensor","Signal wire chafed onto a supply line","Corroded terminals raising circuit resistance"],["MIL on","Lift on bank 2 frozen","Reduced power"],3,3,["P266A","P266C","P264D"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P266E:['"A" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 2)',"P266E describes a bank 2 position signal from actuator A that flickers: brief dropouts or spikes appear while the reading is otherwise fine. Heat cycling near the exhaust side, vibration on a loose pin or a harness rubbing on a bracket can produce it, and it often comes and goes. No manufacturer documents P266E publicly.",["Loose pin vibrating in the bank 2 sensor plug","Connector contact degraded by heat cycling near the exhaust","Harness rubbing on a bracket"],["MIL comes and goes","Hesitation or uneven running","Fault often not present at the workshop"],3,3,["P266A","P266B","P264E"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ A — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 2)"],P266F:["A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve A Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High","Refrigerant distribution valve A is a solenoid that opens or closes one branch of the A/C circuit, for instance a rear evaporator or a battery chiller. Its driver stage in the control module protects itself: when the output current rises above its limit or the chip overheats, it switches off and reports P266F.",["Valve coil with shorted turns drawing excessive current","Short in the valve harness or connector","Valve mechanically stuck so the coil stays loaded","Overheated or defective driver stage in the control module"],["One A/C zone or the battery cooling stays inactive","Fault may return after cooling down"],2,0,["P2611","P2612","P2613"],"שסתום חלוקת גז מזגן‏ A — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה"],P2670:["Actuator Supply Voltage B Circuit Low","P2670 is set when the second high-side actuator supply delivers too little voltage while it is switched on, which nearly always means a short to ground somewhere on the supply line or in a load connected to it. GM documents it in several controllers. In the 16OBDG08 TCM tables for Silverado and Sierra a ground short is recognised at an impedance of 0.43 ohm or less, confirmed after three events, Type A.",["Supply wire chafed and shorted to ground","Shorted solenoid on the supplied group pulling the line down","Faulty high-side driver in the controller"],["Failsafe gear, no normal shifting","MIL on immediately","Further solenoid circuit codes stored alongside"],3,3,["P2669","P2671","P0658","P2685"],"מתח אספקה מפעיל‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2671:["Actuator Supply Voltage B Circuit High","P2671 points to voltage on the second actuator supply when the controller has switched it off, so the line is fed from outside or the switch inside the module no longer opens. The solenoids on that supply can then no longer be de-energised as a group, which defeats the failsafe.",["Supply line shorted to another powered circuit","High-side switch in the controller stuck closed","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the transmission connector"],["Warning lamp after the next start","Often no immediate shift complaint","Failsafe may not engage correctly if another fault occurs"],3,3,["P2669","P2670","P0659","P2686"],"מתח אספקה מפעיל‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2672:["Injection Pump Timing Offset","On diesels with an electronically controlled rotary or distributor pump, the controller needs to know how far the pump's actual delivery start sits from its nominal position relative to the crankshaft. P2672 flags that this stored or measured offset is wrong or outside the window the software accepts. CARB requires 2010-on diesels to detect injection that is too early or too late.",["Injection pump fitted or re-timed incorrectly after repair","Faulty pump timing or crank/cam reference signal","Worn pump drive (gear, belt, coupling) shifting the timing","Engine control software fault or wrong calibration"],["Check engine light on","Hard starting or rough idle","Diesel knock, smoke or reduced power"],3,3,["P2673","P2674","P0216","P0251"],"היסט תזמון משאבת הזרקה"],P2673:["Injection Pump Timing Calibration Not Learned","This code says the engine controller holds no valid learned value for the start of delivery of its injection pump. Such a value is usually taught after the pump or the controller is replaced, or after a software reflash, and lets the controller correct the pump's individual timing tolerance. The same Dodge campaign (T21, new engine software for 2004–2006 Sprinter vans) also lists P2673 beside P2672;",["Timing relearn skipped after pump or controller replacement","Software update interrupted or learned values lost","Relearn aborted because enable conditions (temperature, voltage) were not met"],["Check engine light on","Slightly rough running or more noise"],2,1,["P2672","P2674","P0216"],"כיול תזמון משאבת הזרקה — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2674:["Injection Pump Fuel Calibration Not Learned","Electronically governed diesel injection pumps meter the quantity per stroke themselves, and each unit differs slightly in how much it delivers for a given command. P2674 reports that the quantity correction for the installed pump has not been learned or stored in the controller. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; P2672 and P2673 cover the timing side of the same pump.",["Quantity learn not run after pump or controller replacement","Pump calibration data missing, wrong or not matching the installed pump","Fuel metering actuator fault preventing the learn from completing"],["Check engine light on","Smoke or uneven idle","Reduced power"],2,3,["P2672","P2673","P0251","P0252"],"כיול דלק משאבת הזרקה — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2675:["Air Cleaner Inlet Control Circuit/Open","Some engines can change where the air cleaner draws its air, for example switching between a cold inlet at the front and a second opening in the engine bay, with a flap or valve moved by a solenoid or small motor. P2675 is the open or general circuit fault of this control: the module driving the flap detects that its output line carries no current or reports a fault it cannot classify further.",["Connector at the inlet flap actuator loose or unplugged, often after air filter service","Broken wire in the actuator circuit","Open coil or motor winding in the flap actuator"],["Warning light or stored code, often without MIL","Inlet flap no longer switches","Usually no noticeable change in driving"],1,0,["P2676","P2677"],""],P2676:["Air Cleaner Inlet Control Circuit Low","P2676 means the control line of the air cleaner inlet flap sits at too low a voltage for the state the controller has commanded. On a low-side driven solenoid this typically appears when the line is shorted to ground and the actuator is energised permanently; on other designs a shorted coil pulls the voltage down.",["Control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Shorted coil in the inlet flap actuator","Water in the actuator connector"],["Code stored, often without warning lamp","Inlet flap stuck in one position","Possibly changed intake noise"],1,0,["P2675","P2677"],""],P2677:["Air Cleaner Inlet Control Circuit High","The counterpart to P2676: the controller sees the drive line of the air cleaner inlet flap at too high a voltage, so it cannot pull the actuator in when asked. A short from the control wire to battery voltage, a failed output stage, or an open coil that leaves the line at supply level produce this pattern.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Open coil in the flap actuator","Failed output stage in the control module"],["Code stored, often without warning lamp","Inlet flap remains in its default position"],1,0,["P2675","P2676"],""],P2678:["Coolant Degassing Valve Control Circuit/Open","In a sealed cooling system, air and vapour bubbles are carried through a thin vent line into the expansion tank, where they separate from the liquid; a bubble-free circuit avoids local hot spots, as cooling suppliers such as MAHLE point out. Some engines put an electrically switched valve in this degassing path so the controller can close it, for example to speed up warm-up.",["Unplugged connector or broken wire to the degassing valve","Open solenoid coil in the degassing valve","Faulty driver in the control module"],["Check engine light or stored code","Longer warm-up or slow heater output","Gurgling or air in the cooling system"],2,1,["P2679","P2680","P2681"],""],P2679:["Coolant Degassing Valve Control Circuit Low","P2679 indicates that the control line of the switched valve in the coolant vent path to the expansion tank reads too low. Usually the wire is grounded somewhere, or the solenoid has shorted turns; with a low-side driver the valve may then stay energised regardless of the command. The engine controller compares the line voltage with the state it set.",["Control wire shorted to ground","Shorted turns in the degassing valve solenoid","Coolant or water leaking into the valve connector"],["Check engine light or stored code","Slow warm-up","Coolant level fluctuations in the expansion tank"],2,1,["P2678","P2680"],""],P267A:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit (Bank 2)',"Continuously variable lift systems turn a control or eccentric shaft with an electric motor and report the shaft angle back to the engine controller. On V engines each cylinder bank has its own mechanism; Nissan's VVEL on the VQ37VHR V6 and VK50VE V8 is an example of such a two-bank layout.",["Loose, corroded or damaged plug at the bank 2 position sensor","Broken or chafed signal, reference or ground wire","Internal fault of position sensor B, bank 2","Fault in the engine or lift control module input"],["Check engine light on","Variable lift on bank 2 held at a fixed default","Reduced power or rough idle"],3,3,["P267B","P267C","P267D","P267E","P265A","P266A","P2660"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2)"],P267B:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2)',"P267B concerns the bank 2 feedback of lift actuator B when the signal is electrically sound but the angle it reports does not follow the commanded value, moves too slowly, or contradicts the mechanism's known travel. Faulty learning of the end stops, a slipping sensor mount, wear in the shaft drive or a sticking actuator can all produce this picture. No manufacturer documents P267B publicly.",["End-stop learn values lost or wrong after repair or battery disconnect","Worn or sticking shaft drive of actuator B on bank 2","Position sensor drifting or loose in its mount","Lift control software needing an update"],["Check engine light on","Hesitation or reduced power","Uneven idle when lift is frozen on one bank"],3,3,["P267A","P267C","P267D","P265B","P266B","P2661"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2)"],P267C:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2)',"With P267C the engine controller reads the bank 2 position signal of lift actuator B below its lowest valid value. A sensor of this kind is designed so that even the end stop of the shaft keeps a margin to zero volts, so a reading near ground points to an electrical cause: the signal line shorted to chassis, a lost 5 V reference, or a sensor with an internal short.",["Signal wire shorted to ground through damaged insulation","5 V reference supply to the sensor missing","Internal short in position sensor B, bank 2"],["Check engine light on","Lift on bank 2 fixed at a default position","Noticeably weaker acceleration"],3,3,["P267A","P267D","P267B","P265C","P266C"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P267D:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2)',"P267D is stored when the angle feedback of lift actuator B on bank 2 rises above its upper valid limit. Typical causes are an open sensor ground, which lets the signal float toward the reference, a signal conductor touching a supply line, or water bridging contacts in the connector.",["Open or high-resistance ground of the position sensor","Signal wire shorted to reference or battery voltage","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the sensor plug","Defective position sensor B, bank 2"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power with lift fixed on bank 2","Slightly higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P267A","P267C","P267E","P265D","P266D"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P267E:['"B" Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic (Bank 2)',"Here the bank 2 angle signal of lift actuator B is mostly plausible, yet it drops out for moments or jumps by amounts the motor-driven shaft could not cover in the time between two readings. The engine controller counts such events and sets P267E once they exceed its tolerance.",["Loose or fretted terminal in the sensor connector","Wire broken inside insulation, opening under heat or vibration","Interference from nearby ignition or actuator wiring"],["Check engine light that may come and go","Brief hesitation or surging","Uneven running when lift control on bank 2 hunts"],3,3,["P267A","P267B","P267D","P265E","P266E"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל נדנד שסתומים‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל (בנק 2)"],P267F:["Control Module Internal Temperature Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","Many control modules carry a temperature sensor on their own circuit board to protect output stages and, in transmission units, to back up fluid temperature. P267F adds an intermittent or erratic variant to the established family P0666 to P0669: the reading flickers, jumps or drops out briefly instead of being permanently too low, too high or implausible.",["Internal defect of the control module or its temperature sensor","Unstable module supply or ground causing erratic readings","Module software misinterpreting the sensor signal"],["Check engine or transmission warning light","Harsh or delayed shifts if the module uses substitute values","Often no noticeable symptom"],3,3,["P0666","P0667","P0668","P0669","P0634"],"חיישן טמפרטורה פנימית מודול בקרה‏ A — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2680:["Coolant Degassing Valve Control Circuit High","P2680 is the high-voltage fault of the degassing valve drive: the controller cannot pull the line down, so the valve stays in its unpowered state whatever is commanded. A wire touching a battery feed, an internally open solenoid, or a defective output transistor are the classic reasons.",["Control wire shorted to a battery feed","Internally open solenoid of the degassing valve","Defective output stage in the control module"],["Check engine light or stored code","Air pockets, gurgling or weak cabin heat","Temperature gauge higher than usual"],2,1,["P2678","P2679"],""],P2681:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Control Circuit/Open","Bypass valve A is an electrically driven coolant valve whose role differs by maker. P2681 flags an open or otherwise faulty drive circuit. GM's 2011 Volt table checks it in the HPC2/VICM: 40 failures in 50 samples at 100 ms, Type B. Ford's 2020–2023 gasoline summary defines valve A as the automatic transmission cooler flow (transmission warm-up) valve and sets the code when its smart driver reports a fault for 5 s.",["Failed bypass valve (motor, gear or electronics)","Chafed harness or open fuse in the valve supply","Loose or corroded valve connector","Engine control software causing false detection"],["Check engine light on","Slow warm-up of engine or transmission","Maintenance or temperature warning message"],2,1,["P2682","P2683","P26A3","P26A6","P26AC","P26B7"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2682:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Control Circuit Low","P2682 narrows the drive fault of bypass valve A to the low side: the output is pulled toward ground when it should not be. In GM's 2016 table for the second-generation Volt, the VICM sets it when motor driver 1 reports a short to low while the valve is commanded to the low position, with 4 failures in 5 samples and Type B.",["Drive wire to the valve motor shorted to ground","Internal short in the valve motor or electronics","Coolant or water corrosion in the valve plug"],["Check engine light on","Weak cabin heat or slow warm-up","Possible overheating warning under load"],2,1,["P2681","P2683","P26AB","P26AD"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2683:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Control Circuit High","For P2683 the drive of bypass valve A is shorted toward supply voltage or draws too much current. GM's 2016 Volt table has the VICM evaluate a short-to-high report from motor driver 1 while the valve is stopped or commanded to the high position; 16 failures out of 20 samples at 100 ms give a Type B fault.",["Jammed valve or shorted valve motor drawing excess current","Drive wire shorted to battery voltage","Faulty motor driver in the control module"],["Check engine light on","Changed heater output or warm-up time","Temperature warning in severe cases"],2,1,["P2681","P2682","P26AB","P26AE"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2684:["Actuator Supply Voltage C Circuit/Open","Some transmission controllers power groups of solenoids through several internal high-side outputs; supply C is the third of these rails, after A (P0657) and B (P2669). P2684 reports an open load on it.",["Broken wire or loose terminal between the module output and the supplied solenoids","Corroded or unseated transmission connector or internal lead frame","High-side output inside the controller defective"],["Transmission in default gear or limp mode","MIL on after restart","Several solenoid circuit codes stored together"],3,3,["P2685","P2686","P2669","P0657","P26E7"],"מתח אספקה מפעיל‏ C — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2685:["Actuator Supply Voltage C Circuit Low","P2685 means the third actuator supply rail sags while it is switched on, almost always because the line or one of the loads it feeds has a path to ground. Unlike the open and switch faults of this rail, GM's 2023 and 2024 TCM tables check this one continuously during operation: if the voltage at high-side output 7 falls below a share of the supply, or the averaged output current runs too high, a timer counts up and…",["Supply wire chafed through and touching ground","Shorted solenoid coil on this rail drawing excess current","Weak battery or charging fault pulling the whole supply down"],["MIL on during the same trip","Failsafe gear, no normal shifting","Blown fuse possible on the transmission supply"],3,3,["P2684","P2686","P2670","P0658","P26E8","P0882"],"מתח אספקה מפעיל‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2686:["Actuator Supply Voltage C Circuit High","The high case of supply C concerns voltage that should not be there: the rail stays live although the controller has turned it off. Causes are an internal high-side switch that no longer opens or an outside wire touching battery positive. GM's 2023 and 2024 TCM tables run this check during shutdown. With output 7 disabled, a reading above 70 % of battery voltage counts as a shorted switch;",["Internal high-side switch of the controller stuck conducting","Supply wire shorted to a battery-fed circuit in the harness","Moisture in the transmission connector creating a leakage path"],["MIL after a second trip with the fault","Limp mode or fixed gear after restart","Code returns after clearing once the key has been off"],3,3,["P2684","P2685","P2671","P0659","P26E9","P0883"],"מתח אספקה מפעיל‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2687:["Fuel Supply Heater Control Circuit/Open","Diesel engines warm the fuel at the filter so that wax crystals do not block it in frost. P2687 says the control line of that heater is open. In GM's diesel ECM tables the engine computer switches the heater relay with a low-side driver and judges the off-state voltage; more than 200 kOhm between pin and ground means open. The 2014 version (14OBDG04) needed 11 V for 3 s and 2 s of fault, Type B with MIL;",["Heater relay coil open or relay not seated","Broken control wire or corroded terminal at the filter housing","Heater element open where it is switched directly without a relay"],["Hard starting or stalling in severe cold","Power loss from a waxed fuel filter","Often no warning lamp, depending on model year"],2,1,["P2688","P2689","P269B"],"גוף חימום אספקת דלק — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2688:["Fuel Supply Heater Control Circuit Low","With P2688 the heater control line reads too low while the driver is off, which points to a grounded wire: the relay would then be energized all the time, and the filter heater runs even in summer and drains the battery after shutdown. GM's 2020 diesel table requires 0.5 ohm or less to ground and counts 10 failures in 20 samples taken every 100 ms;",["Control wire chafed against the engine or frame and grounded","Heater relay coil shorted internally","Water or fuel in the filter-housing connector"],["Service message or MIL, depending on model year","Battery drained after the vehicle stands","Fuel heater running constantly"],2,1,["P2687","P2689","P269D"],"גוף חימום אספקת דלק — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2689:["Fuel Supply Heater Control Circuit High","P2689 is logged when the fuel heater control line stays high even though the controller has commanded it on, so the relay coil is fed from battery positive and cannot be pulled in; the heater never works. GM's diesel ECM checks the low-side driver in its on state and treats 0.5 ohm or less to power as a short;",["Control wire shorted to a battery-fed wire","Heater relay sticking so feedback no longer matches the command","Low-side driver in the engine controller defective"],["No fuel heating, gelling risk below freezing","Hard cold starts and rough idle until warm","Warning lamp only on some model years"],2,1,["P2687","P2688","P269E","P26A0"],"גוף חימום אספקת דלק — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P268A:["Fuel Injector Calibration Not Learned/Programmed","P268A covers injector correction that relies on a learn routine rather than a printed code. GM's diesel tables 17OBDG04 to 19OBDG04A set it, Type A in one trip, when the small quantity learning (SQL) routine was not completed and stored before the vehicle left the assembly line. VW's 2014 Touareg 3.0 TDI (CNRB) lists it for a rail pressure deviation above 1,500–2,000 kPa lasting over 40 s.",["Injector quantity learn not completed after injector or controller replacement","Engine control software fault (e.g. Audi 2.0 TFSI 2025–2026)","Rail pressure deviation preventing correct learning","Injector worn beyond the correction range"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle or louder combustion noise","Often no noticeable change in driving"],2,1,["P268B","P2696","P262A","P0087","P0088"],""],P268B:["High Pressure Fuel Pump Calibration Not Learned/Programmed","Common rail and direct-injection petrol systems use a high pressure pump whose delivery is trimmed by a metering or volume control valve. Where the pump comes with individual correction data, or the controller has to learn its behaviour, P268B reports that this data is missing or was never taught. No manufacturer documents P268B publicly;",["Pump correction data not entered after pump replacement","Controller replaced or reflashed without transferring pump data","Pump variant does not match the software"],["Check engine light on","Long cranking or hard start","Reduced power with rail pressure deviations"],2,3,["P268A","P0087","P0088","P0089","P0090"],""],P268C:["Cylinder 1 Injector Data Incompatible","Every modern diesel injector carries a correction code from the factory flow test, and the controller must hold the code of the injector in cylinder 1. P268C sets when that code is missing, outside its range or fails the checksum. GM's 2014 four-cylinder diesel table (14OBDG04) checks the injector quantity adjustment (IQA) checksum once per drive cycle before driving, Type B.",["Correction code of a new cylinder 1 injector not entered","Code entered with a typing error, so the checksum fails","Controller replaced without transferring injector codes"],["Check engine light on","Uneven running or knock from cylinder 1"],2,1,["P268D","P2696","P268A","P0201","P02EE"],""],P268D:["Cylinder 2 Injector Data Incompatible","P268D concerns the stored flow correction for the injector in cylinder 2. In GM's 2016 four-cylinder diesel table (16OBDG04) the test runs with ignition on and passes once the end-of-line injector adjustment (EIA) value has been written via DID $61; a missing value only counts as a failure when the manufacturer enable counter is zero, i.e. on a finished production controller.",["Adjustment value of the cylinder 2 injector not programmed after replacement","Injectors moved between cylinders without updating codes","Programming session aborted (voltage drop, communication loss)"],["Check engine light on","Slight misfire feel or noise from cylinder 2"],2,1,["P268C","P268E","P2696","P0202","P02EF"],""],P268E:["Cylinder 3 Injector Data Incompatible","For cylinder 3 the controller compares the injector's correction value with what its software accepts. Ford's 2023 diesel OBD summary explains the idea well: each injector's code, kept in EEPROM, describes how far that unit departs from an idealised mean part, and a DTC is logged if the value is absent, out of range or its checksum is wrong. The monitor runs continuously and needs about half a second.",["Cylinder 3 injector replaced, code not programmed","Code from an injector variant the software does not accept","Stored injector data corrupted in the controller"],["Check engine light on","Usually no noticeable driveability change"],2,1,["P268D","P268F","P2696","P0203","P02F0"],""],P268F:["Cylinder 4 Injector Data Incompatible","P268F flags missing or unusable correction data for the injector in cylinder 4. On four-cylinder diesels it closes the series: GM's 2014 table 14OBDG04 and 2016 table 16OBDG04 list P268C to P268F and nothing beyond. The 2014 version checks the IQA checksum before each trip and rates the fault Type B, so the lamp waits for a second failed trip; the 2016 version uses the DID $63 write check and Type A.",["New cylinder 4 injector fitted without code programming","Code typed incorrectly into the scan tool","Used or replacement controller carrying another engine's codes"],["Check engine light on","Possible rough idle or higher combustion noise"],2,1,["P268E","P2690","P2696","P0204","P02F1"],""],P2690:["Cylinder 5 Injector Data Incompatible","P2690 is the first code of the series that a four-cylinder engine cannot set; it needs at least five cylinders. It reports that the flow correction for the cylinder 5 injector is absent or rejected by the controller. GM uses it in its 2025 six-cylinder diesel table 25OBDG04B as well as in its V8 diesel tables, Type A, with the value stored under DID $64.",["Cylinder 5 injector replaced without entering its code","Code entered for the wrong cylinder because of the bank numbering","Injector code programming interrupted"],["Check engine light on","Rarely uneven running"],2,1,["P268F","P2691","P2696","P0205","P02F2"],""],P2691:["Cylinder 6 Injector Data Incompatible","P2691 refers to the injector in cylinder 6. For six-cylinder diesels it is the last of the per-cylinder codes: GM's 2025 table 25OBDG04B stops at P2691, while the V8 table 25OBDG04A goes on to P2693. In both 2025 tables the check is always active on production controllers and fails if the end-of-line adjustment value was never written;",["Cylinder 6 injector code missing after replacement","Entered value rejected as implausible by the software","Controller memory fault losing stored injector data"],["Check engine light on","Possible knock or smoke from the affected cylinder"],2,1,["P2690","P2692","P2696","P0206","P02F3","P060C"],""],P2692:["Cylinder 7 Injector Data Incompatible","Only engines with seven or more cylinders can log P2692, which in practice means V8 diesels. It tells that the correction code for the cylinder 7 injector has not been stored or is unusable. GM carries it in every eight-cylinder diesel table from 17OBDG04 (2017) to 25OBDG04A (2025); the 2017 and 2020 versions evaluate it at ignition on, Type A in one trip, with the value expected under DID $66.",["Injector in cylinder 7 replaced, code not programmed","Replacement controller without the vehicle's injector codes","Software variant for the wrong engine configuration"],["Check engine light on","Usually no drivability change"],2,1,["P2691","P2693","P2696","P0207","P02F4"],""],P2693:["Cylinder 8 Injector Data Incompatible","P2693 completes the series on V8 engines and covers the injector in cylinder 8. It is set when the controller finds no valid flow correction code for that position. In GM's 2018 table 18OBDG04 the code reads DID $67 and fails only once the manufacturer enable counter is zero; the 2025 table 25OBDG04A instead keeps the check permanently on in production units. Both rate it Type A.",["Code of the new cylinder 8 injector not entered","New or reset controller lacking all injector codes","Typing error in the cylinder 8 code"],["Check engine light on","Possible rough idle or knock"],2,1,["P2692","P2694","P2696","P0208","P02F5"],""],P2694:["Cylinder 9 Injector Data Incompatible","P2694 would flag bad or missing correction data for the injector in cylinder 9 and therefore only fits engines with nine or more cylinders, in road vehicles essentially V10s. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM's diesel tables end at P2693 for eight cylinders, and Ford's 2023 diesel summary covers the same eight codes; neither lists a cylinder 9 entry.",["Cylinder 9 injector code not programmed (ten-cylinder engines)","Scan tool decoding error on engines without a ninth cylinder","Controller software for a different engine"],["Check engine light on","Usually no noticeable symptoms"],2,1,["P2693","P2695","P2696","P0209","P02F6"],""],P2695:["Cylinder 10 Injector Data Incompatible","P2695 is reserved for the injector in cylinder 10, the highest cylinder number the J2012 series provides with its own data code. A ten-cylinder engine with individually coded injectors would be needed to set it, and none of the public OBD summaries reviewed here contains it: GM's 2025 V8 diesel table 25OBDG04A and Ford's 2023 diesel summary both stop at cylinder 8.",["Cylinder 10 injector code missing on a ten-cylinder engine","Misread code on engines with fewer cylinders","Controller memory or software fault"],["Check engine light on","Usually no noticeable symptoms"],2,1,["P2694","P2696","P0210","P02F7"],""],P2696:["Injector Data Incompatible","P2696 is the collective version of P268C–P2695: the controller rejects stored injector correction data without naming a cylinder. That suits systems that check the data block as a whole, or engines with more than ten cylinders. No manufacturer documents P2696 publicly; GM and Ford use the per-cylinder codes instead.",["Injector codes lost during a software update or controller replacement","Injector replaced without programming its code","Corrupted injector data block in the controller"],["Check engine light on","Louder engine noise or rough running"],2,1,["P268A","P268C","P2693","P2695"],""],P2697:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Circuit/Open","Many heavy diesels do not raise exhaust temperature for filter regeneration by late in-cylinder injection, but spray diesel straight into the exhaust ahead of the oxidation catalyst through a separate doser, often called the seventh injector. P2697 means the solenoid that meters this fuel cannot be driven because its circuit is open.",["Loose, corroded or damaged connector at the dosing module","Harness to the dosing valve broken by heat or vibration","Dosing valve coil inside the module burnt open"],["Active particulate filter regeneration not possible","Rising soot load, later derate","MIL on"],2,3,["P2698","P2699","P269A","P24F6","P24F7"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2698:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Performance","P2698 is not about wiring but about whether the exhaust fuel doser does what it is told; most often the check looks for leakage when no dosing is requested. Ford's 3.2 L Transit (2017 and 2018 summaries) compares a measured temperature downstream of the injection point with a model after at least 6 h engine-off.",["Doser valve or nozzle leaking fuel into the exhaust","Coked nozzle or line causing low flow","Exhaust temperature sensor drifting and skewing the model comparison","Engine software needing the manufacturer update"],["MIL on, often without noticeable drivability change","Regenerations fail or take unusually long","Higher fuel use or white exhaust smoke"],3,3,["P2697","P2699","P269A","P24A0","P24F6"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2699:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Circuit Low","P2699 flags the drive circuit of the exhaust fuel doser as too low, usually a grounded control wire or a shorted valve coil. The difference to P2697 matters in practice: an open circuit simply stops dosing, while a grounded line can switch the valve on without command if the short sits behind the driver, so raw fuel may reach a cold catalyst.",["Doser control wire grounded against the frame or exhaust bracket","Shorted coil of the dosing valve","Fuel or water inside the module connector"],["MIL on and regeneration inhibited","Possible white smoke if the valve opens uncommanded","Derate after prolonged soot build-up"],2,3,["P2697","P2698","P269A"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P269A:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Circuit High","The high variant of the exhaust doser circuit means the control line shows supply voltage where the driver expects it to be pulled down, typically a short to battery positive or a driver that no longer conducts. In that state the valve cannot be opened, and a hard short can also overload the output, which the controller then switches off for protection.",["Doser control wire shorted to a positive supply","Output stage in the controller not switching","Pin damage in the dosing module connector"],["MIL on, regeneration requests fail","Filter soot level climbs over time","Derate in later stages"],2,3,["P2697","P2698","P2699"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P269B:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Control Circuit/Open","Some diesels inject fuel into the exhaust through a small vaporizer whose glow plug turns the fuel into vapor before it reaches the oxidation catalyst. Ford calls this downstream injection (DSI) on the 3.2 L Transit, used so that filter regeneration needs fewer in-cylinder post injections and less oil is diluted. P269B covers an open in the circuit by which the engine computer controls that glow plug.",["Open wire or connector between engine computer and glow plug relay","Vaporizer glow plug relay coil open","Blown fuse in the glow plug control feed"],["MIL on","Particulate filter regenerations fail or become rare","More frequent in-cylinder regeneration, oil level may rise"],2,1,["P269C","P269D","P269E","P269F","P26A0","P2687"],"מצת להט טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P269C:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Control Performance","P269C is the plausibility counterpart to the electrical control codes: the wires test fine, yet the control stage of the exhaust glow plug does not behave as commanded, for example a relay or driver that does not report the expected state or reacts too slowly. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Glow plug relay switching late or not at all","Faulty feedback signal from the relay or driver","Low system voltage during the control check"],["MIL on","Particulate filter regeneration incomplete"],2,1,["P269B","P269D","P269E","P26A0"],"בקרת מצת להט טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P269D:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Control Circuit Low","A low reading on the exhaust glow plug control line points to a path to ground before the load, so the control stage cannot set the right level and the vaporizer glow plug may be switched wrongly.",["Control wire chafed on the exhaust or body and grounded","Shorted coil in the glow plug relay","Heat-damaged connector near the vaporizer"],["MIL on","Regeneration suspended, rising soot load","Possible blown fuse in the glow plug feed"],2,1,["P269B","P269C","P269E","P26A1","P2688"],"מצת להט טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P269E:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Control Circuit High","When the exhaust glow plug control circuit reads close to battery voltage at the wrong moment, the control side has contact with a positive feed or the switching stage hangs open, so the vaporizer glow plug may stay energized or ignore commands. On Ford's 3.2 L Transit diesel the 2017 and 2018 summaries set P269E once the circuit holds between 10.9 and 12.32 V for 5 s with the ignition on.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-fed circuit","Relay contacts welded, glow plug permanently powered","Output stage in the engine computer defective"],["MIL on","Glow plug failing early from constant heating","Regeneration curtailed"],2,1,["P269B","P269C","P269D","P26A2","P2689"],"מצת להט טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P269F:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Circuit/Open","While P269B concerns the line that commands the exhaust glow plug, P269F targets the load circuit itself: the heating element or its power feed is open, so no current flows even when the control stage switches correctly. A burnt-out element is the usual reason, followed by a loose terminal at the plug in the hot exhaust area. There is no public manufacturer documentation for P269F.",["Glow element burnt out","Loose or corroded terminal nut at the plug","Blown fuse in the glow plug power circuit"],["MIL on","Particulate filter regenerations fail"],2,1,["P26A0","P26A1","P26A2","P269B"],"מצת להט טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P26A0:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Performance","P26A0 says the exhaust glow plug system does not perform as intended, even if no electrical fault is present. Ford gives the clearest picture for the 3.2 L Transit diesel: from the 2017 summary on, the code is set when the feedback of the vaporizer glow plug relay disagrees with its command for roughly 60 s while the key is on, a fault filed under P2689 in earlier years.",["Fuel vaporizer glow plug degraded","Outdated engine module calibration","Blown fuse or relay feedback not matching the command"],["MIL on","Exhaust temperature control code P24A0 stored too","Regenerations take longer or fail"],2,1,["P269F","P26A1","P26A2","P269C","P24A0"],"מצת להט טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P26A1:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Circuit Low","P26A1 describes a load circuit of the exhaust glow plug that reads too low: the feed or the element has found a path to ground, so the current bypasses the heater or exceeds what the circuit allows. Shorted elements, insulation damage at the hot plug body and wiring melted against the exhaust are the expected causes; a fuse in the glow plug feed may blow repeatedly. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Glow element shorted to its housing","Feed wire melted or chafed against the exhaust","Fuse blown as a result of the short"],["MIL on","Fuse for the glow plug circuit blows again after replacement","Regeneration blocked"],2,1,["P269F","P26A0","P26A2","P269D"],"מצת להט טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P26A2:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Circuit High","The high case of the exhaust glow plug load circuit is set when the monitored point sits too close to supply voltage. Depending on how the module measures, this means the heater circuit is shorted to another positive feed or the element draws almost no current, so the voltage barely drops across it. The plug then stays cold or cannot be switched off. Public manufacturer data for P26A2 are lacking.",["Glow plug feed shorted to another battery-fed circuit","Element with greatly increased resistance near the end of its life","Glow plug relay contacts stuck closed"],["MIL on","Exhaust dosing and regeneration limited"],2,1,["P269F","P26A0","P26A1","P269E"],"מצת להט טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P26A3:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Range/Performance","P26A3 is a functional fault: the electrics of bypass valve A look fine, but the valve does not reach or report the position it should. GM's 2011 Volt table sets it, Type B, when the end-position learn fails with coolant above 50 °C, or when the valve has not arrived at its commanded position within 15 s.",["Broken gear or jammed rotor inside the bypass valve","Contaminated coolant, e.g. stop-leak additives, blocking the valve","Engine or climate control software commanding the valve incorrectly","End-position learn not completed after replacement"],["Check engine light on","Weak or delayed cabin heat","Unusual coolant or transmission temperatures"],2,1,["P2681","P26A9","P26A6","P26AB","P26B1","P26B0"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P26A4:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit","Many electric coolant valves carry a potentiometer or Hall element that reports the actual valve angle back to the controller. P26A4 is the general circuit code for that feedback on valve A: the signal is missing or cannot be assigned to a more specific low, high or erratic fault. No manufacturer documents P26A4 itself in public.",["Moisture or corrosion inside the valve's position sensor section","Loose, corroded or damaged connector or feedback wiring","Missing 5 V reference or ground for the position sensor"],["Check engine light","Slow warm-up or weak cabin heat","Possible additional valve or coolant temperature codes"],2,1,["P26A5","P26A6","P26A7","P26A8","P2681"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P26A5:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","Here the feedback signal is electrically present but sits where a healthy valve should never be. In GM's 2016 Volt table the VICM treats readings between 5 and 30 % or between 70 and 95 % of the reference as invalid; 80 failures in 100 samples at 100 ms give a Type B fault, provided the drive codes P2682/P2683/P26AD/P26AE and P26A6/P26A7 are clear. The same GM document lists a faster 3-of-5 variant for the ELR.",["Worn or corroded position sensor track inside the valve","Damaged gear or coupling between valve motor and sensor","High contact resistance at the valve connector"],["Check engine light after two drives","Engine runs too cool or warms up slowly","Fluctuating heater output"],2,1,["P26A4","P26A6","P26A7","P26A9","P26A3"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P26A6:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit Low","P26A6 means the valve A feedback voltage has dropped below its plausible floor, typically from a short to ground, a lost reference voltage or a failed sensor. GM sets it on the Volt (2011 HPC2/VICM and 2016 VICM) once the signal falls under 5 % of reference, about 0.25 V, in 40 of 50 samples at 100 ms; it is Type B, so the lamp comes on after two trips.",["Feedback wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Open 5 V reference supply to the sensor","Internal sensor failure, e.g. after coolant intrusion","Cracked valve gear (Ram 3.6 L, 07-005-24)"],["Check engine light","Delayed warm-up or reduced heater output","Valve position shown at or near zero on the scan tool"],2,1,["P26A7","P26A4","P26A5","P26A8","P2681","P26A3"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P26A7:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit High","The counterpart to P26A6: the feedback from valve A reads too high. GM's 2016 Volt table counts both a signal above its window and a broken signal circuit here, because an interrupted wire lets the input float toward the reference. The limit is 95 % of the reference (4.75 V), checked as 40 failures in 50 samples at 100 ms, Type B. The 2011 Volt table uses the same 95 % rule but prints the voltage as 4.25 V.",["Open feedback or sensor ground wire","Feedback wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Defective sensor in the valve housing"],["Check engine light","Scan tool shows valve position at maximum","Engine slow to reach operating temperature"],2,1,["P26A6","P26A4","P26A5","P26A8","P2681"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P26A8:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P26A8 targets a feedback signal that jumps or drops out briefly instead of staying wrong. No manufacturer publishes a definition for this exact code. The closest documented logic is in GM's 2011 Volt table, where under P26A9 the controller flags a reading that changes by more than 6 % between samples ten steps apart (8 of 10 or 80 of 100 samples) although no movement was commanded.",["Loose or spread terminal in the valve connector","Worn or contaminated sensor track giving dropouts","Harness rubbing on engine parts and shorting intermittently"],["Check engine light that may come and go","Erratic heater output or engine temperature","Code returns after clearing, often on rough roads"],2,1,["P26A4","P26A5","P26A6","P26A7"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ A — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P26A9:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Stop/Minimum Stop Performance","The title refers to the learned end stop of valve A. GM's use of P26A9 shifted over time. On the 2011 Volt it covered feedback sitting in a forbidden zone (5–30 % or 70–95 %), sudden jumps above 6 % and slow drift above 3 %, all Type B. In the 2016 Volt table the VICM uses it when the valve misses its commanded position within 15 s, retries the end-position learn up to three times with 10 s each, and still fails;",["Valve rotor sticking from deposits or contaminated coolant","End position not relearned after valve or module replacement","Open motor drive circuit preventing the learn routine","Drifting position sensor misreporting the stop"],["Check engine light after two drives","Engine overheats or stays too cool depending on stuck position","Weak or uneven cabin heat"],2,1,["P26AA","P26A5","P26A3","P2681","P26AB","P26B1"],""],P26AA:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Maximum Stop Performance","P26AA is the upper-limit partner of P26A9: the controller cannot confirm or learn the maximum end stop of valve A, or the reported value at full travel lies outside the expected window. No manufacturer publishes criteria for this code. GM's Volt logic for P26A9 shows how such checks work: the valve is driven to an end, given a fixed time to arrive and relearned several times before a fault is stored.",["Valve binding before reaching its maximum position","Worn or broken mechanical end stop or gear","Position sensor out of calibration near its upper end"],["Check engine light","Reduced cooling under high load","Heater or engine temperature not as expected"],2,1,["P26A9","P26A5","P26A3","P26AB"],""],P26AB:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Stuck/Open","P26AB is stored when valve A stays open although it was told to close. Ford's hybrid summaries (2014–2019) define the valve as the switch between a combined loop, with engine coolant through the heater core, and an isolated loop heated by a PTC heater;",["Valve jammed open by deposits, wear or a broken drive part","Corroded vacuum change-over valve (smart fortwo 453)","Engine control software misjudging valve state (Ram flashes)","Drive circuit fault leaving the valve in its open default"],["Check engine light","Engine takes long to warm up, higher fuel use when cold","Heater works with engine off only poorly (hybrids)"],2,1,["P26B1","P26AF","P2682","P2681","P26A3","P26A9"],""],P26AC:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Control Circuit/Open","Which valve carries the letter B depends on the maker. Ford names it in its gasoline OBD summaries for 2020–2023 and 2024–2025: valve B is the active transmission cooling valve, which sends engine coolant to the automatic transmission oil cooler, while valve A heats the transmission. P26AC is set when the smart driver in the PCM reports a fault on that output for 5 s;",["Broken wire or unplugged connector at valve B","Open solenoid or motor winding in the valve","Faulty output driver in the PCM"],["Check engine light","Transmission fluid temperature higher than normal when towing","Usually no change in normal driving"],2,1,["P26AD","P26AE","P26AF","P26B0","P2681","P26B7"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P26AD:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Control Circuit Low","P26AD indicates a drive line of valve B pulled to ground. GM uses the code differently from the title: on the second-generation Volt (2016 table, VICM) the single coolant bypass valve has an H-bridge motor with two drive lines, and P26AD stands for driver 2 reporting a short to low while the valve is commanded toward the high position. Four failures in five samples at 100 ms set it as Type B;",["Drive wire chafed and shorted to ground","Shorted valve motor winding","Coolant or water in the connector creating a leak path"],["Check engine light after two drives (GM)","Valve no longer moves, heating or warm-up affected"],2,1,["P26AE","P26AC","P2682","P26A9"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P26AE:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Control Circuit High","With P26AE the valve B drive output sees voltage where it expects none, typically a short to battery. GM's 2016 Volt table again applies it to the second drive line of the one bypass valve: the VICM sets it when driver 2 flags a short to high while the valve is stopped or commanded low, after 16 failures in 20 samples at 100 ms, Type B.",["Drive wire shorted to a battery-voltage wire","Internally shorted valve motor or solenoid drawing excess current","Damaged output stage in the control module"],["Check engine light","Valve stays in its last position","Transmission or cabin temperature control off target"],2,1,["P26AD","P26AC","P2683","P26A9"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P26AF:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Stuck/Open","P26AF is the functional fault for valve B remaining open against its command. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; Ford, for instance, monitors its valve B (transmission cooling) only electrically through P26AC/P26AE. How an open-stuck check can work is shown by Ford's hybrid logic for P26AB on valve A, which compares two coolant temperatures for 60 s after the valve should have changed state.",["Valve held open by deposits or debris","Seized actuator or broken drive gear","Coolant temperature sensor bias misleading the check"],["Check engine light","Longer warm-up, higher fuel use on short trips","Lower cabin heat in cold weather"],2,1,["P26B2","P26AB","P26B0","P26AC"],""],P26B0:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Range/Performance","P26B0 covers a valve B that is electrically sound but does not perform: it moves too slowly, stops short of its target or reports a position that does not match the command. No manufacturer publishes criteria for P26B0.",["Valve moving slowly due to contaminated or wrong coolant","Worn gear train or weak valve motor","Low supply voltage or high resistance in the drive circuit"],["Check engine light","Engine or transmission temperature outside its normal band"],2,1,["P26A3","P26AF","P26B2","P26AC"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P26B1:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Stuck Closed","P26B1 reports that valve A does not open when it should. The best documented user is the Volkswagen group plug-in hybrids. Porsche stores P26B100 in the thermal management unit (TME) of the 2019–2022 Cayenne E-Hybrid and the 2019–2021 Panamera E-Hybrid for the valve that admits engine coolant to the heating circuit once the engine passes 40 °C.",["Thermal management software misjudging the valve (Porsche, Bentley)","Valve seized closed by deposits or a failed actuator","Swapped or kinked coolant lines after repair","Drifting coolant temperature sensor used for the check"],["Check engine light, sometimes only intermittent","Cabin heat relies on the electric heater longer than usual","Possible rise in engine temperature under load"],4,1,["P26AB","P26B2","P26A3","P26A9"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ A — תקוע במצב סגור"],P26B2:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Stuck Closed","P26B2 is the closed-stuck counterpart for valve B: the controller expects coolant to flow through the valve but sees no sign of it. No manufacturer documents P26B2 in public sources. Porsche's handling of the valve A code P26B1 on its E-Hybrids illustrates the method: the thermal management unit judges the valve from the temperature difference between two coolant sensors, so a borderline reading can trip the code…",["Valve seized in the closed position","Failed actuator motor or broken coupling","Blocked or kinked coolant line downstream of the valve","Control software misjudging valve state"],["Check engine light","Rising temperature of the component served by the valve","Possible temperature warning under heavy load"],2,1,["P26AF","P26B1","P26B0","P26AC"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ B — תקוע במצב סגור"],P26B3:["Fuel Shutoff Valve A Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","Fuel shut-off valves are electrically opened valves that isolate a gaseous or liquefied fuel, as on CNG or propane systems. P26B3 says valve A does not achieve its intended effect although it was commanded.",["Leaking check valve or supply solenoid in the rail pressure module","Clogged bleed restrictor or kinked EVAP line","Shut-off valve A not switching as commanded","Blown fuse in the valve supply"],["Hard starting after the vehicle has been parked","Check engine light on some vehicles","Possible fuel odour"],3,3,["P26B4","P26B5","P0005","P009E"],"מעגל בקרת שסתום ניתוק דלק‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P26B4:["Fuel Shutoff Valve A Control Circuit Stuck On","P26B4 is the opposite failure to P26B3: shut-off valve A stays open or energised when the module wants it closed. No manufacturer documents P26B4 in public sources. On the Roush propane system for Ford trucks, valve A is the tank solenoid (its open-circuit code is P0005), and GM's 2015 Impala Bi-Fuel uses two normally closed CNG cut-off valves that the ECM opens only in gas mode while the engine cranks or runs.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Supply relay or driver stuck on","Valve A mechanically jammed open"],["Check engine light","Fuel odour after shut-off","Fuel pressure remains in the lines with the engine off"],3,3,["P26B3","P26B6","P0005","P0007"],"שסתום ניתוק דלק‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקוע במצב פעיל"],P26B5:["Fuel Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","With P26B5 shut-off valve B fails to open or pass fuel when commanded. Roush CleanTech documents the code for its Gen 4 propane system on 2016–2018 Ford trucks, where valve B is the supply solenoid in the module that regulates rail pressure (its circuit code there is P2665). Once a start is initiated, the system module checks how far rail pressure climbs; too small an increase stores P26B5.",["Supply or tank solenoid not opening","Manual valve partly closed or excess flow valve tripped","Weak fuel pumps, clogged filter or kinked lines","Blown fuse in the valve circuit"],["Engine cranks but does not start, or runs poorly","Long start sequence with pumps cycling repeatedly","Check engine light on some models"],3,3,["P26B6","P26B3","P2665","P2666","P2667"],"מעגל בקרת שסתום ניתוק דלק‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P26B6:["Fuel Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit Stuck On","P26B6 reports that shut-off valve B cannot be switched off: the control circuit or the valve remains in the on state after the module removes the command. No manufacturer documents P26B6 publicly.",["Control line shorted to battery voltage","Welded relay contact keeping the valve powered","Valve B stuck open mechanically"],["Check engine light","Fuel odour near the engine or regulator after shut-off"],3,3,["P26B5","P26B4","P2665","P2667"],"שסתום ניתוק דלק‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקוע במצב פעיל"],P26B7:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Control Circuit/Open","P26B7 is the basic electrical test of the drive output for coolant bypass valve C, with an open load as its main case. The letter is not tied to one design. Ford defines valve C as the radiator bypass in the 2020–2023 and 2024–2025 editions of its gasoline OBD summary and logs P26B7 (in 2024 also as P26B7_13) once the PCM's smart driver reports an output fault, checked continuously over 5 s.",["Failed actuator motor or coil inside bypass valve C","Unplugged, corroded or broken connector or drive wire","Engine harness chafed through near the valve","Outdated engine control software (Ford 2013 Escape 1.6L)"],["Check engine light","Engine warms up slowly or runs warmer than usual","Valve C stays in its default position"],2,1,["P26B8","P26B9","P26BB","P23C4","P26BD"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P26B8:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Control Circuit Low","With P26B8 a drive line of valve C is pulled toward ground. The best public description comes from GM's 2025 ECM table 25OBDG04B for the six-cylinder diesel: valve C sits on an H-bridge, and the controller looks for a grounded line separately in the opening and the closing direction, each time only while the other direction is free of the same fault.",["Drive wire chafed against the engine or body and shorted to ground","Internal short in the valve C motor","Water or coolant in the valve connector"],["Check engine light after two trips","Unstable or high coolant temperature","Further valve or harness codes stored at the same time"],2,1,["P26B7","P26B9","P26BB","P26BE"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P26B9:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Control Circuit High","P26B9 reports supply voltage where the valve C driver should see none, in practice a short to battery positive. Two makers document it. Ford's 2024–2025 gasoline summary pairs it with the open-circuit code as P26B9/P26B7_12: the smart driver for the radiator bypass valve flags the fault and the PCM stores it after 5 s of continuous monitoring. The 2020–2023 edition did not yet list a high code.",["Drive wire shorted to a battery-voltage circuit","Engine harness damaged by chafing or heat","Internal fault in the valve C actuator"],["Check engine light","Temperature gauge higher or more erratic than usual","Valve does not respond to scan tool commands"],2,1,["P26B7","P26B8","P26BB","P26BF"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P26BA:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Stuck/Open","P26BA is meant for a valve C that stays open although the controller wants it shut, while its circuit tests fine. No manufacturer documents this code in public sources. GM and Ford, which both use the letter C, cover their valve C functionally through other codes: GM's L3B and diesel tables treat a valve that misses its target angle as P26BB, and Ford watches its radiator bypass only electrically.",["Valve C jammed in the open position by wear or deposits","Dirty or mixed coolant hindering valve movement","Incorrectly learned end positions after a repair"],["Check engine light","Slow warm-up and lower temperature gauge reading","Weak cabin heating in cold weather"],2,1,["P26BB","P26BC","P26B7","P0128"],""],P26BB:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Range/Performance","P26BB is GM's main functional code for its rotary coolant flow control valve. The ECM compares commanded and measured angle; a gap above 12° after the target has settled, or movement slower than calibrated, counts as a fault. In the 2019 L3B table this is Type A (4 of 5 s), in the 2025 diesel table Type B (8 of 10 s).",["New valve still in its break-in phase (GM, low mileage)","ECM calibration needing an update per GM bulletin","Valve or actuator sticking or worn","Inaccurate valve position feedback"],["Check engine light","Coolant temperature higher or lower than normal","Code may disappear after further driving on a new valve"],2,3,["P26BA","P26BC","P26B7","P23C4","P23C5","P2B60"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P26BC:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Stuck Closed","P26BC covers a valve C that will not open on command even though its drive circuit is intact. Public criteria for this code are not available from any manufacturer. GM folds a valve C that fails to reach its target into the range/performance code P26BB, and Ford checks its radiator bypass valve C only for circuit faults.",["Valve C seized in the closed position","Actuator too weak to overcome friction or deposits","Low coolant level or trapped air distorting the temperature check"],["Check engine light","Rising engine temperature, possible overheat warning","Reduced engine power to protect the engine"],2,3,["P26BA","P26BB","P26B7","P0217"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ C — תקוע במצב סגור"],P26BD:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve D Control Circuit/Open","P26BD is the open-load or general circuit fault on the output that drives coolant bypass valve D. Ford is the documented user. Both editions of its gasoline OBD summary, 2020–2023 and 2024–2025, assign valve D to cabin heating, meaning the valve that routes engine coolant to the heater core, and set P26BD once the PCM's smart driver signals an output fault during continuous 5 s monitoring;",["Open coil or motor winding in valve D","Loose or corroded valve connector","Broken drive wire between PCM and valve"],["Check engine light","Weak or no cabin heat","Heater output that cannot be regulated"],2,1,["P26BE","P26BF","P26C1","P26B7"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ D — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P26BE:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve D Control Circuit Low","P26BE flags a drive circuit of valve D that reads too low, normally because the wiring or the valve itself is grounded. No manufacturer documents P26BE publicly. Ford, whose valve D is the cabin heating valve, reports only the general circuit code P26BD and, from 2024, the short-to-battery code P26BF.",["Drive wire shorted to ground","Internal short in valve D","Moisture or corrosion in the connector"],["Check engine light","Cabin heat stuck at full or at minimum","Valve D does not react to commands"],2,1,["P26BD","P26BF","P26B8"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P26BF:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve D Control Circuit High","P26BF stands for battery voltage on the valve D control line where the driver expects a switched or grounded level. Ford documents it in its 2024–2025 gasoline OBD summary: the cabin heating bypass valve is valve D, and a short to battery reported by the PCM's smart driver is stored as P26BF, internally also as P26BD_12, after continuous monitoring for 5 s.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Harness damaged near hot or moving engine parts","Internal fault in valve D"],["Check engine light","Heater stays hot or stays cold regardless of setting"],2,1,["P26BD","P26BE","P26B9"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P26C0:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve D Stuck/Open","GM uses P26C0 for the block rotary valve, which controls coolant flow through the engine block between two mechanical end stops; its tables label it as the engine block coolant valve stuck open. The ECM counts a failure when requested and measured position differ by at least 10° while the raw feedback sits at 50° or more, i.e. on the open side. The 2019 L3B table grades it Type A, one trip;",["Block valve jammed on the open side","Chafed engine harness disturbing drive or feedback (GM 21-NA-149)","Position feedback reporting a wrong angle"],["Check engine light","Longer warm-up, especially in cold weather","Higher fuel consumption on short trips"],2,1,["P26C1","P26C2","P26BD","P26BA","P0128"],""],P26C1:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve D Range/Performance","P26C1 means valve D works electrically but does not deliver the expected effect. Ford is the documented user, and on its plug-in hybrids valve D governs the cabin heating loop. Ford special service message 50325 and bulletin 22-2127 cover 2020–2022 Escape and 2021–2022 Corsair PHEVs that set P2183 for the second coolant temperature sensor, at times with an overheat warning; P26C1 can follow as a consequence.",["PCM software miscalculating heater soak time (Ford PHEV)","Contaminated connector of coolant temperature sensor 2","Valve D moving slowly or sticking","Low coolant level"],["Check engine light","Engine overheat message in the cluster","P2183 stored at the same time"],2,1,["P2183","P26C0","P26C2","P26BD"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P26C2:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve D Stuck Closed","P26C2 is the closed-side partner of P26C0, and GM again applies it to the block rotary valve of its engines. The test is the same comparison of commanded and actual angle, at least 10° apart in the 2019 L3B table (Type A, one trip) and 5° in the 2025 table 25OBDG03B (Type B), but here the raw feedback stays below 50°, so the valve is judged closed.",["Block valve seized on the closed side","Chafed engine harness (GM bulletin 21-NA-149)","Weak actuator motor unable to open the valve"],["Check engine light, immediately on GM 2019 L3B","Rising coolant temperature or overheat warning","Reduced engine power"],2,3,["P26C0","P26C1","P26BC","P0217"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ D — תקוע במצב סגור"],P26C3:["Internal Control Module Transmission Range Sensor Performance","P26C3 comes from a second, independent checking layer inside the powertrain module: it recalculates the gear selector position (P-R-N-D) and logs a fault when it cannot confirm what the main signal path reports. Ford lists the code in its gasoline OBD summaries 2020–2024 as non-MIL; the 2024 edition splits it into sub-faults for range sensor A, range sensor B and the comparison of both.",["Water ingress or corrosion in connectors of the range sensor or module wiring","Worn or misadjusted range sensor or selector giving inconsistent positions","Control module software fault, cured by a calibration update"],["Transmission or gear selector warning in the instrument cluster","Difficulty engaging a gear or leaving Park","Further codes such as P2800 or network faults stored at the same time"],2,2,["P0705","P2800","P2805","P26C4","P060D"],"חיישן טווח תיבת הילוכים מודול בקרה פנימי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P26C4:["Internal Control Module Clutch Pedal Performance","On cars with a manual gearbox, the powertrain module reads the clutch pedal through its own sensors, and an independent monitoring path inside the module checks whether that reading is credible. P26C4 is set when this check rejects the pedal information. In Ford's gasoline OBD summaries for 2020–2024 it is a non-MIL code for manual transmissions;",["Worn or misaligned clutch pedal sensor so that sensors A and B disagree","Loose or corroded pedal sensor connector or chafed wiring","Powertrain module software needing an update"],["Cruise control or stop/start not available","Engine cranks only reluctantly or not at all with the pedal pressed","Service warning without check engine lamp"],2,0,["P08A7","P08B4","P08B9","P26C3"],"דוושת מצמד מודול בקרה פנימי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P26C5:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve A Control Circuit/Open","Exhaust flow control valve A is the electrically driven flap that switches the sound path or back pressure of the exhaust, mostly on sporty models with selectable exhaust modes. P26C5 means the output stage driving valve A finds the circuit open or otherwise unusable. In Ford's gasoline OBD summaries 2020–2024 a smart driver watches the output continuously and reports the fault after about five seconds;",["Pinched, broken or unplugged actuator wiring near the exhaust","Misaligned actuator bracket or poorly seated exhaust straining the harness","Open winding or internal fault in the valve actuator"],["Exhaust mode selection not available message","Exhaust sound no longer changes between modes","Check engine lamp on some vehicles"],2,1,["P26C6","P26C7","P26FE","P2BF8"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P26C6:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve A Control Circuit Low","P26C6 reports that the drive circuit of exhaust valve A sits at too low a voltage – typically because the wiring or the actuator has shorted to ground. Ford's 2024 OBD summary shows that the PCM handles it as failure type 11 of the valve A circuit check, which runs continuously and needs about five seconds; the gasoline summaries 2020–2024 carry a typo here and print P25C6 instead of P26C6 in the threshold table.",["Control wire chafed through against the body or exhaust and shorted to ground","Internal short in the flap actuator","Water or road salt in the actuator connector"],["Check engine lamp on","Exhaust mode cannot be changed","Flap stuck in one position, exhaust permanently quiet or loud"],2,1,["P26C5","P26C7","P2BF9","P26FE"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P26C7:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve A Control Circuit High","P26C7 is the high-side counterpart: the control line of exhaust valve A carries more voltage than the driver expects, usually because the line touches battery positive or the actuator is damaged. In Ford's 2024 OBD summary it appears as failure type 12 of the valve A check, monitored all the time with a five-second window; the earlier summaries misprint it as P25C7 in their threshold list.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage or another powered circuit","Defective flap actuator electronics","Missing ground at the actuator pulling the line high"],["Check engine lamp on","Exhaust mode warning in the instrument cluster","No change in exhaust sound between modes"],2,1,["P26C5","P26C6","P2BFA","P26FE"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P26C8:["Chassis Control Module 1 Requested MIL Illumination","P26C8 is not a fault of the engine module itself. It is stored when a unit outside the powertrain, which the manufacturer designates chassis control module 1, has logged an emission-related code of its own and asks the engine module over the network to light the check engine lamp.",["Emission-related fault stored in chassis control module 1","Replaced module with mismatched or missing software configuration","Low supply voltage or network disturbance during start-up"],["Check engine lamp on","Service transmission or chassis warning message","Additional codes stored in the chassis module"],3,1,["P26C9","P25A2","P25C9","P0700"],""],P26C9:["Chassis Control Module 2 Requested MIL Illumination","P26C9 is the message slot for a second chassis control module: if module 2 detects an emission-related fault, it can ask the engine module to switch on the check engine lamp, and the engine module records this request as P26C9. No manufacturer documents this code in public.",["Emission-related fault stored in chassis control module 2","Incorrect configuration or software after module replacement","Low voltage or network fault corrupting the request message"],["Check engine lamp on","Codes stored in a chassis module in addition to the engine module"],3,1,["P26C8","P25C9","P2561","P0700"],""],P26CA:["Engine Coolant Pump Control Circuit/Open","Many engines replace the belt-driven water pump with an electric pump that has its own control electronics. P26CA flags a fault in the control connection to that pump. In the Ford 2.0 L hybrid system the pump is commanded over LIN and also has a backup run line wired to ignition; the PCM compares the state of this line reported by the pump with the real ignition state and sets P26CA after five seconds of mismatch.",["Water or corrosion in the pump connector or harness connectors","Coolant leaking from the pump body into its electronics","Broken control or backup run wire between module and pump"],["Check engine lamp on","Rising coolant temperature or temperature warning","Coolant traces at the electric pump"],2,3,["P26CB","P26CC","P26CD","P26D3","U019F"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P26CB:["Engine Coolant Pump Performance/Stuck Off","P26CB means the engine coolant pump does not deliver the expected work, typically because the impeller is blocked or turns too slowly. Ford's OBD summaries for hybrids let the pump's own electronics judge this from current and speed: too much current at too low a speed through four restart attempts is reported over LIN, and the PCM records P26CB after five seconds.",["Seized or obstructed impeller in the electric pump","Diverter shroud of a switchable mechanical pump not moving","Worn pump motor or bearing drawing excessive current","Engine module logic needing a software update"],["Check engine lamp on","Cooling fans running constantly at high speed","Rising engine temperature or reduced power"],2,3,["P26CA","P26CE","P26D2","P2601","P0217"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P26CC:["Engine Coolant Pump Control Circuit Low","P26CC reports that the circuit controlling the engine coolant pump stays at too low a voltage while the pump should be active. Honda uses the code on its two-motor hybrids and calls it a low voltage in the circuit of the electric pump: service bulletin 25-020 (Accord and CR-V Hybrid 2023–2024, Civic Hybrid 2025) explains that moisture in the pump relay can freeze at or below 0 °C, the relay then fails to switch, the…",["Moisture inside the pump relay freezing in cold weather","Pump control or supply wire shorted to ground","Blown fuse or poor supply to the relay"],["Check engine lamp on after a cold start","Poor cabin heating or rising engine temperature"],1,1,["P26CA","P26CD","P2602","P26D4"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P26CD:["Engine Coolant Pump Control Circuit High","P26CD is set when the control circuit of the engine coolant pump shows a higher voltage than the commanded state allows, for example while the driver is switched off. No manufacturer documents this code in public. CARB's OBD rule asks for output components to be monitored for circuit faults, and the same pump circuit is known from its low-side partner P26CC, which Honda documents on its hybrids in bulletin 25-020.",["Pump control wire shorted to battery voltage","Pump relay contacts stuck closed","Open ground at the pump pulling the circuit high"],["Check engine lamp on","Pump running after the engine is switched off","Longer warm-up phase"],2,1,["P26CA","P26CC","P2603","P26D5"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P26CE:["Engine Coolant Pump Overspeed/Air In System","P26CE covers a pump that spins too fast for the current it draws – a sign that it is running dry or pumping air instead of coolant. Ford's hybrid OBD summaries spell out the check: the electronics in the pump report a dry-run state over LIN when speed exceeds 4,909 rpm while current stays too low, and the PCM sets the code after five seconds.",["Low coolant level from a leak","Air pockets left after coolant service or pump replacement","Impeller loose or broken on the pump shaft"],["Coolant temperature warning in the cluster","Check engine lamp on","Gurgling noises or poor heater output"],2,3,["P26CB","P26CA","P26D2","P0217"],""],P26CF:["Engine Coolant Pump Control Module System Voltage","Smart coolant pumps carry their own electronics, which measure the supply voltage they receive. P26CF is the general code for that voltage when it is implausible but cannot be assigned to too low or too high. No manufacturer documents P26CF itself in public.",["Loose, corroded or intermittent pump supply or ground connection","Weak battery or charging system fault","Faulty voltage measurement in the pump electronics"],["Check engine lamp on","Other voltage-related codes stored at the same time"],2,1,["P26D0","P26D1","P26D3","P0562","P0563"],"מתח מערכת מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע"],P26D0:["Engine Coolant Pump Control Module System Voltage Low","P26D0 means the electronics in the engine coolant pump see less voltage than they should. On Ford's 2.0 L hybrids (C-Max, Fusion, MKZ) the pump module reports its electronics voltage over LIN, the PCM compares it with the battery voltage it measures itself and sets the code when the gap reaches about four volts for five seconds.",["Water or corrosion in a connector of the pump supply","High resistance in the pump ground or feed wire","Weak 12 V battery or low charging voltage"],["Check engine lamp on","Network codes such as U019F stored alongside","Rising engine temperature under load"],2,1,["P26CF","P26D1","P26CA","U019F","P0562"],"מערכת מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — מתח נמוך"],P26D1:["Engine Coolant Pump Control Module System Voltage High","P26D1 is stored when the electronics of the engine coolant pump report a supply voltage clearly above the vehicle system voltage. Ford documents the check in its OBD summaries for hybrid and plug-in models: the pump module passes its measured electronics voltage on via the LIN link, and a reading more than about four volts above the battery voltage seen by the PCM for five seconds sets P26D1.",["Faulty voltage regulator or overvoltage from jump starting","Poor PCM ground making the reference voltage look low","Voltage measurement drift inside the pump electronics"],["Check engine lamp on","Unusually bright lights or other overvoltage codes"],2,1,["P26CF","P26D0","P26D5","P0563"],"מערכת מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — מתח גבוה"],P26D2:["Engine Coolant Pump Control Module Over Temperature","The electronics of a smart coolant pump also measure their own temperature. P26D2 is set when this value climbs too high: in Ford's hybrid OBD summaries the pump module reports the temperature over LIN and the PCM stores P26D2 once it passes 130 °C for five seconds.",["Low coolant level or air around the pump reducing cooling of its electronics","Stiff impeller or bearing making the motor draw high current","Internal fault in the pump electronics or temperature sensor"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine temperature rising or temperature warning","Reduced heater output"],2,3,["P26CB","P26CE","P0217","U019F"],"מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — חום יתר"],P26D3:["Engine Coolant Pump Supply Voltage Circuit","P26D3 concerns the power feed and ground of the engine coolant pump. On Ford's 2.0 L hybrids the pump module has no way of reporting a loss of these lines, since without power it goes quiet on the LIN bus. The PCM therefore draws a conclusion: if pump communication is lost (U019F) and the coolant has meanwhile warmed by more than 10 °C, it assumes the pump has stopped and sets P26D3 after five seconds;",["Blown pump fuse or failed supply relay","Broken power feed or loose ground at the pump","Pump electronics dead so that the pump neither runs nor communicates"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine temperature climbing quickly","U019F stored at the same time"],2,3,["P26D4","P26D5","P26CA","U019F"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P26D4:["Engine Coolant Pump Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P26D4 narrows the supply fault of the engine coolant pump down to too low a voltage on its power feed. There is no public manufacturer documentation for this code. CARB's OBD rule requires circuit monitoring for electrical components, and Ford shows how the supply of a smart pump is judged with the general code P26D3: there the PCM infers a dead feed from lost pump communication plus a rising coolant temperature.",["Corroded fuse holder or connector in the pump feed","Supply relay with burnt contacts","Partial short to ground on the feed wire"],["Check engine lamp on","Fluctuating engine temperature or heater output"],2,1,["P26D3","P26D5","P26D0","P26CC"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P26D5:["Engine Coolant Pump Supply Voltage Circuit High","P26D5 is set when the power feed of the engine coolant pump carries a higher voltage than the system allows. No manufacturer documents this code in public. It belongs to the same supply group as P26D3 and P26D4; Ford's hybrid OBD summaries explain the supply logic on the general code, and CARB requires electrical faults of monitored components to be detected.",["Overcharging alternator or DC/DC converter","Supply relay stuck closed so the feed stays live","Feed or sensing wire shorted to another powered circuit"],["Check engine lamp on","Overvoltage codes in other control modules"],2,1,["P26D3","P26D4","P26D1","P26CD"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P26D6:["Engine Coolant Pump Clutch Control Circuit/Open","Some engines drive their mechanical coolant pump through a switchable clutch: following a cold start the pump is left idle so the coolant stays still and the engine reaches temperature sooner, and once a target is met the clutch couples the pump to its drive again.",["Broken wire or corroded, loose connector in the clutch control circuit","Open solenoid coil in the coolant pump clutch","Blown fuse or missing supply to the clutch solenoid","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Engine and cabin heater take longer to warm up","Coolant temperature behaves differently from normal after a cold start"],2,1,["P26D7","P26D8","P26D9","P26DA","P0128"],"מצמד משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P26D7:["Engine Coolant Pump Clutch Performance/Stuck Off","P26D7 is the serious case for a clutched coolant pump: the module has asked the clutch to couple the pump, but the cooling system shows no sign of circulation, so the pump is assumed to stay disconnected. The electrical side may be intact; worn friction faces, a seized armature or a pump that slips under load are typical mechanical reasons. No manufacturer documents P26D7 in public.",["Worn or slipping clutch friction surfaces","Armature or switching mechanism seized in the disengaged position","Slipping or damaged pump drive belt","Implausible coolant temperature input or outdated engine software"],["Check engine light on","Coolant temperature rises quickly, possible overheating warning","Radiator fans run at high speed","Reduced engine power to protect the engine"],3,3,["P26D6","P26D8","P26CB","P0217"],"מצמד משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P26D8:["Engine Coolant Pump Clutch Stuck On","With P26D8 the opposite of the warm-up strategy happens: the engine module wants the coolant pump decoupled after a cold start, but the pump keeps turning, so coolant circulates from the first second and the engine warms up as slowly as with a plain belt-driven pump.",["Clutch mechanically jammed or welded in the engaged position","Weak return spring or demagnetised holding magnet","No current at the solenoid in designs that need current to disengage"],["Check engine light on","Slow warm-up, heater gets warm late","Slightly higher fuel consumption on short trips"],3,1,["P26D7","P26D6","P0128"],"מצמד משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P26D9:["Engine Coolant Pump Clutch Control Circuit Low","P26D9 narrows the electrical fault of the coolant pump clutch down to a control line that sits too close to ground. The output stage in the engine module notices that the voltage on the line stays low when it should be high, which almost always points to a chafed wire touching the engine block or body, a coil with shorted turns, or water in a connector near the pump.",["Chafed control wire shorted to ground","Clutch solenoid with shorted windings","Moisture or coolant in the connector at the pump"],["Check engine light on","Changed warm-up behaviour of the engine","Possibly a blown fuse with further faults on the same circuit"],2,1,["P26DA","P26D6","P26D7"],"מצמד משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P26DA:["Engine Coolant Pump Clutch Control Circuit High","P26DA is the high-side counterpart of P26D9: the control line of the coolant pump clutch shows more voltage than the commanded state permits, for instance while the driver should be pulling it low or while it is switched off. Typical causes are a wire rubbing against a live circuit, a missing ground at the clutch so the line floats up, or an open coil that the driver reads as high.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage circuit","Open ground or poor ground contact at the clutch solenoid","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Pump clutch does not switch, warm-up or cooling behaves differently"],2,1,["P26D9","P26D6","P26D8"],"מצמד משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P26DB:["Engine Sound Control A Circuit/Open","Some sporty cars shape the sound reaching the cabin or the tailpipe with an electrically driven part, such as a switchable flap in the silencer or a valve in an intake sound pipe. Circuit A is the first of up to two such actuators. P26DB flags an interrupted drive circuit: the module switches the output but sees no load, typically a cut wire, an unplugged connector or a burnt actuator coil.",["Actuator connector unplugged or not fully seated, often after exhaust or intake work","Broken wire near the hot exhaust or at a moving section of the harness","Internal open circuit in the sound valve or actuator","Sound component removed or replaced by an aftermarket part without electrical equivalent"],["Check engine light, depending on the manufacturer","Sport sound or valve opening no longer noticeable","Driving behaviour otherwise unchanged"],2,1,["P26DC","P26DD","P26DE","P26EC","P26C5"],"בקרת צליל מנוע‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P26DC:["Engine Sound Control A Circuit Low","P26DC reports that the control line of sound actuator A sits at too low a voltage, which points to the wire or the actuator being grounded rather than interrupted. Depending on the design, the driver stage then cannot switch the flap or valve, or switches it permanently because the ground path bypasses it.",["Control wire chafed through and touching body or exhaust metal","Moisture or corrosion in the actuator connector","Shorted winding inside the sound actuator","Faulty output stage in the controlling module"],["Check engine light","Exhaust or intake sound does not change between driving modes","Possibly a blown fuse for the actuator circuit"],2,1,["P26DB","P26DD","P26DE","P26ED","P26C6"],"בקרת צליל מנוע‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P26DD:["Engine Sound Control A Circuit High","With P26DD the module measures a voltage on the drive line of sound actuator A that is higher than the switching state allows. The usual reason is contact with a live conductor, for instance a neighbouring supply wire in a melted harness, or an internal fault in the actuator that feeds battery voltage back. The flap or valve may then stay energised regardless of the selected mode.",["Drive wire shorted to a supply wire, often where heat has damaged the harness","Internal fault in the actuator feeding voltage back into the drive line","Incorrect or aftermarket actuator with different electrical layout","Output stage of the controlling module defective"],["Check engine light","Valve stays in one position, sound permanently loud or quiet"],2,1,["P26DB","P26DC","P26DE","P26EE","P26C7"],"בקרת צליל מנוע‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P26DE:["Engine Sound Control A Circuit Performance","Unlike the pure wiring codes, P26DE means the circuit of sound actuator A is electrically intact but the part does not behave as commanded, for example a flap that sticks, moves too slowly or reports an implausible position.",["Exhaust sound valve sticking or worn","Engine software with too strict an evaluation, update available from the maker","Flap linkage blocked by deposits, ice or damage","Weak actuator motor or faulty position feedback"],["Check engine light","Exhaust note no longer changes, or changes late","Rattling or buzzing from the silencer area"],2,1,["P26DB","P26DC","P26DD","P26EF","P26FE"],"בקרת צליל מנוע‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P26DF:["Sensor Power Supply D Circuit/Open","Sensor power supplies A to D are separate outputs of a control module that feed groups of sensors; they are a different family from the 5 V sensor reference voltages (P0641 and following). D is the fourth such output. P26DF is the general or open-circuit code for it.",["Broken supply wire or splice to the sensors on output D","Loose or corroded pin at the control module or a sensor","Supply output D inside the control module failed"],["Check engine light","Several sensor codes stored together","Reduced power or emergency mode depending on the sensors affected"],2,3,["P26E0","P26E1","P06E6","P06B0","P06B3"],"אספקת מתח חיישן‏ D — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P26E0:["Sensor Power Supply D Circuit Low","P26E0 means the fourth sensor supply output of the control module is pulled below its normal level. Deutz documents it for the fourth ECU sensor supply, SPN 3512, in two variants: excessive current or a grounded circuit (FMI 6), and a reading below the physical limit with top severity (FMI 1).",["One sensor on supply D with an internal short pulling the output down","Supply wire chafed and touching engine ground","Moisture in a sensor plug bridging supply and ground"],["Check engine light","Group of sensor faults appearing at once","Engine derate or emergency mode"],2,3,["P26DF","P26E1","P06E7","P06B1","P06B4"],"אספקת מתח חיישן‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P26E1:["Sensor Power Supply D Circuit High","With P26E1 the fourth sensor supply of the control module reads higher than its regulated value. Deutz assigns it to SPN 3512 with FMI 0, meaning a reading beyond the upper physical limit, rated as most severe. Since the module regulates this output itself, an excessive reading normally comes from outside: a wire of supply D shorted to battery voltage or to another, higher supply, or a sensor feeding voltage back.",["Supply D wire shorted to battery voltage or a higher supply","Faulty sensor feeding voltage back into the supply rail","Regulator for supply D in the control module defective"],["Check engine light","Implausible readings from several sensors","Possible derate depending on the sensors involved"],2,3,["P26DF","P26E0","P06E8","P06B2","P06B5"],"אספקת מתח חיישן‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P26E2:["Fuel Mode Indicator Lamp Control Circuit Low","Bi-fuel vehicles show the active fuel with an indicator, often a lamp in the selector switch. GM's 2015 Impala bi-fuel lights it while running on CNG and flashes it during a fuel change; GM's 2016 CNG pickups also flash it fast to signal a gas system fault, and Ford's earlier bi-fuel trucks combined the ALT/GAS selector with its lamp in one assembly.",["Lamp control wire chafed to ground","Shorted LED or bulb in the fuel selector switch","Faulty lamp output in the controlling module"],["Fuel mode lamp dark or permanently lit","No visible warning when the gas system has a fault"],1,0,["P26E3","P2668","P25A4"],"נורת חיווי מצב דלק — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P26E3:["Fuel Mode Indicator Lamp Control Circuit High","P26E3 is the opposite case of P26E2: the module that drives the fuel mode lamp sees a voltage on its control line that is higher than its commanded state allows. With a ground-side driver this is usually a short to a 12 V feed, or an open lamp that lets the line float to supply level; with a positive-side driver it points to outside voltage reaching the output.",["Lamp control wire shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Burnt-out bulb or open LED in the selector switch","Damaged or wet connector at the selector switch"],["Fuel mode lamp stays dark","Driver cannot tell which fuel is in use"],1,0,["P26E2","P2668","P25A4"],"נורת חיווי מצב דלק — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P26E4:["Starter Relay B Circuit","Stop-start systems often use a second starter relay, and P26E4 is the general circuit fault of this relay B. On GM's 12 V stop-start engines it switches the pinion of a tandem starter: the module's high-side driver flags an open circuit when, at standstill with at least 11 V, more than 200 kOhm appear toward ground in 40 of 50 samples (50 ms each); type B, so the lamp lights after two trips.",["Open wire or loose terminal between module and relay B or pinion solenoid","Control module software misjudging the circuit, update available on some FCA models","Open coil in relay B or in the tandem starter pinion solenoid","Faulty high-side driver in the engine module"],["Check engine light","Engine does not restart from an automatic stop","Stop-start function disabled, occasional no-crank"],2,1,["P26E5","P26E6","P0615","P26F2","P26F3"],"ממסר מתנע‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P26E5:["Starter Relay B Circuit Low","P26E5 indicates that the control circuit of starter relay B is shorted against ground. GM documents it for the tandem starter pinion relay of its 12 V stop-start engines: while the driver is switched on, an impedance of 0.5 Ohm or less toward ground in 8 of 10 samples of 50 ms sets the code, enabled at standstill once run/crank voltage is at least 6.41 V; the lamp follows as type B after two trips.",["Engine harness chafed so the relay B control wire touches ground","Shorted coil in relay B or the pinion solenoid","Damaged high-side driver in the engine module"],["Check engine light","No crank or no restart after an automatic engine stop","Blown fuses and further unrelated codes if a harness short is the cause"],2,1,["P26E4","P26E6","P0616","P26F3"],"ממסר מתנע‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P26E6:["Starter Relay B Circuit High","P26E6 reports a short to positive on the control line of starter relay B. GM tests for it while its driver for the tandem starter pinion relay is off: if the line still shows 0.5 Ohm or less toward a power source for 40 out of 50 checks taken every 50 ms, with the engine stopped and at least 11 V available, the code is stored as type B.",["Relay B control wire shorted to a battery-powered wire, e.g. under the battery tray","Relay B internally fed or contacts welded","Engine module driver output not switching off"],["Check engine light","Stop-start disabled","Starter noise or grinding without a start command"],2,1,["P26E4","P26E5","P0617","P26F2"],"ממסר מתנע‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P26E7:["Actuator Supply Voltage D Circuit/Open","Supply D is the fourth switched rail with which a control module powers a group of solenoids or other loads, after A (P0657), B (P2669) and C (P2684). P26E7 reports an open load on it. GM's 2023 and 2024 TCM tables assign the code to high-side output 8 and run the check only while the module shuts down: once the output is off and a low-side output on the same load is switched on, the load should pull the line down.",["Broken wire or loose, corroded connector between the module output and the loads on supply D","Open coil in a solenoid powered from this rail","Internal fault in the high-side output of the transmission control module"],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Transmission stays in a substitute gear or limp mode","Several solenoid or clutch codes stored at the same time"],3,3,["P26E8","P26E9","P2684","P2669","P0657"],"מתח אספקה מפעיל‏ D — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P26E8:["Actuator Supply Voltage D Circuit Low","P26E8 says the voltage on supply rail D drops too far while the rail is switched on. In GM's 2023 and 2024 TCM tables this is watched continuously at high-side output 8: a timer runs when the voltage falls below a share of the supply or the averaged current is too high, and after 60 ms the code is set, Type A; it is suspended while P0882 or P0883 is present.",["Supply line or a connected load shorted to ground","Loose or corroded battery, fuse or ground connections feeding the module, or weak batteries (Volvo/Mack aftertreatment module)","Faulty sensor or solenoid on the rail drawing too much current","Internal fault in the module output stage"],["Warning light on, often only briefly or intermittently","Transmission failsafe mode with loss of the solenoids on that rail","On trucks, lost communication with NOx, PM and DEF sensors and a derate warning"],3,3,["P26E7","P26E9","P2685","P2670","P0658"],"מתח אספקה מפעיל‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P26E9:["Actuator Supply Voltage D Circuit High","The high fault of rail D is about voltage where none should be: the controller has turned supply D off, yet the line stays live. Either the high-side switch inside the module no longer opens or an outside wire touches battery positive. GM's 2023 and 2024 TCM tables check this for output 8 during shutdown;",["High-side switch in the control module stuck closed","Supply D wire chafed against a battery or ignition feed","Water or corrosion in the module connector creating a leakage path"],["Warning light on after two drive cycles","Transmission in limp mode or with restricted gears","Code appears after restarting rather than while driving"],3,3,["P26E7","P26E8","P2686","P2671","P0659"],"מתח אספקה מפעיל‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P26EA:["Fuel Pump Control Module B","Vehicles with a second fuel pump give it its own driver module, and P26EA means that module B has reported an internal fault of its own. Ford documents the code in its gasoline OBD summary for 2020 to 2023 and again in 2024 as an internal error reported by the driver module of pump B.",["Internal failure of fuel pump driver module B","Open or corroded fuel pump monitor wire between module B and the PCM or relay module","Poor power or ground at module B","Worn or seized fuel pump B overloading the module"],["Warning light on, depending on the vehicle calibration","Hesitation or power loss at high load","Hard starting or stalling if the second pump is needed"],2,1,["P2632","P027B","P025A","P064A","U016C"],"מודול בקרת משאבת דלק‏ B"],P26EB:["Alternative Fuel Control Module System Voltage","On bi-fuel engines a separate alternative fuel control module often runs the gas side. In Ford's bi-fuel CNG documentation of 2002 it contains drivers for both injector sets, switches the fuel relays, picks the active fuel from the selector switch and shuts the tank valve when gas pressure falls below 517 kPa.",["Loose, corroded or undersized power or ground connection at the gas control module","Faulty fuse, relay or feed circuit of the gas system","Weak battery or alternator voltage outside the normal range","Internal fault in the alternative fuel control module"],["Gas mode not available or vehicle switches back to gasoline","Fuel mode indicator flashes or shows a fault","Warning light on"],2,1,["P0618","P0562","P0563","P25BE","P26E2"],"מתח מערכת מודול בקרת דלק חלופי"],P26EC:["Engine Sound Control B Circuit/Open","Where a vehicle has two sound actuators, for instance one flap per tailpipe side or a valve in addition to an intake sound tube, B designates the second one. P26EC is stored when its drive circuit is broken, so switching the output produces no current. No manufacturer documents P26EC or the rest of the B row in public;",["Connector of the second actuator loose or disconnected","Wire to actuator B broken, for example by heat or vibration","Open winding inside actuator B"],["Check engine light, depending on the manufacturer","Sound changes only on one side or not at all"],2,1,["P26ED","P26EE","P26EF","P26DB","P2BF8"],"בקרת צליל מנוע‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P26ED:["Engine Sound Control B Circuit Low","P26ED concerns the second sound actuator and indicates a drive line pulled toward ground. A conductor rubbed bare on the exhaust bracket, a pinched loom or corrosion bridging the pins of a wet plug are the classic culprits, along with a shorted coil inside the actuator. No maker publishes this code or its limits; the A counterpart P26DC appears in Ford's 2014 code list, which is the closest reference.",["Insulation of the actuator B wire worn through against metal","Corroded or wet connector at actuator B","Short circuit inside actuator B"],["Check engine light","Second flap does not respond, sound only partly changes"],2,1,["P26EC","P26EE","P26EF","P26DC","P2BF9"],"בקרת צליל מנוע‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P26EE:["Engine Sound Control B Circuit High","For the second sound actuator, P26EE signals a drive circuit carrying more voltage than expected, i.e. a short to battery positive or a feed coming back from a damaged actuator. Because the line is then powered from elsewhere, flap B may hold its position no matter what the driver selects. P26EE is not published by any maker;",["Actuator B wire in contact with a positive supply wire","Damaged actuator B feeding voltage back","Faulty output stage for circuit B in the module"],["Check engine light","Second flap stuck in one position"],2,1,["P26EC","P26ED","P26EF","P26DD","P2BFA"],"בקרת צליל מנוע‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P26EF:["Engine Sound Control B Circuit Performance","P26EF is the functional fault of the second sound actuator: wiring checks pass, yet flap or valve B does not reach or report the commanded state in time. No maker documents P26EF publicly. The A-side equivalent P26DE is well described for the Nissan GT-R, where the electric valve on the main muffler was the cause and could be renewed separately after a software check, and Ford monitors its exhaust valves for a stuck…",["Flap B binding due to soot, rust or a seized shaft","Worn gearbox or weak motor in actuator B","Evaluation in the module software too sensitive"],["Check engine light","Sound of the second branch changes late or not at all","Rattle from the flap housing"],2,1,["P26EC","P26ED","P26EE","P26DE","P2BFB"],"בקרת צליל מנוע‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P26F0:["Starter Relay A Stuck On","P26F0 says that starter relay A remains closed even though the module has withdrawn its command, so current keeps flowing to the starter or its solenoid. Unlike the circuit codes P0615 to P0617, the wiring may be intact; the problem lies in the switching itself, typically welded contacts or a sticking armature.",["Welded or sticking contacts in starter relay A","Relay A control circuit fed from elsewhere so the coil stays energised","Faulty crank feedback signal suggesting a closed relay"],["Starter keeps running or grinding after the engine has started","Check engine light, stop-start disabled","Burning smell or flat battery after short trips"],1,1,["P26F1","P26F2","P0615","P0617"],"ממסר מתנע‏ A — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P26F1:["Starter Relay A Stuck Off","P26F1 is the opposite case to P26F0: the module commands starter relay A on, but the expected reaction never arrives, so the starter receives no power. Possible reasons are burnt or contaminated contacts, a coil that no longer pulls in, or a missing feed on the load side, for example a blown fuse or a loose battery cable at the relay. No maker documents P26F1 publicly.",["Burnt or dirty contacts in starter relay A","Blown fuse or loose power cable on the load side of the relay","Relay coil no longer pulling in","Feedback wire to the module interrupted"],["Engine does not crank, or only after several attempts","Check engine light","No restart after an automatic stop"],1,1,["P26F0","P26F3","P0615","P0616"],"ממסר מתנע‏ A — תקוע במצב כבוי"],P26F2:["Starter Relay B Stuck On","P26F2 concerns the second starter relay, which on stop-start vehicles may engage the pinion of a tandem starter (GM) or form the second switching path of a two-relay layout (FCA Starter Control 2). The code means relay B fails to drop out after its command ends. Depending on wiring, the pinion may then remain in mesh, or the starter could be energised as soon as relay A closes.",["Contacts of relay B welded or stuck","Control line of relay B fed from another circuit","Pinion solenoid of the tandem starter sticking mechanically"],["Grinding or whining from the starter after the engine runs","Check engine light, stop-start unavailable"],2,1,["P26F3","P26F0","P26E4","P26E6"],"ממסר מתנע‏ B — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P26F3:["Starter Relay B Stuck Off","P26F3 reports that starter relay B does not switch through when commanded, so the start sequence that depends on it cannot complete. It is the one code of this group with a public manufacturer case: an FCA STAR case for the Jeep Gladiator, released in March 2022, describes a check engine light and a no-start with P26F3, P00FD and P0562 stored, caused by loose power cables at the power control relay;",["Loose power cable at the relay or power distribution unit","Burnt contacts in starter relay B","Weak battery or low system voltage so the relay does not pull in","Open coil in relay B"],["Check engine light","Engine does not start or crank","Further codes for low system voltage or battery state"],1,1,["P26F2","P26F1","P26E4","P0562","P00FD"],"ממסר מתנע‏ B — תקוע במצב כבוי"],P26F4:["Coolant Pump C Control Circuit/Open","Coolant pump C is a third electric pump next to pumps A and B; which circuit it serves is defined by each manufacturer. In Bentley's V8 models from the Volkswagen group it is the auxiliary pump for the heater circuit, while GM's diesel tables use the C codes for the pump of the low-temperature loop. P26F4 means the control line to this pump is open, so the module cannot command it or receives no feedback.",["Broken control wire or loose connector at pump C","Corroded pins from road splash or coolant ingress","Internal electronics of the pump failed"],["Check engine light on","Weak cabin heating at idle or with the engine stopped","Higher charge air or component temperatures, depending on the loop"],2,1,["P26F5","P26F6","P26F7","P2600","P261A"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P26F5:["Coolant Pump C Control Circuit Low","P26F5 reports that the control circuit of coolant pump C is pulled too low. Bentley documents the code in the engine electronics of the Continental GT/GTC and Flying Spur. Bulletin 2058340/1 (Continental 2018–2019, cars without parking heater) blames internal corrosion of the additional coolant pump that shorts it out; cars built before 15 July 2019 get a pump from another supplier together with a new bracket.",["Internal corrosion of the pump causing a short circuit","Over-sensitive internal diagnosis of the pump (known pump part number)","Control wire shorted to ground or coolant in the connector"],["Check engine light on","Often no noticeable change in heating or engine behaviour","Fault may come and go (stored as intermittent)"],2,1,["P26F4","P26F6","P2C48"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P26F6:["Coolant Pump C Control Circuit High","P26F6 is stored when the control line of coolant pump C carries a higher voltage than the commanded state allows. In practice that means the wire touches a live circuit, the pump has lost its ground so the line floats up, or the line is open between driver and pump in a way the output stage reads as high. No public service document covers P26F6 itself.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Missing or corroded ground at pump C","Internal electronics of the pump failed"],["Check engine light on","Pump runs on after switch-off or does not run at all","Weak heater output with the engine idling"],2,1,["P26F5","P26F4","P26F7"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P26F7:["Coolant Pump C Supply Voltage Circuit","Unlike P26F4 to P26F6, which concern the control signal, P26F7 points to the power feed of coolant pump C: the voltage arriving at the pump is missing or implausible. A blown fuse, a relay with burnt contacts, a broken feed wire or a loose ground are the usual causes; a weak battery during cranking can also trigger it. No manufacturer documents P26F7 in public.",["Blown fuse or faulty relay in the pump C feed","Broken feed wire or loose, corroded ground","Low system voltage from a weak battery or charging fault"],["Check engine light on","Pump C does not run at all","Further codes for the same fuse or for low voltage"],2,1,["P26F4","P26F8","P26D3"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ C — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P26F8:["Coolant Pump C Stuck/Stalled","P26F8 is about mechanics rather than wiring: coolant pump C is powered and commanded but its rotor does not turn or stops under load. Smart pumps recognise this themselves from a high motor current at little or no speed, and report it to the controlling module. Debris or deposits in the pump housing, a seized bearing, a rotor stuck after a long standstill or ice in the loop are typical reasons.",["Seized bearing or rotor in pump C","Debris or deposits in the pump from contaminated coolant","Frozen coolant from an incorrect mixture"],["Check engine light on","Heating or component cooling of the affected loop fails","Pump may hum without turning"],2,1,["P26FA","P26F9","P2C48","P2BA0","P26CB"],""],P26F9:["Coolant Pump C Control Module Overtemperature","Electric coolant pumps carry their own control electronics, which are cooled by the liquid passing through the pump. P26F9 means the electronics of pump C have reported a temperature above their limit. That rarely points to a defect in the module itself; far more often coolant is missing around it, air is trapped in the pump, the impeller is partly blocked and draws high current, or the pump sits in a very hot spot.",["Low coolant level or air trapped in pump C","Partly blocked impeller causing high current","Faulty temperature sensing in the pump electronics"],["Check engine light on","Pump C runs at reduced speed or switches off temporarily","Heating or cooling of the affected loop varies"],2,1,["P26F8","P26FA","P26D2"],"מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור‏ C — חום יתר"],P26FA:["Coolant Pump C Overspeed/Air in System","P26FA flags a coolant pump C that turns far faster than it should – the classic sign of a pump moving air instead of liquid. GM uses the code in the engine module of its diesel calibrations for the pump of the low-temperature coolant loop: in table 20OBDG04 an actual speed of at least 4,500 rpm in 5 of 8 one-second samples sets it, in 25OBDG04A 4 of 5 samples suffice.",["Low coolant level or air left in the low-temperature loop after service","Leak in the loop drawing in air","Chafed engine harness corrupting pump signals","Impeller slipping on its shaft or broken"],["Check engine light on after two trips","Gurgling from the pump area","Higher charge air temperature and possibly reduced power"],1,3,["P2BA0","P26F8","P2C48","P26CE"],""],P26FB:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Stuck Closed (Bank 1)","A diesel engine routes recirculated exhaust around the EGR cooler while it is cold, so that the gas warms the engine and aftertreatment; later the bypass flap closes and the gas passes through the cooler. P26FB means the bypass on bank 1 does not open when commanded and stays in the closed, cooling position. FCA uses the code on the 3.0 L EcoDiesel (Ram 1500 2020, Jeep Wrangler).",["Blocked orifice or kinked vacuum line to the bypass actuator","Bypass flap sticking from soot and deposits","Faulty vacuum solenoid or weak vacuum supply","Outdated PCM calibration with too sensitive detection"],["Check engine light on","Longer warm-up of engine and exhaust aftertreatment","Usually no noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P26FC","P2493","P24C4","P2457"],"בקרת מעקף מצנן EGR — תקוע במצב סגור (בנק 1)"],P26FC:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Stuck Closed (Bank 2)","P26FC is the bank 2 version of P26FB and only exists on engines with a separate EGR cooler and bypass for each cylinder bank, typically V-configuration diesels. The engine module has commanded the bypass of the second bank open, but position feedback or the resulting gas temperature shows it is still closed, so the exhaust gas keeps flowing through the cooler during warm-up.",["Blocked, leaking or kinked vacuum line to the bank 2 actuator","Bypass flap of bank 2 sticking from soot deposits","Faulty actuator or control solenoid"],["Check engine light on","Slower warm-up of the exhaust aftertreatment"],2,1,["P26FB","P24C5","P2457"],"בקרת מעקף מצנן EGR — תקוע במצב סגור (בנק 2)"],P26FD:["A/C Compressor Internal Control Module Performance","Electric A/C compressors in hybrids and electric vehicles carry their own inverter and control electronics. P26FD says this built-in module does not work as expected, as judged by the module that supervises the compressor. Audi documents the code for the 2016 A3 e-tron: the Climatronic unit J255 logs it instead of the engine module, and the MIL comes on purely as a network request.",["Software error in the climate or compressor control","Internal electronics or inverter of the compressor failing","Fault in the high-voltage supply or fuse of the compressor"],["Check engine light on without a code in the engine module","Air conditioning weak or not cooling","Further A/C codes stored as sporadic"],4,1,["P0D71","P0EAE","P0EBF"],"מודול בקרה פנימי מדחס מזגן — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P26FE:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve A Control Performance","P26FE concerns the electrically driven exhaust flap A on models with selectable exhaust sound. The circuit is fine, but the flap does not reach the commanded position. Ford's OBD summaries 2020–2024 assign it to bank 1 and use two checks: the flap's smart driver reports a stuck valve over its PWM line, and a rationality test compares measured with commanded position, with a duration that depends on ambient…",["Flap sticking from corrosion, soot or freezing moisture","Exhaust or actuator bracket not seated correctly","Actuator not aligned after replacement or outdated PCM software","Worn or failed flap actuator"],["Check engine light on","Message that exhaust or drive mode is not available","No audible change in exhaust sound between modes"],2,1,["P26C5","P26C6","P26C7","P2BFB"],"בקרת שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P26FF:["Auto Configuration Throttle Input Not Present (Bank 2)","Some engine controllers set themselves up at power-on by checking which inputs are connected, so one module can serve several engine layouts. On V engines with a separate throttle body for each cylinder bank this includes a throttle position signal per bank. P26FF means the controller expects a throttle input for bank 2 but finds none during this self-configuration; P063E is the same finding for bank 1.",["Bank 2 throttle body connector unplugged or not fully seated","Open signal, reference or ground wire to the bank 2 throttle position sensor","Engine controller programmed or replaced with software for a different engine variant"],["Check engine light on","Reduced engine power or limp mode","Poor throttle response or rough idle"],2,3,["P063E","P063F","P2135"],""],P2700:["Transmission Friction Element A Apply Time Range/Performance","Automatic transmissions shift by filling and releasing clutches or brakes, the friction elements, and the controller learns how long each one takes to apply. P2700 is set when element A engages too slowly, too quickly or not plausibly compared with the commanded shift. Which part A is depends on the gearbox.",["Worn or damaged clutch A components, such as a cylinder, piston seal or one-way clutch","Sticking valve or solenoid in the main control valve body","Low, aged or incorrect transmission fluid","Adaptive shift values not relearned after repair or software update"],["Harsh, delayed or slipping shifts involving clutch A","Check engine or transmission warning light on","Incorrect gear ratio codes stored at the same time"],4,3,["P2701","P2702","P2703","P2704","P2705","P0751","P0730"],""],P2701:["Transmission Friction Element B Apply Time Range/Performance","P2701 concerns friction element B: the controller has measured an apply time for this clutch or brake that falls outside its learned window. The letter is assigned per gearbox, and bulletins show how varied the causes are. Ford's SSM 47361 pairs P2701 with P0757 on the 2018 Mustang 10R80 when it will not shift beyond second gear and traces it to one-way clutch damage in the front support.",["Mechanical damage in clutch B, such as a displaced snap ring or damaged hub","Damaged one-way clutch working together with element B","Sticking valve or pressure control solenoid for clutch B","Low or contaminated transmission fluid"],["Harsh shifts or engine flare during shifts","One or more gears missing, e.g. no upshift beyond second","Warning light on"],4,3,["P2700","P2702","P2703","P2704","P2705","P0756","P0757"],""],P2702:["Transmission Friction Element C Apply Time Range/Performance","With P2702 the transmission controller reports that friction element C does not engage within the time it expects, measured from the shift command to the moment the speed ratio changes. Which clutch C stands for differs between gearbox designs. Ford names the code in several valve body bulletins.",["Sticking valves in the main control valve body","Worn clutch C plates or leaking piston seals","Low or contaminated transmission fluid","Outdated transmission software or lost adaptive values"],["Harsh or delayed shifts on gears using clutch C","Vehicle may not shift out of Park on some Ford 8F35 units","Wrench or engine warning light on"],4,3,["P2700","P2701","P2703","P2704","P2705","P0761","P0760"],""],P2703:["Transmission Friction Element D Apply Time Range/Performance","P2703 points at friction element D: the time it needs to take up torque, as seen from turbine and output speed, no longer matches what the controller has learned. In Ford's eight-speed front-drive units the code turns up with reverse problems. TSB 21-2029 covers 2020 Escape models with the 1.5L EcoBoost and 8F24 built before 7 August 2020 that lose reverse while storing P0766 and P2703;",["Faulty or contaminated selectable one-way clutch (Ford 8F24/8F35)","Sticking valve in the main control valve body","Worn clutch D plates or leaking seals","Debris in the transmission fluid"],["No reverse or harsh engagement into reverse","Harsh or delayed shifts on gears using clutch D","Check engine light on"],4,3,["P2700","P2701","P2702","P2704","P2705","P0766","P0767"],""],P2704:["Transmission Friction Element E Apply Time Range/Performance","P2704 is stored when friction element E takes too long or too short a time to apply, judged against the speed change the controller expects for the shift. Ford bulletins tie the code directly to the E clutch.",["Pressure loss in the E clutch circuit from worn hub or damaged O-rings","Sticking valves in the main control valve body","Transmission control software needing an update","Low fluid level from a leak"],["Harsh engagement into drive or poor shift quality","Wrench, engine or gearbox warning on","Limp mode in a fixed gear on some gearboxes"],4,3,["P2700","P2701","P2702","P2703","P2705","P0771","P0772"],""],P2705:["Transmission Friction Element F Apply Time Range/Performance","P2705 covers the sixth friction element, F, so only transmissions with at least six shift elements use it, such as Ford's ten-speed and eight-speed families. The controller has found that F applies outside the time it has learned. Ford's SSM 50617 for Edge ST and Nautilus models from 2020 to 2022 with the 8F57 built up to 18 March 2022 reports cars returning to Park when drive or reverse is selected;",["Damaged F clutch piston seal (Ford 8F57)","Sticking valves in the main control valve body","Shift solenoid F not controlling pressure correctly","Low or degraded transmission fluid"],["Harsh or slipping shifts in the gears using clutch F","Vehicle may fall back into Park when drive or reverse is selected (Ford 8F57)","Warning light on"],4,3,["P2700","P2701","P2702","P2703","P2704","P2707","P2706"],""],P2706:["Shift Solenoid F","P2706 is the general code for the sixth shift solenoid, F. Ford's 2024 OBD summary uses it as the base for all shift solenoid F faults in its 10R60/10R80, 8F35/8F40, 8F57 and 8F24 transmissions: with a fault-type byte added, P2706 marks an open, a short to ground, a short to supply, an intermittent connection, stuck off and stuck on, each also carrying its own two-byte code such as P097F, P2707 or P2708.",["Open or shorted wiring or connector to shift solenoid F, often inside the transmission","Failed shift solenoid F or main control valve body","Control module software that needs reprogramming (Ram 68RFE)","Faulty solenoid driver in the PCM or TCM"],["Harsh shifts, missing gears or limp mode","Vehicle may not shift out of Park on some Ford 8F35 units","Warning light on"],3,3,["P2707","P2708","P2709","P2710","P097F","P0998","P0999","P0770"],"סולנואיד העברת הילוכים‏ F"],P2707:["Shift Solenoid F Performance/Stuck Off","P2707 is not an electrical fault: the circuit to shift solenoid F is intact, but the clutch it controls does not apply when commanded, as if the solenoid stayed off. Ford stresses that a ratio-based check cannot tell a solenoid failure apart from other faults in the clutch hydraulics. In its 2024 summary P2707 equals P2706 with the functionally-failed-off byte for the 10R and 8F families.",["Leaking or damaged clutch F piston or seals","Shift solenoid F or its valve sticking in the off position","Insufficient supply pressure, e.g. damaged fluid pump gasket","Low transmission fluid level"],["Gears using clutch F missing or slipping","Return to Park or no engagement in drive or reverse","Check engine light on"],4,3,["P2706","P2708","P2705","P0771","P0751"],"סולנואיד העברת הילוכים‏ F — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2708:["Shift Solenoid F Stuck On","P2708 means the clutch fed by shift solenoid F stays applied when the controller expects it released, although the wiring checks pass. Ford's 2024 OBD summary maps it to P2706 with the failed-on byte 7E for its 10R60/10R80, 8F35/8F40, 8F57 and 8F24 units. One bad event lasts roughly 2.5 s outside a shift or 1 s during one; each adds 3 to a counter, each correct reading removes 1, and 9 stores the code.",["Internal oil leak at a clutch cylinder or sleeve keeping the clutch applied (Ford 10R80 CDF cylinder)","Shift solenoid F mechanically sticking in the applied position (dirt, wear)","Outdated PCM/TCM calibration; Ford bulletins combine reprogramming with the repair","Debris or degraded fluid jamming valves in the valve body"],["Harsh or delayed engagement and shifts","MIL lit, often with other stuck-on or gear-ratio codes","Binding or shudder as two clutches work against each other","Transmission may hold a fixed gear for protection"],4,3,["P2706","P2707","P2709","P2710","P0772","P0767","P2705"],"סולנואיד העברת הילוכים‏ F — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2709:["Shift Solenoid F Electrical","P2709 flags an electrical fault on shift solenoid F, found by the output driver rather than by watching the gearbox shift. Hyundai and Kia list it as the circuit code for that valve: Kia bulletin TRA 051 and Hyundai 15-AT-010 call solenoid F SS-B on their six-speed transaxles and replace parts instead of the gearbox, Kia first the solenoid, then the harness to the PCM, and only then the PCM if the code returns;",["Defective coil in shift solenoid F (Hyundai/Kia replace the solenoid first)","Chafed or corroded wiring or connector between PCM/TCM and transmission","Damaged internal transmission harness or lead frame","Faulty output driver in the PCM/TCM"],["MIL lit and transmission in a fail-safe gear","Missing gears or sudden harsh shifts","Code returns immediately after clearing if the fault is permanent"],2,3,["P2706","P2710","P097F","P0998","P0999","P2708","P0753","P0758"],"חשמלי סולנואיד העברת הילוכים‏ F"],P270A:["Transmission Friction Element A Temperature Too High","P270A opens a row of six codes (A to F) for an overheated clutch or brake inside the gearbox. The controller keeps track of how hot element A gets when it slips during launches and shifts and sets the code once that value passes its limit; the code is a warning of thermal overload rather than proof of a broken part. Which physical clutch carries letter A depends on the gearbox.",["Repeated launches, creeping or towing that load element A with long slip phases","Worn element A slipping because of low apply pressure or worn linings","Low or aged transmission fluid reducing cooling of the clutch","Restricted fluid cooler or faulty cooling valve"],["Reduced engine power or gearbox warning message","Harsh or slipping engagement of the affected gear","Burnt smell of transmission fluid after heavy use"],3,2,["P270B","P270C","P270D","P270E","P270F","P2700","P2787","P0218"],"טמפרטורת אלמנט חיכוך תיבת הילוכים‏ A — ערך גבוה מדי"],P270B:["Transmission Friction Element B Temperature Too High","P270B concerns the shift element lettered B. A multi-plate clutch has no sensor of its own, so the controller usually derives its heat from the energy turned into warmth while the plates slip and from the oil temperature, then compares the result with a limit. When B exceeds it, P270B is logged and the transmission software protects the element, typically by cutting engine torque or changing shift timing.",["Slow or weak apply of element B creating extra slip (pressure or seal problem)","Stop-and-go, steep grades or trailer loads","Wrong, low or degraded fluid","Implausible fluid temperature input distorting the calculated value"],["Torque reduction or limited acceleration","Changed shift points or skipped gears","Shudder when element B engages"],3,2,["P270A","P270C","P270D","P270E","P270F","P2701","P0711"],"טמפרטורת אלמנט חיכוך תיבת הילוכים‏ B — ערך גבוה מדי"],P270C:["Transmission Friction Element C Temperature Too High","With P270C the controller reports that clutch or brake C has run hotter than its permitted limit. Typical triggers are long slip phases: creeping in heavy traffic, holding the car on a slope with the throttle, or a trailer launch.",["Creeping or holding on a grade with the throttle instead of the brake","Element C slipping from low apply pressure or worn plates","Faulty clutch cooling oil valve or restricted cooler (where fitted)","Low fluid level"],["Warning in the cluster with reduced power","Gear using element C avoided or held only briefly","Hot, darkened fluid"],3,2,["P270A","P270B","P270D","P270E","P270F","P2702"],"טמפרטורת אלמנט חיכוך תיבת הילוכים‏ C — ערך גבוה מדי"],P270D:["Transmission Friction Element D Temperature Too High","P270D is stored when the thermal state of shift element D rises above the controller's limit. The heat comes from friction during slip, so anything that lengthens slip on D counts: a sluggish apply, leaking seals in its hydraulic circuit, or hard use with a heavy load. Cooling also matters, because the fluid carries the heat away;",["Leaking seals in the apply circuit of element D lengthening slip","Blocked or undersized fluid cooler, especially when towing","Old or wrong fluid with reduced friction and cooling properties","Worn plates of element D"],["Limited torque or gear range for protection","Transmission temperature warning","Flare or slip on shifts involving element D"],3,2,["P270A","P270B","P270C","P270E","P270F","P2703","P0218"],"טמפרטורת אלמנט חיכוך תיבת הילוכים‏ D — ערך גבוה מדי"],P270E:["Transmission Friction Element E Temperature Too High","P270E reports an over-temperature of the shift element labelled E. Because the value is normally calculated rather than measured inside the clutch, a wrong input can also trigger it: an implausible fluid temperature signal or incorrect slip data from the speed sensors would distort the estimate.",["Faulty fluid temperature or speed sensor signal distorting the calculated temperature","Real slip of element E under load","Poor internal contact in the transmission control electronics","Low fluid level"],["Gearbox warning with reduced performance","Additional sensor codes stored","Slipping or delayed shifts through element E"],3,2,["P270A","P270B","P270C","P270D","P270F","P2704","P0711"],"טמפרטורת אלמנט חיכוך תיבת הילוכים‏ E — ערך גבוה מדי"],P270F:["Transmission Friction Element F Temperature Too High","P270F closes the A-to-F series and signals that element F has exceeded its temperature limit. Only gearboxes with at least six shift elements carry a letter F, so the code belongs to modern multi-speed automatics, but no maker publishes its use or thresholds.",["Element F slipping due to low pressure or wear","Severe duty such as towing, mountain driving or repeated launches","Low fluid or restricted cooler"],["Torque reduction and warning message","Gears using element F temporarily unavailable","Harsh or slipping shifts"],3,2,["P270A","P270B","P270C","P270D","P270E","P2705","P2787","P0218"],"טמפרטורת אלמנט חיכוך תיבת הילוכים‏ F — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2710:["Shift Solenoid F Intermittent","P2710 is the sporadic counterpart to P2709: the circuit of shift solenoid F drops out now and then and recovers, so a check at standstill often finds nothing. In Ford's 2024 OBD summary it equals P2706 with the intermittent byte 1F in the general solenoid list and in the 8F57 and 8F24 tables; the tables for 10R60/10R80 and 8F35/8F40 instead list P2710 for a short to supply voltage.",["Loose or spread terminal at the transmission or module connector","Wire rubbing through intermittently inside or outside the case","Moisture or corrosion in the connector","Heat-dependent internal break in the solenoid coil"],["Occasional harsh shift or brief fail-safe operation","MIL that comes and goes with the fault","No fault found during a static circuit test"],2,3,["P2706","P2709","P097F","P0999","P2708"],"סולנואיד העברת הילוכים‏ F — תקלה לסירוגין"],P2711:["Unexpected Mechanical Gear Disengagement","P2711 is set when the transmission controller sees the drivetrain act as if a gear were no longer properly engaged although it never commanded that, for example because a clutch drags or a gear does not engage as selected.",["Excessive drag torque in the dual clutch (worn or early-production plates)","Debris inside the clutch assembly","Shift fork or gear actuator not holding the gear"],["Gear indicator flashing or lit in the cluster","Shudder on the first drive-away","Selected Drive or Reverse does not engage after start-up"],4,2,["P2712","P271E","P0730","P0700"],""],P2712:["Hydraulic Power Unit Leakage","P2712 targets gearboxes whose clutches or shift forks are worked by a separate hydraulic power unit, typically an electric pump that charges a pressure accumulator. Such a system loses pressure only slowly when sealed; if pressure drops faster than expected or the pump has to recharge too often, the controller concludes there is a leak. No manufacturer documents P2712 publicly.",["Leaking or worn pressure accumulator","Internal leakage at valves or seals of the hydraulic unit","External oil leak at housing, lines or connector seals","Implausible pressure sensor signal"],["Hydraulic pump running often or for long periods","Gears not engaging or delayed engagement","Gearbox warning and emergency mode"],4,3,["P0944","P2711","P0868","P0C29"],""],P2713:["Pressure Control Solenoid D","P2713 is the umbrella code for pressure control solenoid D; it names the valve but not the kind of fault, so the failure type byte behind it carries the detail. Toyota works this way. Bulletin T-SB-0076-24 lists P271371 (actuator stuck) among several valve codes on the 2024 Tacoma and fixes it by replacing gearbox and torque converter, while T-SB-0160-18 names P27137F for 2017-2018 Highlander and Sienna with the…",["Internal transmission damage that makes the valve or its clutch stick (Toyota replaces the unit)","Pressure control solenoid D sticking from debris or wear","Wrong fluid level or degraded fluid","Wiring or connector fault on the valve circuit"],["MIL lit with further transmission codes","Harsh, late or missing shifts","Whine noise or reduced power in some vehicles"],4,3,["P2714","P2715","P2716","P2717","P2722","P0745","P0795"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ D"],P2714:["Pressure Control Solenoid D Performance/Stuck Off","P2714 says the clutch served by solenoid D does not apply as commanded, so the gearbox slips in a gear that needs it. In GM's 2016 table 16OBDG03 valve D is clutch 4 (C2-3-4-6-8) on the eight-speed and the 2-6 brake on the T76 six-speed; slip of 400 rpm or more for 3 s, counted over three events, sets it after one trip.",["Leaking clutch piston seal or damaged clutch housing (GM 10L1000 C4)","Regulator or line pressure valve stuck by debris or sediment","Internal mechanical failure such as a dislodged retainer ring (GM 10L80)","Low fluid level reducing apply pressure"],["Slipping or flare in gears that use the affected clutch","No reverse or no forward drive in some cases","MIL lit and transmission in a substitute mode"],4,3,["P2713","P2715","P2718","P2732","P2723","P0796","P0746"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ D — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2715:["Pressure Control Solenoid D Stuck On","With P2715 the opposite of P2714 has happened: the clutch fed by valve D keeps holding although the controller wants it released, so it drags into the next gear. GM checks this on its eight-speed through torque-phase and inertia-phase tests on clutch 4, and its 2018 table 18OBDG04 links the code on the nine-speed to C4 exhaust delay times (Type A).",["Debris holding a valve in the applied position","Solenoid D or redundant shutdown valve mechanically stuck","False detection during a stability-control fail-safe (Subaru CVT)","Faulty TCM/solenoid assembly (GM 2-mode hybrid date codes)"],["Harsh shift or binding as two clutches overlap","Vehicle feels braked when pulling away","MIL lit, transmission may hold a safe gear"],4,3,["P2713","P2714","P2724","P2733","P0797","P0747"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ D — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2716:["Pressure Control Solenoid D Electrical","P2716 is the general electrical code for pressure control solenoid D: the output stage sees a wrong current or voltage on the coil, without saying whether the circuit is open, grounded or shorted to supply. No manufacturer documents P2716 publicly.",["Open or shorted coil in solenoid D","Loose, corroded or not fully seated connector","Chafed internal or external harness","Faulty driver stage in the TCM"],["MIL lit and transmission in fail-safe mode","Fixed gear or missing gears","Harsh engagement after start"],2,3,["P2713","P2717","P2718","P2720","P2721","P2725"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ D"],P2717:["Pressure Control Solenoid D Intermittent","P2717 reports that the circuit or response of solenoid D drops out briefly and then comes back. Unlike a hard open or short, the fault is gone by the time the vehicle reaches the workshop, so a static measurement often looks fine. No manufacturer documents P2717 publicly.",["Spread or loose terminal at transmission or TCM connector","Wire rubbing through intermittently","Moisture or corrosion in the connector","Heat-dependent break inside the coil"],["Occasional harsh or flared shift","MIL that comes and goes","No fault found during a workshop check"],2,3,["P2713","P2716","P2718","P2726","P2710"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ D — תקלה לסירוגין"],P2718:["Pressure Control Solenoid D Control Circuit/Open","P2718 points to an open control circuit of solenoid D: the coil draws no current because a wire, pin or the winding itself is broken. GM's 2016 eight-speed table runs the open check on the clutch 4 valve and fails it after 0.3 s within a 0.5 s window (one trip); the 2017 and 2018 nine-speed tables use an impedance measurement.",["Valve body solenoid connector not fully seated (GM 8L45/8L90)","Broken wire or pushed-out pin in the harness","Open winding in solenoid D","TCM output stage fault"],["Limp-home mode with limited forward gears","MIL on immediately","Harsh engagements"],2,3,["P2716","P2719","P2720","P2721","P2727","P0960"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ D — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2719:["Pressure Control Solenoid D Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2719 means the electrical readings on the control circuit of solenoid D are implausible, although neither a clear open nor a clear short is present. In GM's 2016 table 16OBDG03 the T76 six-speed flags it when the hardware layer reports an invalid voltage in at least 4.4 of 5 seconds; valve D is the 2-6 brake there, and the code is listed without MIL.",["False history code near freezing fluid temperature in Park/Neutral (GM 6T70/6T75)","High resistance at a terminal or splice","Solenoid coil with drifting resistance","Internal TCM measurement fault"],["Stored history code without noticeable symptoms","No MIL on GM vehicles (Type C)","Occasional shift quality changes if the fault is real"],2,0,["P2718","P2720","P2721","P2728","P0965"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P271A:["Park Pawl Position Sensor A Circuit Low","With park-by-wire the pawl is moved by an actuator instead of a cable, and a position sensor tells the controller whether it is engaged. P271A means the signal of sensor A has dropped below its valid band.",["Corrosion on the park module circuit board (Ford HF55, recall 26V688)","Sensor A signal wire shorted to ground","Missing or low reference voltage to sensor A","Failed position sensor A"],["Vehicle cannot be shifted out of Park","Unexpected shift to Neutral while driving","Service warning such as Shifting System Error"],4,2,["P271B","P271C","P271D","P272C","P07B5"],"חיישן מצב תפס חניה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P271B:["Park Pawl Position Sensor A Circuit High","P271B is the upper-limit partner of P271A: the signal from park pawl position sensor A reads above its plausible range. Typical electrical causes are a broken ground or signal wire, which lets the input float towards the reference, or a short to a supply line. No manufacturer documents P271B publicly.",["Open sensor ground or signal wire","Signal wire shorted to reference or battery voltage","Corroded or loose connector at the park actuator","Failed position sensor A"],["Shift system warning on the display","Park cannot be selected or released"],4,2,["P271A","P271D","P271C","P272C"],"חיישן מצב תפס חניה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P271C:["Park Pawl Position Sensor B Circuit Low","P271C covers the second park pawl position sensor, B, whose signal has fallen below the valid range. Park-by-wire designs often fit two position signals so that a single faulty reading cannot release or engage the pawl by itself; sensor B is the backup or comparison channel to sensor A. A low reading points to a short to ground, a missing reference voltage or a sensor that has failed low.",["Sensor B signal wire shorted to ground","Reference voltage to sensor B missing or low","Corrosion inside the park actuator module","Failed position sensor B"],["Shift system warning, vehicle usually still drivable","Delayed or refused Park engagement"],4,2,["P271D","P271A","P271B","P272C"],"חיישן מצב תפס חניה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P271D:["Park Pawl Position Sensor B Circuit High","P271D is logged when the signal of park pawl position sensor B sits above its upper limit. Electrically this is the mirror image of P271C: an interrupted sensor ground, an open signal line pulled up inside the controller, or contact with a supply wire. No manufacturer documents P271D publicly, so neither thresholds nor debounce times are known;",["Open ground or signal wire of sensor B","Signal shorted to a voltage source","Moisture or corrosion in the actuator connector","Failed position sensor B"],["Shift system warning on the display","Park function restricted"],4,2,["P271C","P271B","P271A","P272C"],"חיישן מצב תפס חניה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P271E:["Transmission Performance","P271E is a broad performance code for the transmission as a whole, used when the controller finds that the gearbox does not deliver what it should even though no single sensor or valve has failed. Honda applies it to the CVT of the 2016-2020 HR-V: service bulletin A21-046 adds P271E with new PCM software that detects early slip of the primary drive belt.",["Slipping or deteriorating CVT drive belt (Honda HR-V)","Insufficient clamping or line pressure in the transmission","Control software without the latest calibration"],["Flashing D indicator and MIL on","Reduced engine power","Engine flare or weak acceleration"],4,3,["P2711","P0868","P0730","P0700"],"תיבת הילוכים — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P271F:["Electronic Gear Shift - Position Not Learned","P271F tells the technician that the controller of an electronically actuated gear shift lacks valid learned positions, so it cannot place the shift elements precisely. Automated and dual-clutch gearboxes store the end and engagement points of their actuators;",["Learn procedure not run after replacing the control unit or transmission parts","Learn procedure aborted (conditions not met, low battery voltage)","Learned values lost after a software update or power interruption","Actuator or position sensor fault preventing a successful learn"],["Gearbox warning, gear selection limited or blocked","Rough or imprecise engagement","Code returns until a successful learn"],2,2,["P0914","P0919","P2711"],""],P2720:["Pressure Control Solenoid D Control Circuit Low","P2720 reports a low signal on the control line of solenoid D, which in practice is a short to ground. GM's 2016 eight-speed table sets it on the clutch 4 valve after a 0.3 s ground-short flag within one trip; the six-speed tables do the same for their valve D.",["Control wire pinched or chafed against ground","Valve body connector not fully seated","Internally shorted solenoid D","TCM driver fault"],["MIL on and limp-home operation","Limited forward gears","Harsh shifts"],2,3,["P2716","P2718","P2719","P2721","P2729","P0962"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2721:["Pressure Control Solenoid D Control Circuit High","P2721 is logged when the control line of solenoid D reads too high, typically because it touches battery positive. GM's 2016 six-speed tables describe it as circuit high covering an open or a short to power, set after 0.3 s in one trip, so on those units an open line can land here too.",["Moisture in the control valve connector (Subaru TR580)","Control wire shorted to a supply circuit","Open circuit on units that report it as high (GM six-speed)","Faulty solenoid D or TCM driver"],["MIL on and fail-safe operation","Shift shock or missing gears","Fault may follow wet weather or washing"],2,3,["P2716","P2718","P2719","P2720","P2730","P0963","P2763"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2722:["Pressure Control Solenoid E","P2722 is the base code for pressure control solenoid E and leaves the type of fault open. No manufacturer documents P2722 publicly. The pattern can be seen on the neighbouring valve: Toyota stores P2713 for solenoid D with a failure type byte appended, so a scan tool would show the same structure for E.",["Solenoid E sticking or failing","Wiring or connector problem on the solenoid E circuit","Contaminated or low transmission fluid","TCM fault"],["MIL lit with possible further transmission codes","Irregular shifting or fail-safe gear","Engagement delay into drive or reverse"],4,3,["P2713","P2723","P2724","P2725","P2726","P2731"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ E"],P2723:["Pressure Control Solenoid E Performance/Stuck Off","P2723 means valve E fails to build the pressure its clutch needs, so that element slips or does not engage. GM's eight-speed table ties E to clutch 5 (C4-5-6-7-8-R) and sets the code after 400 rpm of slip lasting 3 s. On the Allison 1000 GM's tables call the valve PCS 1: if the on-coming clutch has not taken hold after 2 s of slip during a forward shift, a Type A fault follows.",["Blocked feed orifice in the separator plate (foreign material, GM Allison 1000)","Low fluid level or pump losing prime, especially on cold starts","Solenoid E or its regulator valve sticking","Worn clutch seals leaking apply pressure"],["Delayed, intermittent or no reverse","Slip or flare in affected gears","MIL on and range inhibit or fail-safe mode"],4,3,["P2722","P2724","P2727","P2714","P2732","P0877","P0701"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ E — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2724:["Pressure Control Solenoid E Stuck On","P2724 flags valve E as delivering pressure when it should not, so its clutch stays engaged too long. On the Allison 1000 GM watches the off-going element during shifts: an accumulated fail time of 0.3 s on upshifts, 0.5 s on closed-throttle downshifts or 3 s on direction changes counts as stuck on (Type A).",["Valve or regulator held in the applied position by debris","Internal TCM fault (GM 8L90, PIP5646)","Solenoid E mechanically stuck","Restricted clutch exhaust passage"],["Wheels lock or vehicle stops abruptly at low speed","Tie-up or harsh shift feel","MIL on, transmission may hold a safe gear"],4,3,["P2722","P2723","P2727","P2729","P2715","P2733"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ E — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2725:["Pressure Control Solenoid E Electrical","P2725 covers an unspecified electrical fault of pressure control solenoid E. The driver notices a coil current or voltage that does not fit the command but does not classify it further. No manufacturer documents P2725 publicly. GM splits the electrical checks of valve E into P2727, P2729 and P2730;",["Faulty coil in solenoid E","Corroded or loose connector","Damaged wiring between TCM and solenoid","Defective TCM output stage"],["MIL lit and default gear","Firm shifts from fallback pressure","Code returns at once if the fault is permanent"],2,3,["P2722","P2726","P2727","P2729","P2730","P2716"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ E"],P2726:["Pressure Control Solenoid E Intermittent","P2726 describes a fault on solenoid E that is there one moment and gone the next. The controller has seen short drop-outs in the circuit or in the valve's response, not a lasting failure, which makes the code hard to reproduce. No manufacturer documents P2726 publicly.",["Terminal with weak contact pressure","Harness damaged by engine movement or heat","Water or corrosion in the plug","Coil with intermittent internal break"],["Sporadic harsh shift or brief fail-safe","MIL that switches on and off","No fault visible at standstill"],2,3,["P2722","P2725","P2727","P2717"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ E — תקלה לסירוגין"],P2727:["Pressure Control Solenoid E Control Circuit/Open","P2727 is set when the control circuit of solenoid E is open, so no current can flow through the coil. GM's eight-speed table checks the clutch 5 valve for an open-circuit flag over 0.3 s, and on the Allison 1000 the test on PCS 1 is rated Type A.",["Broken wire or backed-out pin","Open winding in solenoid E","Internal TCM fault (GM 8L90, PIP5646)","Connector not latched"],["MIL on and limp-home gear","Rear wheels may lock at low speed (GM 8L90 case)","Harsh or missing shifts"],2,3,["P2725","P2728","P2729","P2730","P2718","P2724"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ E — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2728:["Pressure Control Solenoid E Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2728 marks the circuit of solenoid E as working but not plausible. GM uses it in two ways. On the Allison 1000 (16OBDG08, 17OBDG04) the TCM compares desired with actual current on PCS 1; a gap of at least 0.5 A in 10 of fewer than 20 samples sets a Type A fault with MIL. On the T76 six-speed table of 2016, where valve E serves the 1-2-3-4 clutch, an invalid voltage flag for 4.4 of 5 s sets it without MIL.",["Coil current deviating from command (resistance change, poor contact)","False history code near 0 °C fluid temperature (GM 6T70/6T75)","Unstable supply voltage to the TCM","Worn solenoid E"],["MIL on Allison-equipped trucks","History code without symptoms on GM six-speeds","Firm shifts if pressure control is degraded"],2,3,["P2719","P2727","P2729","P2730","P0965"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ E — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2729:["Pressure Control Solenoid E Control Circuit Low","P2729 indicates the control line of solenoid E is pulled low, usually by a short to ground. On the Allison 1000 GM detects this when the output connection has almost no impedance to ground and confirms it within 75 ms (Type A). The eight-speed and six-speed tables of 2016 flag the low state for 0.3 s and set it after one trip.",["Control wire shorted to ground","Shorted winding in solenoid E","TCM internal failure (GM 8L90)","Conductive contamination in the connector"],["MIL on and fail-safe mode","Abrupt stop or wheel lock at low speed in the GM 8L90 case","Limited gear selection"],2,3,["P2725","P2727","P2728","P2730","P2720"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ E — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P272A:["Transmission Range Select Motor Control Circuit","P272A refers to the control circuit of the electric motor that moves the gearbox into the selected range in shift-by-wire designs. Mitsubishi documents it for the 2022 Outlander with CVT: the shift actuator has two three-phase windings fed through separate relays, and motor A is the one reported as range select motor.",["Shift actuator relay A open or stuck off","Open U, V or W phase wire to motor A","Faulty motor coil A in the shift actuator","Electric shift control module fault"],["MIL and shift warning, often no change in driving","Gear selection refused, vehicle in neutral (second fault)"],4,3,["P272B","P272C","P272D","P271F","P0915"],"מנוע בחירת טווח תיבת הילוכים — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],P272B:["Transmission Range Select Motor Control Circuit Current Too High","P272B flags excessive current in the circuit of the range select motor, normally caused by a winding or wire shorted to supply. On the 2022 Mitsubishi Outlander with CVT, Mitsubishi checks this with ignition on: when one of the two phases that should be energised shows the non-energised voltage level (9-16 V instead of about 0 V), the code is set.",["Motor coil A or B phase shorted to power","Damaged harness between shift module and actuator","Electric shift control module fault"],["Vehicle stays in neutral, no gear can be selected","MIL and shift system warning"],4,3,["P272A","P272D","P272C","P271F"],"זרם מעגל בקרת מנוע בחירת טווח תיבת הילוכים — ערך גבוה מדי"],P272C:["Park Pawl Motor Control Circuit","P272C concerns the control circuit of the motor that engages and releases the park pawl. In the shift actuator of the 2022 Mitsubishi Outlander with CVT this is winding B, powered through its own relay B, while winding A is reported under P272A.",["Shift actuator relay B open or stuck off","Open phase wire to motor coil B","Faulty motor coil B in the actuator","Electric shift control module fault"],["MIL on, Park still works normally","Shifting blocked if the other circuit also fails"],4,3,["P272D","P272A","P271A","P271C"],"מנוע תפס חניה — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],P272D:["Park Pawl Motor Control Circuit Current Too High","P272D reports overcurrent in the park pawl motor circuit, the counterpart of P272B for the second winding. Mitsubishi's 2022 Outlander CVT service data sets it with ignition on when one of two phases of motor B that ought to carry current sits at the idle voltage level instead of near 0 V, the pattern of a line shorted to supply.",["Motor coil B or A phase shorted to power","Chafed harness at the shift actuator","Electric shift control module fault"],["Shifting locked out, vehicle held in neutral","MIL and shift warning lamp on","Park may not engage fully"],4,3,["P272C","P272B","P272A","P271A"],"זרם מעגל בקרת מנוע תפס חניה — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2730:["Pressure Control Solenoid E Control Circuit High","P2730 is stored when the control line of solenoid E sits too high, pointing to contact with a supply voltage. GM's Allison 1000 logic looks for a power short at the PCS 1 output and treats it as Type A. Its 2016 six-speed tables word the code as circuit high for an open or a power short, so there a broken wire may show up as P2730 instead of P2727.",["Control wire chafed against a supply circuit","Open line on units that report it as high (GM six-speed)","Defective solenoid E","TCM driver fault"],["MIL on and transmission in fail-safe","Harsh or missing shifts","Code sets again immediately after clearing"],2,3,["P2725","P2727","P2728","P2729","P2721"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ E — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2731:["Pressure Control Solenoid F","P2731 is the parent code for pressure control solenoid F; the standard title names the valve without the kind of fault. GM gives it a concrete job on its nine-speed (GF9) units, where valve F feeds the C6 clutch and the selectable one-way clutch.",["Outdated TCM calibration (GM 9-speed, 18-NA-097, N182200080)","Selectable one-way clutch releasing too slowly","Solenoid F or its regulator valve sticking","Contaminated or low transmission fluid"],["Hesitation or weak acceleration from low speed","Tie-up feel on the 1-2 shift or stuck in first gear","MIL on, sometimes only intermittently"],4,3,["P2732","P2733","P2734","P2735","P2722","P2713"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ F"],P2732:["Pressure Control Solenoid F Performance/Stuck Off","P2732 says that the clutch behind valve F does not take up torque although the solenoid works electrically, so the gearbox slips wherever that clutch is needed. On GM nine-speed units valve F serves clutch C6; the TCM counts a failure when C6 slip stays at 200 rpm or more for 3 s, and three such events give a Type A fault after one trip (tables 18OBDG04 and 20OBDG03A).",["Mis-stamped spacer plate or worn check ball in the valve body (GM 10L80)","Worn clutch piston seal losing apply pressure (GM 10L1000)","Solenoid F or regulator valve sticking closed","Low fluid level or aerated fluid"],["No reverse","Transmission will not shift beyond third gear","Slip or flare and MIL on"],4,3,["P2731","P2733","P2736","P2714","P2723"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ F — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2733:["Pressure Control Solenoid F Stuck On","P2733 is the reverse case of P2732: valve F keeps pressure on its clutch after the TCM has commanded it off, so the off-going element still carries torque during the shift. GM checks this on its nine-speed units by watching C6 slip while shifting. If slip stays below 50 rpm for 0.8 s during power downshifts or 0.15 s on any other shift, one failure is counted;",["Solenoid F held open mechanically (solenoid body)","Debris holding the regulator valve in the apply position","Restricted clutch exhaust passage"],["Tie-up or bind-up feel during shifts","Harsh shifts or engine flare","MIL on and fail-safe gear"],4,3,["P2731","P2732","P2715","P2724"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ F — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2734:["Pressure Control Solenoid F Electrical","P2734 is the catch-all electrical code for solenoid F: the driver stage notices coil current or voltage at odds with the command, without saying whether the line is broken, touching ground or touching battery voltage. Public documentation of P2734 by any maker is lacking.",["Corroded, loose or damaged connector at the valve body","Chafed or broken wire in the solenoid F circuit","Faulty solenoid F coil","Faulty output stage in the TCM"],["MIL on with limp-home mode","Harsh, late or missing shifts"],2,3,["P2731","P2735","P2736","P2738","P2739","P2725"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ F"],P2735:["Pressure Control Solenoid F Intermittent","By its standard title P2735 reports that solenoid F or its circuit fails only now and then, so a static check in the workshop often finds nothing. GM uses the code differently on the dual-clutch gearbox of the 2023 and 2024 Corvette: there valve F is the clutch cooling valve, and P2735 stands for a stuck lube valve.",["Clutch cooling/lube valve sticking (GM Corvette dual-clutch)","Loose or corroded connector causing dropouts","Contaminated fluid affecting valve movement","Harness chafing that opens under vibration"],["Often no noticeable symptom, code stored without MIL (GM)","Occasional harsh shift or clutch judder","Clutch overheating warning after hard driving"],4,0,["P2731","P2734","P2736","P2726"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ F — תקלה לסירוגין"],P2736:["Pressure Control Solenoid F Control Circuit/Open","P2736 points to an open control circuit on solenoid F, meaning the coil path is interrupted. GM documents the code for several gearboxes. On the eight-speed of 2016 valve F is the line pressure solenoid, and an open-circuit flag for 0.3 s within 0.5 s sets the fault in one trip.",["Broken wire or pushed-back terminal","Valve body connector not fully seated","Open winding in solenoid F","Internal TCM fault"],["MIL on and limp-home mode","Firm shifts from maximum line pressure or missing gears"],2,3,["P2734","P2737","P2738","P2739","P2727","P2812"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ F — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2737:["Pressure Control Solenoid F Control Circuit Range/Performance","The standard title describes implausible readings on the control circuit of solenoid F that are neither a clean open nor a short. GM's 2025 table 25OBDG03A fills the code with a hydraulic test on its CVT, where valve F switches the binary oil pump between half and full capacity.",["Binary pump control valve sticking (GM CVT)","Primary or secondary pulley pressure sensor reading wrong","Low or degraded CVT fluid","High resistance in the solenoid F circuit"],["MIL on after two trips","Belt slip, flare or reduced power","Whine from the CVT"],4,3,["P2736","P2738","P2739","P2728","P0841"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ F — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2738:["Pressure Control Solenoid F Control Circuit Low","P2738 reports a control line on solenoid F that reads too low, which in practice means a short to ground. In GM's 2025 table 25OBDG03A an impedance below 0.5 Ohm between the signal and controller ground, lasting 0.3 s inside a 0.5 s sampling period, is a Type A fault in one trip; the valve there controls a clutch on the nine- or ten-speed, line pressure on the eight-speed or the CVT binary pump.",["Control wire chafed through to ground","Shorted turns in solenoid F","Fluid or metal debris bridging connector pins","Faulty TCM output stage"],["MIL on and fail-safe gear","Harsh engagements or clutch drag"],2,3,["P2734","P2736","P2737","P2739","P2729","P2814"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ F — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2739:["Pressure Control Solenoid F Control Circuit High","P2739 appears when solenoid F's control line sits too high, usually because it touches battery voltage. GM reacts faster here than for the low case: 25OBDG03A needs only 0.06 s within 0.13 s before the Type A fault is set.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Short between two solenoid lines in the harness or connector","Solenoid F coil shorted internally","TCM output stage damaged"],["MIL on and limp-home mode","Shifts missing or valve function lost"],2,3,["P2734","P2736","P2737","P2738","P2730","P2815"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ F — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P273A:["Transmission Friction Element G Apply Time Range/Performance","P273A carries the apply-time test of P2700 to P2705 on to a seventh shift element, G. The controller measures how long element G needs from command to full engagement and stores the code if this time is implausibly long or short. Only gearboxes with more than six clutches and brakes need a letter G, and no manufacturer documents P273A publicly.",["Leaking piston seals in the apply circuit of element G","Pressure control or shift solenoid feeding element G sticking","Worn plates or wrong clearance of element G","Adaptive shift values out of range after repair or software update"],["Engine flare or harsh shift into gears using element G","MIL lit, possibly with ratio codes","Fail-safe gear operation"],4,3,["P273B","P2700","P2701","P2702","P2703","P2704","P2705"],""],P273B:["Transmission Friction Element H Apply Time Range/Performance","P273B is the apply-time check for an eighth shift element, H, and therefore only applies to gearboxes with at least eight clutches and brakes. The test is the same as for its siblings: the time between command and full engagement is compared with a calibrated window, and a result outside it sets the code. No manufacturer documents P273B publicly.",["Pressure loss in the apply circuit of element H (seals, valve body)","Slow-responding valve controlling element H","Worn friction plates of element H"],["Delayed or harsh shifts involving element H","MIL lit","Transmission in fail-safe mode"],4,3,["P273A","P2700","P2701","P2702","P2703","P2704","P2705"],""],P273C:["Gear Shift Control Module A Supply Voltage Low","Gear shift control module A is the electronic selector used where the gearbox is shifted by wire – lever, rotary knob or push buttons – which turns the driver's choice into a message for the transmission control module. P273C means the supply voltage that this module sees, or reports, has fallen below its lower limit. No manufacturer documents P273C or its threshold publicly.",["Weak or discharged 12 V battery, voltage dips at start","Corroded fuse contact, feed wire or ground of the selector module","Alternator or DC/DC converter not supplying enough voltage","Internal fault in the gear shift module"],["Selector warning, range cannot be changed","Vehicle will not shift out of Park","Gear indicator flickers or goes blank"],2,3,["P273D","P273E","P2DA1","P0860","U0103"],"אספקת מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים‏ A — מתח נמוך"],P273D:["Gear Shift Control Module A Supply Voltage High","P273D is the over-voltage counterpart of P273C: the gear shift control module A, the electronic selector of a by-wire gear selection, registers a supply above its permitted maximum. No manufacturer documents P273D publicly or names the limit.",["Alternator voltage regulator overcharging","Jump-start or charger delivering excessive voltage","Selector module misjudging its supply (software or hardware)"],["Selector or gearbox warning in the cluster","Range selection blocked","Other over-voltage faults in several modules"],2,3,["P273C","P273E","P2DA2","P0860","U0103"],"אספקת מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים‏ A — מתח גבוה"],P273E:["Gear Shift Control Module A Over Temperature","P273E is a condition code: the gear shift control module A – the shift-by-wire selector unit – reports that its internal temperature exceeds the safe limit. No manufacturer documents P273E or its threshold publicly.",["Internal fault or overloaded output stage in the selector module","High ambient or radiant heat at the module location","Shorted lock solenoid or actuator driven by the module"],["Selector warning, functions limited","Range changes refused until the module cools"],3,3,["P273C","P273D","P2DA3","P085D"],"מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים‏ A — חום יתר"],P273F:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor B Over Temperature Condition","P273F is a condition code, not a wiring fault: sensor B delivers a valid reading, but that reading lies above the overheating limit the calibration allows. No manufacturer publishes P273F or its threshold. The analogous code for sensor A is P0218; Saab's Aisin automatic, for instance, sets it once the fluid stays above 170 °C for over 10 s.",["Sustained high load – towing, track use, long climbs","Fluid cooler clogged or cooler valve not opening","Fluid level low or fluid aged","Sensor B reading too hot while still in range"],["Transmission overheating message","Reduced torque or changed shift pattern","Burnt-smelling or darkened fluid"],2,2,["P2740","P2741","P2742","P0218","P2753"],""],P2740:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor B Circuit","P2740 is the umbrella circuit code for a second transmission fluid temperature sensor, labelled B. The control module supplies the thermistor with a reference voltage and flags an electrical fault when the returned signal leaves its plausible window, without separating short from open.",["Loose, corroded or damaged connector or lead to sensor B","Sensor B thermistor open or shorted internally","Faulty input stage in the transmission control module"],["Warning lamp or transmission message","Fluid temperature B shows an implausible fixed value on the scan tool","Cooler or hot-fluid protection works with a substitute value"],2,1,["P2741","P2742","P2743","P2744","P0710"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2741:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2741 flags a sensor B signal that is electrically intact but physically impossible or inconsistent. The clearest published test is a rate check: GM's 2023/24 dual-clutch module calls the cooler-outlet reading faulty when its filtered gradient exceeds 700 °C per second, confirmed over five samples, as a Type B code (MIL after two trips).",["Contact resistance or loose pin causing signal jumps","Sensor B thermistor drifting or responding erratically","Fault in a control unit with built-in sensor (e.g. Mitsubishi TC-SST)"],["Warning lamp after repeated detection","Fluid temperature B jumps on the scan tool","Temperature-dependent clutch or cooler control restricted"],3,3,["P2740","P2742","P2743","P2744","P0711"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2742:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor B Circuit Low","P2742 reports that the sensor B signal sits below its valid range, and how low is defined differs by maker. GM's 2023/24 dual-clutch TCM treats a cooler temperature sensor value under 200 mV, with hysteresis, for at least 500 ms as too low, Type B; for the usual NTC thermistor that equals an extremely hot reading or a signal wire shorted to ground.",["Signal lead of sensor B chafed through and touching ground","Sensor B shorted internally","Control unit with built-in sensor faulty (Mitsubishi TC-SST)"],["Warning lamp after two trips on GM","Scan tool shows sensor B extremely hot (GM, Ford) or extremely cold (Mitsubishi)","Protective strategy with substitute temperature"],2,3,["P2740","P2741","P2743","P2744","P273F","P0712"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2743:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor B Circuit High","P2743 is the counterpart of P2742: the sensor B signal is above its valid range. In GM's 2023/24 dual-clutch TCM the cooler temperature sensor must exceed 4745 mV for 500 ms, Type B; with an NTC thermistor fed from 5 V that points to a broken wire, an unplugged connector or a short to supply voltage, and the reading looks extremely cold.",["Open circuit – broken lead or unplugged connector at sensor B","Signal lead shorted to a voltage source","CAN fault or control unit with built-in sensor (Mitsubishi TC-SST)"],["Warning lamp or transmission message","Scan tool shows sensor B extremely cold (GM, Ford) or extremely hot (Mitsubishi)","Cooler control falls back on sensor A"],2,3,["P2740","P2741","P2742","P2744","P0713"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2744:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","P2744 covers brief dropouts or jumps in the sensor B signal that do not last long enough for the steady low or high codes. No manufacturer documents P2744 publicly; the makers that do use sensor B (GM and Ford dual-clutch units, Mitsubishi Twin Clutch SST) file erratic readings under P2741 instead. By analogy, Ford's 2012 strategy for the main sensor names P0714 alongside open, short and in-range checks.",["Loose or spread terminal in the transmission connector","Harness to sensor B chafing on hot or moving parts","Moisture or corrosion in the connector"],["Warning lamp that comes and goes","Short spikes in fluid temperature B on the scan tool"],2,1,["P2740","P2741","P2742","P2743","P0714"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ B — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2745:["Intermediate Shaft Speed Sensor B Circuit","P2745 is the general circuit code for a second intermediate shaft speed sensor, called B. Such a sensor reads a shaft that turns between input and output, on a dual-clutch box typically the second clutch shaft.",["Signal or supply lead to sensor B broken or chafed to ground","Corroded or loose pins at the transmission connector","Internal fault of intermediate shaft speed sensor B","Faulty sensor input in the transmission control module"],["Check engine light and transmission warning","Harsh or delayed shifts","Limp-home mode with a fixed gear"],3,3,["P2746","P2747","P2748","P07C7","P07C8","P0791"],"חיישן מהירות ציר ביניים‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2746:["Intermediate Shaft Speed Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2746 means the sensor B signal exists but does not make sense. GM's 2023/24 dual-clutch TCM uses it for the clutch 2 speed sensor: with that clutch fully closed and no microslip, its speed must equal engine speed, and a gap of 150 rpm or more for 1.1 s sets the code; further tests compare it with the speed derived from the output shaft and watch synchronizer speed during gear engagement (above 200 rpm for 50 ms).",["Metal debris on the sensor tip or incorrect air gap to the reluctor","Interference or poor shielding causing signal spikes","Slipping clutch making the speed comparison fail","Damaged or loose reluctor ring on the shaft"],["Check engine light, often immediately","Jerky clutch engagement or erratic shifts","Limp-home mode or one half of the gearbox disabled"],3,3,["P2745","P2747","P2748","P0792","P2750"],"חיישן מהירות ציר ביניים‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2747:["Intermediate Shaft Speed Sensor B Circuit No Signal","P2747 is meant for the case where sensor B stays silent although the car is clearly moving. No manufacturer documents P2747 publicly. Ford's 2024 summary describes exactly this test for its intermediate sensors – vehicle inferred to be driving under positive torque, yet the sensor shows under 250 rpm lasting 2.5 s – but for sensor B it names only P2745, P2746 and P2748, so Ford apparently files missing pulses…",["Sensor B failed internally and delivers no pulses","Open supply or signal wire, unplugged connector","Reluctor ring displaced or sensor not seated in its bore"],["Warning lamp and transmission message while driving","Limp-home mode, often stuck in one gear","Rough or missing upshifts"],3,3,["P2745","P2746","P2748","P0793","P2751"],"מעגל חיישן מהירות ציר ביניים‏ B — אין אות"],P2748:["Intermediate Shaft Speed Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","P2748 records short interruptions in the sensor B circuit that heal before a permanent fault can be confirmed. Ford is the one maker that documents it: in the 2024 OBD summary, P2748 is the intermittent check of intermediate shaft sensor B on its ten-speed automatics, run continuously alongside the circuit code P2745 and the plausibility code P2746 within a 30 s monitoring window.",["Terminal with weak contact pressure in the sensor or gearbox connector","Harness rubbing through and touching ground intermittently","Moisture or corrosion in the connector"],["Warning lamp that comes and goes","Occasional harsh shift or shift flare"],2,3,["P2745","P2746","P2747","P0794","P2752"],"חיישן מהירות ציר ביניים‏ B — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2749:["Intermediate Shaft Speed Sensor C Circuit","P2749 covers an electrical fault in the circuit of a third intermediate shaft speed sensor, C. No manufacturer documents P2749 publicly, and it is unclear which transmission carries three such sensors: Ford's ten-speeds stop at B, and dual-clutch units have only two clutch shafts. CARB requires transmission inputs like this to be watched for broken circuits and readings beyond their span.",["Open or grounded wire between module and sensor C","Sensor C defective","Transmission control module input fault"],["Check engine light","Harsh shifts or limp-home mode"],3,3,["P2750","P2751","P2752","P07C9","P07CA","P2745"],"חיישן מהירות ציר ביניים‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P274A:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor C Circuit","P274A is the general circuit code for a third transmission fluid temperature sensor, labelled C. Few gearboxes carry three fluid sensors, and no manufacturer publicly documents which measuring point C stands for or what limits apply to P274A. CARB obliges the module to detect broken circuits and readings outside the possible span on such inputs.",["Connector or lead to sensor C damaged or corroded","Sensor C failed electrically","Control module input stage faulty"],["Warning lamp","Implausible value for temperature C on the scan tool","Restricted adaptation or protection functions"],2,1,["P274B","P274C","P274D","P274E","P0710"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P274B:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P274B means the sensor C signal is within electrical limits but does not fit the other information, for example because it barely changes while the gearbox warms or contradicts the other temperature values.",["PCM software (Ford 2020 Super Duty 6.7 L, TSB 20-2044)","Sensor C drifting or slow to respond","Added resistance in connector or lead"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Temperature C stays nearly constant while driving"],2,1,["P274A","P274C","P274D","P274E","P0711"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P274C:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor C Circuit Low","P274C indicates that the sensor C signal has fallen below the lowest value the module accepts. With the negative-temperature-coefficient thermistors normally used for fluid temperature, a low voltage corresponds to very hot fluid, so the usual culprit is a signal lead touching ground or a sensor with an internal short; real heat rarely drives the reading that far. No manufacturer publishes P274C with a threshold.",["Signal lead of sensor C shorted to ground","Internal short in sensor C","Control module input faulty"],["Warning lamp","Temperature C shows an extremely hot value"],2,1,["P274A","P274B","P274D","P274E","P274F","P0712"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P274D:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor C Circuit High","P274D is set when the sensor C signal climbs above its highest permitted value. On a thermistor supplied with 5 V via a resistor, that happens when the circuit opens – a broken wire, a corroded or unplugged connector – or when the signal line touches a voltage source; the display would then show fluid colder than any real climate produces. No manufacturer documents P274D publicly.",["Open circuit in sensor C lead or connector","Signal lead shorted to voltage","Sensor C open internally"],["Warning lamp","Temperature C shows an extremely cold value","Late converter lock-up or cautious shifting"],2,1,["P274A","P274B","P274C","P274E","P0713"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P274E:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor C Circuit Intermittent","P274E stands for an unsteady sensor C signal: short interruptions or spikes that recover before a permanent low or high fault can mature. No manufacturer publishes this code or its debounce logic. Comparable intermittent coverage exists for the main sensor, where Ford's 2012 transmission strategy lists P0714 next to the open, short and in-range checks.",["Terminal with weak contact pressure","Harness rubbing on the transmission case","Moisture in the connector"],["Intermittent warning lamp","Temperature C drops out briefly on the scan tool"],2,1,["P274A","P274B","P274C","P274D","P0714"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ C — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P274F:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor C Over Temperature Condition","P274F means sensor C reports a plausible value that is nevertheless above the overheat limit set in the calibration. It is a condition report rather than a circuit defect, and no manufacturer documents its threshold or the location of sensor C publicly. For the main sensor the equivalent is P0218, which Saab's Aisin gearbox stores at over 170 °C held longer than 10 s.",["High load or heavy clutch slip","Restricted oil flow or clogged cooler","Low or worn-out fluid","Sensor C reading too hot within range"],["Overheating warning","Limited torque or altered shifting"],2,2,["P274A","P274B","P274C","P0218","P273F"],""],P2750:["Intermediate Shaft Speed Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P2750 says that sensor C produces pulses whose speed is implausible – it disagrees with what the engaged gear and the other shaft speeds predict, jumps too fast or carries noise. No manufacturer documents P2750 publicly.",["Metal particles on the sensor tip distorting the signal","Electrical interference on the signal lead","Internal clutch slip making the speeds disagree"],["Check engine light after driving","Erratic shift points or flare between gears"],3,3,["P2749","P2751","P2752","P2746"],"חיישן מהירות ציר ביניים‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2751:["Intermediate Shaft Speed Sensor C Circuit No Signal","P2751 is reserved for a sensor C that sends no pulses at all while the vehicle is demonstrably under way. No manufacturer documents P2751 publicly. For comparison, Ford's intermediate shaft logic treats a reading below 250 rpm as missing – for 2.5 s on the 2024 ten-speeds, for 5 s on the 2012 transmissions – and it only runs once turbine and output speeds prove that the gearbox is turning.",["Sensor C electronics failed","Open circuit or disconnected plug","Reluctor missing, loose or too far from the sensor"],["Warning lamp during the drive","Limp-home gear or missing shifts"],3,3,["P2749","P2750","P2752","P2747"],"מעגל חיישן מהירות ציר ביניים‏ C — אין אות"],P2752:["Intermediate Shaft Speed Sensor C Circuit Intermittent","P2752 flags a sensor C circuit that cuts out now and then, briefly enough that neither the circuit code P2749 nor the no-signal code P2751 matures. No manufacturer documents P2752 publicly. The closest published counterpart is Ford's P2748 for sensor B on its ten-speed automatics, an intermittent check that runs continuously beside the circuit and plausibility tests.",["Terminal losing contact when hot","Insulation worn through at a bracket or edge","Water ingress into the connector"],["Sporadic warning lamp","Occasional rough shift"],2,3,["P2749","P2750","P2751","P2748"],"חיישן מהירות ציר ביניים‏ C — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2753:["Transmission Fluid Cooler Control Circuit/Open","P2753 is set when the control module finds no closed circuit to the actuator that regulates transmission fluid cooling, usually an electrically switched coolant valve that opens or shuts the flow of engine coolant through the fluid heat exchanger. With the valve output open, the module cannot steer warm-up or cooling of the gearbox oil.",["Open coil in the transmission fluid cooling valve","Loose or corroded connector at the valve, often after coolant contact","Broken control wire between module and valve","Faulty output stage in the control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Transmission fluid warms up slowly or runs hot when towing","Transmission overheat warning in severe cases"],2,1,["P2754","P2755","P0218","P0711"],"מצנן שמן תיבה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2754:["Transmission Fluid Cooler Control Circuit Low","P2754 reports that the drive line to the transmission fluid cooling actuator sits at too low a voltage, which in practice means a short to ground or a heavily loaded output. The module then cannot switch the coolant valve or cooler control as intended, and depending on design the valve may remain permanently open or closed. No manufacturer documents P2754 publicly.",["Control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Water or coolant in the valve connector","Shorted turns in the valve coil"],["Check engine lamp on","Fluid temperature higher or lower than normal for the conditions","Usually no change in shift behaviour"],2,1,["P2753","P2755","P0218"],"מצנן שמן תיבה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2755:["Transmission Fluid Cooler Control Circuit High","With P2755 the module sees a high level on the cooler actuator line at a moment when its driver should pull it down, the signature of a short to battery voltage or of a low-side driver that no longer switches. The cooling valve then either cannot be activated or stays energised all the time. No manufacturer publishes P2755;",["Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage line","Valve internally shorted to its supply terminal","Module output transistor no longer switching"],["Check engine lamp on","Cooling valve permanently on or off","Slower warm-up of the transmission in cold weather"],2,1,["P2753","P2754","P0218"],"מצנן שמן תיבה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2756:["Torque Converter Clutch Pressure Control Solenoid","P2756 is the base code for the solenoid that meters apply pressure to the torque converter clutch. On its own it names only the component; in UDS-based systems a failure-type byte says what went wrong.",["Internal transmission damage or debris in the valve body (Toyota 8-speed)","Lockup pressure solenoid sticking or worn","Wiring or connector fault on the solenoid circuit"],["Converter lockup missing or unstable","Higher engine speed and fuel use at steady speed","Whine noise or harsh shifts (Toyota 8-speed)"],3,3,["P2757","P2758","P2759","P0740","P0741"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ מצמד ממיר מומנט"],P2757:["Torque Converter Clutch Pressure Control Solenoid Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P2757 means the converter clutch was commanded to apply, yet the speed difference between engine and turbine stayed too large, so the lockup never really happened. It is a functional verdict: the circuit may be electrically sound while the valve, the hydraulic feed or the clutch lining fails to deliver. Toyota uses it on the 2014–2019 Corolla CVT, where it points to shift solenoid SL;",["Sticking lockup solenoid or valve body (Toyota CVT solenoid SL)","Internal converter fault such as a dislodged snap ring (Ram AS69RC)","Low, aged or contaminated fluid","Worn converter clutch lining"],["Engine speed stays high at steady cruise","Higher fuel consumption","Transmission fluid runs hot","Check engine lamp on"],3,1,["P2758","P2756","P0741","P2762"],"מעגל בקרת סולנואיד בקרת לחץ מצמד ממיר מומנט — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2758:["Torque Converter Clutch Pressure Control Solenoid Control Circuit Stuck On","P2758 is the opposite of P2757: the converter clutch stays engaged although the module has asked it to release. Ford detects it when slip remains below 20 rpm while the release command is active and input torque is above 60 Nm, and the fault has to show up in more than one gear.",["Lockup pressure valve stuck in the apply position","Debris or varnish in the valve body","Converter clutch dragging internally"],["Engine stalls or nearly stalls when coming to a stop","Shudder or jolt when selecting a gear","Warning lamp depends on manufacturer (Ford none, Mitsubishi MIL)"],3,2,["P2757","P2756","P0741","P0740"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ מצמד ממיר מומנט — מעגל הבקרה תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2759:["Torque Converter Clutch Pressure Control Solenoid Control Circuit Electrical","P2759 is a general electrical fault on the control circuit of the converter clutch pressure solenoid, used where a module cannot distinguish an open from a ground or supply short. No manufacturer documents P2759 publicly.",["Damaged wire or connector between TCM and solenoid","Solenoid coil open or shorted","Faulty TCM output driver"],["No converter lockup","Slightly higher fuel consumption","Warning lamp on"],2,1,["P2761","P2763","P2764","P2760","P0740"],"חשמלי מעגל בקרת סולנואיד בקרת לחץ מצמד ממיר מומנט"],P275A:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor D Circuit","P275A flags an electrical fault in the circuit of transmission fluid temperature sensor D, the fourth position in the SAE lettering. A gearbox with four separate fluid temperature inputs is rare, and no manufacturer publicly assigns sensor D or describes when P275A is stored. CARB requires every such powertrain input to be checked for interrupted circuits and for values beyond the sensor span.",["Fault in connector or lead of sensor D","Sensor D electrically defective","Module input stage faulty"],["Warning lamp","Temperature D missing or implausible on the scan tool"],2,1,["P275B","P275C","P275D","P275E","P0710"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P275B:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor D Circuit Range/Performance","P275B is the rationality code for sensor D: the circuit is electrically sound, yet the value does not behave like real fluid temperature. Published tests on other fluid sensors show what modules look for – a warm-up check (GM's 2025 TCMs expect the main sensor to pass 15 °C within a calibrated time), a stuck-value check and a rate check against impossible jumps, such as Mitsubishi's rejection of 10 °C changes within…",["Sensor D thermistor aged or slow","Added resistance in a contact","Sludge or deposits on the sensor tip"],["Warning lamp after repeated detection","Temperature D lags behind or deviates from the other readings"],2,1,["P275A","P275C","P275D","P275E","P0711"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P275C:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor D Circuit Low","P275C reports that sensor D delivers less signal than the module considers possible. Read against an NTC thermistor this means a reading far hotter than the fluid could be, which almost always points to a pinched or melted lead touching ground, or to a short inside the sensor body. P275C is not documented by any manufacturer.",["Pinched or melted lead of sensor D touching ground","Short inside sensor D","Module input faulty"],["Warning lamp","Temperature D shows an impossibly hot value"],2,1,["P275A","P275B","P275D","P275E","P275F","P0712"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P275D:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor D Circuit High","P275D is stored when the sensor D signal rises past the top of its window. With a thermistor on a pull-up resistor the voltage climbs towards the supply when current can no longer flow, so an interrupted lead, a pushed-back terminal or an unplugged connector is the usual explanation, followed by a short to a voltage source. No manufacturer publishes P275D with limits;",["Interrupted lead or pushed-back terminal at sensor D","Sensor D open internally","Signal lead shorted to a voltage source"],["Warning lamp","Temperature D shows an extremely cold value"],2,1,["P275A","P275B","P275C","P275E","P0713"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P275E:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor D Circuit Intermittent","P275E marks an intermittent sensor D circuit: the value drops out or spikes for moments and then returns, too briefly for P275C or P275D. Public manufacturer documentation for this code is lacking; the closest published counterpart is the main sensor's P0714, which Ford's 2012 strategy names among its fluid temperature checks.",["Contact that opens under vibration","Heat-damaged lead that fails when hot","Sensor D with an internal loose connection"],["Warning lamp that appears sporadically","Dropouts of temperature D in a data log"],2,1,["P275A","P275B","P275C","P275D","P0714"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן תיבה‏ D — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P275F:["Transmission Fluid Temperature Sensor D Over Temperature Condition","P275F is the overheating condition for sensor D: the reading is valid and above the calibrated limit. No manufacturer documents the code, the limit or where sensor D sits. The sensor A equivalent P0218 gives an idea of the logic – Saab's Aisin automatic sets it beyond 170 °C lasting over ten seconds and recommends fresh fluid afterwards, because overheated oil loses its additives.",["Heavy trailer or long steep climbs","Slipping clutch or torque converter","Cooler blocked or not keeping up"],["Overheating warning or message","Changed shifting or reduced power","Dark or burnt-smelling fluid"],2,2,["P275A","P275B","P275C","P0218","P274F"],""],P2760:["Torque Converter Clutch Pressure Control Solenoid Control Circuit Intermittent","P2760 records a converter clutch control circuit that drops out now and then and recovers by itself. Ford names it in its 2024 OBD summary as the circuit-intermittent result of the TCC solenoid, written as P0740 with failure byte 1F; its electrical check compares the driver feedback with the commanded state and reacts when they disagree for 1.5 seconds.",["Loose or spread terminal at the case connector","Wire chafing intermittently against a bracket","Moisture or heat-related contact fault"],["Lockup drops out briefly, felt as an rpm flare","Fault not reproducible in the workshop","Warning lamp may come and go"],2,1,["P2759","P2761","P2758","P0740"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ מצמד ממיר מומנט — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל הבקרה"],P2761:["Torque Converter Clutch Pressure Control Solenoid Control Circuit/Open","P2761 says the TCM has lost continuity to the converter clutch pressure solenoid. GM documents the check in its six-speed TCM tables (16OBDG08 for the MW7 unit in Silverado/Sierra, 18OBDG04 for the T87A): with the driver switched off, an impedance of 173 kΩ or more counts as open, while 9.6 kΩ or less does not;",["Broken wire or backed-out pin to the solenoid","Open solenoid winding","Internal controller fault (Ram 6.7 l ECM capacitor leak)"],["No torque converter lockup","MIL on after two trips (GM Type B)","Higher cruise rpm and fuel use"],2,1,["P2763","P2764","P2762","P0741","P0740"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ מצמד ממיר מומנט — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2762:["Torque Converter Clutch Pressure Control Solenoid Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2762 covers a solenoid circuit that is neither open nor shorted but does not behave as commanded. In GM's six-speed TCM tables for the MW7 (2016) and T87A (2018) the module compares desired with measured solenoid current; a gap of 0.5 A or more in at least 40 of fewer than 80 samples sets the code as Type B, with battery voltage above 10 V.",["Solenoid coil resistance out of specification","Weak supply voltage or poor ground at the TCM","High-resistance terminal in the circuit","Current sensing fault inside the TCM"],["Harsh or slipping converter lockup","Shudder at light throttle in higher gears","Warning lamp depending on application (GM T76 none)"],2,1,["P2761","P2763","P2764","P2757"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ מצמד ממיר מומנט — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2763:["Torque Converter Clutch Pressure Control Solenoid Control Circuit High","P2763 means the control circuit of the lockup pressure solenoid reads high. GM's 2018 T87A table treats it as a short to power, at 1.16 Ω or less to a voltage source while the driver is on, Type B. Its 2016 tables add variants: on the T76 six-speed the high-voltage flag also covers an open circuit and must persist 4.4 of 5 seconds over two trips;",["Moisture in the valve-body connector (Subaru TR580)","Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Open circuit where the maker includes it in this code (GM T76/T54)","Faulty TCM output stage"],["No converter lockup, higher cruise rpm","Transmission warning and MIL","Other solenoid high codes at the same time (Subaru)"],2,3,["P2764","P2761","P2762","P2721","P0740"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ מצמד ממיר מומנט — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2764:["Torque Converter Clutch Pressure Control Solenoid Control Circuit Low","P2764 is the low counterpart of P2763: the lockup solenoid circuit is pulled toward ground. GM's 2018 T87A table defines it as 0.01 Ω or less to vehicle ground, checked while the driver is off every 6.25 ms. In 2016, the T76 six-speed sets it on a ground-short flag in 4.4 of 5 seconds after a single trip, and the T54 CVT when the hardware sees a ground short for 480 ms or longer while lockup is on.",["Control wire shorted to ground","Solenoid winding shorted to its housing","Failed torque converter when the solenoid tests good (FCA 62TE)"],["No lockup and higher fuel consumption","Jerking or slipping (62TE)","MIL after one trip on some GM units"],2,3,["P2763","P2761","P2762","P0740","P0742"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ מצמד ממיר מומנט — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2765:["Input/Turbine Shaft Speed Sensor B Circuit","P2765 is the circuit code of a second input speed sensor, B, and what B measures varies. On Ford's DPS6 dual-clutch box (2012) it is the input shaft 2 sensor for reverse and the even gears, faulted when the TCM hardware detects a circuit failure.",["Moisture or corrosion at the sensor B connector pins","Defective sensor B or integrated sensor module inside the gearbox","Open or shorted wiring between sensor and TCM","TCM input stage faulty"],["Check engine light and gearbox malfunction message","Limp-home mode, sometimes without reverse or even gears","Slow take-off and no torque converter lock-up"],3,3,["P2766","P2767","P2768","P07C1","P07C2","P0715"],"חיישן מהירות ציר כניסה/טורבינה‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2766:["Input/Turbine Shaft Speed Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2766 marks a sensor B signal that is present but erratic or implausible. Ford's 2012 strategy applies it to the DPS6 dual-clutch box, where sensor B reads input shaft 2. In Mitsubishi's 2022 CVT, sensor B is in fact the secondary pulley sensor on the output side: with the converter locked and engine, primary pulley and input speeds within 1,000 rpm of one another, a pulley ratio above 2.9 or below 0.3 for 5 s sets…",["Sensor B fouled with metal debris or not seated firmly","Interference or poor ground on the signal circuit","TCM fault keeping the code stored permanently"],["Check engine light after two drives","Sluggish acceleration, manual mode unavailable","Torque converter lock-up disabled"],3,3,["P2765","P2767","P2768","P0716","P2784"],"חיישן מהירות ציר כניסה/טורבינה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2767:["Input/Turbine Shaft Speed Sensor B Circuit No Signal","P2767 reports that pulses from sensor B are missing. Ford's DPS6 dual-clutch box of 2012 checks input shaft 2 for lack of signal under this code, alongside P2765 for circuit faults and P2766 for erratic readings.",["Connector or terminal letting go, open signal wire","Sensor B failed with no output","TCM sensor input defective"],["Warning lamp and transmission fail-safe","Slow start-off and weak acceleration","Manual shift mode not available"],3,3,["P2765","P2766","P2768","P0717"],"מעגל חיישן מהירות ציר כניסה/טורבינה‏ B — אין אות"],P2768:["Input/Turbine Shaft Speed Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","P2768 stands for a sensor B signal that drops out or jumps only now and then. Audi bulletin 2067653/9 (2024) covers 2020–24 A4, A5, A6, A7 and Q5 models with gearboxes built from 15 June 2020 to 30 November 2023: if P276800 is stored as passive/sporadic, alone or with P071800, control unit J217 or, where not sold separately, the mechatronic unit is replaced; an active entry calls for normal guided diagnosis.",["Transmission control unit fault on affected production batches","Loose contact or damaged wire in the sensor B circuit","Electrical noise producing false speed spikes"],["Gearbox malfunction message, intermittent","Limp mode, loss of power or no reverse gear","Occasional missed up- or downshifts"],4,3,["P2765","P2766","P2767","P0718"],"חיישן מהירות ציר כניסה/טורבינה‏ B — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2769:["Torque Converter Clutch Circuit Low","P2769 reports a low level on the converter clutch circuit, in practice a short to ground. It belongs to the P0740 family for converters with a single TCC solenoid, unlike P2764, which refers to a dedicated pressure control solenoid.",["TCC control wire pinched or chafed to ground","TCC solenoid coil shorted","Damaged internal transmission harness or lead frame"],["No converter lockup","Higher rpm and fuel use at highway speed","Check engine lamp on"],2,1,["P2770","P0740","P0742","P0741","P2764"],"מצמד ממיר מומנט — אות נמוך במעגל"],P276A:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Motor Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","P276A means the power feed to the motor of a second electric transmission fluid pump, labelled B, is interrupted. Such pumps keep hydraulic pressure or lubrication alive when the engine-driven pump is idle, for instance during stop-start or in a dual-clutch gearbox. No manufacturer documents P276A publicly.",["Blown fuse in the pump supply","Corroded or oil-contaminated pump connector","Broken supply wire or relay contact"],["Transmission warning lamp","Stop-start deactivated","Reduced performance or limp mode in some designs"],2,3,["P276B","P276C","P276D","P27A3","P2796"],"מתח אספקה מנוע משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P276B:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Motor Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P276B is set when the supply voltage reaching the motor of auxiliary transmission pump B sags below its lower limit. Audi names this code in bulletin 34-17-25 (revision of September 2017) covering 2017 A4/A5/A6 models and the 2018 Q5 fitted with the 0CJ, 0CK or 0CL twin-clutch gearbox.",["Defective gear oil pump V553 (Audi 0CJ/0CK/0CL)","High resistance in supply or ground of the pump","Low system voltage from a weak battery"],["Rattle noise from under the vehicle (Audi)","Transmission warning lamp","Further pump B codes stored"],3,3,["P276A","P276C","P276D","P27A3","P27A6","P0B0A"],"מנוע משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P276C:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Motor Supply Voltage Circuit High","P276C flags an excessive voltage on the motor supply of auxiliary pump B. Either the circuit is shorted to another powered line, the pump module measures wrongly, or the vehicle charging system itself overshoots. No manufacturer documents P276C publicly. Audi's bulletin 34-17-25 identifies pump B on its 0CJ, 0CK and 0CL dual-clutch units as the gear oil pump V553 and lists the low-voltage sibling P276B for it;",["Charging system voltage too high","Supply wire shorted to another powered circuit","Faulty measurement in the pump control electronics"],["Transmission warning lamp","Pump switched off, stop-start unavailable","Other overvoltage codes if charging is at fault"],2,3,["P276A","P276B","P276D","P0B0B"],"מנוע משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P276D:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Motor Current","P276D is the general current code for the motor of auxiliary transmission pump B: the measured current does not fit the commanded speed or load, without the module saying whether it is too low or too high. The narrower siblings P276E and P276F carry that distinction, and P0C26 is the same check for pump A. No manufacturer documents P276D publicly.",["Worn bearings or binding impeller in pump B","Contaminated or wrong transmission fluid","Poor ground or connector resistance at the pump"],["Noise from the pump area","Transmission warning lamp","Stop-start or shift quality restricted"],3,3,["P276E","P276F","P276B","P0C26","P27A3"],"זרם מנוע משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B"],P276E:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Motor Current Low","P276E tells you that the motor of a second electric transmission fluid pump, called B, takes less current than its commanded duty would require. A small draw usually means the motor is not really working: a broken winding, worn brushes, extra resistance in the feed or ground, or an impeller spinning freely because it has no fluid to move. No manufacturer documents P276E publicly.",["Worn brushes or open winding in the pump B motor","Corroded connector or high-resistance feed/ground to the pump","Low fluid level so the impeller runs without load","Faulty current measurement in the pump controller or TCM"],["Check engine or transmission warning lamp","Engine stop-start no longer operates","Delayed or harsh drive engagement after an engine restart"],3,3,["P276F","P276D","P277C","P0C27","P276B"],"זרם מנוע משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — ערך נמוך"],P276F:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Motor Current High","P276F is stored when the motor of auxiliary pump B pulls more current than the module allows. Excess draw points to a motor that is working too hard or is electrically damaged: a dragging bearing, debris or varnish in the pump, very cold thick fluid, a partially shorted winding or a chafed lead touching ground. No manufacturer documents P276F publicly.",["Dragging bearing or debris inside pump B","Partially shorted motor winding","Chafed pump lead shorting to ground","Contaminated or wrong-viscosity transmission fluid"],["Warning lamp with transmission fault message","Stop-start function disabled","Possible whine or rattle from the pump area"],3,3,["P276E","P276D","P277C","P277D","P0C28"],"זרם מנוע משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — ערך גבוה"],P2770:["Torque Converter Clutch Circuit High","P2770 flags a high level on the torque converter clutch circuit, meaning a short to the battery supply on the TCC solenoid or its wiring. Ford documents it in the 2024 OBD summary for the 6R80, 6R140, 10R60/10R80 and the 8F front-drive families: P2770 corresponds to UDS P0740_12, while P0740_13 covers an open line and P2769 (P0740_11) a short to ground.",["TCC circuit chafed against a powered wire","Damaged or contaminated transmission case connector","Internal short in the TCC solenoid","Faulty TCC output driver in the TCM/PCM"],["MIL on","No converter lockup, higher rpm at highway speed","Higher fuel consumption and fluid temperature"],2,1,["P2769","P0740","P0744","P0741","P2758"],"מצמד ממיר מומנט — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2771:["Four Wheel Drive (4WD) Low Switch Circuit","P2771 concerns the input that reports whether the transfer case sits in its low range. GM uses it on 2016 Silverado/Sierra with the MW7 gearbox as a plausibility test in the TCM: if the switch says high range while gear ratio math says low, or the reverse, for at least 0.5 s with fluid between 20 and 130 °C, the Type B code sets.",["Loose tone wheel or moving output shaft in the transfer case (GM PIP4966B)","Transfer case shift actuator damaged, e.g. by water through the breather (Toyota Tacoma)","Low-range switch or position encoder defective","Damaged wiring or corroded connector between switch and control module"],["Check engine light, often together with a flashing 4WD indicator","Erratic speedometer or ABS warning when a speed signal is affected","Low range not engaging, or transfer case disengaging under load"],3,3,["P2772","P2773","P2774","P0836","P279B"],""],P2772:["Four Wheel Drive (4WD) Low Switch Circuit Range/Performance","P2772 flags a low-range switch whose signal is electrically valid but does not fit what the drivetrain is actually doing. No manufacturer documents P2772 publicly. The natural cross-check is the one GM describes under P2771: the control unit derives the active range from turbine or input speed, output speed and the resulting ratio, then compares that with the switch.",["Low-range switch or encoder worn or out of adjustment","Range shift not completed (shift fork, actuator or linkage)","Output or turbine speed signal distorted, so the calculated range is wrong"],["Flashing 4WD indicator or range message on the cluster","Low range refused or engaged only after several attempts","Warning light depending on manufacturer"],3,3,["P2771","P2773","P2774","P0837","P279B"],""],P2773:["Four Wheel Drive (4WD) Low Switch Circuit Low","P2773 is stored when the signal line of the low-range switch stays below its permitted voltage band, typically because it is pulled to ground. No manufacturer documents P2773 publicly. Toyota shows that the fault type exists in practice but files it differently: on 2024–2025 Tacoma the short to ground appears as P2771 with failure byte 11, and bulletin T-SB-0093-25 traces it to a shift actuator damaged through the…",["Signal wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Moisture in shift actuator or connector (Toyota Tacoma breather issue)","Low-range switch shorted internally"],["4WD indicator flashing and warning light on","Low range cannot be selected or is reported permanently"],2,3,["P2771","P2772","P2774","P0838"],""],P2774:["Four Wheel Drive (4WD) Low Switch Circuit High","P2774 reports that the low-range switch input sits above its valid voltage range. With a pulled-up signal line this usually points to an open circuit, a broken ground at the switch or a short to battery voltage. No manufacturer documents P2774 publicly; the monitoring logic follows the CARB demand for out-of-range checks on inputs, and the switch itself is the one GM and Toyota describe under P2771.",["Open signal or ground wire, connector unplugged at the transfer case","Switch contacts open internally","Signal wire shorted to battery voltage"],["Warning light and flashing 4WD indicator","Low range not recognised after selection"],2,3,["P2771","P2772","P2773","P0839"],""],P2775:["Upshift Switch Circuit Range/Performance","P2775 covers an upshift paddle or tip switch whose voltage is electrically possible but belongs to neither of its two legal states. GM's twin-clutch TCM tables for 2023 and 2024 read the plus paddle as an analogue input: pressed should give 2.2–3.52 V, released 3.826–4.744 V. If the voltage sits outside both windows for 120 s, P2775 sets as Type C, so without MIL.",["Worn or dirty contacts or drifting coding resistor in the paddle","Added resistance in the clock spring or steering wheel connector","Moisture or spilled liquid in the switch"],["Upshift paddle has no effect, manual mode unavailable","Message on the cluster, normally no check engine light"],2,0,["P2776","P2777","P2778","P0815","P2779"],"מתג העלאת הילוך — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2776:["Upshift Switch Circuit Low","P2776 means the upshift switch input has dropped below the lowest voltage the module accepts. In GM's 2023 twin-clutch TCM the TAPUP input is supposed to stay above 2.519 V even with the paddle pulled; a lower reading, held for at least 150 ms with battery voltage between 8.75 and 18 V and the engine not cranking, sets P2776 as Type C without MIL.",["Signal wire shorted to ground, e.g. in the clock spring area","Paddle switch shorted internally","Liquid in switch or connector creating a leak path to ground"],["Upshift paddle or tip function inoperative","Manual mode message, no check engine light on GM"],2,0,["P2775","P2777","P2778","P0815","P2780"],"מתג העלאת הילוך — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2777:["Upshift Switch Circuit High","P2777 is the over-voltage counterpart for the upshift switch. GM's 2023 twin-clutch TCM watches the TAPUP input and counts up a timer once it exceeds 4.774 V; after 150 ms above that limit, with supply voltage in the 8.75–18 V band, the code is logged as Type C, so no MIL. Ford's July 2024 OBD summary lists P2777 as out-of-window-high on the TR9070 upshift paddle.",["Open signal or ground circuit, steering wheel connector loose","Broken track in the clock spring","Signal wire shorted to a voltage source"],["Upshift paddle without function","Driver information message about manual shifting"],2,0,["P2775","P2776","P2778","P0815","P2781"],"מתג העלאת הילוך — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2778:["Upshift Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2778 is meant for an upshift switch signal that jumps around or drops out briefly instead of staying in one state. No manufacturer documents P2778 publicly. GM's 2023/2024 twin-clutch TCM and Ford's TR9070 split the same paddle input into low, high, implausible and stuck faults (P2775–P2777, P0815) but list no intermittent check, so on those cars a flickering contact will rather end up as one of these.",["Clock spring track cracked, opening at certain steering angles","Loose terminal or poor crimp in the column or wheel connector","Worn or bouncing contact in the paddle"],["Upshift requests occasionally ignored","Occasional unwanted upshift requests","Fault comes and goes, often depending on steering angle"],2,0,["P2775","P2776","P2777","P0815","P2782"],"מתג העלאת הילוך — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2779:["Downshift Switch Circuit Range/Performance","P2779 is the plausibility fault of the downshift paddle or tip switch. GM's 2023 and 2024 TCM tables for the twin-clutch gearbox define two voltage windows for the minus paddle: 2.2–3.52 V when pulled and 3.826–4.744 V at rest. A reading caught between or around these windows for 120 s is treated as invalid and logged as Type C, no MIL. The same tables use P0816 for a minus paddle held too long.",["Corroded contacts or drifting coding resistor in the minus paddle","Added resistance in the clock spring","Corrosion in the steering wheel connector"],["Downshift paddle inoperative","Manual mode refused, usually no MIL"],2,0,["P2780","P2781","P2782","P0816","P2775"],"מתג הורדת הילוך — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P277A:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Hydraulic Leakage","P277A is not an electrical fault. The motor of auxiliary pump B runs, yet the oil it delivers escapes before pressure can build, so the module concludes that the hydraulic path around the pump leaks. Typical suspects are a damaged pump seal or O-ring, a check valve that does not close, worn bores in the valve body or a fluid level so low that the pump draws air. No manufacturer documents P277A publicly.",["Damaged pump seal or O-ring at the pump mounting","Low transmission fluid level letting the pump draw air","Check valve in the pump circuit not sealing","Worn valve body bores causing internal leakage"],["Stop-start disabled or rough engine restarts","Delayed drive engagement after standstill","Warning lamp, possibly fluid traces under the gearbox"],3,3,["P0B0C","P27A3","P277C","P276D"],""],P277B:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Driver Circuit Performance","P277B concerns the power stage that energises the motor of auxiliary pump B, wherever it sits: inside a separate pump controller or in the transmission module. The stage is switched on, but what comes back – current, speed or a status signal – does not fit the command, so the module rates the driver as implausible rather than reporting a plain open or short. No manufacturer documents P277B publicly.",["Failing output stage in the pump controller or TCM","Poor ground or low system voltage at the driver","Pump motor loading the driver abnormally","Loose or corroded pins between driver and pump"],["Transmission warning or service message","Stop-start unavailable","Jerky drive-off after engine restarts"],3,3,["P0C29","P277D","P276F","P276B"],"נהג משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P277C:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Motor Stalled","P277C means the motor of auxiliary pump B is commanded to turn but stands still or nearly so. Volvo uses it: its technical journal 36774 covers 2024–2027 mild-hybrid S60, S90, V60/V90 Cross Country, XC40, XC60 and XC90 models with the Aisin TG-81SC eight-speed, where the TCM stores P277C07.",["Jammed impeller or seized pump bearing","Known hardware issue in early gearboxes (Volvo TG-81SC before the serial break)","Pump lost prime because of low fluid","One-off detection without a real fault"],["Transmission warning message in the cluster","Stop-start not working","Shifts too early, too late or erratic"],4,3,["P0C2A","P276F","P276E","P277A","P277D"],""],P277D:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Motor Over Temperature","P277D reports that the motor or the integrated electronics of auxiliary pump B have become too hot. Pumps of this kind measure their own temperature and stop before damage occurs; the code records that protective shutdown.",["Long high-load operation in hot conditions","Mechanical drag raising motor current and heat","Overheated or aged transmission fluid","Faulty temperature sensing in the pump electronics"],["Stop-start temporarily unavailable, especially in hot weather","Warning lamp or transmission message"],3,0,["P0DE4","P276F","P277C","P277B"],"מנוע משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — חום יתר"],P277E:["Clutch A Unexpected Mechanical Gear Disengagement","P277E reports that a gear on the shaft served by clutch A dropped out of engagement by itself while that clutch was carrying the drive, without any shift being commanded. GM's 2023 TCM tables for its dual-clutch gearbox run this check continuously: if the synchronizer of the driving gear shows a speed difference although the odd-gear clutch slips by less than 50 rpm, and this lasts 1000 ms, the code is stored as…",["Worn shift-fork detent or rounded engagement teeth on an odd gear","Shift rod drifting due to internal hydraulic leakage or a weak actuator","Fork end positions not relearned after repair or module replacement","Faulty shaft speed signal making a slip appear at the synchronizer"],["Sudden loss of drive as if the gearbox had shifted into neutral","Odd gears locked out, limp mode with reduced gear choice","Warning lamp and transmission message in the cluster"],4,3,["P277F","P2711","P284D","P2832"],""],P277F:["Clutch B Unexpected Mechanical Gear Disengagement","P277F is the even-gear twin of P277E: the controller has found that a gear carried by the shaft of clutch B lost its engagement on its own while the car was driving through that clutch. The evidence comes from speed sensors, which show the synchronizer of the active gear turning at a different speed even though clutch B is practically locked (GM: slip below 50 rpm, 1 s confirmation, Type A in the 2023 dual-clutch…",["Worn detent or engagement teeth on an even gear or its sleeve","Shift rod of the even shaft creeping due to leakage in the hydraulic unit","Wrong or missing fork position learning after repair","Implausible even-shaft speed signal"],["Momentary loss of drive in an even gear","Even gears unavailable, gearbox skips between odd gears","Warning lamp with stored transmission fault"],4,3,["P277E","P2711","P284D"],""],P2780:["Downshift Switch Circuit Low","P2780 tells you the downshift switch voltage has fallen under its lower limit. GM's twin-clutch TCM (tables 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07) checks the TAPDN input against 2.519 V; if the signal stays under that mark for 150 ms while the supply is inside 8.75–18 V and the starter is not engaged, P2780 is logged as Type C, no MIL.",["Signal wire rubbed through or pinched to ground","Minus paddle shorted internally"],["Downshift paddle has no effect","Manual mode not available, normally no check engine light"],2,0,["P2779","P2781","P2782","P0816","P2776"],"מתג הורדת הילוך — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2781:["Downshift Switch Circuit High","P2781 sets when the downshift switch input climbs above its upper voltage limit. GM's 2023 dual-clutch TCM tables cap the TAPDN signal at 4.774 V; staying above it for 150 ms produces a Type C entry, no MIL. Ford's TR9070 table in the 2024 summary uses P2781 for the out-of-window-high case of the downshift paddle.",["Open signal or ground circuit, loose connector at the wheel","TCM software reporting a false permanent code (2021 Corvette, N212350930)","Broken track in the clock spring"],["Downshift paddle not working","Permanent code shown at an emissions inspection although the paddle works (software case)"],2,0,["P2779","P2780","P2782","P0816","P2777"],"מתג הורדת הילוך — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2782:["Downshift Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2782 targets a downshift switch signal that flickers, bounces or vanishes for moments. No manufacturer documents P2782 publicly. The documented paddle monitors (GM's dual-clutch TCM tables of 2023/2024, Ford's TR9070 entry) cover low, high, implausible and held-too-long (P2779–P2781, P0816) without a separate dropout test, so such a fault there tends to surface under those codes.",["Clock spring losing contact at certain steering angles","Loose pin in the steering column connector","Bouncing or worn contact in the minus paddle"],["Downshift occasionally missed","Sporadic unexpected downshift request"],2,0,["P2779","P2780","P2781","P0816","P2778"],"מתג הורדת הילוך — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2783:["Torque Converter Temperature Too High","P2783 warns that the torque converter is at risk of overheating. Ford's 2012 OBD summary shows one concrete use in its 6F front-drive six-speed. There, two valves route oil to the converter clutch; if the control valve hangs in its applied setting, no oil flows through an open converter and it heats up.",["TCC control valve stuck in the apply position","Debris or varnish in the valve body","Restricted converter or cooler oil flow"],["MIL on","Changed shift and lockup behaviour","Transmission overheating, burnt fluid smell"],3,3,["P0218","P0741","P2758","P0711"],"טמפרטורת ממיר מומנט — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2784:["Input/Turbine Speed Sensor A/B Correlation","P2784 belongs to transmissions with two input or turbine speed sensors whose readings can be compared. When both are healthy their values agree, or differ only by a known ratio; P2784 is set when they drift apart for longer than the module tolerates while each circuit on its own looks fine. No manufacturer documents P2784 publicly, so it stays open which sensor pairs are compared in practice.",["Metal debris on a magnetic speed sensor tip","One sensor giving a weak or distorted signal","Damaged tone wheel or excessive air gap","Signal interference from poor shielding or connectors"],["Harsh or erratic shifts","Emergency mode with fixed gear","MIL on"],3,3,["P0715","P0716","P2765","P2766","P2767"],"חיישן מהירות כניסה/טורבינה‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2785:["Clutch Actuator Temperature Too High","P2785 indicates that the actuator which opens and closes the clutch has become hotter than the controller allows. In automated manual and dry dual-clutch gearboxes this part is usually an electric motor or an electro-hydraulic unit; creeping, hill starts and stop-and-go traffic make it work hard, and the controller measures or models its temperature to protect windings and electronics.",["Long creeping, repeated hill starts or towing in slow traffic","Stiff release bearing or lever forcing high actuator current","Worn actuator motor or blocked actuator pump","Faulty temperature sensing or outdated control software"],["Gearbox warning and request to stop or let the system cool","Reduced engine torque or harsh, delayed take-off","Vehicle may refuse to engage a gear until cooled"],3,2,["P2786","P2787","P0900","P0901"],"טמפרטורת מפעיל מצמד — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2786:["Gear Shift Actuator Temperature Too High","P2786 is stored when the drive that moves the shift forks inside an automated gearbox runs too hot. Single-clutch automated manuals use electro-mechanical or electro-hydraulic actuators to push the selector across and along the gate, and some dual-clutch designs drive their forks with motors as well.",["Binding shift fork, selector shaft or linkage raising actuator load","Very frequent shifting, e.g. manual mode on hilly roads or in traffic","Worn shift actuator motor or low hydraulic pressure in the shift unit","Temperature model or software error in the gearbox controller"],["Shifts refused or delayed, gearbox stays in current gear","Transmission warning in the instrument cluster","Gearbox may select neutral and only restart after cooling"],3,2,["P2785","P0919","P0920","P0910"],"טמפרטורת מפעיל העברת הילוכים — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2787:["Clutch A Temperature Too High","P2787 means the controller has calculated or measured a temperature for clutch A above its permitted limit. Two quite different uses are documented. Stellantis bulletin 21-040-26 lists P2787-00 as clutch 1 overtemperature for 2022-2025 European Jeep Renegade and Compass with the 1.5 litre mild hybrid and the 7HDT300 dual-clutch gearbox;",["Clutch slipping because its actuator or actuator pump does not deliver full force","On all-wheel-drive couplings, damaged front differential forcing constant slip","Repeated launches, creeping or towing with high clutch slip","Worn friction lining reducing torque capacity"],["Overheating message, odd gears or all-wheel drive unavailable","MIL or transmission warning lamp on","Shudder or slipping when pulling away"],4,3,["P27F3","P2785","P2789","P270A"],"טמפרטורת מצמד‏ A — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2788:["Auto Shift Manual Adaptive Learning at Limit","P2788 is the system-level code for an automated manual gearbox whose learned correction values have reached the end of their allowed range. Such units learn the clutch bite point, engagement speed and the end stops of the shift and select movements so that gear changes stay smooth as parts wear; when a value would have to move beyond its limit, the controller can no longer compensate and stores this code.",["Worn clutch moving the bite point beyond the learnable range","Basic setting or relearn skipped after clutch, actuator or module work","Worn or sticking shift and clutch actuators changing their travel","Outdated software or implausible engine torque signal"],["Jerky take-off and harsh or slow shifts","Transmission warning lamp","Clutch slip or engine flare during shifts"],3,2,["P2789","P278F","P0919"],""],P2789:["Clutch A Adaptive Learning at Limit","P2789 says the controller has pushed its learned fill or pressure corrections for a clutch to the edge of the permitted window and still cannot reach the shift quality it aims for. The code is well documented by Allison for its 1000/2000 Series automatics, where it lights the Check Transmission lamp and the Prognostics view flags the affected clutch as not OK.",["Outdated transmission calibration needing a reflash","Engine reports torque inaccurately, so clutch adaptation drifts","Worn clutch plates or leaking clutch piston seals","Degraded fluid or a sluggish pressure control solenoid"],["Check Transmission or warning lamp on","Engine flare or slip during upshifts","Harsh or delayed engagement of the affected clutch"],4,3,["P278F","P2788","P2787"],""],P278A:["Kick Down Switch Circuit","P278A is the general circuit fault of the kickdown switch, the contact at the end of accelerator pedal travel that asks the transmission for the lowest possible gear. No manufacturer documents P278A publicly. Many current cars no longer have an electrical switch: Mazda states for the 2024 CX-90 that its kickdown element only adds a felt detent and sends no signal, the pedal position sensor alone deciding.",["Kickdown switch in or under the pedal defective","Wiring or connector of the pedal module damaged","Kickdown message missing on the data bus (networked designs)"],["No forced downshift at full throttle","Reduced acceleration when overtaking"],1,0,["P278B","P278C","P278D","P278E","P2138"],""],P278B:["Kick Down Switch Circuit Range/Performance","P278B describes a kickdown switch whose state contradicts the pedal position. No manufacturer documents P278B publicly. The obvious cross-check is the accelerator pedal sensor: a switch reporting kickdown at part throttle, or staying open although the pedal is pressed to the stop, is implausible.",["Kickdown switch misadjusted or detent worn","Floor mat or object preventing full pedal travel","Pedal position sensor offset so that both signals disagree"],["Kickdown missing at the pedal stop","Unexpected downshift at part throttle"],1,0,["P278A","P278C","P278D","P278E","P2138"],""],P278C:["Kick Down Switch Circuit Low","P278C is recorded when the kickdown switch line reads lower than the module allows. No manufacturer documents P278C publicly, and many modern pedals have no electrical kickdown contact at all, as Mazda notes for the 2024 CX-90.",["Signal wire shorted to ground at the pedal bracket","Switch contact welded or shorted","Water from the footwell in the connector"],["Kickdown always or never active, depending on circuit","Unexpected downshifts or lack of downshift at full throttle"],1,0,["P278A","P278B","P278D","P278E","P2122"],""],P278D:["Kick Down Switch Circuit High","P278D means the kickdown switch circuit shows a voltage above its permitted maximum. No manufacturer documents P278D publicly. With the usual pull-up input this is the reading of an interrupted line: the pedal module unplugged after a repair, a broken wire at the hinge of a floor-mounted pedal, or a missing ground at the switch. A short to battery voltage produces the same picture but is rarer.",["Open signal or ground wire, pedal module unplugged","Wire broken by pedal movement","Signal wire shorted to battery voltage"],["No kickdown at full throttle","Slower acceleration from speed"],1,0,["P278A","P278B","P278C","P278E"],""],P278E:["Kick Down Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P278E stands for a kickdown switch signal that drops out or toggles irregularly. No manufacturer documents P278E publicly; the monitoring idea follows CARB's call for circuit checks on inputs, and Eaton's Endurant HD diagnostics show the networked equivalent, where a kickdown message that is invalid or absent for 5 s is logged as fault 167.",["Bouncing switch contact due to worn detent","Pedal connector loosened by vibration","Wire strands breaking where the harness flexes with the pedal"],["Kickdown works only sometimes","Fault not reproducible when stationary"],1,0,["P278A","P278B","P278C","P278D"],""],P278F:["Clutch B Adaptive Learning at Limit","P278F flags that the learned values for clutch B have run out of room. In a dual-clutch gearbox this is usually the clutch for the even gears; the controller keeps adjusting its touch point and pressure or travel so that handovers between the two clutches stay seamless, and stores the code once a correction hits its end stop. No manufacturer documents P278F publicly with set conditions;",["Worn clutch B lining or plates shifting the touch point","Clutch adaptation not reset or relearned after repair","Clutch B actuator or release mechanism sticking or losing pressure","Outdated software or inaccurate engine torque information"],["Shudder or slip when an even gear takes over","Rough or slow shifts between gears","Transmission warning lamp"],4,3,["P2789","P2788","P27F3"],""],P2790:["Gate Select Direction Circuit","P2790 is the basic circuit fault for the signal that tells the controller in which direction the selector mechanism is moving across the gate, that is sideways between the shift lanes of the H pattern. In automated manual gearboxes the select actuator or its sensor provides this information; on some shift-by-wire levers it comes from the lever itself, so the exact part depends on the manufacturer.",["Open wire or loose, corroded connector at the select sensor","Failed select direction sensor or select actuator electronics","Fault in the shift lever module where it supplies the signal","Defective input stage in the transmission controller"],["Gear changes refused or gearbox stuck in one gear","Vehicle may not move off from standstill","Warning lamp with transmission message"],2,3,["P2791","P2792","P0904","P0910"],"כיוון בחירת שער — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2791:["Gate Select Direction Circuit Low","P2791 is set when the gate select direction signal sits below the lowest value the controller accepts. For a voltage-type sensor this usually points to a short to ground on the signal wire, a missing reference supply or a sensor pulling the line down internally; with switch-type inputs the contact may read as permanently closed to ground.",["Signal wire chafed and shorted to ground","Sensor reference voltage missing or shorted","Select direction sensor failed with low output"],["No change between shift lanes, limited gear choice","Gearbox holds the current gear or selects neutral","Transmission warning lamp"],2,3,["P2790","P2792","P0906"],"כיוון בחירת שער — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2792:["Gate Select Direction Circuit High","P2792 reports a gate select direction signal stuck above its valid band. Common reasons are a short between the signal line and a supply voltage, a broken sensor ground that lets the input float up, or an open signal wire on inputs with an internal pull-up resistor; a sensor with a failed output stage can also hold the line high.",["Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage","Broken sensor ground or open signal line pulled up internally","Select direction sensor failed with high output"],["Sideways selection blocked, shifts possible only in one lane","Gearbox may stay in gear or neutral","Transmission warning lamp"],2,3,["P2790","P2791","P0907"],"כיוון בחירת שער — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2793:["Gear Shift Direction Circuit","P2793 covers the circuit that reports the shift direction, the fore-and-aft movement along a lane that actually engages or releases a gear, as opposed to the sideways lane choice monitored by P2790. Depending on the design, an automated manual reads it from a sensor on the shift actuator, while shift-by-wire systems may take it from the lever or a separate selector module.",["Open circuit or poor contact at the shift direction sensor connector","Failed shift direction sensor on the actuator","Faulty shift lever or selector module where it sends the signal","Transmission controller input fault"],["No up- or downshifts, gearbox keeps the current gear","Selector input ignored","Warning lamp and transmission message"],2,3,["P2794","P2795","P0914","P0920"],"כיוון העברת הילוכים — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2794:["Gear Shift Direction Circuit Low","P2794 means the shift direction signal, which tells the controller whether a gear is being pushed in or pulled out along its lane, reads lower than the permitted minimum. The usual suspects are a signal line rubbed through to ground, a collapsed sensor supply shared with other sensors, or water in a connector creating a leakage path to ground.",["Signal line chafed through to ground","Shared sensor supply pulled down by another sensor or wiring","Moisture or corrosion in the connector","Shift direction sensor failed low"],["Gearbox stays in the current gear","Manual shift requests ignored","Transmission warning lamp"],2,3,["P2793","P2795","P0916"],"כיוון העברת הילוכים — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2795:["Gear Shift Direction Circuit High","P2795 is the upper-limit fault of the shift direction signal: the value seen by the controller is higher than any real sensor position could produce. That pattern fits a signal wire touching a battery or 5 volt feed, a lost sensor ground, or an interrupted signal line on an input that is pulled up inside the module. A sensor whose output stage has failed may also report a constant high level.",["Signal wire shorted to battery or 5 V supply","Lost sensor ground or open signal line pulled up internally","Shift direction sensor stuck at a high output"],["Gear changes refused, current gear held","Selector or paddle inputs have no effect","Transmission warning lamp"],2,3,["P2793","P2794","P0917"],"כיוון העברת הילוכים — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2796:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump A Control Circuit/Open","P2796 points to an interrupted control line between the module and the motor of auxiliary pump A. GM's 2025 TCM tables define the test: provided the battery supplies 9 to 15 V, the controller sees more than 200 kΩ from signal to ground in at least 20 of 25 samples taken every 100 ms; the code is Type B, so the MIL comes on after two trips.",["Broken control wire or unplugged pump connector","Poor terminal contact at the pump or module","Module software (Ford F-150 Lightning, TSB 26-2010)","Open circuit inside the pump electronics"],["MIL or wrench indicator on","Stop-start inoperative","Reduced performance message on electrified models"],2,3,["P2797","P2798","P2799","P27A2","P0C2B"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2797:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump A Performance/Stuck Off","P2797 says pump A was asked to deliver but no useful pressure resulted. GM checks this on CVTs during an engine auto-start: with the pump commanded and over 400 kPa requested at both pulleys, both pressure sensors reading under 200 kPa for more than 0.525 s set the Type B code.",["Internal failure of the auxiliary pump or its motor","Control software misjudging pump output (TCM update available)","Damaged pump wiring harness","Low fluid or internal leakage preventing pressure build-up"],["MIL on","Stop-start inoperative","Shock or surge when the engine restarts at a stop","Service transmission message"],4,3,["P2796","P2798","P2799","P27A1","P27A3","P0B0C"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2798:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump A Control Circuit Low","P2798 reports the control circuit of auxiliary pump A pulled low, which in practice means a short to ground. In GM's 2025 TCM tables the controller registers less than 0.5 Ω between the signal and controller ground in 20 of 25 samples at a 100 ms rate, with battery voltage between 9 and 15 V; it is a Type B fault with the MIL after two trips.",["Control wire chafed through to ground","Internal defect in the pump electronics (e.g. faulty solder joints, Bolt EV/EUV)","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the connector","Faulty control output in the module"],["Reduced propulsion power message on electric vehicles","Service vehicle soon lamp or MIL","Stop-start disabled on combustion models"],2,3,["P2796","P2799","P2797","P0C2D","P27A4"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2799:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump A Control Circuit High","P2799 is set when the control line of auxiliary pump A sits at too high a level, normally because it touches a powered wire. GM's 2025 TCM tables are the only public manufacturer description: the module measures under 0.5 Ω from the signal line to a voltage source in 20 of 25 samples spaced 100 ms apart, provided supply voltage is between 9 and 15 V, and treats the result as Type B with the MIL after two trips.",["Control wire shorted to a powered circuit","Moisture bridging pins in the pump connector","Internal short in the pump electronics","Faulty high-side driver in the module"],["MIL after two drive cycles","Stop-start inoperative","Rough engagement after an auto-start"],2,3,["P2796","P2798","P2797","P27A5"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P279A:["Transfer Case Gear High Incorrect Ratio","P279A fires when the transfer case should be in its high range, but the measured ratio says otherwise. GM explains the check in its 2019 ECM tables (section for the LCV engine): the ratio is calculated from transmission output speed divided by transfer case output speed, both from real sensors. If the control module commands 4WD high and the result falls in the window for low range or for neutral, the fault counts.",["Range shift to high not completed by the shift motor","Worn shift fork or range sleeve slipping out of high","Implausible transfer case output speed signal","Mismatched tire sizes affecting the computed ratio"],["MIL and 4WD warning on","Unexpected low-range feel or loss of drive","Grinding from the transfer case"],3,3,["P279B","P279C","P2771","P279D","P2160"],""],P279B:["Transfer Case Gear Low Incorrect Ratio","P279B is the reverse case of P279A: 4WD low has been commanded, yet the transfer case behaves like high range or neutral. For a vehicle crawling off-road this is a real safety concern, because the expected reduction and engine braking are missing.",["Shift motor stopping short of the low position","Worn or damaged reduction planetary set","Broken or bent range shift fork","Faulty speed signal distorting the ratio"],["No reduction in 4WD low, weak crawling and engine braking","4WD warning lamp and MIL","Clunking or grinding when selecting low range"],3,3,["P279A","P279C","P2771","P2772","P279D"],""],P279C:["Transfer Case Gear Neutral Incorrect Ratio","P279C applies when neutral is commanded on the transfer case, as is done for flat towing, but the shafts still turn with a fixed ratio that matches high or low range. The transfer case therefore still transmits drive. GM's 2019 ECM tables (LCV section) use the same output-speed ratio as for the other two range tests, but allow more time before deciding: the failure must last 10.5 seconds within a 15-second window.",["Range shift motor not reaching neutral","Sticking shift sleeve keeping a range engaged","Wrong position feedback from the range sensor"],["Vehicle still drives or creeps with neutral selected","Neutral request rejected, 4WD warning on","MIL on"],3,1,["P279A","P279B","P279D","P279E","P2771"],""],P279D:["Four Wheel Drive (4WD) Range Signal Circuit","P279D concerns the signal that tells the powertrain which transfer case range is active: 4WD high, 4WD low or neutral. Drivetrain controllers need it to apply the right ratio, torque limits and shift logic.",["Open circuit or bad connector on the range switch or sensor","Range message from the transfer case module corrupted or out of sequence","Faulty transfer case control module or range sensor","Software mismatch between the modules after a replacement"],["Check engine lamp","4WD range indicator wrong, flashing or unavailable","Range change between high and low refused"],2,1,["P279E","P279F","P27A0","P279A","P2771"],""],P279E:["Four Wheel Drive (4WD) Range Signal Circuit Range/Performance","P279E flags a 4WD range signal that is electrically present but does not make sense: it may show a range the transfer case cannot be in, jump between high, low and neutral without a request, or contradict what the speed ratio across the transfer case shows. Such a plausibility check typically compares the reported range with commanded shifts and with the measured ratio monitored by P279A to P279C.",["Worn or misadjusted transfer case range sensor","Transfer case shift motor stopping between ranges","Intermittent contact in the range signal wiring"],["4WD indicator shows a range that does not match the actual drive","Range shifts refused or completed only partly","Warning lamp"],2,1,["P279D","P279F","P27A0","P279C"],""],P279F:["Four Wheel Drive (4WD) Range Signal Circuit Low","P279F means the wired 4WD range signal is below the lowest valid level. Many transfer cases report their range through a resistor-coded switch or a position sensor that produces a defined voltage for each of high, low and neutral; a reading under the lowest of these bands points to a short to ground, a missing sensor supply or a sensor that pulls the line down. No manufacturer documents P279F publicly;",["Range signal wire shorted to ground near the transfer case","Sensor reference voltage missing","Range switch or encoder failed with low output"],["4WD range indicator dark or flashing","4WD low or range changes unavailable","Warning lamp on"],2,1,["P279D","P279E","P27A0"],""],P27A0:["Four Wheel Drive (4WD) Range Signal Circuit High","P27A0 is logged when the line reporting which transfer case range is engaged (4WD high, 4WD low, neutral) reads above its highest valid level. Range encoders usually present a defined voltage or resistance band for each position; a value above all bands typically means the wire is open and pulled up inside the module, the encoder lost its ground, or the line touches a battery feed.",["Range signal wire or encoder ground interrupted (corroded or loose connector near the transfer case)","Signal wire chafed against a powered conductor","Transfer case range encoder or switch defective"],["4WD indicator flashing or showing no range","Shift between 4WD high and low refused","Warning lamp or driveline message"],2,1,["P279D","P279E","P279F","P2771"],""],P27A1:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump A Stuck On","P27A1 means auxiliary transmission fluid pump A keeps running although the controller has not asked for it, or the module still sees current or rotation with the command off. Such electric pumps hold pressure in the gearbox while the engine rests during stop-start or hybrid operation.",["High-side driver or pump relay stays closed","Pump control or enable line shorted to battery voltage","Integrated pump electronics ignore the off command"],["Pump hum from the gearbox after the engine or ignition is off","12 V battery discharged after standing","Stop-start disabled and warning shown"],2,1,["P2796","P2797","P2798","P2799","P27A6"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ A — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P27A2:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Control Circuit/Open","P27A2 flags a broken control circuit between the module and auxiliary pump B, the second electric fluid pump on gearboxes that carry two. While its output is energised, the controller compares the voltage on the line with the level an intact load would pull it to; a floating line reveals the interruption. No manufacturer documents P27A2 publicly.",["Control wire broken in the harness to pump B","Pump connector unplugged, pin pushed back or corroded","Open motor winding or internal connection in pump B"],["Stop-start no longer active","Transmission warning or MIL","Harsh engagement when driving off after a restart"],2,3,["P27A3","P27A4","P27A5","P2796","P276B"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P27A3:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Performance/Stuck Off","P27A3 means auxiliary pump B was commanded but did not deliver: no pressure build-up, too little speed or a motor that does not respond at all. Audi documents the code. Its bulletin 34-17-25, revision 3 from 2017, covers model year 2017 A4, A5, A6 and the 2018 Q5 with the 0CJ, 0CK and 0CL seven-speed twin-clutch boxes and names P27A300, next to P27A6, P276B and U28A0, as possible companions of a rattling gear oil…",["Pump B mechanically defective or seized (e.g. assembly fault on Audi V553)","Fluid level too low, pump draws air","Worn pump motor or high resistance in its supply"],["Rattle from below the car near the gearbox","Stop-start disabled","Delayed or harsh engagement after an engine restart"],4,3,["P27A2","P27A6","P276B","P2797","P277C"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P27A4:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Control Circuit Low","P27A4 indicates that the control line of auxiliary pump B is pulled toward ground. The module checks the line while its driver is switched on; if the measured level stays close to zero, the circuit counts as shorted low. No manufacturer documents P27A4 publicly.",["Control wire insulation chafed through to ground","Water or corrosion bridging pins to ground in the pump connector","Internal short to ground inside pump B"],["Stop-start unavailable","MIL or transmission warning after repeated trips","Blown fuse in the pump supply possible"],2,3,["P27A2","P27A5","P2798","P276B"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P27A5:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Control Circuit High","P27A5 sets when the control line of auxiliary pump B sits at a level that only a connection to a voltage source can explain. In practice the wire touches a powered conductor, or moisture links it to a neighbouring supply pin. No manufacturer documents P27A5 publicly.",["Control wire chafed against a powered conductor","Moisture bridging the control pin to a supply pin","Faulty output stage in the controlling module"],["Stop-start switched off","Pump B may run continuously or not at all","MIL after two trips on Type B systems"],2,3,["P27A2","P27A4","P27A6","P2799"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P27A6:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Stuck On","P27A6 reports that auxiliary pump B keeps running, or keeps drawing current, while the controller has it switched off. Audi lists P27A600 in bulletin 34-17-25 for 2017 A4, A5 and A6 and 2018 Q5 models with 0CJ, 0CK and 0CL dual-clutch gearboxes; there the code may appear together with a rattle from the gear oil pump V553, which Audi traced to an assembly fault at the supplier and cures with a new pump.",["Pump B module or electronics defective (e.g. Audi V553 supplier fault)","Driver output or relay remains closed","Control line shorted to battery voltage"],["Pump noise or rattle from the gearbox area with the engine off","Weak or flat 12 V battery","Transmission warning stored"],3,1,["P27A1","P27A3","P27A5","P276B"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P27A7:["Pressure Control Solenoid A Data Incompatible","P27A7 means the transmission controller holds no usable calibration curve for pressure control solenoid A. Each valve body is measured at the factory, and GM writes its current-to-pressure data into TCM memory; at every start-up the module checks that record.",["New or service TCM installed without loading the solenoid characterization data","Valve body replaced but the data for its part number not written to the TCM","Data set for a different solenoid class or valve body entered","Programming aborted, leaving a corrupted block (checksum error)"],["MIL on right after start-up","Harsh engagements or firm shifts from imprecise line pressure","Transmission may run a substitute program"],4,3,["P27A8","P27A9","P27AA","P27AB","P27AC","P27AD","P27AE"],""],P27A8:["Pressure Control Solenoid B Data Incompatible","With P27A8 the TCM rejects the stored characterization record of pressure control solenoid B. GM's 2016 eight-speed table 16OBDG03 ties B to clutch 2 (CB12345R) and logs the code within one trip when that record is marked as not programmed.",["Characterization download skipped after TCM or valve body replacement","Data loaded for the wrong valve body part number","TCM non-volatile memory corrupting the stored block"],["MIL illuminated","Converter lock-up shudder or no lock-up on the nine-speed","Uneven upshifts involving the affected clutch"],4,3,["P27A7","P27A9","P27AA","P27AB","P27AC","P27AD","P27AE"],""],P27A9:["Pressure Control Solenoid C Data Incompatible","P27A9 concerns solenoid C. GM's controller compares the calibration it holds for this valve with the valve body actually fitted; if the block for C is absent, of the wrong device class, damaged or non-monotonic, the fault is stored at power-up and lights the MIL in that same trip (Type A in 20OBDG04 and in the 2025 table 25OBDG03A).",["Replacement TCM fitted without solenoid C data","Valve body or solenoid assembly swapped without updating the TCM","Stored data corrupted, checksum no longer matches"],["MIL on in the first drive after the fault","Slipping or harsh application of the clutch fed by valve C","On the CVT, unstable line pressure and belt slip risk"],4,3,["P27A7","P27A8","P27AA","P27AB","P27AC","P27AD","P27AE"],""],P27AA:["Pressure Control Solenoid D Data Incompatible","P27AA is set when the TCM finds the calibration block for pressure control solenoid D unusable. Which hardware that is depends on the gearbox: GM's 2016 eight-speed assigns D to clutch 4 (C23468), while the 2017-2020 tables put the nine-speed's C2 clutch (CB29), the ten-speed's C5 clutch and the CVT's C1 clutch behind the same letter, so the D used by stuck-off code P2714 is not always the same part.",["Solenoid data not loaded after a transmission or TCM repair","Used TCM from another vehicle still carrying its old valve body data","Wrong valve body part number used for the download"],["MIL and stored DTC at key-on","Rough shifts into gears using the clutch behind valve D"],4,3,["P27A7","P27A8","P27A9","P27AB","P27AC","P27AD","P27AE","P2714"],""],P27AB:["Pressure Control Solenoid E Data Incompatible","Solenoid E's characterization data failing the TCM's plausibility test produces P27AB. In GM's 2018 table 18OBDG04 the record is written at vehicle assembly according to the valve body part number and must be rewritten by the dealer whenever the valve body is serviced; a missing or partial block, a device class mismatch, a checksum error or falling axis values all count as failures (Type A, one trip).",["Valve body serviced without rewriting the solenoid data","Incomplete programming session after TCM replacement","Solenoid class in the data does not match the TCM calibration"],["MIL lit","Flare or bump on shifts using the clutch behind valve E","On the CVT, irregular torque converter lock-up"],4,3,["P27A7","P27A8","P27A9","P27AA","P27AC","P27AD","P27AE"],""],P27AC:["Pressure Control Solenoid F Data Incompatible","P27AC reports invalid calibration data for pressure control solenoid F. On GM's 2016 eight-speed this is the line pressure solenoid, and the TCM logs the fault in one trip once the data are found unprogrammed. Later GM tables assign F to the nine-speed's C4 clutch, the ten-speed's C6 clutch and the CVT's binary pump; the 2025 table 25OBDG03A still carries the check, with the same start-up test and Type A rating.",["TCM swapped and solenoid F data never loaded","Remanufactured valve body with a new ID not entered into the TCM","Data block damaged by a voltage drop during programming"],["MIL on","Firm or soft shifts throughout when line pressure depends on valve F","Possible fixed-gear substitute mode"],4,3,["P27A7","P27A8","P27A9","P27AA","P27AB","P27AD","P27AE"],""],P27AD:["Pressure Control Solenoid G Data Incompatible","P27AD flags the stored data for pressure control solenoid G as not matching the hardware. GM's 2016 eight-speed table names G the torque converter clutch solenoid and sets the code in one trip. In the 2017 to 2020 tables G is clutch C5 (C57R) on the nine-speed, the line pressure valve on the ten-speed and, only on CVTs with electronic range select, mode valve A;",["Solenoid G data missing after TCM programming","Valve body changed without matching data","TCM calibration for a different transmission variant"],["MIL illuminated","Converter clutch or range mode problems, depending on transmission","General shift harshness on ten-speed units"],4,3,["P27A7","P27A8","P27A9","P27AA","P27AB","P27AC","P27AE"],""],P27AE:["Pressure Control Solenoid H Data Incompatible","P27AE is the highest letter GM publicly checks for characterization data. It is absent from the 2016 eight-speed table and first appears in 17OBDG04, where H stands for the nine-speed's C6 clutch (C6789) and the ten-speed's torque converter clutch; 20OBDG04 adds mode valve B on CVTs with electronic range select.",["Replacement TCM delivered blank and not set up with valve body data","Valve body or solenoid service without data update","Corrupted solenoid H data block"],["MIL on","Shudder or missing converter lock-up on ten-speed units","Higher fuel consumption if lock-up is suppressed"],4,3,["P27A7","P27A8","P27A9","P27AA","P27AB","P27AC","P27AD","P27AF"],""],P27AF:["Pressure Control Solenoid J Data Incompatible","No manufacturer documents P27AF publicly. By its wording it would mean that the TCM considers the stored calibration of a ninth pressure control solenoid, letter J, invalid. GM's published characterization monitor (P27A7 to P27AE, Type A, run at TCM start-up) stops at H, and Ford reports faulty solenoid data on its 10R and 8F transmissions with its own codes P163E and P163F instead of this series.",["Solenoid data not loaded after TCM or valve body replacement","Data set for another valve body variant","Corrupted calibration block in TCM memory"],["MIL illuminated","Rough or inconsistent shifts involving the element behind valve J"],4,3,["P27AE","P27B0","P27AD","P27AC","P27AB","P27AA","P27A9","P27A8"],""],P27B0:["Pressure Control Solenoid K Data Incompatible","P27B0 closes the data-incompatible series with letter K, and no public manufacturer document uses it. It would describe a tenth pressure control solenoid whose calibration record in the transmission controller is missing, mismatched or corrupt. For comparison, GM's 2020 table checks the records of valves A to H once per power-up and rates failures Type A; the ten-speed there needs only eight such valves.",["Valve K data never programmed into a new or used TCM","Valve body ID in the TCM differs from the fitted unit","Software update overwrote or damaged the data block"],["MIL on","Shift quality problems on gears using valve K"],4,3,["P27AF","P27AE","P27AD","P27AC","P27AB","P27AA","P27A9","P27A8"],""],P27B1:["Internal Control Module Transmission Range Select Performance","P27B1 belongs to a family of codes raised by an independent supervision layer in the transmission or powertrain module. That layer repeats key transmission decisions in parallel and flags the main software when both results disagree, as a guard against unintended vehicle motion.",["Supervision or main software calibration in the module","Implausible clutch shaft speed or position input","Internal fault in the transmission control module"],["Transmission warning or wrench light","Restricted gear selection or default gear"],4,2,["P27B2","P27B3","P27B4","P27B5","P27B6","P0701"],"בחירת טווח תיבת הילוכים מודול בקרה פנימי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P27B2:["Internal Control Module Transmission Range Control Performance","P27B2 is set when the monitoring layer cannot confirm that the gearbox is really in the range the main software intends. In GM's 2024 tables for heavy-duty trucks, the TCM checks actual solenoid and pressure switch states with the pattern expected for the range; if they disagree for a full second, the code is logged, lighting the MIL on the first trip.",["Module software (Ford fixes by reprogramming, e.g. TSB 25-2362)","Unusual operating sequence such as selecting a gear after remote start without braking","Solenoid or pressure switch state not matching the commanded range"],["Vehicle stuck in park or will not start","Warning lamp or transmission message","Range change refused"],4,3,["P27B1","P27B3","P27B4","P07E4","P0705"],"בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים מודול בקרה פנימי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P27B3:["Internal Control Module Transmission Gear Select Performance","P27B3 is the monitoring code for the path that turns a chosen gear into actuator commands. In Ford's wording it supervises the actuator manager. In the 2020–2023 summary it is non-MIL on park-by-wire vehicles;",["Supervision software or calibration","Electrical fault at the selectable one-way clutch actuator (Ford 8/10-speed)","Safety-relevant CAN transmit signal faulty (Ford TR9070)"],["Wrench light or transmission message","Certain gears or engine braking functions blocked"],4,2,["P27B1","P27B2","P27B4","P27B5","P0701"],"בחירת הילוך תיבת הילוכים מודול בקרה פנימי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P27B4:["Internal Control Module Transmission Gear Direction Control Performance","P27B4 concerns the direction in which the vehicle actually moves compared with the selected gear. GM's 2024 heavy-duty TCM tables compare the direction reported by the output speed sensor with the direction implied by solenoid and pressure switch states; disagreement for one second sets the code with MIL on the first trip.",["Module software strategy (Ford reprograms PCM or SOBDMC)","Faulty direction information from the output speed sensor","Solenoid or pressure switch reporting a state that does not match the gear"],["MIL or wrench light","Forced idle or reduced power","Gear engagement blocked until restart"],4,3,["P27B2","P27B5","P27B6","P073D","P073F","P0720"],"בקרת כיוון הילוך תיבת הילוכים מודול בקרה פנימי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P27B5:["Internal Control Module Transmission Gear Ratio Control Performance","P27B5 sets when the supervision software doubts the ratio the transmission is running. Ford describes two triggers in its 2024 summary for the eight- and ten-speed automatics: protection against overspeeding a driveline element (UDS P0701_B1) and a plausibility test of the shaft speed ratio (P0701_64), both non-MIL; the 2020–2023 edition likewise keeps it without MIL on electronically shifted models.",["PCM/TCM software strategy (Ford TSB 20-2336)","Implausible input, intermediate or output shaft speed signal","Real slip of a clutch producing an unexpected ratio"],["Warning lamp or wrench light","Forced idle or torque reduction","Transmission held in a fixed gear"],4,3,["P27B4","P27B6","P0730","P0715","P0720"],"בקרת יחס הילוך תיבת הילוכים מודול בקרה פנימי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P27B6:["Internal Control Module Transmission Speed Sensor Performance","P27B6 is the supervision check on the transmission speed signals. GM's 2024 heavy-duty TCM tables work out the output speed that should result from turbine speed and the current gear ratio and set the code, MIL on the first trip, when the raw output speed deviates by 10 or more for at least 10 seconds while output speed is at least 50, the range is not neutral and no shift is under way.",["Module software (Ford TSB 18-2211, PCM reprogramming)","Turbine or output speed sensor delivering an implausible signal","Damaged tone wheel or interference on sensor wiring"],["MIL or wrench light","Harsh or abrupt deceleration events","Fixed gear or limited shifting"],4,3,["P27B4","P27B5","P0715","P0720","P0721"],"חיישן מהירות תיבת הילוכים מודול בקרה פנימי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P27B9:["Pressure Control Solenoid N Performance/Stuck Off","P27B9 says pressure control solenoid N does not build hydraulic force when commanded. On dual-clutch gearboxes this letter belongs to the second synchronizer pressure valve: Ford's 2024 summary lists it for SPV2 of the TR9070, and GM's 2023 Corvette table 23OBDG07 calls it shift solenoid 2 hydraulically stuck off.",["Valve spool sticking closed from debris or varnish","Low or contaminated transmission fluid reducing supply pressure","Leak in the synchronizer actuator circuit","Mechanically binding shift rod or fork"],["MIL on","Certain gears cannot be selected; gear skipping","Substitute mode with reduced gear set"],4,3,["P27BA","P27BB","P27BC","P27BD","P08C4","P27C1"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ N — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P27BA:["Pressure Control Solenoid N Stuck On","P27BA is the opposite fault to P27B9: solenoid N keeps applying pressure when it should be released. GM's dual-clutch table 23OBDG07 (Corvette) describes the effect of a synchronizer valve 2 stuck on as a constant push on one shift rod. Because the selector routes that pressure differently once the selector moves to another position, one rod relaxes or another moves although no movement was commanded;",["Valve spool stuck open by contamination","Worn solenoid armature not returning to rest","Fluid contaminated with clutch or synchronizer wear particles"],["MIL and transmission warning","Gear clash or grinding on shifts","Limp mode with restricted gears"],4,3,["P27B9","P27BB","P27BC","P27C0","P08C5","P27C2"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ N — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P27BB:["Pressure Control Solenoid N Electrical","P27BB is a catch-all electrical code for pressure control solenoid N, and no manufacturer documents it publicly. The two makers known to use solenoid N, GM on the Corvette dual-clutch unit (23OBDG07) and Ford on the TR9070, both split electrical faults of this synchronizer valve into separate codes instead: P27BD covers an open load, P27BF a grounded line and P27C0 a line shorted to battery voltage.",["Solenoid N coil open or shorted","Corroded or loose internal transmission connector","Damaged harness between TCM and transmission","Faulty output driver in the TCM"],["MIL on","Gears served by solenoid N unavailable"],2,3,["P27BC","P27BD","P27BF","P27C0","P08C6"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ N"],P27BC:["Pressure Control Solenoid N Intermittent","P27BC reports that the signal or response of pressure control solenoid N drops out now and then rather than failing permanently. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; the GM and Ford dual-clutch documents that use solenoid N for the second synchronizer valve (23OBDG07, Ford TR9070 list) only publish its permanent electrical and hydraulic faults.",["Loose or spread terminal at solenoid N or TCM","Chafed wire shorting under vibration","Coil opening intermittently when hot"],["MIL that comes and goes","Occasional missed or delayed shifts"],2,3,["P27BB","P27BD","P27BF","P27C0","P08C7"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ N — תקלה לסירוגין"],P27BD:["Pressure Control Solenoid N Control Circuit/Open","P27BD stands for an open control circuit of solenoid N. GM's 2023 Corvette dual-clutch table 23OBDG07 names the part synchronizer actuation valve 2 and tests it while its low-side output is switched off: the driver chip tries to hold the pin at a small voltage with a tiny current, which only works without a load connected.",["Open solenoid N coil","Connector unplugged or pushed-out terminal","Broken control wire between TCM and solenoid"],["MIL on in the same trip","Gears on the affected shift rod blocked","Transmission substitute mode"],2,3,["P27BB","P27BE","P27BF","P27C0","P08C8","P27C5"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ N — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P27BE:["Pressure Control Solenoid N Control Circuit Range/Performance","P27BE means the control circuit of solenoid N is electrically intact but behaves implausibly, for example a measured current that does not follow the command. No manufacturer documents P27BE publicly.",["Solenoid N coil resistance out of specification","High resistance at connector or crimp","Unstable supply voltage to the TCM"],["MIL on","Slow or incomplete gear engagement on one shift rod"],2,3,["P27BD","P27BF","P27C0","P27BB","P27C6"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ N — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P27BF:["Pressure Control Solenoid N Control Circuit Low","P27BF indicates the control line of solenoid N is pulled too low, in practice a short to ground. GM's 23OBDG07 table for the Corvette dual-clutch gearbox checks synchronizer actuation valve 2 while its low-side switch is on: should the sense-pin voltage fall below about 1.7 V (tolerance 0.5 V), the driver chip reports a ground short; 150 ms confirmation, battery between 8.75 and 18 V, engine not cranking, Type A.",["Control wire chafed through to ground","Moisture or corrosion bridging the connector","Solenoid winding shorted to its housing"],["MIL on immediately","Unintended gear actuation or locked-out gears","Limp mode"],2,3,["P27C0","P27BD","P27BE","P27BB","P08CA","P27C7"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ N — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P27C0:["Pressure Control Solenoid N Control Circuit High","P27C0 reports too high a voltage on the control line of solenoid N, usually a short to battery or to a neighbouring output. On the Corvette with GM's dual-clutch gearbox (table 23OBDG07, 2023), synchronizer actuation valve 2 is flagged when the sense voltage stays above roughly 0.7 to 1.1 V, depending on supply voltage, while the low-side switch is on, or when actual current misses the target by over 70 % for 60 ms…",["Control wire shorted to a supply voltage","Two solenoid lines shorted together in the harness or connector","Partially shorted solenoid coil drawing wrong current","Damaged output stage in the TCM"],["MIL on","Shift rod cannot be actuated; gears missing","Code returns at every start after a shutdown test"],2,3,["P27BF","P27BD","P27BE","P27BB","P08CB","P27C8"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ N — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P27C1:["Pressure Control Solenoid P Performance/Stuck Off","P27C1 is logged when pressure control solenoid P is commanded but the shift rods it serves barely move. In GM's Corvette dual-clutch documentation (23OBDG07, unchanged in 24OBDG07) the part is shift solenoid 3; with the selector valve in one position it pushes rod 3, in the other rod 4, both in the A-to-B direction.",["Valve spool of solenoid P held in the closed position by debris or varnish","Low, aerated or degraded transmission fluid so no pressure builds","Leaking seal on the shift rod actuator piston for rods 3/4","Mechanically binding shift rod or fork"],["MIL on with transmission warning","Certain gears skipped or not selectable","Delayed or failed launch in affected gear"],4,3,["P27C2","P27C5","P27C9","P27D1","P27B9","P08C4"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ P — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P27C2:["Pressure Control Solenoid P Stuck On","P27C2 means solenoid P keeps pressurizing after it should have vented. GM's dual-clutch Corvette table 23OBDG07 (and 24OBDG07) detects this on shift solenoid 3 by watching what happens just after the selector valve switches: if one of rods 3 and 4 travels 1,000 µm or more within 200 ms without a command while the other one drops back by at least 125 µm, valve 3 is judged hydraulically stuck on, Type A.",["Spool of solenoid P jammed in the open (pressure-applying) position","Wear particles in the fluid keeping the valve from closing","Worn valve bore letting pressure bypass to the actuator"],["MIL on and gears blocked by the controller","Clunk or grinding during gear changes","Unexpected loss of drive (neutral)"],4,3,["P27C1","P27C8","P27CA","P27D2","P27BA","P08C5"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ P — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P27C3:["Pressure Control Solenoid P Electrical","P27C3 is the general electrical fault code for pressure control solenoid P. No manufacturer documents it publicly. Where solenoid P is known to exist, on GM's Corvette dual-clutch box (23OBDG07, shift solenoid 3) and Ford's TR9070 (SPV3), electrical faults are reported in finer detail: P27C5 for an open load, P27C7 for a shorted switch and P27C8 for a shorted load or excessive current error.",["Solenoid P winding open or shorted","Damaged or corroded pin in the transmission connector","Chafed or broken lead between solenoid and TCM","Faulty output stage in the TCM"],["MIL on","Gears on the affected shift rods unavailable","Transmission in emergency mode"],2,3,["P27C4","P27C5","P27C7","P27C8","P27CB"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ P"],P27C4:["Pressure Control Solenoid P Intermittent","P27C4 indicates that solenoid P works most of the time but its circuit or response briefly drops out. No manufacturer documents the code publicly; GM's Corvette DCT table 23OBDG07 and Ford's TR9070 list, which both use this solenoid as synchronizer valve 3, only publish hard faults such as P27C5, P27C7, P27C8 and the hydraulic codes P27C1/P27C2.",["Fretting corrosion on connector terminals","Wire strand broken inside intact-looking insulation","Solenoid winding that opens at operating temperature"],["MIL that comes and goes","Occasional harsh or missed shift"],2,3,["P27C3","P27C5","P27C7","P27C8","P27CC"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ P — תקלה לסירוגין"],P27C5:["Pressure Control Solenoid P Control Circuit/Open","P27C5 reports an open control circuit on solenoid P. GM's Corvette dual-clutch table 23OBDG07 tests synchronizer actuation valve 3 for this while its low-side driver (a TLE8242 chip) is off: an intact coil pulls the sense pin up towards battery voltage, whereas without a load the driver manages to hold it in a window of about 1.7 to 3.0 V.",["Open winding in solenoid P","Connector not latched or pin pushed back","Broken control wire between TCM and solenoid"],["MIL on immediately","Shifts on rods 3 and 4 in A-to-B direction not possible","Limp mode with restricted gears"],2,3,["P27C3","P27C6","P27C7","P27C8","P27CD","P27BD"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ P — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P27C6:["Pressure Control Solenoid P Control Circuit Range/Performance","P27C6 describes a control circuit for solenoid P that is neither open nor shorted but behaves outside its expected range, for example current that does not track the command. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Coil resistance drifting with temperature","Corroded contacts adding series resistance","Unstable TCM supply voltage"],["MIL on","Inconsistent shift quality on the affected rods"],2,3,["P27C5","P27C7","P27C8","P27C3","P27CE"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ P — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P27C7:["Pressure Control Solenoid P Control Circuit Low","P27C7 points to a control circuit of solenoid P that is too low, effectively a short to ground on the switched side. GM's 23OBDG07 Corvette dual-clutch table checks synchronizer actuation valve 3 with its low-side switch on and expects the sense resistor voltage to be pulled down only so far;",["Control wire shorted to ground against the case","Moisture or oil bridging pins in the connector","Solenoid winding shorted to its housing"],["MIL on","Unwanted application of rods 3/4, gears blocked","Limp mode"],2,3,["P27C8","P27C5","P27C6","P27C3","P27CF","P27BF"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ P — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P27C8:["Pressure Control Solenoid P Control Circuit High","P27C8 signals too high a level in the control circuit of solenoid P. GM's Corvette DCT tables 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 store it for synchronizer actuation valve 3 in three situations, all Type A. First, with the low-side switch on, the sense voltage stays above a supply-dependent limit of 0.7, 0.9 or 1.1 V (below 11.5 V, 12-15 V, above 15.5 V battery).",["Control line shorted to battery voltage","Control line shorted to a neighbouring solenoid output","Solenoid P coil with too low resistance (shorted turns)","TCM driver stage fault"],["MIL on, possibly at the start after a previous drive","Gears of rods 3/4 unavailable","Limp mode"],2,3,["P27C7","P27C5","P27C6","P27C3","P27D0","P27C0"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ P — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P27C9:["Pressure Control Solenoid R Performance/Stuck Off","Solenoid R is the fourth synchronizer pressure valve on the dual-clutch units that use it, and P27C9 says it failed to move anything. GM's 2023 and 2024 Corvette tables (23OBDG07/24OBDG07) call it shift solenoid 4; it acts on the same two rods as valve 3 but drives them back from B towards A. The integrity check commands that motion for each selector position and expects more than 100 µm of rod travel;",["Spool of solenoid R stuck closed","Supply passage or screen to valve R clogged by debris","Leaking actuator seal on the B-to-A side of rods 3/4"],["MIL on with transmission message","Gear stays engaged or cannot be selected","Reduced gear range"],4,3,["P27CA","P27CD","P27C1","P27D1","P27B9","P08C4"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ R — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P27CA:["Pressure Control Solenoid R Stuck On","P27CA is the stuck-on fault of solenoid R, GM's shift solenoid 4 on the Corvette dual-clutch transmission. The detection in 23OBDG07 mirrors that of valve 3 because both valves share rods 3 and 4, only with opposite pushing direction: a selector change followed by an uncommanded jump of one rod of at least 1 mm inside 200 ms plus a 0.125 mm relaxation of its partner points to valve 4 holding pressure.",["Spool of solenoid R jammed open","Debris lodged in valve R preventing venting","Internal wear of solenoid R armature or seat"],["MIL on","Grinding or clunk when changing gears","Gears locked out by the controller"],4,3,["P27C9","P27D0","P27C2","P27D2","P27BA","P08C5"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ R — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P27CB:["Pressure Control Solenoid R Electrical","An electrical fault of unspecified kind on solenoid R is what P27CB stands for. There is no public manufacturer description of this exact code. GM (shift solenoid 4 in the Corvette DCT table 23OBDG07) and Ford (SPV4 of the TR9070, 2024 overview) both use solenoid R, yet they break its wiring faults down into P27CD, P27CF and P27D0 rather than one lumped code.",["Solenoid R winding resistance out of specification","Poor pin fit in the gearbox connector","Damaged harness insulation","TCM output stage fault"],["MIL on","Gear selection limited","Emergency mode possible"],2,3,["P27CC","P27CD","P27CF","P27D0","P27C3"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ R"],P27CC:["Pressure Control Solenoid R Intermittent","With P27CC the transmission controller has seen solenoid R lose its circuit or its effect for short moments only. A public, code-specific manufacturer description does not exist. The two known users of solenoid R, GM's Corvette dual-clutch transmission (23OBDG07, valve 4) and Ford's TR9070 (SPV4), document only lasting electrical faults and stuck conditions for it.",["Loose or spread terminal pin","Transmission fluid wicking into the connector","Harness conductor breaking under vibration"],["Intermittent MIL","Sporadic rough or delayed shift"],2,3,["P27CB","P27CD","P27CF","P27D0","P27C4"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ R — תקלה לסירוגין"],P27CD:["Pressure Control Solenoid R Control Circuit/Open","P27CD is set when the control circuit of solenoid R appears open, so the module cannot energize the valve. On GM's Corvette with dual-clutch transmission (23OBDG07, again in 24OBDG07) the part is synchronizer actuation valve 4. The test runs with the output switched off: without a coil in the circuit, nothing pulls the sense voltage up to battery level, and it remains between roughly 1.7 and 3.0 V;",["Terminal pushed out of the connector housing","Burnt-out winding of solenoid R","Cut or broken control lead"],["MIL on","Shifts on rods 3 and 4 in B-to-A direction not possible","Limp mode"],2,3,["P27CB","P27CE","P27CF","P27D0","P27C5","P27BD"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ R — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P27CE:["Pressure Control Solenoid R Control Circuit Range/Performance","P27CE would be stored if the control circuit of solenoid R stayed electrically connected yet produced values that make no sense to the controller. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. On the Corvette dual-clutch transmission GM checks valve 4 for a mismatch between commanded and estimated current (over 70 % for 60 ms, or 400 mA for 300 ms in 23OBDG07), but that check reports P27D0.",["Rising contact resistance in the circuit","Solenoid R with partly shorted turns","Weak TCM driver output"],["MIL on","Shift feel varies on rods 3 and 4"],2,3,["P27CD","P27CF","P27D0","P27CB","P27C6"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ R — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P27CF:["Pressure Control Solenoid R Control Circuit Low","P27CF tells that the control line of solenoid R is held low, as if shorted to ground. On the Corvette dual-clutch transmission GM (23OBDG07, still present in 24OBDG07) monitors synchronizer actuation valve 4 while energized; the driver chip compares the sense pin with a threshold of roughly 1.7 V and, after 150 ms below it, reports a ground fault rated Type A.",["Chafed insulation grounding the control line","Harness crushed at a clip or bracket","Solenoid R coil shorted to its housing"],["MIL on","Unwanted rod movement, gears locked out","Limp mode"],2,3,["P27D0","P27CD","P27CE","P27CB","P27C7","P27BF"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ R — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P27D0:["Pressure Control Solenoid R Control Circuit High","P27D0 is the high-side counterpart of P27CF for solenoid R: the control line reads too high, most often because it touches battery voltage or another output. GM applies the same driver diagnostics to synchronizer actuation valve 4 of the Corvette dual-clutch box as to the other valves (23OBDG07, 24OBDG07): a sense voltage stuck above 0.7-1.1 V while switched on, a large gap between target and estimated current, or a…",["Control line touching battery voltage","Cross-short to a neighbouring solenoid line","Solenoid R coil resistance too low","Defective TCM driver"],["MIL on, sometimes only after restart","Gears on rods 3/4 not available","Limp mode"],2,3,["P27CF","P27CD","P27CE","P27CB","P27C8","P27C0"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ R — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P27D1:["Pressure Control Solenoid S Performance/Stuck Off","P27D1 flags pressure control solenoid S as unable to produce force. Only GM documents it publicly: in the Corvette dual-clutch tables 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 it is shift solenoid 5, the only one of these valves serving a single rod, rod 5, which it moves in both directions depending on the selector position.",["Spool of solenoid S sticking closed","Low or worn-out transmission fluid","Leak at the rod 5 actuator piston"],["MIL on","Gears on rod 5 unavailable","Gearbox in substitute mode"],4,3,["P27D2","P27D3","P27D5","P27C1","P27C9"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ S — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P27D2:["Pressure Control Solenoid S Stuck On","With P27D2 the TCM concludes that solenoid S applies pressure that was never requested. GM is the only maker publishing it, for shift solenoid 5 of the Corvette dual-clutch gearbox (23OBDG07, carried over to 24OBDG07). Because valve 5 serves rod 5 on its own, there is no partner rod to relax;",["Spool of solenoid S jammed open","Particles keeping valve S from venting","Worn armature or seat in solenoid S"],["MIL on","Harsh engagement or clunk","Gears on rod 5 blocked, fallback mode"],4,3,["P27D1","P27D3","P27D8","P27C2","P27CA"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ S — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P27D3:["Pressure Control Solenoid S Electrical","P27D3 reports an electrical problem with pressure control solenoid S without saying which kind. No manufacturer publishes this code. GM, the only maker known to fit a fifth synchronizer valve (Corvette dual-clutch, 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07), monitors that valve with separate codes from the S block: P27D5 open load, P27D7 short to ground and P27D8 short to battery, current error or a short to a neighbouring output found…",["Solenoid S coil open or shorted","Corroded or loose connector at the transmission","Damaged wiring between TCM and solenoid S"],["MIL on","Gears on rod 5 unavailable","Limp mode possible"],2,3,["P27D4","P27D5","P27D7","P27D8","P27CB"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ S"],P27D4:["Pressure Control Solenoid S Intermittent","P27D4 means the controller noticed solenoid S dropping out now and then, electrically or in its effect, without the fault staying present. No manufacturer publishes this code. GM, whose Corvette dual-clutch gearbox has a fifth synchronizer valve for rod 5 (tables 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07), reports lasting wiring faults on it as P27D5, P27D7 and P27D8 and its stuck states as P27D1 and P27D2;",["Gearbox connector seal leaking, terminals corroding","Harness conductor breaking under engine movement","Solenoid S winding dropping out when hot"],["MIL comes and goes","Rod 5 gears occasionally refused"],2,3,["P27D3","P27D5","P27D7","P27D8","P27D1","P27CC"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ S — תקלה לסירוגין"],P27D5:["Pressure Control Solenoid S Control Circuit/Open","P27D5 stands for an interrupted control circuit of solenoid S. GM uses it for synchronizer actuation valve 5 in the Corvette DCT, documented in 23OBDG07 and again in 24OBDG07. While the low-side output is off, a working coil pulls the sense pin up to supply voltage; the driver chip then tries to hold that pin low with a tiny current.",["Terminal pushed back in the gearbox connector","Open winding in solenoid S","Broken control wire between TCM and valve"],["MIL on","Gears on rod 5 missing","Emergency program"],2,3,["P27D7","P27D8","P27D6","P27D3","P27D1","P27CD"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ S — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P27D6:["Pressure Control Solenoid S Control Circuit Range/Performance","P27D6 would indicate that the circuit of solenoid S is still closed but its electrical behaviour does not fit what the module commands. There is no public manufacturer description. On the Corvette dual-clutch transmission GM does compare target and estimated coil current of valve 5 (a 70 % gap held 60 ms, or a 400 mA gap held 300 ms, per 23OBDG07), yet files that result under the high-circuit code P27D8, so P27D6…",["Added resistance at a crimp or pin","Solenoid S coil resistance out of specification","TCM output stage losing strength"],["MIL on","Uneven shifts into rod 5 gears"],2,3,["P27D5","P27D7","P27D8","P27D3","P27CE"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ S — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P27D7:["Pressure Control Solenoid S Control Circuit Low","P27D7 reports the control line of solenoid S stuck at too low a level, typically a short to ground. GM applies it to synchronizer actuation valve 5 on the Corvette dual-clutch gearbox (23OBDG07, carried into 24OBDG07): with the output switched on, the sense pin should be pulled down only partly;",["Control wire chafed through to ground","Solenoid S coil shorted to its housing","Faulty low-side driver in the TCM"],["MIL on","Unintended rod 5 movement, gears locked","Limp mode"],2,3,["P27D8","P27D5","P27D6","P27D2","P27CF"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ S — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P27D8:["Pressure Control Solenoid S Control Circuit High","P27D8 says the control line of solenoid S sits too high. GM bundles three checks for valve 5 of the Corvette dual-clutch box under it (23OBDG07, 24OBDG07), all Type A. First, with the output on, a sense voltage above 700, 900 or 1,100 mV, depending on whether supply is below 11.5 V, between 12 and 15 V or above 15.5 V, means a short to battery.",["Control wire touching a supply line","Short to the wire of another valve output","Solenoid S coil with shorted turns"],["MIL on, possibly only after the next start","Rod 5 gears out of reach","Limp mode"],2,3,["P27D7","P27D5","P27D6","P27D1","P27D0"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ S — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P27D9:["Pressure Control Solenoid T Performance/Stuck Off","P27D9 is logged when solenoid T fails to build the pressure it is asked for. Ford's 2024 OBD overview for the TR9070 dual-clutch gearbox assigns it to the selector pilot valve (SELPV) when that valve stays hydraulically off. That pilot valve moves the selector valve, which decides which shift rods the synchronizer valves SPV1 to SPV4 act on;",["Selector pilot valve stuck closed","Low or contaminated transmission fluid","Selector valve spool binding in its bore"],["MIL on","Several gears unavailable","Gearbox in fallback mode"],4,3,["P27DA","P27DD","P27DF","P27E0","P2829"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ T — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P27DA:["Pressure Control Solenoid T Stuck On","P27DA marks solenoid T as delivering pressure while it should be vented. Ford lists it in the 2024 overview for the TR9070 for a selector pilot valve whose hydraulic output stays on; neighbouring entries P178C and P178A cover the selector valve and the complete selector mechanism stuck on. Ford gives no detection limits.",["Selector pilot valve held open by dirt","Worn seat or armature in solenoid T","Abrasion particles from clutch or synchronizer wear"],["MIL on","Gears locked out, wrong gear engagement possible","Fallback mode"],4,3,["P27D9","P27DF","P27E0","P282A"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ T — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P27DB:["Pressure Control Solenoid T Electrical","P27DB is a catch-all for electrical trouble on solenoid T that does not name the kind of fault. No manufacturer publishes it. The only known valve T is the selector pilot valve of Ford's TR9070 dual-clutch gearbox, and Ford's 2024 overview splits that valve's wiring faults into P27DD for open load, P27DF for a shorted switch and P27E0 for a shorted load instead of using this code.",["Solenoid T coil open or shorted","Corrosion or poor fit at the gearbox connector","Defective TCM output for solenoid T"],["MIL on","Restricted gear choice","Limp mode possible"],2,3,["P27DC","P27DD","P27DF","P27E0","P282B"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ T"],P27DC:["Pressure Control Solenoid T Intermittent","With P27DC the module reports that solenoid T misbehaved only briefly before working again. No maker has published a description of this code. Ford's TR9070, the only known application of a valve T (selector pilot valve, 2024 overview), is covered by lasting electrical codes and by stuck-on and stuck-off codes, none of them sporadic. CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 requires the transmission actuators to be monitored.",["Loose pin in the gearbox connector","Particles briefly holding the valve spool","Harness rubbing through under vibration"],["MIL lights up from time to time","Occasional failed or late gear selection"],2,3,["P27DB","P27DD","P27D9","P27DA","P27D4"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ T — תקלה לסירוגין"],P27DD:["Pressure Control Solenoid T Control Circuit/Open","P27DD tells that the control circuit of solenoid T is open, so no current reaches the coil. Ford's 2024 OBD overview gives this code to open load on the selector pilot valve of the TR9070 dual-clutch transmission; the document lists the fault type only, without limits.",["Displaced terminal in the connector","Broken lead to solenoid T","Burnt-through winding of solenoid T"],["MIL on","Only some gears selectable","Fallback mode"],2,3,["P27DF","P27E0","P27DE","P27DB","P282D"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ T — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P27DE:["Pressure Control Solenoid T Control Circuit Range/Performance","P27DE would be set if the circuit of solenoid T is intact but delivers readings the controller considers implausible. No manufacturer documents the code. For the selector pilot valve of the TR9070, Ford's 2024 summary knows just three electrical faults, namely open load, shorted load and shorted switch, and GM checks the comparable Corvette pilot valve under its own K-block codes.",["Rising contact resistance at a terminal","Solenoid T resistance drifted from nominal","TCM output no longer regulating current"],["MIL on","Hesitant or inconsistent gear selection"],2,3,["P27DD","P27DF","P27E0","P27DB","P282E"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ T — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P27DF:["Pressure Control Solenoid T Control Circuit Low","P27DF points to a control line of solenoid T pulled too low. In Ford's 2024 OBD summary it is the shorted-switch fault of the selector pilot valve on the TR9070 dual-clutch gearbox, meaning the switched side of the coil is tied to ground and the valve can be powered permanently. Ford publishes no thresholds.",["Damaged insulation letting the wire touch ground","Solenoid T coil shorted to ground","TCM output switch stuck conducting"],["MIL on","Gears fenced off, shifts limited to some gears","Limp mode"],2,3,["P27E0","P27DD","P27DE","P27DA","P282F"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ T — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P27E0:["Pressure Control Solenoid T Control Circuit High","P27E0 reports a control line of solenoid T sitting too high. Ford's 2024 overview of the TR9070 dual-clutch gearbox uses it for a shorted load on the selector pilot valve, a coil or line bypassed to battery so the driver cannot pull current through the winding. Limits are not stated by Ford.",["Control wire shorted to a supply feed","Shorted turns in solenoid T","Cross-short to an adjacent valve line"],["MIL on","Gears of one rod group lost","Fallback mode"],2,3,["P27DF","P27DD","P27DE","P27D9","P2830"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ T — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P27E1:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump A Pressure Too Low","P27E1 is a hydraulic verdict, not a wiring one: electric auxiliary pump A was running on command, yet the pressure it built stayed below what the module expected. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly.",["Worn pump gears or internal leakage inside pump A","Low or aerated transmission fluid, pump draws air","Intake screen of the pump partly blocked by debris","Check valve in the pump circuit not sealing"],["Stop-start function disabled","Jerky or delayed engagement when the engine restarts after a stop","MIL or transmission warning lit"],3,3,["P27E2","P2797","P0B0C","P2796","P27E3"],"לחץ משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ A — ערך נמוך מדי"],P27E2:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Pressure Too Low","P27E2 flags that the second electric pump, B, delivered too little pressure although it was driven. Nobody publishes this code openly. Where a gearbox carries a pump labelled B, it is often a separate unit on the outside of the case: Audi's bulletin 34-17-25 calls oil pump V553 of the 0CJ, 0CK and 0CL seven-speed twin-clutch boxes pump B and lists P27A3, P27A6 and P276B for it, but not P27E2.",["Pump B worn, motor running but delivering too little","Leaking O-ring or pressure line between pump B and the gearbox","Fluid level too low for pump B to prime","Weak battery or poor ground slowing the pump motor"],["Stop-start no longer stops the engine","Reduced clutch cooling, power limited when hot","Warning light on"],3,3,["P27E1","P27A3","P277A","P27A2"],"לחץ משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — ערך נמוך מדי"],P27E3:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump Control Valve Circuit/Open","The control valve named here decides where the oil from the electric auxiliary pump goes. Volkswagen's training book for the 0GC seven-speed DSG shows such a layout: pressure regulator N218 shifts a spring-loaded changeover piston that sends the flow of pump V475 either to the mechatronic unit or to clutch cooling. No maker publishes P27E3 itself.",["Broken conductor in the valve control line","Pin backed out or corroded at the gearbox connector","Valve coil burnt open"],["Stop-start unavailable","Warning light with stored open-circuit fault"],2,3,["P27E4","P27E5","P27E6","P27E1","P2796"],"שסתום בקרת משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P27E4:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump Control Valve Circuit Range/Performance","P27E4 is the plausibility check for the auxiliary pump control valve: the circuit is intact, but its current or its hydraulic effect does not match the command. No manufacturer lists the code publicly, so the logic can only be inferred.",["Valve or changeover piston sticking from contaminated fluid","Coil resistance drifting with temperature","Contact resistance at the connector distorting the current"],["Stop-start works only sometimes","Harsh engagement after an auto-start","Warning light on"],3,3,["P27E3","P27E5","P27E6","P27E1","P27E2"],"שסתום בקרת משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P27E5:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump Control Valve Circuit Low","P27E5 sets when the voltage on the auxiliary pump control valve line is pulled toward ground, typically by chafed insulation touching the case or by a coil shorted internally. No manufacturer documents the code openly. For orientation: in Volkswagen's 8-speed 09P and 0GC transmissions the electric pump V475 keeps pressure while the engine is stopped, and a regulator-driven valve routes its flow;",["Control line chafed through and touching ground","Valve coil shorted internally","Fluid or water in the connector bridging to ground"],["Stop-start switched off","MIL lit"],2,3,["P27E3","P27E4","P27E6","P2798"],"שסתום בקרת משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר — אות נמוך במעגל"],P27E6:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump Control Valve Circuit High","P27E6 means the control valve circuit of the auxiliary pump reads higher than allowed, as if the line were tied to battery voltage. A wire rubbing against a live conductor in the same harness, or a driver stage that no longer switches off, are the classic triggers. The code is not documented by any manufacturer in public.",["Control line shorted to a supply wire in the harness","Corrosion bridging adjacent pins in the connector","Output stage in the control module stuck on"],["Stop-start inoperative","Warning light on, possibly further pump codes"],2,3,["P27E3","P27E4","P27E5","P2799"],"שסתום בקרת משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר — אות גבוה במעגל"],P27E7:["Transmission Range Control B Circuit/Open","'Transmission Range Control' belongs to shift-by-wire, where the selected range travels as an electrical signal instead of a cable. Only channel A is documented in public: Mitsubishi's 2022 manual sets P07E8 when one of eight electric shift sensors in the selector rises above 4.5 V for 2.4 s with the ignition on, and names no fail-safe reaction.",["Loose or corroded connector at the electric selector","Broken wire between selector and control module","Sensor inside the selector assembly failed open"],["Warning about the shift system in the cluster","Some ranges not accepted from the selector"],2,3,["P27E8","P27E9","P27EA","P07E8","P27EF"],"בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P27E8:["Transmission Range Control B Circuit Performance","P27E8 is the plausibility test for range control circuit B: the signal is neither open nor shorted, yet its value makes no sense, for example a level stuck between the valid on and off windows. The title reads Circuit Performance, without Range. No manufacturer publishes the code.",["Contact resistance at selector terminals shifting the voltage","Spilled drink or moisture inside the selector","Position sensor in the selector degrading"],["Intermittent shift system warning","Displayed range occasionally flickers or lags"],2,1,["P27E7","P27E9","P27EA","P07E9","P27F0"],"בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P27E9:["Transmission Range Control B Circuit Low","P27E9 reports that a line of range control circuit B sits too close to zero volts, pointing to a grounded line or a sensor that pulls its output down. It is not described publicly by any manufacturer.",["Harness pinched under the center console, shorted to ground","Selector sensor output shorted internally","Sensor supply interrupted, output drops to zero"],["Shift system warning on the display","Usually no change in how the car drives"],2,1,["P27E7","P27E8","P27EA","P07EA","P27F1"],"בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P27EA:["Transmission Range Control B Circuit High","With P27EA, a signal of range control circuit B reads near the supply voltage, which usually means a short to a power wire or a broken ground return that lets the line float high. No manufacturer documents the B code openly. Mitsubishi's channel A twin, P07EB, sets above 4.5 V on one of the eight sensors in the electric selector for 2.4 s and lists a short to power as cause; normal driving remains possible.",["Signal line shorted to a supply wire","Sensor ground open, signal floats high","Selector electronics faulty"],["Shift system message in the cluster","Car usually still drives normally"],2,1,["P27E7","P27E8","P27E9","P07EB","P27F2"],"בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P27EB:["Transmission Range Control A Position Sensor/Switch Circuit/Open","GM uses this code on automatics with internal electronic range selection (ETRS), where hydraulic mode valves within the valve body set park, reverse, neutral and drive. Mode valve A carries a Hall position sensor.",["Signal wire of the mode valve A sensor broken or loose","Hall sensor on mode valve A failing","Damaged internal transmission harness or pass-through connector"],["MIL on after the first trip","Range selection restricted or delayed"],3,3,["P27EC","P27ED","P27EE","P27EF"],"חיישן/מתג מצב בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P27EC:["Transmission Range Control A Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance","P27EC is GM's movement check for mode valve A of its internal range selection: after the TCM commands park, drive or reverse, the position sensor must report the new state within a set delay; the logic also watches line pressure and clutch slip. Both the 2018 nine-speed and 2020 ten-speed tables rate it Type A.",["Mode valve A sticking inside the control valve body","No hydraulic pressure from a failed auxiliary pump during auto stop","Mode valve A position sensor reading wrong"],["Delayed or refused shift into park, drive or reverse","MIL on, stop-start may be disabled","Transmission in reduced operating mode"],4,3,["P27EB","P27ED","P27EE","P27F0","P2797"],"חיישן/מתג מצב בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P27ED:["Transmission Range Control A Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Low","P27ED tells that the Hall sensor on mode valve A of GM's internal range selection delivers almost no voltage. In both the 2018 9-speed and the 2020 10-speed RWD tables the limit is a raw value under 0.414 V for 0.100 s within 0.163 s, with at least 9 V on the battery; GM itself blames a grounded or interrupted line. The code is Type A and lights the MIL on the first trip.",["Sensor signal shorted to ground in the internal harness","Sensor supply open, output collapses","Hall sensor on mode valve A failed"],["MIL lit immediately","Shifts out of park slow or blocked"],3,3,["P27EB","P27EC","P27EE","P27F1"],"חיישן/מתג מצב בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P27EE:["Transmission Range Control A Position Sensor/Switch Circuit High","The opposite of P27ED: the position sensor of mode valve A reads higher than any valid state. GM's TCM tables for the T87A nine-speed of 2018 and the rear-drive ten-speed of 2020 set P27EE when the raw signal exceeds 2.538 V for 0.100 s inside a 0.163 s sample, describing it as a short to voltage on the sensor circuit; the MIL comes on at once (Type A).",["Sensor signal shorted to a voltage source","Sensor ground open, signal drifts high","Hall sensor output stage faulty"],["MIL on from the first trip","Range changes restricted, possible reduced mode"],3,3,["P27EB","P27EC","P27ED","P27F2"],"חיישן/מתג מצב בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P27EF:["Transmission Range Control B Position Sensor/Switch Circuit/Open","P27EF concerns the second mode valve, B, of GM's internal electronic range selection. Its Hall sensor is expected to sit clearly high or clearly low; GM's 2018 9-speed and 2020 10-speed RWD tables treat a raw value between 1.263 and 1.504 V, held for 0.100 s of a 0.163 s sample, as an illegal level. A level in that gap typically comes from an interrupted signal line or a sensor that has stopped switching.",["Mode valve B sensor signal line interrupted","Hall sensor on mode valve B no longer switching cleanly","Fluid or corrosion at the transmission pass-through connector"],["Transmission warning, neutral or drive engagement may be restricted","Fault stored in the TCM"],3,3,["P27F0","P27F1","P27F2","P27EB"],"חיישן/מתג מצב בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P27F0:["Transmission Range Control B Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance","P27F0 checks whether mode valve B really moves. In GM's 2020 table for the T87A 10-speed RWD transmission, the TCM expects the valve B sensor to follow commands to park, reverse, neutral high or low, neutral shift and drive within a delay; if the final state is not reached under adequate line pressure, the Type A code sets. The electrical sensor codes P27EF, P27F1 and P27F2 must be clear for the test to run.",["Mode valve B sticking in the valve body","Insufficient line pressure to move the valve","Position sensor B reporting late or wrong state"],["Delay or refusal when selecting neutral, drive or reverse","MIL on, transmission may enter a protective mode"],4,3,["P27EF","P27F1","P27F2","P27EC"],"חיישן/מתג מצב בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P27F1:["Transmission Range Control B Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Low","P27F1 reports a valve B position signal that has collapsed toward ground in GM's internal range selection. GM describes the trigger as a ground short or open circuit on the mode valve B sensor line and uses the same 0.414 V limit, 0.100 s debounce and 9 V minimum supply as on valve A; both table editions, 2018 and 2020, rate it Type A, MIL on the first trip.",["Valve B sensor line shorted to ground","Sensor supply missing at the internal connector","Hall sensor on mode valve B failed"],["MIL comes on on the first trip","Neutral or drive engagement slow or blocked"],3,3,["P27EF","P27F0","P27F2","P27ED"],"חיישן/מתג מצב בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P27F2:["Transmission Range Control B Position Sensor/Switch Circuit High","With P27F2 the TCM sees the valve B position sensor above its valid range, which GM interprets as a short to voltage on that circuit. The threshold is 2.538 V, which must persist 0.100 s in a 0.163 s sampling period; GM applies it to internal range selection in the 2018 T87A nine-speed and the 2020 rear-drive ten-speed. The 2020 table rates it Type A; in the 2018 edition the MIL entry for P27F2 is blank.",["Valve B sensor line shorted to a voltage source","Sensor ground interrupted","Hall sensor B electronics faulty"],["Warning light and stored transmission fault","Neutral or drive selection restricted"],3,3,["P27EF","P27F0","P27F1","P27EE"],"חיישן/מתג מצב בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P27F3:["Clutch B Temperature Too High","P27F3 reports that the second clutch of a gearbox, usually the clutch on the even-gear side of a dual-clutch unit, has exceeded its permitted temperature, either measured or calculated from slip and load.",["Pump in the electric clutch actuator blocked by particles","Long slipping phases from creeping, towing or hill starts","Worn clutch 2 that needs more slip to transmit torque","Insufficient clutch cooling or low or aged fluid"],["Malfunction indicator and transmission warning lamp on","Even gears or reverse temporarily unavailable","Judder or burning smell when pulling away"],4,3,["P2787","P28D5","P28C7"],"טמפרטורת מצמד‏ B — ערך גבוה מדי"],P27F4:["Gear Shift Lock Solenoid/Actuator A Performance/Stuck On","P27F4 concerns the mechanical result of the shift lock, not its wiring: actuator A was commanded but stays in its active state or does not reach the requested position. Whether active means locked or released depends on the design. No manufacturer documents P27F4 publicly.",["Lock pin or actuator binding in the shifter mechanism","Faulty gear shift module or its software","Implausible brake pedal signal keeping the lock commanded"],["Selector cannot be moved out of Park despite pressing the brake","Shift system warning or wrench lamp in the cluster","Clicking from the shifter with no release"],2,0,["P27F5","P0929","P0928","P0930","P0931"],""],P27F5:["Gear Shift Lock Solenoid/Actuator A Stuck Off","With P27F5 the control unit concludes that shift lock actuator A remains in its passive state although it was told to act. Depending on the design, that can leave the lever free to leave Park without the brake, which defeats the brake interlock, or permanently blocked. No maker publishes this code.",["Loose or badly crimped terminal at the lock solenoid","Weak solenoid coil that no longer moves the lock pin","Broken return spring or worn lock pin","Shifter module software misjudging the actuator position"],["Selector leaves Park without the brake pedal being pressed","Lever stays blocked in Park or Neutral","Shift system warning message"],2,0,["P27F4","P0929","P0928","P0931"],""]};export{e as default};
